}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/03f0797c-24e0-50ae-b096-5e48fcc4495b', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03f0797c-24e0-50ae-b096-5e48fcc4495b'}, {'abstract': 'Rescue workers pulled eight survivors from the mud a day after a huge landslide hit the village of Malin in the Pune district of Maharashtra State in western India.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/01/world/asia/india-dozens-of-villagers-still-missing-after-landslide.html', 'snippet': 'Rescue workers pulled eight survivors from the mud a day after a huge landslide hit the village of Malin in the Pune district of Maharashtra State in western India.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Although heavy rains hindered their work, rescue workers on Thursday pulled eight survivors from the mud a day after a huge landslide hit the village of Malin in the Pune district of Maharashtra State in western India. The workers also recovered the bodies of 31 people. The landslide buried at least 40 homes and more than 150 people, officials said. “The chances of finding anybody else alive are remote, but we still do not rule out the possibility,” said Surjeet Singh Guleria, a senior officer of the National Disaster Rescue Force. “We have deployed 378 soldiers and officers on the ground. They are working around the clock, but their work is hampered by continuous rains.” India’s home minister, Rajnath Singh, and Maharashtra State’s chief minister, Prithviraj Chavan, both visited Malin on Thursday. “This is a very heart-wrenching scene here,” Mr. Singh said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India: Dozens of Villagers Still Missing After Landslide', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India: Dozens of Villagers Still Missing After Landslide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 