 in 1979.) Next month, the Museum of Contemporary Art Chicago presents “David Bowie Is,” a retrospective of his career.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-01T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/4850daa5-c382-5475-9135-018d2331329e', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4850daa5-c382-5475-9135-018d2331329e'}, {'abstract': 'On cellphones, security monitors and dashboard cameras, the residents of Kaohsiung captured the terrifying series of explosions that rocked their city.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/01/videos-capture-terror-of-deadly-taiwan-explosions/', 'snippet': 'On cellphones, security monitors and dashboard cameras, the residents of Kaohsiung captured the terrifying series of explosions that rocked their city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A series of powerful explosions late Thursday in the southern Taiwanese city of Kaohsiung killed 25 people and injured more than 260.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Videos Capture Terror of Deadly Taiwan Explosions', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions (Accidental)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-01T05:08:26+0000', 'doc