t': 'Somi and Gregory Porter, two musicians comfortable in fusing multiple genres, perform their tweaked styles of jazz singing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Borders have always been porous among jazz, R&B, pop, world music and, lately, hip-hop. Two musicians comfortable in the overlaps perform this week. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singers Stretch Their Genres', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop: Singers Stretch Their Genres', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Porter, Gregory', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Somi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-01T16:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0af4b304-67e7-51a0-8594-98d305a11315', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0af4b304-67e7-51a0-8594-98d305a11315'}, {'abstract': 'The Film Society of Lincoln Center presents a series of sleek, soft-core movies by Radley Metzger that pushed the boundaries of sexual explicitness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/03/movies/this-is-softcore-plays-at-the-elinor-bunin-munroe-film-center.html', 'snippet': 'The Film Society of Lincoln Center presents a series of sleek, soft-core movies by Radley Metzger that pushed the boundaries of sexual explicitness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As television and film have pushed the boundaries of sexual explicitness, an examination of the sleek, soft-core movies that were once viewed as upscale exploitation fare for prurient audiences resistant to hard-core pornography is long overdue. On Thursday, the Film Society of Lincoln Center begins its series “This Is Softcore: The Art Cinema Erotica of Radley Metzger” at the Elinor Bunin Munroe Film Center with “Carmen, Baby” (1967), this director’s take on Prosper Mérimée’s 19th-century novella that inspired the Bizet opera “Carmen.” Uta Levka plays the Gypsy temptress who, much to the distress of the policeman who loves her, sleeps her way to the top of the social ladder in 1960s Spain. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/arts/03GUIDE6/03GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 493, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/03/arts/03GUIDE6/03GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 493}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/arts/03GUIDE6/03GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/arts/03GUIDE6/03GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1682, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/arts/03GUIDE6/03GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/03/arts/03GUIDE6/03GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/ar