', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most civic buildings such as post offices and firehouses are spread out every 10 or 20 blocks, solitary outposts of municipal order. In a few cases they were built in little pockets, such as the unusual group around York Avenue in the far East 70s, which included three model tenement complexes, a school, a library, a settlement house and a public bath. All served an area once called Little Bohemia. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/realestate/03SUB-scapes1/03SUB-scapes1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/03/realestate/03SUB-scapes1/03SUB-scapes1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 754}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/realestate/03SUB-scapes1/03SUB-scapes1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 816, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/realestate/03SUB-scapes1/03SUB-scapes1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1631, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/realestate/03SUB-scapes1/03SUB-scapes1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/03/realestate/03SUB-scapes1/03SUB-scapes1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/realestate/03SUB-scapes1/03SUB-scapes1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150,