y like artful misdirection by the intelligence agencies.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/01/problems-with-the-bill-limiting-surveillance/', 'snippet': 'It has shortcomings and aspects that look suspiciously like artful misdirection by the intelligence agencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like other people who have been concerned about the erosion of our constitutional rights since the 9/11 terrorist attacks, the editorial board was happy when Senator Patrick Leahy, the Vermont Democrat who heads the Senate Judiciary Committee, introduced a bill the other day that aims to eliminate the mass collection of data on Americans’ communications. The House had tried to do that, but failed after the White House pressured its members into watering down the measure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Problems With the Bill Limiting Surveillance', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leahy, Patrick J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyden, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-01T18:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/358a4398-b299-5504-86b9-2e25cdc4efa9', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/358a4398-b299-5504-86b9-2e25cdc4efa9'}, {'abstract': 'Gunmen killed the lawmaker, Aden Madeer, as he left a mosque in Mogadishu. He was the fifth member of Somalia’s Parliament to be killed by insurgents this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/02/world/africa/insurgents-kill-a-lawmaker-in-somalia.html', 'snippet': 'Gunmen killed the lawmaker, Aden Madeer, as he left a mosque in Mogadishu. He was the fifth member of Somalia’s Parliament to be killed by insurgents this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOGADISHU, Somalia — Gunmen killed a Somali lawmaker as he left a mosque in Mogadishu on Friday, officials and witnesses said. The lawmaker, Aden Madeer, was the fifth member of Parliament to die in a violent attack this year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insurgents Kill a Lawmaker in Somalia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Somalia: Rebels Assassinate Lawmaker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahim, Mohammed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madeer, Aden', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-01T18:08:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohamed Ibrahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohamed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ibrahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f504bc0-fe39-5f92-8523-aba187f0db99', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f504bc0-fe39-5f92-8523-aba187f0db99'}, {'abstract': 'The automaker on Friday recalled the Santa Fe, Sonata and Veracruz for problems ranging from oil leaks to rust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/02/automobiles/hyundai-recalls-419000-vehicles-in-three-actions.html', 'snippet': 'The automaker on Friday recalled the Santa Fe, Sonata and Veracruz for problems ranging from oil leaks to rust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hyundai is recalling about 419,000 vehicles in the United States in three separate actions for brake, electrical and suspension problems, according to reports the automaker posted Friday on the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration website.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/automobiles/02RECALL-image/02RECALL-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/02/automobiles/02RECALL-image/02RECALL-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/automobiles/02RECALL-image/02RECALL-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/automobiles/02RECALL-image/02RECALL-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/automobiles/02RECALL-image/02RECALL-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/02/automobiles/02RECALL-image/02RECALL-image-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/automobiles/02RECALL-image/02RECALL-image-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hyundai Recalls 419,000 Vehicles in Three Actions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hyundai Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-01T18:17:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbedb068-2318-53f6-b6f2-e252968385e7', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbedb068-2318-53f6-b6f2-e252968385e7'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: In 1939, Nazi Germany marked the outbreak of World War I with historical comparisons.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/01/1939-hitler-proclaims-war-holiday/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: In 1939, Nazi Germany marked the outbreak of World War I with historical comparisons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — The twenty-fifth anniversary of the outbreak of the last war will be celebrated tomorrow [Aug. 2] by the entire German nation. Twenty-five years after Russian troops invaded East Prussia and German troops crossed the Belgian frontier, this anniversary has now completed the full cycle of change from a symbol of defeat to a harbinger of eventual German triumph. By Chancellor Hitler’s personal command, tomorrow will be a holiday for the entire German Army — the largest and strongest in German history. Every garrison in the Third Reich will hold special exercises to mark the beginning of four years of war which ended in defeat for Germany. This paradox is elaborated — if not explained — in columns of historical comment which fill the German press today. The grim situation in Europe this summer is explained in this official history as a parallel to that of 1914 only in its external form. The difference between 1914 and 1939 is summed up in most German newspapers by the black headlines ‘‘August, 1914, Kaiser Wilhelm — August, 1939, Adolf Hitler.’’\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, August 2, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Hitler Proclaims War Holiday', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitler, Adolf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-01T18:19:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6ef4a27-ede6-5426-ad36-57ff3208a90d', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6ef4a27-ede6-5426-ad36-57ff3208a90d'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Clark uses hickory wood chips to grill salmon cured with brown sugar, allspice and mace.', 'web_url':