ne, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/736fb7c3-c8b1-5145-9757-ea804a9bcf66', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/736fb7c3-c8b1-5145-9757-ea804a9bcf66'}, {'abstract': 'The British artist formerly known as Coco, who happens to call Sting “dad,” branches out on her own with a new four-track EP and forthcoming album.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/01/eliot-sumner-i-blame-coco-new-ep-electro-pop/', 'snippet': 'The British artist formerly known as Coco, who happens to call Sting “dad,” branches out on her own with a new four-track EP and forthcoming album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the last four years, Eliot Sumner has performed under her nickname Coco as the frontwoman for the band I Blame Coco. Then this June she scrawled a handwritten note, snapped a photo of it and posted it on her social media accounts. The contents revealed that, after taking some time off since releasing her first album, “The Constant,” she had some news: “I am happy to inform you that I am alive and well. New music is on the way!” A bit further down came this revelation: “New music will be released under my birth name, Eliot Sumner. I am looking forward to you hearing it. It’s nice to be back.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01sumner-molvar/01sumner-molvar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01sumner-molvar/01sumner-molvar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01sumner-molvar/01sumner-molvar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, '