ces bunches of low-end torque.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/03/automobiles/autoreviews/2014-ford-fiesta-ecoboost-review.html', 'snippet': 'The 2014 Ford Fiesta offers a bite-size 1-liter, 3-cylinder EcoBoost engine that produces bunches of low-end torque.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The standard-issue Ford Fiesta is powered by a 1.6-liter 4-cylinder that generates a modest 120 horsepower at 6,350 r.p.m. and 112 pound-feet of torque at 5,000 r.p.m. The lofty r.p.m. numbers for the power and torque peaks tell you all you need to know: This car is largely gutless unless you’re riding it to the redline. Even then, the base Fiesta won’t strain your sternocleidomastoid with undue G forces.', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/automobiles/WHEEL/WHEEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/03/automobiles/WHEEL/WHEEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/automobiles/WHEEL/WHEEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/automobiles/WHEEL/WHEEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 962, 'width': 1579, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/automobiles/WHEEL/WHEEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/03/automobiles/WHEEL/WHEEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/automobiles/WHEEL/WHEEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Version 1.0: More Boost Than Eco', 'kicker': 'Behind the Wheel', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Version 1.0: More Boost Than Eco', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dyer, Ezra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-01T20:37:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'New Cars', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezra Dyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2d6a2a6-5bb7-575c-a570-6583603c33b6', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2d6a2a6-5bb7-575c-a570-6583603c33b6'}, {'abstract': 'Too big to fail? Not so much, now.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/01/good-news-on-financial-reform/', 'snippet': 'Too big to fail? Not so much, now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The two big achievements of the Obama administration are health reform and financial reform. (Maybe carbon regulation will be added to the list; stay tuned.) For the most part, however, neither has gotten much respect. I think this may finally be changing on health reform, as the evidence piles up for a dramatic improvement in coverage in states that didn’t obstruct the law. But financial reform is still unloved, attacked by the right as anti-business and by the left as too weak to work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'h