eries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01bike-towill-1/01bike-towill-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01bike-towill-1/01bike-towill-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01bike-towill-1/01bike-towill-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01bike-towill-1/01bike-towill-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01bike-towill-1/01bike-towill-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01bike-towill-1/01bike-towill-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/01/t-magazine/01bike-towill-1/01bike-towill-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Ride Across America | A Last Meal on a Hilltop Farm in Oregon', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Towill, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fat Radish (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Outstanding in the Field', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-01T22:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Towill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Towill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cf88c15-762c-5ea5-8e07-a1f78f6725d1', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cf88c15-762c-5ea5-8e07-a1f78f6725d1'}, {'abstract': 'I wasn’t going to be one of those pitiful pet people. Not me.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/01/a-man-and-his-cat/', 'snippet': 'I wasn’t going to be one of those pitiful pet people. Not me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I LIVED with the same cat for 19 years — by far the longest relationship of my adult life. Under common law, this cat was my wife. I fell asleep at night with the warm, pleasant weight of the cat on my chest. The first thing I saw on most mornings was the foreshortened paw of the cat retreating slowly from my face and her baleful crescent glare informing me that it was Cat Food Time. As I often told her, in a mellow, resonant, Barry White voice: “There is no luuve … like the luuve that exists … between a man … and his cat.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/03/sunday-review/0803COVER/0803COVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1015, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/03/sunday-review/0803COVER/0803COVER-articleLa