icle/847d52ec-70a3-53f7-9559-376ae6620876'}, {'abstract': 'The states are seeking to block efforts by the Environmental Protection Agency to reduce carbon emissions from coal-powered plants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/02/business/a-dozen-states-file-suit-against-new-coal-rules.html', 'snippet': 'The states are seeking to block efforts by the Environmental Protection Agency to reduce carbon emissions from coal-powered plants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Twelve states filed a lawsuit against the Obama administration on Friday seeking to block an Environmental Protection Agency proposal to regulate coal-fired power plants in an effort to stem climate change. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dozen States File Suit Against New Coal Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dozen States File Suit Against New Coal Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-02T02:03:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Coral Davenport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Coral', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davenport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/057adb4f-7aba-53be-9ca6-5e068deed5ad', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/057adb4f-7aba-53be-9ca6-5e068deed5ad'}, {'abstract': 'There have been some cancellations since the hostilities began, but 6,000 young people have visited Israel as planned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/02/world/middleeast/birthright-trips-to-israel-continue-despite-conflict-between-israel-and-hamas.html', 'snippet': 'There have been some cancellations since the hostilities began, but 6,000 young people have visited Israel as planned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Lila Faria, 19, a student at New York University, heard the whine of a bomb siren for the first time last month in Jerusalem. Along with several dozen other Americans on a trip with the Taglit-Birthright Israel organization, she was quickly hustled into a bomb shelter.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/world/BIRTHRIGHT/BIRTHRIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/02/world/BIRTHRIGHT/BIRTHRIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/world/BIRTHRIGHT/BIRTHRIGHT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/world/BIRTHRIGHT/BIRTHRIGHT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/world/BIRTHRIGHT/BIRTHRIGHT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/02/world/BIRTHRIGHT/BIRTHRIGHT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/world/BIRTHRIGHT/BIRTHRIGHT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Birthright Trips to Israel Continue Despite Mideast Conflict', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Birthright Trips Continue Despite Mideast Conflict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taglit-Birthright Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneider, Elena', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-02T02:06:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elena Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea8c2336-39ef-5abe-abf3-4e85fe75e5e9', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea8c2336-39ef-5abe-abf3-4e85fe75e5e9'}, {'abstract': 'The G.D.P. is up, but jobs, as President Obama said, are what the country really needs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/02/opinion/growth-without-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'The G.D.P. is up, but jobs, as President Obama said, are what the country really needs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a statement last Wednesday — just hours after the government reported headline-grabbing economic growth of 4 percent in the second quarter — the Federal Reserve said it would continue to stimulate the economy because, despite overall growth, the labor market remained weak. In a speech the same day in Kansas City, Mo., President Obama echoed the Fed. “I’m glad that G.D.P. is growing, and I’m glad that corporate profits are high, and I’m glad that the stock market is booming,” he said, (which it was before profit-taking at week’s end dented its performance). “But what I really want to see is a guy working 9 to 5, and then working some overtime.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Growth Without Jobs', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growth Without Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Overtime', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-02T02:07:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce19da6f-4603-5a80-a3c6-56d02c3ed981', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce19da6f-4603-5a80-a3c6-56d02c3ed981'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Drennan, now known as Daniel Ibn Zayd, rediscovered his Lebanese heritage and converted to Islam after he began seeking answers about his adoption as an infant by an American family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/02/us/lebanese-adoptee-searching-for-his-roots-finds-islam.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Drennan, now known as Daniel Ibn Zayd, rediscovered his Lebanese heritage and converted to Islam after he began seeking answers about his adoption as an infant by an American family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The weekly TV recap — the snarky, obsessive, scene-by-scene description of a TV show, written by a fan working through what’s clearly a love/hate relationship — is now a ubiquitous genre, peddled online by Slate, The Onion, New York magazine, and others. But its progenitor was Daniel Drennan’s “Beverly Hills 90210” recap, which he wrote online from 1994 to 1998. Columbia Journalism Review credited Mr. Drennan with inventing the form, citing his successful mix of “opinions on bad writing and terrible acting”; pointed attacks on “receding hairlines and terrible outfits”; and “personal stories tangentially related to what was on the TV screen.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/02/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'c