': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-02T06:27:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/407f1947-8ccc-5537-a6cc-a713d98f6739', 'word_count': 37, 'uri': 'nyt://article/407f1947-8ccc-5537-a6cc-a713d98f6739'}, {'abstract': 'The Israeli military said the soldier who had been thought captured by Palestinian militants during a deadly clash on Friday was now considered to have been killed in battle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/03/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-conflict.html', 'snippet': 'The Israeli military said the soldier who had been thought captured by Palestinian militants during a deadly clash on Friday was now considered to have been killed in battle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The Israeli military said early Sunday morning that an officer thought to have been captured by Palestinian militants during a deadly clash Friday morning, which shattered a planned 72-hour cease-fire, was now considered to have been killed in battle. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missing Soldier Killed in Battle, Israel Confirms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missing Soldier Killed in Battle, Israel Confirms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldin, Hadar (1991-2014)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-02T09:38:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger and Jodi Rudoren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rudoren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a9eef84-6674-51bd-896d-a62ed5d6e293', 'word_count': 1292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a9eef84-6674-51bd-896d-a62ed5d6e293'}, {'abstract': 'Call it a bifurcated market in melon: People rarely buy it for themselves but often serve it to others, ideally at a hotel breakfast buffet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/03/upshot/that-honeydew-melon-looks-good-but-does-anyone-eat-it.html', 'snippet': 'Call it a bifurcated market in melon: People rarely buy it for themselves but often serve it to others, ideally at a hotel breakfast buffet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every time I see a fruit platter at a hotel or a conference, I ask myself the same question: Where does all this honeydew melon come from, and does anyone actually want to eat it?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/upshot/03UP-Melon/03UP-Melon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/02/upshot/03UP-Melon/03UP-Melon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/0