thy, natural childbirth have changed. Yet 33 percent of women still deliver babies through C-sections. How are our expectations of childbirth changing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the filmmaker Irene Lusztig got pregnant, she prepared for the arrival of her child by collecting instructions about motherhood. She ordered home videos and used baby scrapbooks from eBay and unearthed medical and instructional videos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/opinion/nyto-baby/nyto-baby-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/02/opinion/nyto-baby/nyto-baby-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 540}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/opinion/nyto-baby/nyto-baby-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 922, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/opinion/nyto-baby/nyto-baby-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1845, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/opinion/nyto-baby/nyto-baby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/02/opinion/nyto-baby/nyto-baby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/02/opinion/nyto-baby/nyto-baby-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Our Expectations of Childbirth Are Changing', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anesthesia and Anesthetics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caesarean Section', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-03T15:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Altman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/148eca07-ccbb-56cb-9c93-35fa0728069a', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/148eca07-ccbb-56cb-9c93-35fa0728069a'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The first wedding of a woman Member of Parliament at Westminster Crypt, in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/03/1939-woman-m-p-is-1st-to-wed-in-commons-crypt/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The first wedding of a woman Member of Parliament at Westminster Crypt, in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Miss Thelma Cazalet, Conservative Member of Parliament for East Islington, London, was married today [Aug. 3] to David Keir, political correspondent of the London ‘‘News Chronicle,’’ in the ancient crypt of the House of Commons, which had been decorated with lilies. It was the first time that a woman Member of Parliament had been married in the crypt, which members may use for their weddings on payment of £25 for a special license from the Archbishop of Canterbury.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N