be62fec99'}, {'abstract': 'The company is to present three world premieres at the Sept. 23 gala, with choreographers sharing top billing with couturiers.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/03/city-ballet-plans-a-fashionable-fall-gala/', 'snippet': 'The company is to present three world premieres at the Sept. 23 gala, with choreographers sharing top billing with couturiers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do the clothes make the dancer? The worlds of ballet and high fashion have intersected ever since Coco Chanel designed costumes for Diaghilev’s Ballets Russes, and this year the combination of the two fields will once again be the theme of New York City Ballet’s fall gala. City Ballet is to present three world premieres at the Sept. 23 gala, with the choreographers sharing the top billing with the couturiers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Ballet Plans a Fashionable Fall Gala', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Browne, Thom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herrera, Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martins, Peter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peck, Justin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-03T16:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bcec52e-ab4e-531a-bf2f-68b8efbc812c', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bcec52e-ab4e-531a-bf2f-68b8efbc812c'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/03/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:30 P.M. (13) MOYERS & COMPANY Bill Moyers interviews the Tony-winning actor John Lithgow about playing King Lear in the Public Theater’s Shakespeare in the Park production, and how the role speaks to our times. “To me, the most pointed line in the whole play is: ‘I’ve ta’en too little care of this,’\xa0” says Mr. Lithgow (above, with Jessica Collins as Cordelia). “You know, we live fairly comfortable lives. And every day you’re reminded of — of the — the astonishing misery in the rest of the world.” He adds, “I don’t think there is a play which is so nakedly painful.” Mr. Lithgow, who has been blogging about the experience for The New York Times, is in rehearsals with Glenn Close for the Broadway revival of Edward Albee’s “A Delicate Balance.” His new film, “Love Is Strange,” in which he and Alfred Molina play a couple of 39 years who are forced to live apart after marrying, opens on Aug. 22. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-03T16:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/d19f8754-a495-59f4-8cc0-474ac138f7c4', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d19f8754-a495-59f4-8cc0-474ac138f7c4'}, {'abstract': 'In a neighborhood once synonymous with being down and out, a building owned by the Archdiocese of New York has traded offering showers to the homeless for serving as a cultural center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/nyregion/on-the-bowery-questions-about-the-catholic-churchs-shifting-mission.html', 'snippet': 'In a neighborhood once synonymous with being down and out, a building owned by the Archdiocese of New York has traded offering showers to the homeless for serving as a cultural center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Men lined up outside St. Joseph House on the Lower East Side on a recent morning, some with their belongings stuffed in worn bags, all with their stomachs empty. Inside the dining hall, which is run by Catholic Worker, a hearty meal of stew and bread awaited. Most of the men were homeless, though not necessarily hopeless — this daily ritual gave sustenance and respite in a neighborhood that has steadily pushed them aside as tenements and poor people give way to luxury buildings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/nyregion/04SIDESTREET/04SIDESTREET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/04/nyregion/04SIDESTREET/04SIDESTREET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/nyregion/04SIDESTREET/04SIDESTREET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/nyregion/04SIDESTREET/04SIDESTREET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1405, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'cro