 and ocean patterns in the last couple of decades — including Pacific wind, sea level and ocean patterns, the decade-plus hiatus in global warming and even California’s deepening drought.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Study Sees Atlantic Warming Behind a Host of Recent Climate Shifts', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'El Nino Southern Oscillation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Climate Change (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Hawaii', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of New South Wales', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlantic Ocean', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-03T17:05:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aac47518-1070-553c-a8a5-b57416fb3477', 'word_count': 1423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aac47518-1070-553c-a8a5-b57416fb3477'}, {'abstract': 'David Hertzberg has been named the first winner of the Catherine Doctorow Prize for Music.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/03/gotham-chamber-opera-hands-out-music-award/', 'snippet': 'David Hertzberg has been named the first winner of the Catherine Doctorow Prize for Music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Gotham Chamber Opera, a small outfit that has become an increasingly important voice in New York 