 'Portugal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salgado, Ricardo Espirito Santo Silva', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bento, Vitor', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Agricole SA', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-03T21:44:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing and Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5537734d-325d-5d6b-878a-589ad406d778', 'word_count': 1212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5537734d-325d-5d6b-878a-589ad406d778'}, {'abstract': 'When a 14-year-old boy was robbed of his trombone, one of the best-known musicians in New Orleans decided to do something.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/arts/music/trombone-shorty-helps-a-young-victim.html', 'snippet': 'When a 14-year-old boy was robbed of his trombone, one of the best-known musicians in New Orleans decided to do something.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news reports shook New Orleans: A 14-year-old boy was robbed of his trombone last week by a gunman who fired several shots at him as he ran away. When one of the city’s best-known musicians, Troy Andrews, who performs as Trombone Shorty, heard about it while on tour in the Northeast, he decided to do something: He asked his foundation to replace the boy’s stolen instrument. “It is very unfortunate that this young man was robbed of his instrument and had to be a victim of New Orleans crime,” Mr. Andrews said in a statement. “I’m replacing his horn, because I want to make sure that he has what he needs to continue his education in music without missing a beat. He is the future of our music.” Mr. Andrews’s band, Trombone Shorty & Orleans Avenue, has performed at the Grammy Awards and the White House and has become familiar to television viewers of the HBO series “Treme.” His Trombone Shorty Foundation is dedicated to passing on New Orleans’s musical heritage through educational initiatives. Bill Taylor, the foundation’s executive director, said that on Saturday he brought the new trombone to the robbery victim, whose name was withheld for his safety. Then he put the teenager on the phone with Mr. Andrews, who was at the Newport Jazz Festival.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/arts/subarts2/subarts2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/04/arts/subarts2/subarts2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/arts/subarts2/subarts2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/arts/subarts2/subarts2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1480, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/arts/subarts2/subarts2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/04/arts/subarts2/subarts2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/arts/subarts2/subarts2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trombone Shorty Helps a Young Victim', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trombone Shorty Helps a Young Victim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trombone Shorty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-03T21:53:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0908e87-9782-5677-9755-c32067942584', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0908e87-9782-5677-9755-c32067942584'}, {'abstract': 'The Tribune Company’s publishing unit, including eight well-known newspapers, will venture forth as an independent entity in troubled times, led by Jack Griffin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/business/media/spinoff-set-to-create-tribune-publishing-a-print-unit-going-it-alone.html', 'snippet': 'The Tribune Company’s publishing unit, including eight well-known newspapers, will venture forth as an independent entity in troubled times, led by Jack Griffin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After spending years in the shadow of bankruptcy proceedings, management turmoil and its more prominent broadcasting stations, the Tribune Company’s publishing division, including well-known newspapers like The Los Angeles Times and The Chicago Tribune, is striking out on its own. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/business/TRIBUNE1/TRIBUNE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/04/business/TRIBUNE1/TRIBUNE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/business/TRIBUNE1/TRIBUNE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/business/TRIBUNE1/TRIBUNE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1503, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/business/TRIBUNE1/TRIBUNE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/04/business/TRIBUNE1/TRIBUNE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/business/TRIBUNE1/TRIBUNE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A News Giant Going It Alone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A News Giant Going It Alone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribune Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haughney, Christine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffin, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tribune Publishing Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-03T21:53:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d62e645-9a28-5e19-be3c-01297ad1bed2', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d62e645-9a28-5e19-be3c-01297ad1bed2'}, {'abstract': 'A book examines the broad effects golf has had on China, from the poor worker who becomes a golf pro to the farmer whose land is taken to build a new course.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/03/q-and-a-dan-washburn-on-the-forbidden-game/', 'snippet': 'A book examines the broad effects golf has had on China, from the poor worker who becomes a golf pro to the farmer whose land is taken to build a new course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a journalist in Shanghai, Dan Washburn discovered that, while writing about golf for outlets like ESPN.com, Slate and Foreign Policy, he was able to tell not just stories about a sport, but also about the vast transitions sweeping across China. He expanded that focus into a book,