nces at the age of 15 for a series of armed robberies he committed with his mother’s crack dealer, Kenneth Ray Young, above, came to believe that he would die in prison. But in 2010, the Supreme Court ruled in Graham v. Florida that life sentences for juveniles convicted of crimes other than murder were unconstitutional. This “POV” documentary, directed by Nadine Pequeneza, follows Mr. Young’s case while examining a social system that doles out sentences to juvenile offenders intended for the most dangerous criminals. In “Bob Herbert’s OP-ED.TV,” at 9:30 a.m. on CUNY, Ms. Pequeneza and Mishi Faruqee, a juvenile justice policy strategist at the American Civil Liberties Union, discuss the issue.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-04T04:16:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9d749b7-a629-531d-b3f9-c57d5c3ecc72', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9d749b7-a629-531d-b3f9-c57d5c3ecc72'}, {'abstract': 'David Phelps, who has stepped into a rotation plagued by injury, was the Yankees’ latest victim, leaving with inflammation in his right elbow during a victory over the Red Sox.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/sports/baseball/yanks-overcome-the-latest-injury-to-a-starting-pitcher-.html', 'snippet': 'David Phelps, who has stepped into a rotation plagued by injury, was the Yankees’ latest victim, leaving with inflammation in h