': 'In the excitement of admiring our newly acquired furniture, we failed to ask an important question: What will this new space say about who we are?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In February, my company, RJMetrics, moved into a new office. It was bittersweet to outgrow our old space, partially because it had a pretty amazing legacy. Before us, a company called VoiceStar had built a business in the exact same suite and sold it to Marchex for millions. “Those guys drove away in Ferraris,” our old landlord liked to say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Balancing Lean Company Culture With the Perks of Success', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Robert J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RJMetrics Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-04T11:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert J. Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6c97ffe-4d4d-52fb-814e-29e52f035b69', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6c97ffe-4d4d-52fb-814e-29e52f035b69'}, {'abstract': 'Ruth Padawer, a contributing writer for the magazine, wrote this week’s cover story on kids who recovered from autism.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/behind-the-cover-story-ruth-padawer-on-autistic-children-who-shed-their-symptoms/', 'snippet': 'Ruth Padawer, a contributing writer for the magazine, wrote this week’s cover story on kids who recovered from autism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ruth Padawer, a contributing writer for the magazine, is the author of this week’s cover story about children who have recovered from autism. Her previous article for the magazine was about gender-fluid children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/magazine/10-ruth-padawer/10-ruth-padawer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 809, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/magazine/10-ruth-padawer/10-ruth-padawer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 809, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/magazine/10-ruth-padawer/10-ruth-padawer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/10/magazine/10-ruth-padawer/10-ruth-padawer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/10/magazine/10-ruth-padawer/10-ruth-padawer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Ruth Padawer on Autistic Children Who Shed Their Symptoms', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-04T11:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By RACHEL NOLAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'NOLAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2293d52d-95af-517e-abc3-cf91905c587d', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2293d52d-95af-517e-abc3-cf91905c587d'}, {'abstract': 'To grab some of television’s ad dollars, Facebook is trying to help advertisers reach potential buyers with exacting precision.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/daily-report-turning-users-into-customers-at-facebook/', 'snippet': 'To grab some of television’s ad dollars, Facebook is trying to help advertisers reach potential buyers with exacting precision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since it began selling ads 10 years ago, Facebook has been fighting doubts about its value to marketers. Search engines like Google offer advertisers a direct link to people seeking out particular products, while television remains the dominant way to reach a mass audience. Now, Facebook claims, it can provide the best of both, Vindu Goel reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None