oors festival, featuring Emmylou Harris, Cassandra Wilson and Rosanne Cash, among others.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/from-out-of-doors-to-your-device-lincoln-center-festival-to-stream-three-concerts/', 'snippet': 'Lincoln Center will stream three concerts from the final week of its Lincoln Center Out of Doors festival, featuring Emmylou Harris, Cassandra Wilson and Rosanne Cash, among others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lincoln Center will be streaming three concerts from the final week of its free Lincoln Center Out of Doors festival. The concerts, part of the first Americanafest, a collaboration between Lincoln Center and the Americana Music Association, a Nashville organization that promotes American roots music, will be streamed live in their entirety, including the opening acts.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Out of Doors to Your Device: Lincoln Center to Stream Three Concerts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lincoln Center to Stream 3 ‘Out of Doors’ Concerts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Out of Doors Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cash, Rosanne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowell, Rodney', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Emmylou', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Cassandra', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-04T15:02:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c65b43d-5c56-565a-8224-88000fc7afb1', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c65b43d-5c56-565a-8224-88000fc7afb1'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Belgians prepare themselves for war in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/1914-belgians-eager-to-take-arms/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Belgians prepare themselves for war in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — An extraordinary wave of patriotism has passed over Brussels, and, indeed, the whole of Belgium since the news of the declaration of war. No fewer than 45,000 volunteers have been enrolled, and eager crowds fight for entry to the recruiting offices. In fact, it has become a question whether the Ministry of War possesses sufficient rifles and ammunition to equip all those who wish to take arms for the defence of their country. King Albert will proceed to the frontier to defend the national territory, which was invaded this morning by the Germans, who entered Belgium, near Arlon.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, August 5, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/blogs/05iht-retrospective-belges/05iht-retrospective-belges-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/blogs/05iht-retrospective-belges/05iht-retrospective-belges-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/blogs/05iht-retrospective-belges/05iht-retrospective-belges-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo'