he living room? Odds are, it’s not Grandma’s as multigenerational households trend younger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are we really seeing a return to “The Waltons”? Family members sharing the old farmhouse, with Grandma and Grandpa helping to raise the young ’uns and then, when they get too frail to bake pies or go fishing, being cared for by their adult children?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/science/waltonsnoa/waltonsnoa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/science/waltonsnoa/waltonsnoa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/science/waltonsnoa/waltonsnoa-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/04/science/waltonsnoa/waltonsnoa-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/science/waltonsnoa/waltonsnoa-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who’s Moving In Now?', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-04T18:41:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f053bef-6cc0-5474-9cd9-d52c25350420', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f053bef-6cc0-5474-9cd9-d52c25350420'}, {'abstract': 'Dufner’s 2013 P.G.A. Championship title has made more people pay attention to him and his game, even if his putting remains shaky and he has not won lately.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/05/sports/golf/a-year-after-pga-win-jason-dufner-finds-power-if-not-more-titles.html', 'snippet': 'Dufner’s 2013 P.G.A. Championship title has made more people pay attention to him and his game, even if his putting remains shaky and he has not won lately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AKRON, Ohio — Enlisted to make a celebrity appearance during a gala charity announcement on the eve of last week’s Bridgestone Invitational, Jason Dufner appeared to have put the most trying part behind him when he stepped away from the microphone after delivering a brief speech.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/sports/GOLF/GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/sports/GOLF/GOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/sports/GOLF/GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 's