s whose works are also cutting-edge scientific advances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/05/science/colliding-worlds-explores-art-driven-by-science.html', 'snippet': 'Arthur I. Miller’s new book examines the trend of contemporary artists and inventors whose works are also cutting-edge scientific advances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientists are logical, making observations and running experiments, then building theories that explain the data. Artists are emotional, working in solitude and by intuition. Or so we are told. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/05SCIB/05SCIB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/science/05SCIB/05SCIB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 731}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/05SCIB/05SCIB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 841, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/05SCIB/05SCIB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1682, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/05SCIB/05SCIB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/05/science/05SCIB/05SCIB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/05SCIB/05SCIB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width