'$320 Million Facility to Stoke China’s Musical Theater Industry', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-04T18:56:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9af19afc-ab7d-5051-93c7-e8424fc21c73', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9af19afc-ab7d-5051-93c7-e8424fc21c73'}, {'abstract': 'An unreleased recording by the singer-songwriter, who died in 1974, was withdrawn from sale after a legal challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/early-nick-drake-recording-pulled-from-auction/', 'snippet': 'An unreleased recording by the singer-songwriter, who died in 1974, was withdrawn from sale after a legal challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An early demo tape by the singer-songwriter Nick Drake, which was to have been auctioned this week in London, may make its way to court before it gets near an auctioneer’s gavel. The tape, a demo probably recorded\xa0 in 1968, before Drake began\xa0work on his debut album, “Five Leaves Left,” has been in the possession of the British folksinger Beverley Martyn, a close friend of Drake’s, since shortly after Drake’s death from an overdose of antidepressant medicine in 1974, when he was 26. Martyn had consigned the tape this spring to Ted Owen & Company, a London auction house, saying that she was selling it because she was in poor health and needed the money.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Nick Drake Recording Pulled From Auction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nick Drake Recording Pulled From Auction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drake, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-04T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/657e8846-63ac-503e-9db3-0f592521ae24', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/657e8846-63ac-503e-9db3-0f592521ae24'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/walkabout-c-d-c-issues-ebola-travel-guidelines/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Agency Issues Ebola Warnings\xa0The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention has issued guidelines to airlines in response to the Ebola outbreak that has killed more than 800 people in western Africa. People exposed to the disease are asked not to travel for 21 days, and the C.D.C. suggests that airlines consider using their legal authority to deny boarding to sick passengers suspected of carrying the virus. The C.D.C. has also advised Americans to avoid nonessential travel to Guinea, Sierra Leone and Liberia, the three countries most affected by the outbreak. (The New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/travel/04walkabout/