article/26a7994a-4347-545c-9f35-c4881d8d3447'}, {'abstract': 'A judge in Florida ruled that three men who administered the estate of the artist Robert Rauschenberg had done “an exemplary job” and merited significant payment.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/judge-awards-24-6-million-to-former-rauschenberg-trustees/', 'snippet': 'A judge in Florida ruled that three men who administered the estate of the artist Robert Rauschenberg had done “an exemplary job” and merited significant payment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Robert Rauschenberg Foundation said Monday it was considering its legal options after a judge in Florida awarded $24.6 million to three trustees who had administered the late artist’s estate.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Awards $24.6 Million to Former Rauschenberg Trustees', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rauschenberg Trustees Win Court Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldston, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grutman, Bennet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pottorf, Darryl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauschenberg, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rauschenberg, Robert, Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-04T19:07:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f6096e4-5cfb-56bb-9d00-28fc5d12e56e', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f6096e4-5cfb-56bb-9d00-28fc5d12e56e'}, {'abstract': 'Despite their vulnerabilities, Senator Lamar Alexander of Tennessee and Senator Pat Roberts of Kansas hold wide fund-raising advantages against opponents struggling to gain traction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/05/us/politics/in-tennessee-and-kansas-tea-partys-primary-challenges-falling-short.html', 'snippet': 'Despite their vulnerabilities, Senator Lamar Alexander of Tennessee and Senator Pat Roberts of Kansas hold wide fund-raising advantages against opponents struggling to gain traction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Like most incumbent Republican senators this year who are facing a primary challenge from the right, Pat Roberts of Kansas refused a one-on-one debate against his hard-line opponent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/us/PRIMARY/PRIMARY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/us/PRIMARY/PRIMARY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/us/PRIMARY/PRIMARY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/us/PRIMARY/PRIMARY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/us/PRIMARY/PRIMARY-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/05/us/PRIMARY/PRIMARY