1b'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Andres Gonzalez captured new and established acts — and the rain-soaked but enthusiastic crowd — in Chicago over the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/lollapalooza-street-style-lykke-li-andre-benjamin-blood-orange-eminem-photos/', 'snippet': 'The photographer Andres Gonzalez captured new and established acts — and the rain-soaked but enthusiastic crowd — in Chicago over the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year, the blissful Chicago summer turned nasty during Lollapalooza. The music festival, which celebrated its 10th year in Grant Park, saw plenty of rain and mud — conditions that have become as much a part of the festival’s tradition as shirtless frat boys and the sight of its its wiry founder, the Jane’s Addiction frontman Perry Farrell, roaming the premises. Still, the 300,000 revelers (including Malia Obama) who turned out didn’t seem to mind. They roared their approval for young stars like Lykke Li and the Chicago native Chance the Rapper (“This is the coolest show I’ve ever done,” he told the Sunday-night crowd), and turned out in full voice for elder statesmen like Eminem and OutKast. The photographer Andres Gonzalez braved the inclement conditions — and the mosh pits — to capture it all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Lykke Li, André Benjamin, Blood Orange and Other Stars Were Wearing at Lollapalooza', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lollapalooza (Music Festival)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andre 3000', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eminem', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farrell, Perry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li, Lykke', 'rank': 6