 and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manson, Charles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-05T00:41:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'Olivia Klaus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Olivia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klaus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f5c2e513-1f63-53e2-887c-5d31ee2a659f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f5c2e513-1f63-53e2-887c-5d31ee2a659f'}, {'abstract': 'Forty-five years ago, Patricia Krenwinkel killed for Charles Manson. Now she provides an emotional account of her life from prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/05/opinion/my-life-after-manson.html', 'snippet': 'Forty-five years ago, Patricia Krenwinkel killed for Charles Manson. Now she provides an emotional account of her life from prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I vividly remember entering the California Institution for Women for the first time in 2001. As the prison guard slammed the gate behind me, I wondered if I had made the right decision to become a volunteer for an inmate support group. But my nerves were eased by a woman who introduced herself as “Krenny.” Welcoming me into the group, she seemed quiet and insecure — yet also exuded an inner strength. I had no idea how she got here and didn’t ask.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘My Life After Manson’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krenwinkel, Patricia', 'rank': 1, 'm