o prosecute any officers, and on what charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/05/nyregion/after-eric-garner-chokehold-prosecuting-police-is-an-option.html', 'snippet': 'The death of Eric Garner, who was put in a police chokehold on Staten Island, has been ruled a homicide, and officials have to decide whether to prosecute any officers, and on what charges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For two weeks after the death of a Staten Island man in police custody, frustration simmered as the city awaited the results of the autopsy. The mayor offered sympathy. The police promised better training. But now, with the medical examiner’s conclusion that the death was a homicide, by chokehold and chest compression, the investigation — and most significantly, the question of whether to prosecute any police officers — rests in the hands of the Staten Island district attorney’s office.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/nyregion/05chokehold/05chokehold-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/nyregion/05chokehold/05chokehold-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 467}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/nyregion/05chokehold/05chokehold-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 797, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/nyregion/05chokehold/05chokehold-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1595, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/nyregion/05chokehold/05chokehold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/05/nyregion/05chokehold/05chokehold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/nyregion/05chokehold/05chokehold-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Difficult Decisions Ahead in Responding to Police Chokehold Homicide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Difficult Decisions Ahead in Responding to Police Chokehold Homicide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pantaleo, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'District Attorneys', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Daniel M Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Civilian Complaint Review Board', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emery, Richard D', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-05T01:39:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90f66885-e51e-57a5-a022-5d95bfb4169c', 'word_count': 1187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90f66885-e51e-57a5-a022-5d95bfb4169c'}, {'abstract': 'Google’s automated eyes tipped law enforcement about a Houston-area man whom the police say was using the company’s Gmail service to email pornographic images of a child.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/04/google-gives-child-pornography-email-evidence-to-police/', 'snippet': 'Google’s automated eyes tipped law enforcement about a Houston-area man whom the police say was using the company’s Gmail service to email pornographic images of a child.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal law requires people and companies to report child exploitation when they see it. This includes Google, whose automated eyes tipped law enforcement about a Houston-area man whom the police say was using the company’s Gmail service to email pornographic images of a child.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Gives Child Pornography Email Evidence to Police', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Pornography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skillern, John Henry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-05T01:41:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Conor Dougherty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Conor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dougherty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb37ddf1-03c1-548d-83ce-4fe5297ea244', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb37ddf1-03c1-548d-83ce-4fe5297ea244'}, {'abstract': 'If the law requiring abortion facilities to be licensed as ambulatory surgery centers takes effect, Texas would be left with fewer than 10 clinics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/08/04/us/shrinking-number-of-abortion-clinics-in-texas.html', 'snippet': 'If the law requiring abortion facilities to be licensed as ambulatory surgery centers takes effect, Texas would be left with fewer than 10 clinics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the law requiring abortion facilities to be licensed as ambulatory surgery centers takes effect, Texas would be left with fewer than 10 clinics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/us/shrinking-number-of-abortion-clinics-in-texas-1420664250552/shrinking-number-of-abortion-clinics-in-texas-1420664250552-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 304, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/04/us/shrinking-number-of-abortion-clinics-in-texas-1420664250552/shrinking-number-of-abortion-clinics-in-texas-1420664250552-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 304}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/us/shrinking-number-of-abortion-clinics-in-texas-1420664250552/shrinking-number-of-abortion-clinics-in-texas-1420664250552-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 519, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/us/shrinking-number-of-abortion-clinics-in-texas-1420664250552/shrinking-number-of-abortion-clinics-in-texas-1420664250552-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1038, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnai