the Vesdre has assumed undreamt of proportions. Several thousand Germans were killed and wounded or taken prisoners before their hasty retreat to Dutch soil. The Prussian cavalry suffered severely. All the German assaults on the city of Liège and its forts have so far been repulsed, and the hope increases that the progress of the invaders will be arrested until the French forces come up. The German artillery is proving inefficient against the powerfully armed turrets of the Liège forts. The glorious behavior of the Belgians exceeds any dream. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 6, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06/06iht-oldaug06-jumbo.png', 'height': 532, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06/06iht-oldaug06-superJumbo.png', 'height': 532, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06/06iht-oldaug06-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06/06iht-oldaug06-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/blogs/06iht-oldaug06/06iht-oldaug06-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: German Army Attacks Liège', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords'