prices for medical tests and procedures is that American patients are not very skilled consumers of health care and will assume high prices mean high quality. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/well_costs/well_costs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/science/well_costs/well_costs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/well_costs/well_costs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 780, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/well_costs/well_costs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 780, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/well_costs/well_costs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/05/science/well_costs/well_costs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/science/well_costs/well_costs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why We Should Know the Price of Medical Tests', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magnetic Resonance Imagers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-05T17:20:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c36963ed-be92-5218-95fa-1a38f150ba98', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c36963ed-be92-5218-95fa-1a38f150ba98'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker has shot a new series of images for Calder, an L.A.-based collection of soft jersey layers designed by her cousin-in-law Amanda Blake.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/05/caldercalder-sofia-coppola-latest-project-look-book-for-new-line-of-california-casual-wear/', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker has shot a new series of images for Calder, an L.A.-based collection of soft jersey layers designed by her cousin-in-law Amanda Blake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sofia Coppola has long acted as muse to marquee fashion designers like Marc Jacobs and Karl Lagerfeld (she interned at Chanel as a teenager). She has also directed commercials for Dior’s fragrance Miss Dior. Now the director of the upcoming live-action adaptation of “The Little Mermaid” is lending her talent to a lesser-known name:\xa0Calder, a made-in-L.A. label started last year by her cousin-in-law Amanda Blake. Coppola recently shot the look book for Calder’s fall/winter 2014 collection, a series of soft jersey tees, tanks and T-shirt dresses whose easygoing aesthetic dovetails with Coppola’s own. “I tried to show the line how I would wear it,” says Coppola, who shot the images in her New York apartment so as to feel “intimate and basic.” The results have the same warm, personal quality as Coppola’s films. “I just tried to show the clothes in a way that felt real.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05bobb-calder/05bobb-calder-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05bobb-calder/05bobb-calder-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05bobb-calder/05bobb-calder-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05bobb-calder/05bobb-calder-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05bobb-calder/05bobb-calder-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05bobb-calder/05bobb-calder-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05bobb-calder/05bobb-calder-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sofia Coppola’s Latest Project: A Look Book for a New Line of California Casual Wear', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Line: In Her Own Style', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coppola, Sofia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-05T17:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooke Bobb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bobb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6353fa3c-75d2-5e22-9770-624afc7fa69d', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6353fa3c-75d2-5e22-9770-624afc7fa69d'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Russia condemns American military actions in Vietnam in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/05/1964-russians-warn-of-broad-war/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Russia condemns American military actions in Vietnam in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The Soviet Union tonight warned that further American ‘‘rash steps’’ in Vietnam could lead to a ‘‘broad armed conflict.’’ In a statement by the Tass news agency, the Russians called American action an ‘‘aggressive’’ act. Such actions, or further steps or provocations, ‘‘could lead to broad conflict with all the ensuing dangerous consequences,’’ Tass said. It added that the responsibility would lie on the United States. The statement was issued after a day in which Soviet news media refrained from comment, reporting only what American and North Vietnamese sources were announcing. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, August 6, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Russians Warn of ‘Broad War’', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', '