e Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/200d8231-5e20-5afb-bb66-7620e9a2399f', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/200d8231-5e20-5afb-bb66-7620e9a2399f'}, {'abstract': 'Pearls are a ladylike option that is very much of the moment.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/05/pearl-rings-jewelry-sophie-bille-brahe-ana-khouri/', 'snippet': 'Pearls are a ladylike option that is very much of the moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the unofficial ladies’ uniform here at T consists mostly of comfortable flats and boyish silhouettes, the staff’s jewelry choices fall on the opposite end of the style spectrum: the pieces are pretty and dainty. And where stones are concerned, there are few options more ladylike than pearls. As charming as grandma’s hand-me-downs can be, modern fine jewelers such as Sophie Bille Brahe and Ana Khouri offer fresh takes on the classic jewelry box staple, as seen in T’s Culture 2014 issue. Here, T’s women’s fashion team rounds up similar designs with real pearls, at a price that won’t break the bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05inspired-koh/05inspired-koh-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05inspired-koh/05inspired-koh-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05inspired-koh/05inspired-koh-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05inspired-koh/05inspired-koh-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05inspired-koh/05inspired-koh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05inspired-koh/05inspired-koh-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/t-magazine/05inspired-koh/05inspired-koh-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dainty Jewelry the Fashion Set Is Wearing Right Now', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nars Cosmetics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-05T19:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Angela Koh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Angela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/751067cd-e31e-5721-993f-6b403c1b8997', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/751067cd-e31e-5721-993f-6b403c1b8997'}, {'abstract': 'The Paul Taylor Dance Company presented three works as part of Lincoln Center Out of Doors on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/arts/dance/paul-taylor-dance-company-at-lincoln-center-out-of-doors.html', 'snippet': 'The Paul Taylor Dance Company presented three works as part of Lincoln Center Out of Doors on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some choreography seems to shrink on an outdoor stage, dwarfed by open space. The opposite was true on Friday at the Damrosch Park Bandshell at Lincoln Center, where the Paul Taylor Dance Company presented three works as part of Lincoln Center Out of Doors. The open-air setting, depending on the piece, served either to free up Mr. Taylor’s movement or complement its inherent freedom; his work contains equal measures of tension and effervescence. In all three dances — “Fibers” (1961), “Aureole” (1962) and “Piazzolla Caldera” (1997) — the company looked ripe, expansive, ready for anything.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/arts/06TAYLOR/06TAYLOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/06/arts/06TAYLOR/06TAYLOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/arts/06TAYLOR/06TAYLOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/arts/06TAYLOR/06TAYLOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1294, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/arts/06TAYLOR/06TAYLOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/06/arts/06TAYLOR/06TAYLOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thu