ame': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe0fb889-800e-5557-a4da-2477d5c21250', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe0fb889-800e-5557-a4da-2477d5c21250'}, {'abstract': '“Web Junkie” is a documentary that observes China’s efforts to treat young people, mostly teenage boys, who have an Internet addiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/movies/web-junkie-examines-internet-addiction-in-china.html', 'snippet': '“Web Junkie” is a documentary that observes China’s efforts to treat young people, mostly teenage boys, who have an Internet addiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the course of procrastinating over a deadline — I mean conducting research for this review — I typed “Is Internet addiction real” into a Google window and received 29 million results and no conclusive answer. Some experts think the addiction model fits compulsive, time-sucking online behavior perfectly, while others are skeptical. After a while, I stopped reading to check for Twitter updates and take a quiz or two, but two hours later, I’m not ready to admit that I have a problem. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/arts/06WEBJUNKIE/06WEBJUNKIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/06/arts/06WEBJUNKIE/06WEBJUNKIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/arts/06WEBJUNKIE/06WEBJUNKIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im