me': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Intelligence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T01:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Mazzetti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40814cfe-f28d-502b-a327-1536cf0d6f5f', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40814cfe-f28d-502b-a327-1536cf0d6f5f'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department is rightly calling for reforms at the jail complex after an investigation found that teenagers faced excessive force over minor infractions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/opinion/a-culture-of-violence-at-rikers-island.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department is rightly calling for reforms at the jail complex after an investigation found that teenagers faced excessive force over minor infractions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A much-anticipated investigation by the Justice Department has uncovered what amounted to a chamber of horrors at Rikers Island, where teenagers were beaten and battered for minor infractions by correction officers who acted without fear of discovery or punishment by senior officials. The report, released on Monday by Preet Bharara, the United States attorney in Manhattan, documents “a deep-seated culture of violence” that demands immediate remedial action by New York City, which is now at risk of facing a federal lawsuit if it does not take the steps outlined in the report — which wisely calls for removing adolescents from the jail complex altogether. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Culture of Violence’ at Rikers Island', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Culture of Violence’ at Rikers Island', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rikers Island Prison Complex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guards', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bharara, Preet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T01:16:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4902c157-e2ad-5424-94b5-e57a84c37f52', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4902c157-e2ad-5424-94b5-e57a84c37f52'}, {'abstract': 'The powerhouses of college sports are expected to gain preliminary approval to break away from some of the strictures of the N.C.A.A., which would give them more freedom to govern themselves and could allow athletes a share of the wealth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/sports/n-c-a-a-s-rich-poised-to-get-richer-with-more-athlete-benefits-.html', 'snippet': 'The powerhouses of college sports are expected to gain preliminary approval to break away from some of the strictures of the N.C.A.A., which would give them more freedom to govern themselves and could allow athletes a share of the wealth.'