article/70216bc3-5e81-5f10-ae00-1b5301a9c498', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70216bc3-5e81-5f10-ae00-1b5301a9c498'}, {'abstract': 'Marina Khodorkovskaya, the mother of the former Russian tycoon Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, has died in a Berlin clinic where she was being treated for cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/world/europe/germany-russian-tycoons-mother-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Marina Khodorkovskaya, the mother of the former Russian tycoon Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, has died in a Berlin clinic where she was being treated for cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marina Khodorkovskaya, the mother of the former Russian tycoon Mikhail B. Khodorkovsky, has died in a Berlin clinic where she was being treated for cancer, a spokeswoman, Christiane Maack, said Tuesday. Russia’s president, Vladimir V. Putin, cited her illness as the reason for his surprising decision in December to release Mr. Khodorkovsky, once Russia’s richest man, after he had spent more than 10 years in Russian prisons. During that time, Mr. Khodorkovsky cited his mother’s strength and perseverance as his inspiration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: Russian Tycoon’s Mother Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khodorkovskaya, Marina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khodorkovsky, Mikhail B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T04:52:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa496d03-cf92-5739-bd33-d1195beeef58', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa496d03-cf92-5739-bd33-d1195beeef58'}, {'abstract': 'The boy was shot on East Tremont Avenue, between Jerome and Walton Avenues, the police said; he was taken in stable condition to St. Barnabas Hospital for treatment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/nyregion/12-year-old-boy-is-shot-in-the-bronx.html', 'snippet': 'The boy was shot on East Tremont Avenue, between Jerome and Walton Avenues, the police said; he was taken in stable condition to St. Barnabas Hospital for treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 12-year-old boy was shot in the Bronx on Tuesday, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '12-Year-Old Boy Is Shot in the Bronx', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T04:52:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall and Kate Pastor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pastor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ef263de-ecb8-5fff-bd0e-34b93fe2c46c', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ef263de-ecb8-5fff-bd0e-34b93fe2c46c'}, {'abstract': 'The head of a human rights organization that searches for hundreds of babies stolen by Argentina’s military dictatorship decades ago has located her grandson after 37 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/world/americas/argentina-man-located-after-37-years.html', 'snippet': 'The head of a human rights organization that searches for hundreds of babies stolen by Argentina’s military dictatorship decades ago has located her grandson after 37 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The head of a human rights organization that searches for hundreds of babies stolen by Argentina’s military dictatorship decades ago has located her grandson after 37 years. Estela de Carlotto, leader of Grandmothers of the Plaza de Mayo, told reporters in Buenos Aires on Tuesday that she had found the son of her daughter Laura Carlotto, who was kidnapped while pregnant in 1977. She was later murdered as part of the dictatorship’s “dirty war” against guerrillas and people associated with leftist ideology. Mrs. Carlotto’s missing grandson, Guido Carlotto, 36, was raised as Ignacio Hurban. He is married and a pianist and approached Mrs. Carlotto’s organization because he doubted his identity. DNA tests proved that he was Mrs. Carlotto’s grandson.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Argentina: Man Located After 37 Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Argentina: Man Located After 37 Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlotto, Estela de', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', '