surance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gilead Sciences Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Sanger-Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0f09319-1313-5398-b689-44e450c4f8c6', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0f09319-1313-5398-b689-44e450c4f8c6'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Kim A. Williams, the president-elect of the American College of Cardiology, saw his cholesterol numbers plummet after adopting a vegan diet, and he advises many of his patients to go vegan.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/advice-from-a-vegan-cardiologist/', 'snippet': 'Dr. Kim A. Williams, the president-elect of the American College of Cardiology, saw his cholesterol numbers plummet after adopting a vegan diet, and he advises many of his patients to go vegan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Kim A. Williams, the president-elect of the American College of Cardiology, often sees patients who are overweight and struggling with hypertension, Type 2 diabetes and high cholesterol. One of the things he advises them to do is to change their diets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/health/well_cardiologist/well_cardiologist-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/health/well_cardiologist/well_cardiologist-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 628}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/