Ultrasonic Imaging and Sonograms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Meredith', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'uBeam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T14:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0248c4d5-79aa-5e0b-a958-77645d9af19f', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0248c4d5-79aa-5e0b-a958-77645d9af19f'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: General Motors workers and management reached a deal after a strike in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/1939-strike-at-g-m-c-ends/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: General Motors workers and management reached a deal after a strike in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The four-week strike in the plants of the General Motors Corporation came to an end last night when the company’s representatives and the strikers of the Congress of Industrial Organizations overwhelmingly ratified a settlement. William S. Knudsen, president of General Motors, announced that production would be resumed as soon as possible in the company’s scores of plants, possibly tomorrow and certainly on Tuesday. ‘‘We want to get everybody back to work,’’ Mr. Knudsen said. ‘‘We want to forget all the names we have called each other.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 7, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Strike at G.M.C. Ends', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print