otten', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikimedia Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T15:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Conor Dougherty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Conor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dougherty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/381ae6e3-8f64-5ee2-96ab-e7a3233fca38', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/381ae6e3-8f64-5ee2-96ab-e7a3233fca38'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty-one percent say they don’t think their Congressman is doing a good job.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/facts-figures-americans-now-hate-their-own-representatives/', 'snippet': 'Fifty-one percent say they don’t think their Congressman is doing a good job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans have long hated Congress, and yet reported liking their own representatives. (Congress is terrible, they tell pollsters, but my Congressman is OK.) That’s changing. Now they’re giving up on the individual lawmakers that they voted into office.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts & Figures: Americans Now Hate Their Own Representatives', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014