'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamul (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Johnsville (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T15:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74de6cb8-7fc1-53f2-b75c-097293ff1cfe', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74de6cb8-7fc1-53f2-b75c-097293ff1cfe'}, {'abstract': 'Following projects in Dubai and London, the newly founded Moving Museum sets up shop in the ancient Turkish city with a series of artist residencies.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/istanbul-moving-museum-ark-kultur-jumana-manna/', 'snippet': 'Following projects in Dubai and London, the newly founded Moving Museum sets up shop in the ancient Turkish city with a series of artist residencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Moving Museum is pretty much exactly what it sounds like: an artistic institution that is perpetually on the go. Founded by Aya Mousawi and Simon Sakhai, who live and work together, it launched in May 2013 with a show in Dubai devoted to the lost cuisine of Iraqi Jews, who thrived in that country prior to the 1940s. A show in London followed last fall that was devoted to the city’s contemporary art scene. As part of the museum’s continuing effort to “respond to a city through artistic practice,” in Sakhai’s words, the duo has now headed to Istanbul, both for its bubbling political energy and its geographic and cultural location on the boundary between east and west.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ