dio/2014/08/06/t-magazine/06odessa.html', 'snippet': 'The first single by the singer-songwriter from her self-titled debut EP.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first single by the singer-songwriter from her self-titled debut EP.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '“I Will Be There” by Odessa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T16:45:52+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/26ca4f57-1e3d-5523-9c37-9d889b412ef1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/26ca4f57-1e3d-5523-9c37-9d889b412ef1'}, {'abstract': 'Though Rupert Murdoch misfired on his takeover bid for Time Warner, the pressure is on its chief executive, Jeffrey Bewkes, to deliver results to his shareholders, Jeffrey Goldfarb writes for Reuters Breakingviews.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/rupert-murdoch-loses-but-could-still-come-out-ahead/', 'snippet': 'Though Rupert Murdoch misfired on his takeover bid for Time Warner, the pressure is on its chief executive, Jeffrey Bewkes, to deliver results to his shareholders, Jeffrey Goldfarb writes for Reuters Breakingviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rupert Murdoch miscalculated. The sly old fox of global media abruptly yanked his $80 billion offer to buy rival Time Warner on Tuesday after failing to anticipate his quarry’s resolve and the price demands of investors. Shares of 21st Century Fox rallied after the market officially closed while Time Warner’s retreated toward their pre-bid level. That means the refusenik boss, Jeffrey Bewkes, has something more to prove.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/business/dealbook/dbpix-murdoch/dbpix-murdoch-arti