ae42', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/6eb94016-404c-5b70-bc65-9f8ac64eae42'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: French authorities clamped down on rising hotel prices in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/1964-police-to-watch-for-gouging/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: French authorities clamped down on rising hotel prices in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Police here have been ordered to keep a sharp watch for any sudden price increases by the capital’s hotels and restaurants as part of a government campaign to prevent tourists from being overcharged during the peak holiday season. The move coincided with reports that tourist traffic in Paris this year is 20 percent below that of 1963 and that foreign travel agencies are advising against France for vacations because of high costs. Legal proceedings have already been taken against 37 Paris hotel and restaurant owners who allegedly made sudden price increases for drinks. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, August 7, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Police to Watch for ‘Gouging’', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T16:57:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 