None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbe8ade0-d3fd-5335-9c66-747a79800684', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbe8ade0-d3fd-5335-9c66-747a79800684'}, {'abstract': 'Immigration unilateralism is a presidential strategy, not just a response to gridlock.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/06/when-caesarism-is-a-choice/', 'snippet': 'Immigration unilateralism is a presidential strategy, not just a response to gridlock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I talked a little bit, in my last post, about the argument that anything President Obama might do unilaterally on immigration policy is, if not justified, at least explained by congressional gridlock and particularly by the extraordinary intransigence of the current G.O.P. But I want to say something more about this point, because it’s come up in various responses to my warnings against presidential caesarism\xa0— this one from Ezra Klein, for instance, and this one from Jonathan Bernstein. I think Bernstein does a good job of making the case that the president faces an unusual situation with House Republicans, given their incentives and dysfunctions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Caesarism Is a Choice', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T18:25:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d3d1632-a447-5530-81f7-a876692a2e96', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d3d1632-a447-5530-81f7-a876692a2e96'}, {'abstract': 'The death toll from the quake that struck Yunnan Province on Sunday has jumped to 589 as rescuers reached isolated villages and recovered the bodies of 179 more victims, the state media reported', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/world/asia/earthquake-death-toll-rises-to-nearly-600-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'The death toll from the quake that struck Yunnan Province on Sunday has jumped to 589 as rescuers reached isolated villages and recovered the bodies of 179 more victims, the state media reported', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The death toll from an earthquake that struck Yunnan Province in southwestern China on Sunday has jumped to 589 as rescuers reached isolated villages and recovered the bodies of 179 more victims, state media reported Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Earthquake Death Toll Rises to Nearly 600 in China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Earthquake Toll Nears 600', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value