 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b56cb581-7d5d-5170-98b1-e7ab3cbe4fd6', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b56cb581-7d5d-5170-98b1-e7ab3cbe4fd6'}, {'abstract': 'The Mostly Mozart Festival’s concert on Tuesday evening at Avery Fisher Hall included works by Alfred Schnittke, Haydn and Mozart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/arts/music/work-by-schnittke-and-haydn-at-mostly-mozart.html', 'snippet': 'The Mostly Mozart Festival’s concert on Tuesday evening at Avery Fisher Hall included works by Alfred Schnittke, Haydn and Mozart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parody and chaos are integral elements of the works of the Russian composer Alfred Schnittke, whose musical humor, like the most sophisticated jokes, sometimes surfaces unexpectedly with a witty turn of phrase. His “Moz-Art à la Haydn,” a pastiche based on an unfinished fragment by Mozart called “Music to a Carnival Pantomime,” opened the Mostly Mozart Festival’s concert on Tuesday evening at Avery Fisher Hall. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Homage to Mozart, Musical Wit and Allusions', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Homage to Mozart, Musical Wit and Allusions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mostly Mozart Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avery Fisher Hall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haydn, Franz Joseph', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schnittke, Alfred', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam