Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8fa2aff-800e-5fb6-9f20-21d86907cfeb', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8fa2aff-800e-5fb6-9f20-21d86907cfeb'}, {'abstract': 'Mutations in the PALB2 gene raise risk in women by almost as much as mutations in BRCA1 and BRCA2, the genes implicated in most inherited cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/health/gene-indicator-breast-cancer-risk.html', 'snippet': 'Mutations in the PALB2 gene raise risk in women by almost as much as mutations in BRCA1 and BRCA2, the genes implicated in most inherited cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mutations in a gene called PALB2 raise the risk of breast cancer in women by almost as much as mutations in BRCA1 and BRCA2, the infamous genes implicated in most inherited cases of the disease, a team of researchers reported Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study Shows Third Gene as Indicator for Breast Cancer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study Shows Third Gene as Indicator for Cancer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breast Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bakalar, Nicholas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T21:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title'