mons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/174a65cb-6c10-52b3-8852-7dc3ced34d6f', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/174a65cb-6c10-52b3-8852-7dc3ced34d6f'}, {'abstract': 'The British textile designer Donna Wilson’s first fabric collection, Forest and Friends, is as quirky as her knitted creatures and painted ceramics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/garden/inviting-your-friends-to-stay-for-a-while.html', 'snippet': 'The British textile designer Donna Wilson’s first fabric collection, Forest and Friends, is as quirky as her knitted creatures and painted ceramics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, the British textile designer Donna Wilson introduced her first fabric collection, Forest and Friends, and it’s as quirky as her existing menagerie of knitted creatures and face-painted ceramics. “Designing things that will make people smile and be happy just sort of comes naturally to me,” she said. “But I’m always trying to get new inspiration so it doesn’t get so predictable.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/garden/07TEXTILES/0807CURRENTS8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/07/garden/07TEXTILES/0807CURRENTS8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/garden/07TEXTILES/0807CURRENTS8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/garden/07TEXTILES/0807CURRENTS8-superJumbo.jpg', 'heigh