p_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/07/business/Corptaxjp1/Corptaxjp1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/Corptaxjp1/Corptaxjp1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Muddled Road to Overhauling Corporate Taxes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tax Trouble', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Shelters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T23:25:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e56115f-775f-5465-84fa-ebc182eb1eb0', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e56115f-775f-5465-84fa-ebc182eb1eb0'}, {'abstract': 'The willingness of courts to weigh whether the abortion right has become unduly burdened is critical in the struggle to preserve reproductive freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/opinion/new-judicial-approaches-to-abortion-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The willingness of courts to weigh whether the abortion right has become unduly burdened is critical in the struggle to preserve reproductive freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listening to politicians talk about abortion, watching state legislatures put up ever more daunting obstacles, reading the opinions of judges who give the states a free pass, it’s abundantly clear to me that some constitutional rights are more equal than others. Or to put it another way, there are constitutional rights and then there is abortion — a right, increasingly, in name only, treated as something separate and apart, vulnerable in its isolation from the mainstream of those rights the Constitution actually protects.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/greenhouse-circular/greenhouse-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Right Like Any Other', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Second Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Jackson Women's Health Organization", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Myron H', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-06T23:26:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/30015f4e-6188-5ca7-851a-9eeefbe136d9', 'word_count': 1268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30015f4e-6188-5ca7-851a-9eeefbe136d9'}, {'abstract': 'Legal Sea Foods, the restaurant company, has a new campaign to put some distance between itself and the word “chain.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/business/call-it-what-you-like-but-not-a-chain.html', 'snippet': 'Legal Sea Foods, the restaurant company, has a new campaign to put some distance between itself and the word “chain.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHITE CASTLE claims with pride that it is the first fast-food hamburger chain, and for good reason. It opened in 1921, just 15 years after Upton Sinclair’s “The Jungle” exposed horrific conditions in meat-processing plants. With its pure-sounding name, white interiors and fully viewable food preparation areas, White Castle helped restore America’s appetite for beef, promising consistency regardless of which location a customer visited. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/07/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/Adco/Adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1077, 'width': 1917, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/07/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/Adco/Adco-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Call It What You Like, but Not a Chain', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Call It What You Like, but Not a Chain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [