d barely a mile from the largest natural freshwater lake in the state, the trailer sat on a hill, hidden from the main drag. Behind it rose a flimsy fence, tall enough to shield its bounty: 50 marijuana plants in hastily constructed wooden boxes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dry California Fights Illegal Use of Water for Cannabis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dry California Fights Illegal Use of Water for Cannabis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Marijuana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Irrigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaitanya, Swami', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T00:45:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dffc6c1-fe3f-5c31-99cd-7c55b1b3c382', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dffc6c1-fe3f-5c31-99cd-7c55b1b3c382'}, {'abstract': 'Any action against the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria is seen as having unintended and potentially harmful consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/world/middleeast/islamic-militants-in-iraq-are-widely-loathed-yet-action-to-curb-them-is-elusive.html', 'snippet': 'Any action against the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria is seen as having unintended and potentially harmful consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — Its fighters have seized oil fields, held water supplies hostage, and commandeered heavy artillery that the United States once supplied to a friendly government in Iraq. In late July, they decapitated Syrian soldiers, put their heads on fence posts and published photographs online. For the last five days, they have drawn the Lebanese Army into a firefight over control of a border town, their first territorial foray into Lebanon.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Islamic Militants in Iraq Are Widely Loathed, Yet Action to Curb Them Is Elusive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Islamic Militants in Iraq Are Widely Loathed, Yet Action to Curb Them Is Elusive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T00:46:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47c499d1-ba46-54ad-837e-ffd718cdef9f