bodia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nuon Chea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khieu Samphan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Khmer Rouge', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T03:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller and Julia Wallace', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wallace', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e371046c-728d-5b50-9614-1001ae4f4299', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e371046c-728d-5b50-9614-1001ae4f4299'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Patrick Worthington reveals the beauty of swaths of paint on the sides of city buildings, which bear an uncanny resemblance to the work of artists like Mark Rothko and Robert Motherwell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/t-magazine/patrick-worthington-graffiti-city-as-canvas-tagging.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer Patrick Worthington reveals the beauty of swaths of paint on the sides of city buildings, which bear an uncanny resemblance to the work of artists like Mark Rothko and Robert Motherwell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekly series, T’s photo editors share the most compelling visual projects they’ve discovered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Covered-Up Graffiti Tags as Art', 'kicker': 'Viewfinder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TCulture', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Poggi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poggi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6530646d-680b-595b-9c90-a0bdd972106a', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6530646d-680b-595b-9c90-a0bdd972106a'}, {'abstract': 'Cool-weather pieces are arriving now in stores and online. Here, a roundup of some of the most promising options for the coming season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/t-magazine/get-a-jump-on-autumn-with-classics-from-the-pre-fall-collections.html', 'snippet': 'Cool-weather pieces are arriving now in stores and online. Here, a roundup of some of the most promising options for the coming season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer is in full swing: glowing fireflies, humming air conditioners. But while we’ve all been living in gauzy dresses and sandals, the stores are suddenly stocked with nubby wool sweaters, oversized coats and Dr. Martens-inspired boots, thanks to the phenomenon known as the pre-fall collections. Though layering up may feel far-off, this is the optimal moment — before the September shopping rush — to start building a cool-weather wardrobe. And the current retail landscape includes some especially well-executed takes on the essentials, such as vintage Levi’s jeans, cool sneakers, a perfect ribbed turtleneck and a versatile miniature black doctor’s bag. While some of these pieces’ price tags are formidable, consider them an investment in your style’s future. Get your hands on them now, before someone else does.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 's