t on August 7, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/pageoneplus/corrections-august-7-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 7, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: August 7, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T05:12:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5da8f219-7a35-5314-a530-27075363379b', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5da8f219-7a35-5314-a530-27075363379b'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the diaries, contracts, letters and other documents from the American Ballet Theater will go on view next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/arts/dance/ballet-theater-donating-trove-of-materials-to-library-of-congress.html', 'snippet': 'Some of the diaries, contracts, letters and other documents from the American Ballet Theater will go on view next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Balanchine’s 1947 contract for “Theme and Variations” is there. It stipulated that he would be paid $25 per performance in the first year, with his compensation falling to $15 by the third. Amid the mounds of papers also lies Jerome Robbins’s 1944 contract for “Fancy Free.” As a novice choreographer, he was offered only $10 per performance, with no mention of the ballet being staged beyond one year. (Little did they know.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ballet Theater Donating Trove of Materials to Library of Congress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance Trove Is Headed to Library of Congress', 'name': None, 's