al products from Europe and the United States, among others. The move raised the level of confrontation over Ukraine with measures that seemed likely to affect Russian consumers at least as much as European farming.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/world/SANCTIONS/SANCTIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/08/world/SANCTIONS/SANCTIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/world/SANCTIONS/SANCTIONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/world/SANCTIONS/SANCTIONS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/world/SANCTIONS/SANCTIONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/08/world/SANCTIONS/SANCTIONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/world/SANCTIONS/SANCTIONS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Responds to Western Sanctions With Import Bans of Its Own', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Responds to Western Sanctions With Import Bans of Its Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T10:33:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar and Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c00b7b1-b6b7-539b-8c7a-b0843049a30c', 'word_count': 1379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c00b7b1-b6b7-539b-8c7a-b0843049a30c'}, {'abstract': 'Opinions on peace talks in Egypt, a desperate situation in Iraq, a second Suez Canal, Boris Johnson for Parliament and safety measures in Texas.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/morning-views-53/', 'snippet': 'Opinions on peace talks in Egypt, a desperate situation in Iraq, a second Suez Canal, Boris Johnson for Parliament and safety measures in Texas.', 'lead_paragraph': '“In the first good news in a long time, a 72-hour cease-fire appeared to be holding on Wednesday as Israelis and Palestinians tallied what was lost, and gained, during the latest war over the desperate Gaza Strip,” states an editorial in The New York Times. Both sides are claiming victory — “Israel for wiping out 32 underground tunnels” and “Hamas for still being alive” — but the result is a more entrenched status quo: “Neither side has achieved its main goal of destroying the other.” The possibility of a peace plan appears ever more remote: “There seems to be little room left in Israeli politics for those who would end the occupation of the West Bank and Gaza and create an independent Palestinian state.” The editorial adds, “it is so important that indirect talks between Israelis and Palestinians this week, mediated by Egypt, lay the ground for something bigger and more durable than one cease-fire.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T10:34:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Altman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/538a77ed-7f1d-5b4f-9a9b-62ee5385cc91', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/538a77ed-7f1d-5b4f-9a9b-62ee5385cc91'}, {'abstract': 'China, which has been criticized for projects in disputed waters, is reportedly planning to build lighthouses on five islands in the South China Sea.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/china-lighthouse-plan-likely-to-raise-tensions-in-disputed-sea/', 'snippet': 'China, which has been criticized for projects in disputed waters, is reportedly planning to build lighthouses on five islands in the South China Sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China is planning to build lighthouses on five islands in the South China Sea, the official China News Agency reported on Thursday, in what would be Beijing’s latest rebuttal of criticisms of its construction projects in the disputed waters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/world/07sino-PARACEL/07sino-PARACEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/07/world/07sino-PARACEL/07sino-PARACEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/world/07sino-PARACEL/07sino-PARACEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/world/07sino-PARACEL/07sino-PARACEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/world/07sino-PARACEL/07sino-PARACEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/07/world/07sino-PARACEL/07sino-PARACEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/world/07sino-PARACEL/07sino-PARACEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height'