k Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Bank of America’s Big Mortgage Settlement', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T12:08:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/844d986a-1cd7-50e1-a5ad-f44e67d87429', 'word_count': 1976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/844d986a-1cd7-50e1-a5ad-f44e67d87429'}, {'abstract': 'On Aug. 7, 1974 Philippe Petit walked a tightrope between the twin towers, later telling The Times, “If I see three oranges I have to juggle, and if I see two towers I have to walk.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/throwback-thursday-philippe-petit-walks-tightrope-between-the-twin-towers/', 'snippet': 'On Aug. 7, 1974 Philippe Petit walked a tightrope between the twin towers, later telling The Times, “If I see three oranges I have to juggle, and if I see two towers I have to walk.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 7, 1974, Philippe Petit, the French-born high-wire artist and street performer, walked a tightrope strung between the World Trade Center towers. “After perhaps 45 minutes of knee bends and other stunts, Phillippe Petit, balancing pole in hand, turned himself over to waiting policemen,” The Times reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Throwback Thursday | Philippe Petit Walks Tightrope Between the Twin Towers', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T12:14:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 's