e had been following him and his wife for weeks, his colleagues said. The tail was so blatant that Mr. Rezaian, The Washington Post’s correspondent in Tehran, had even managed to take a picture of the license plate.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A U.S. Journalist’s Arrest Points to a Power Struggle in the Leadership of Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A U.S. Journalist’s Arrest Points to a Power Struggle in the Leadership of Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rezaian, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rouhani, Hassan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salehi, Yeganeh', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T13:17:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c5dea43-7fb8-59ac-951a-f42deeec5360', 'word_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c5dea43-7fb8-59ac-951a-f42deeec5360'}, {'abstract': 'The firms have agreed to pay a combined $325 million to settle accusations that they colluded with one another to drive down the prices of corporate takeover targets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/07/k-k-r-agrees-to-settle-lawsuit-on-private-equity-collusion/', 'snippet': 'The firms have agreed to pay a combined $325 million to settle accusations that they colluded with one another to drive down the prices of corporate takeover targets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 8:05 p.m. | Three of the leading private equity firms on Wall Street have agreed to pay a combined $325 million to settle accusations that they colluded with one another to drive down the prices of corporate takeover targets, according to a court filing on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/dbpix-buyout2/dbpix-buyout2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/07/business/dbpix-buyout2/dbpix-buyout2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/dbpix-buyout2/dbpix-buyout2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/dbpix-buyout2/dbpix-buyout2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/dbpix-buyout2/dbpix-buyout2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/07/business/dbpix-buyout2/dbpix-buyout2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/business/dbpix-buyout2/dbpix-buyout2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumb