'The documentary “The Dog” examines John Wojtowicz, the real-life model for Al Pacino’s character in Sidney Lumet’s 1975 classic, “Dog Day Afternoon.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It turns out that the true story bit about “Dog Day Afternoon” was, well, pretty true. That’s one of the jaw droppers in “The Dog,” an absorbing, rollicking documentary about John Wojtowicz, who’s best known as the guy Al Pacino performed, with heart, soul and a river of flop sweat, in “Dog Day Afternoon.” In Sidney Lumet’s magnificently squalid 1975 classic, Mr. Pacino plays Sonny Wortzik, whose new career as Clyde Barrow goes south as soon as he pulls out a gun in a Brooklyn bank. Thwarted by bad planning and legions of cops, Sonny eventually ends up in cuffs. The same pretty much happened to Mr. Wojtowicz, except that he was immortalized in a Hollywood masterwork. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/arts/05THEDOG2/05THEDOG2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/arts/05THEDOG2/05THEDOG2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/arts/05THEDOG2/05THEDOG2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/arts/05THEDOG2/05THEDOG2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 988, 'width': 1756, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/arts/05THEDOG2/05THEDOG2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name