 been reading on tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patti Smith, who reviews Haruki Murakami’s “Colorless Tsukuru Tazaki and His Years of Pilgrimage” this week, first discovered the Japanese author’s work while browsing in the East Village. “Attracted by the title, I picked up ‘A Wild Sheep Chase’ about five years ago in St. Mark’s Bookshop,” Smith said in a recent email interview. She quickly read that novel and “Dance Dance Dance,” and was hooked. “I love how he weaves the interdimensional and the mundane and the offhanded way certain characters negotiate these shifts,” Smith said. “I love that there are sequels and reoccurring characters. Like Roberto Bolaño, he offers an ever-expanding, interconnected universe.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/books/review/10OPENBOOK2/10OPENBOOK2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/10/books/review/10OPENBOOK2/10OPENBOOK2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/books/review/10OPENBOOK2/10OPENBOOK2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/books/review/10OPENBOOK2/10OPENBOOK2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1297, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/books/review/10OPENBOOK2/10OPENBOOK2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/20