s-wars-still-the-one/', 'snippet': 'Announcing a new feature, and rebutting outrageous claims about “Guardians of the Galaxy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For readers who wish this blog had more pop culture commentary and fewer rants against presidential despotism, I’m very pleased to announce that my colleague Frank Bruni and I are launching a new feature in which we ping-pong back and forth about the movies we’ve seen lately (and possibly the occasional TV show as well, when it seems appropriate), sometimes touching on their political significance but hopefully also offering a partial refuge from the politicized life as well. The feature should run monthly, roughly, but perhaps more frequently depending the quality and significance of what’s showing at a given moment; I hope readers find it to be an entertaining, not-too-self-serious diversion amid the Op-Ed team’s coverage of the\xa0grim and getting grimmer issues of the day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '“Star Wars”: Still The One', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruni, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamill, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T21:07:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2db94bf0-46bc-5422-b62f-1c5a36020858', 'word_count': 987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2db94bf0-46bc-5422-b62f-1c5a36020858'}, {'abstract': 'Times editors and reporters revisit the use of the word “torture” in connection to C.I.A. interroga