cle', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c84f4f59-648a-5795-96b1-7aff158dc807', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c84f4f59-648a-5795-96b1-7aff158dc807'}, {'abstract': 'Works by Zhang Huan and Virginia Overton at Storm King offer operatic showiness and Buddhist simplicity, but maybe not the ones you’d expect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/arts/design/zhang-huan-and-virginia-overton-contrast-at-storm-king.html', 'snippet': 'Works by Zhang Huan and Virginia Overton at Storm King offer operatic showiness and Buddhist simplicity, but maybe not the ones you’d expect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOUNTAINVILLE, N.Y. — Sculptures by the two artists featured here in temporary presentations at Storm King Art Center this year couldn’t be less alike. A single Minimalist piece by the New York sculptor Virginia Overton is gracefully fitted to the landscape of gently rolling hills. Six monumental, figurative sculptures by Zhang Huan of Shanghai are ponderously theatrical. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-33A9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Minimalist Meets Showy', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Minimalist Meets Showy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Storm King Art Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Huan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Overton, Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T21:41:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/06f32eb3-64fa-5f89-9ec9-5e398bcb74dd', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06f32eb3-64fa-5f89-9ec9-5e398bcb74dd'}, {'abstract': 'A walk on the High Line will include the “Archeo” exhibition as well as other outdoor artworks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/arts/design/artworks-along-the-high-line.html', 'snippet': 'A walk on the High Line will include the “Archeo” exhibition as well as other outdoor artworks.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Archeo” is this season’s exhibition of artworks presented on the High Line, the elevated railway turned greenway on the West Side of Manhattan that has become a tourist magnet and emblem of gentrified New York. Shortening the word “archaeology,” the exhibition of outdoor sculpture by seven contemporary artists focuses on technology and obsolescence. It also provides some connection with the history and culture of the High Line, which, with its carefully selected benches and botanicals, can otherwise feel like a detached people mover carrying you through a bucolic landscape in the sky.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-40OZ/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-40OZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-40OZ/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-40OZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-40OZ/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-40OZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/design/20140808-OUTDOORS-slide-40