ater', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/409b5838-0d92-545c-aa30-27ff72be8727', 'word_count': 4387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/409b5838-0d92-545c-aa30-27ff72be8727'}, {'abstract': 'Jacob deGrom faced something he has not encountered recently — adversity — as the Mets had trouble scoring against the Nationals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/sports/baseball/degrom-keeps-mets-in-the-game-but-harpers-home-run-ends-it.html', 'snippet': 'Jacob deGrom faced something he has not encountered recently — adversity — as the Mets had trouble scoring against the Nationals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Jacob deGrom put his glove under his armpit, massaged a baseball with his hands and paced a few feet beyond the mound. He had just allowed his first home run in about two months, a period in which he had become the Mets’ most consistent starter and adversity had faded to a foreign concept. The question now was simple: How would he respond?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/sports/08mets1/08mets1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/08/sports/08mets1/08mets1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/sports/08mets1/08mets1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/sports/08mets1/08mets1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}