ing group show imagines the consequences of drastic environmental change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/arts/design/the-fifth-season.html', 'snippet': 'This stimulating group show imagines the consequences of drastic environmental change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title of this stimulating group show comes from a centrally placed installation by Mark Dion. Called “Harbingers of the Fifth Season,” it presents the imaginary workroom of a scientist-illustrator who is studying shifts in animal behavior caused by drastic environmental change.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/08FIFTH/08FIFTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/08FIFTH/08FIFTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 617}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/08FIFTH/08FIFTH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 996, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/08FIFTH/08FIFTH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1992, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/08FIFTH/08FIFTH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/08FIFTH/08FIFTH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/08FIFTH/08FIFTH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Fifth Season’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Fifth Season’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T22:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/72157485-31fc-5168-b79d-93bc8fa84c20', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72157485-31fc-5168-b79d-93bc8fa84c20'}, {'abstract': '“Human Resources,” on Pivot, is a workplace reality series that offers an example of meaningful work for millennials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/arts/television/human-resources-on-pivot-gives-hope-to-the-working-young.html', 'snippet': '“Human Resources,” on Pivot, is a workplace reality series that offers an example of meaningful work for millennials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Participant Media’s Pivot aims its programming at millennials and uses the motto “It’s your turn.” But plenty of millennials have found that it is not their turn. They’re stuck in drab low-level jobs despite excellent educations and high aspirations. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the Best of Trash, While Finding Meaning', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making the Best of Trash, While Finding Meaning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pivot (TV Network)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Human Resources (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-07T22:08:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d650c67-a794-5499-9481-4596ad8e07eb', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d650c67-a794-5499-9481-4596ad8e07eb'}, {'abstract': 'Emmylou Harris and Rodney Crowell played at Americanafest NYC, a collaboration between Lincoln Center Out of Doors and the American Music Association, which runs through Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/arts/music/americanafest-nyc-at-damrosch-park-bandshell.html', 'snippet': 'Emmylou Harris and Rodney Crowell played at Americanafest NYC, a collaboration between Lincoln Center Out of Doors and the American Music Association, which runs through Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Emmylou Harris and Rodney Crowell foraged through history both distant and recent at the Damrosch Park Bandshell on Wednesday night, finding some of the strongest traction in vintage songs of their own design. Among them was “\xa0’Til I Gain Control Again,” written by Mr. Crowell and originally recorded by Ms. Harris in 1975, not long after their first meeting. Underplaying its broken reassurance and desperate devotion, they made it feel lived-in and true.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/08/arts/08AMERICANA/08AMERICANA-articleLarge