ae0-92fc77a5ac9b'}, {'abstract': 'How to handle ill-timed condolences, house-sitting mishaps, scratched cars and patronizing nicknames.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/fashion/Social-Qs-No-Sympathy-Now-Please.html', 'snippet': 'How to handle ill-timed condolences, house-sitting mishaps, scratched cars and patronizing nicknames.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, we lost our 18-year-old son to an undiagnosed heart condition. We are still grieving, though time is making things a little better. But we find it extremely distressing when people we haven’t seen in the last year rush up to us at social events to tell us how sorry they are and how they “just can’t imagine” our loss. We know they mean well, but it makes us overwhelmingly sad and ruins festive occasions. My husband doesn’t want to go out anymore! What can we do to stop people from launching into their grief for us?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/