itions announced Thursday, nearly a year after a devastating nerve agent attack in a Damascus suburb focused global attention on the Syrian stockpile. The announcement, by the Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons, said a significant volume of the material had been incinerated at Ellesmere Port, a site in Britain, mainly ingredients for making the nerve agent and hydrochloric acid. Facilities in Finland, Germany and the United States are also destroying portions of the Syrian stockpile, which was exported from Syria in June after repeated delays. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria: Progress on Chemical Stockpile', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Progress on Chemical Stockpile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stockpiling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T04:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/53e7de75-dcb6-5e5e-9476-cd2e48523d05', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53e7de75-dcb6-5e5e-9476-cd2e48523d05'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Palmer shot a six-unde