highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Starz) AMERICAN HUSTLE (2013) Irving Rosenfeld (Christian Bale), a con man with a rococo comb-over, and Sydney Prosser (Amy Adams), his seductive mistress, are forced by an F.B.I. agent (Bradley Cooper, above right, with Ms. Adams and Mr. Bale) to help ensnare politicians in this screwball comedy directed by David O. Russell and inspired by the Abscam sting operation begun in 1978, which netted corrupt elected officials but also resulted in charges of entrapment. Jennifer Lawrence plays Irving’s adenoidal stay-at-home wife; Jeremy Renner is the mayor of Camden, N.J., whose ambitions trump his decency. “Mr. Bale has long been a great actor, if not an especially likable screen presence,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “It’s a pleasure to see him warm up, soften up, not only because he looks as if he were having a good time, but also because he’s extraordinary here.” The film “giddily embraces the excesses of its era, from spandex to ’staches, though it’s a farce that speaks as well to this tarnished age,” she added. “But all the shiny surfaces, the glitter ball and the gaudiness, also suggest a world in which everyone is anxious to shake off the post-Vietnam War, post-Watergate funk. The ghost of Richard M. Nixon hovers in the air; everyone is a fake, and everyone wears a mask.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/5942eb7c-fca1-53ae-b900-5ece72408bfc', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5942eb7c-fca1-53ae-b900-5ece72408bfc'}, {'abstract': 'Israel and Palestinian militants resumed cross-border air assaults after a three-day cease-fire expired, but the renewed violence seemed less about meeting military goals than about jockeying for leverage in talks that had made little progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/world/middleeast/israel-gaza-strip-conflict.html', 'snippet': 'Israel and Palestinian militants resumed cross-border air assaults after a three-day cease-fire expired, but the renewed violence seemed less about meeting military goals than about jockeying for leverage in talks that had made little progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GAZA CITY — Israel and Palestinian militants in the Gaza Strip resumed cross-border air assaults after a three-day cease-fire expired on Friday, but the renewed violence seemed less about meeting military goals than about jockeying for leverage in talks that had made little progress toward a more durable truce. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Fighting a Bid for Leverage as a Gaza Cease-Fire Expires', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Fighting a Bid for Leverage as a Gaza Cease-Fire Expires', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudoren, Jodi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T05:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article',