s://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/why-terracycle-keeps-trying-to-create-a-reality-tv-series/', 'snippet': 'Today, the revenue our marketing department generates offsets a large percentage of the costs it incurs. And every year we get closer to running a truly profitable marketing department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 2011, I wrote a post about TerraCycle’s ongoing quest to create what we call negative-cost marketing. In other words, we’re always looking for ways to persuade other people to pay us to tell the world about TerraCycle, rather than our having to pay them. So far, we’ve had a good bit of success doing this.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why TerraCycle Keeps Trying to Create a Reality TV Series', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Participant Media LLC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pivot (TV Network)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Trenton (NJ)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T11:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d51bbbf-7167-5712-b39d-4f117e0bcd9a', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d51bbbf-7167-5712-b39d-4f117e0bcd9a'}, {'abstract': 'This week our Penguin Young Adult guest judge is Meg Wolitzer, and submissions are due by Aug. 15 at 7 a.m. Eastern.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/summer-reading-contest-week-9-what-interested-you-most-in-the-times-this-week/', 'snippet': 'This week our Penguin Young Adult guest judge is Meg Wolitzer, and submissions are due by Aug. 15 at 7 a.m. Eastern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In The Times this week: news about Russian hackers stealing more than a billion Internet passwords, as well as advice for keeping your passwords out of hackers’ hands. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/business/06secure-web1-LN/06secure-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/06/business/06secure-web1-LN/06secure-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/business/06secure-web1-LN/06secure-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06/business/06secure-web1-LN/06secure-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1029, 'width': 1544, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/06