graph': 'WHAT’S BEHIND THE STAMPEDE OF MERGERS | “Something big is happening on Wall Street that is making investment bankers richer,” Peter Eavis and David Gelles write in DealBook. That something is a boom in mergers and acquisitions, which is expected to continue even after Rupert Murdoch’s bid for Time Warner and Sprint’s attempt to buy T-Mobile crumbled earlier this week. A sharp upturn in deal activity is often thought to herald a stronger economy and a buoyant stock market. The theory is that corporate chieftains see strength building in their business lines, which gives them the confidence to pursue ambitious acquisitions of other companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: What’s Behind the Surge in Mergers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T11:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b8b1705-848c-511b-90fb-279697ec3e46', 'word_count': 1832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b8b1705-848c-511b-90fb-279697ec3e46'}, {'abstract': 'Frank O’Hara’s “Lunch Poems,” a volume published in 1964, has been reissued for its 50th anniversary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/books/frank-oharas-lunch-poems-turn-50.html', 'snippet': 'Frank O’Hara’s “Lunch Poems,” a volume published in 1964, has been reissued for its 50th anniversary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank O’Hara’s “Lunch Poems,” the little black dress of American poetry books, redolent of cocktails and cigarettes and theater tickets and phonograph records, turns 50 this year. It seems barely to have aged.', 'print_s