 'nyt://article/1f3a2645-23e1-53f3-ae5e-a8bc2e22ab97', 'word_count': 1311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f3a2645-23e1-53f3-ae5e-a8bc2e22ab97'}, {'abstract': 'Retirement coaches are available for people who forget to plan the aspect of their postwork lives that doesn’t involve money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/your-money/retirement-coaches-help-plan-beyond-the-workplace.html', 'snippet': 'Retirement coaches are available for people who forget to plan the aspect of their postwork lives that doesn’t involve money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Guy Johnson retired from his tax management position at Unilever, one of the world’s largest consumer products companies, he was sure that he was prepared. But he was fooling himself.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/business/Retiring/Retiring-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/09/business/Retiring/Retiring-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/business/Retiring/Retiring-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/business/Retiring/Retiring-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1372, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/business/Retiring/Retiring-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/09/business/Retiring/Retiring-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/business/Retiring/Retiring-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding an Identity Beyond the Workplace', 'kicker': 'Retiring', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding an Identity Beyond the Workplace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hannon, Kerry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Directions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T13:23:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerry Hannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4d05940-8798-5c4e-ab54-6b99d02c3509', 'word_count': 1417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4d05940-8798-5c4e-ab54-6b99d02c3509'}, {'abstract': 'A look at some of the different approaches when drafting a fantasy football wide receiver along with sleeper, bust and breakout picks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/sports/football/fantasy-football-wide-receiver-primer.html', 'snippet': 'A look at some of the different approaches when drafting a fantasy football wide receiver along with sleeper, bust and breakout picks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last season was a record-setting offensive year in the N.F.L., which included the most passing touchdowns (804) and combined passing yards per game (471). In the fantasy world, that resulted in the most total points generated in the last 15 years (standard 74,798; PPR 85,900). As if we needed another reason to covet the wide receiver position, the league decided to make things even more difficult for N.F.L. secondaries by instructing its officials to emphasize the 5-yard contact and defensive holding rules.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Football: Wide Receiver Primer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Calvin (1985- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Dez', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Brandon (1984- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, A J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Julio (1989- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T13:24:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Sablich and Justin Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec6c4f90-6fea-546c-8b2c-e64b8e1d6075', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec6c4f90-6fea-546c-8b2c-e64b8e1d6075'}, {'abstract': '“Do you want to put on your shoes now?” “Should we have macaroni and cheese for dinner?” “How about you go brush your teeth?” These are not really questions.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/need-kids-to-follow-instructions-dont-ask-tell/', 'snippet': '“Do you want to put on your shoes now?” “Should we have macaroni and cheese for dinner?” “How about you go brush your teeth?” These are not really questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, I committed what is known as a “mom fail” (basically any false move committed during the act of mothering). Preparing my then-2½-year-old son to go out in the morning for a play date, I asked him, “Do you want to go to H.’s house?” Emphatically, he said no. “Well, we have plans; he’s expecting us,” I amended lamely. My son burst into tears, and no matter how I tried to spin it, he was adamant. Maybe he was tired; maybe the dark, cloudy morning visible from our windows was too uninviting. Whatever the case, I was now in the awkward position of having to drag him, kicking and screaming, down four flights of stairs (we lived in a walk-up) while also toting my younger boy, then an infant. So I canceled the play date (thus committing a “friendship fail,” too, all in one morning). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/31/us/motherlode-toothbrushes/motherlode-toothbrushes-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/31/us/motherlode-toothbrushes/motherlode-toothbrushes-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/31/us/motherlode-toothbrushes/motherlode-toothbrushes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/31/us/motherlode-toothbrushes/mot