lesome Inheritance” and more.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘A Troublesome Inheritance’', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters: ‘A Troublesome Inheritance’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T15:20:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb695b05-f4c7-5ee3-b36a-e390fda52ed7', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb695b05-f4c7-5ee3-b36a-e390fda52ed7'}, {'abstract': 'Two sisters from Ohio reinvent themselves in 1940s America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/books/review/lucky-us-by-amy-bloom.html', 'snippet': 'Two sisters from Ohio reinvent themselves in 1940s America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No Amy Bloom character ever acted out of boredom. Once a practicing psychotherapist, Bloom knows that dire circumstances can drive people to their most compelling extremes. At her best, when she sets these driven souls on a journey across a landscape shadowed by immigration or war, the results can be stunning.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/books/review/10LANDIS/10LANDIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 452, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/books/review/10LANDIS/10LANDIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 452, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp