n undeniable frenzy in the spring of 1849. “No one,” Edward Dolnick writes, “could have imagined how quickly the West would change.” Shouts of “Gold!” would later be raised in such scattered locales as Bannack, Mont., Cripple Creek, Colo., and Nome, Alaska, but it all began in California near a place called Sutter’s Mill.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Striking It Rich', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Striking It Rich', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolnick, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T15:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Walter R. Borneman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Walter', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Borneman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2c030c4-5f8e-521c-a674-56a123bb4431', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2c030c4-5f8e-521c-a674-56a123bb4431'}, {'abstract': 'Following three women to Afghanistan and back home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/books/review/soldier-girls-by-helen-thorpe.html', 'snippet': 'Following three women to Afghanistan and back home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Helen Thorpe’s comprehensively researched new book, “Soldier Girls,” follows the lives of three women from enlistment in the Indiana National Guard through deployment and back home again. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/books/review/10hoffman/10hoffman-articleLarge.jpg',