: 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f45fee8e-bfd8-52b4-bbdc-0058e5fc0805', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f45fee8e-bfd8-52b4-bbdc-0058e5fc0805'}, {'abstract': 'Restoring the 54-room, 18th-century manse to its former glory has been one man’s life-long labor of love.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/rundale-palace-latvia-renovation-imants-lancmanis/', 'snippet': 'Restoring the 54-room, 18th-century manse to its former glory has been one man’s life-long labor of love.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last May, Rundale Palace, a 18th-century Baroque palace in Latvia, celebrated the completion of 50 years of renovation work with the opening of the Duke’s Library, one of several rooms finally open to the public for the first time. The Duke in question was Ernst Johann von Biron, the Duke of Courland, for whom the palace was built between 1736 and 1740 by the Italian architect Francesco Bartolomeo Rastrelli as a summer residence. It boasts 54 rooms, including a 1770s-era billiards room and a banquet hall known as the Great Gallery, which have also finally been restored to their original splendor. Some have called the palace the Versailles of Latvia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Half-Century-Long Renovation of Rundale Palace, the Versailles of Latvia', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Riga (Latvia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T21:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nadja Sayej', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nadja', 'middlename': None, 'la