ne': 'Truscott/United States Playing Card Senior Swiss Teams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T21:34:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a0e7ca9-f9ed-58dd-bc76-556fad255920', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a0e7ca9-f9ed-58dd-bc76-556fad255920'}, {'abstract': 'Paavo Jarvi led the Deutsche Kammerphilharmonie Bremen in an all-Brahms program as part of the Mostly Mozart Festival on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/arts/music/mostly-mozart-with-the-conductor-paavo-jarvi.html', 'snippet': 'Paavo Jarvi led the Deutsche Kammerphilharmonie Bremen in an all-Brahms program as part of the Mostly Mozart Festival on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mostly Mozart Festival has been offering more varied fare lately, but plenty of it still looks staid. At first glance, an overture-concerto-symphony program of Brahms, Brahms and Brahms — with encores of Brahms — appears conservative. But it didn’t turn out that way with Paavo Jarvi and the Deutsche Kammerphilharmonie Bremen, who stormed through this Thursday concert at Alice Tully Hall with a rare intensity.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/arts/09MOSTLY/09MOSTLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy':