amala Dance offered an unexpectedly contagious performance of Bharatanatyam at Lincoln Center Out of Doors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You don’t generally go to a performance of Bharatanatyam, the classical South Indian dance style, expecting to want to get up and dance. The form inspires a more removed kind of reverence, as something to be admired from afar, like a sacred object. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/arts/09RAGAMALA/09RAGAMALA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/09/arts/09RAGAMALA/09RAGAMALA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/arts/09RAGAMALA/09RAGAMALA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/arts/09RAGAMALA/09RAGAMALA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1403, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/arts/09RAGAMALA/09RAGAMALA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/09/arts/09RAGAMALA/09RAGAMALA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/arts/09RAGAMALA/09RAGAMALA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sacred Music and Movement, With an Infectious Beat', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sacred Music and Movement, With an Infectious Beat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Out of Doors Festival', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ragamala Dance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahanthappa, Rudresh', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T22:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/23a34e6c-7540-5800-87fd-5d1b136fd27e', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23a34e6c-7540-5800-87fd-5d1b136fd27e'}, {'abstract': 'Two new shows harness the longstanding television strategy of making people look stupid to attract viewers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/arts/television/fat-guys-in-the-woods-and-idiotest-exploit-stupidity.html', 'snippet': 'Two new shows harness the longstanding television strategy of making people look stupid to attract viewers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s basic economics: If you have a natural resource, try to exploit it. One resource we have in abundance is stupidity, and television’s long history of exploiting it continues with two new shows in the next few days, one whose title is its most attention-getting feature, the other equally drab but in different ways.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'Th