evolving stage presence of the band, hate the haircuts — but hey, it’s Brooklyn. They’re in Prospect Park tomorrow night:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: San Fermin, Revised', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-08T22:13:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2ef19e6-8713-529f-9c59-94c47ec1b715', 'word_count': 28, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2ef19e6-8713-529f-9c59-94c47ec1b715'}, {'abstract': 'Zero Freitas is buying up all the world’s records. Here’s a sampling of 10 from his collection.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/08/choice-cuts-zero-freitass-rarest-records/', 'snippet': 'Zero Freitas is buying up all the world’s records. Here’s a sampling of 10 from his collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s magazine, Monte Reel writes about Zero Freitas, a Brazilian bus magnate whose personal mission is to buy up all of the world’s vinyl records. Among the several million he has amassed so far, stored in a 25,000-square-foot warehouse in São Paulo, are some rare albums that could easily sell for thousands of dollars on eBay. Here’s a sampling of 10 from his collection.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/magazine/FreitasRecords-slide-XZZL/FreitasRecords-slide-XZZL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/10/magazine/FreitasRecords-slide-XZZL/F