old-to-park-to-save-fuel.html', 'snippet': 'Motorbike use by ordinary citizens has been cut to rush hours to ensure fuel for the government and the military personnel, two websites that monitor North Korea said, adding that a decline in Chinese oil imports was probably responsible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — It is no secret that North Korea suffers chronic shortages of fuel, to the point that nighttime satellite photographs of the Korean Peninsula show a glittering south and a darkened north, beginning exactly at the 38th parallel that divides them. Now the scarcity, apparently made even worse by a drop in oil imports from China, has claimed a new class of victims: motorbike riders.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Motorbikers in North Korea Are Told to Park to Save Fuel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Motorbikers in North Korea Are Told to Park to Save Fuel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T00:52:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c3bcecc-be8c-5ac4-a47a-14072597ede2', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c3bcecc-be8c-5ac4-a47a-14072597ede2'}, {'abstract': 'As tensions between Muslims and Jews worsen abroad, an American Jew working for an Islamic nonprofit organization has received vitriol from Jewish communities for his criticism of Israel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/us/guided-by-history-a-jew-tries-to-unite-two-faiths-divided-by-war-in-gaza.html', 'snippet': 'As tensions between Muslims and Jews worsen abroad, an American Jew working for an Islamic nonprofit organization has received vitriol from Jewish communities for his criticism of Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK, Del. — Shortly after the latest cease-fire expired in Gaza on Friday, Jacob Bender gingerly climbed the steps of the mimbar, the pulpit at the Islamic Society of Delaware here. A Jew in a mosque, his hands palpably quivering but his reedy voice steady, he read some brief comments to close the afternoon’s worship service, called Juma’a.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/09/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/09/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/09/us/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guided by History, a Jew Tries to Unite Two Faiths Divided by War in Gaza', 'kicker': 'On Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guided by History, a Jew Tries to Unite Two Faiths Divided by War in Gaza', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freedman, Samuel G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bender, Jacob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prayers and Prayer Books', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council on American-Islamic Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T01:09:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samuel G. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91906cc3-3ea5-5105-b9ce-32468e83ceaf', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91906cc3-3ea5-5105-b9ce-32468e83ceaf'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said Friday that they would use a retooled state health exchange website for this fall’s open enrollment period.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/us/massachusetts-health-site-will-stay-state-based-.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said Friday that they would use a retooled state health exchange website for this fall’s open enrollment period.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Officials said\xa0Friday\xa0that they would use a retooled state health exchange website for this fall’s open enrollment period. The Massachusetts Health Connector was established by the state’s 2006 health overhaul law, but\xa0it sputtered when it was updated to comply with the Affordable Care Act, sending 250,000 people to temporary coverage. In the spring, Connector officials decided to buy new software for the state health insurance marketplace while preparing to join the federal exchange if necessary. They met\xa0Thursday\xa0with federal officials, who supported the decision to move forward with the state-based exchange. Connector officials plan to contact up to 450,000 individuals, including those with temporary or legacy coverage, who need to apply this fall for plans that comply with the Affordable Care Act. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Health Site Will Stay State-Based ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Health Site Will Stay State-Based', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T01:13:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c2f0c0d-5073-53fb-9d26-a4143f362ca5', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c2f0c0d-5073-53fb-9d26-a4143f362ca5'}, {'abstract': 'The Inn at Pound Ridge by Jean-Georges, with its keen attention to detail and its bountiful expenditure of resources to get things right, should quell critics who deride the trend in name-chef empire building.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/nyregion/a-review-of-the-inn-at-pound-ridge-by-jean-georges.html', 'snippet': 'The Inn at Pound Ridge by Jean-Georges, with its keen attention to detail and its bountiful expenditure of resources to get things right, should quell critics who deride the trend in name-chef empire building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a November night swirling with snow, weeks before the Inn at Pound Ridge by Jean-Georges opened, I caught a glimpse of white toques bobbing under bright lights in the new kitchen as I drove past. The late hour, and the formality of the toques, somehow spoke to the seriousness of the enterprise.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/nyregion/10DINEWE3/10DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/10/nyregion/10DINEWE3/10DINEWE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/nyregion/10DINEWE3/10DINEWE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jum