 landmark decision may cost the N.C.A.A. hundreds of millions of dollars, but it may not create a windfall for any individual athlete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The landmark decision in the so-called O’Bannon case that found that the N.C.A.A. violated antitrust laws may be precedent setting and may ultimately cost colleges hundreds of millions of dollars. But it is unlikely to create a windfall for any individual athlete. In her 99-page decision, Judge Claudia Wilken laid out the justification for her injunction.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the O’Bannon Ruling Means for Colleges and Players', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What the Ruling Means for Colleges and Players', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilken, Claudia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Bannon, Ed", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T02:46:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d84d5ad-1fb9-5d3a-a586-21ae1e8257cc', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d84d5ad-1fb9-5d3a-a586-21ae1e8257cc'}, {'abstract': 'For China, the strategic importance of a proposed line can barely be overstated: It would provide an alternate to the l