'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-saturday-august-9-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, August 9, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Fifty percent of my questions are about why their hair is not falling out. It is the zillionth time I have answered it.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, August 9, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T04:52:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/4061bb17-9493-553c-b7e8-f6614190056d', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4061bb17-9493-553c-b7e8-f6614190056d'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Starz) OUTLANDER Claire Randall (Caitriona Balfe, above), an English combat nurse, touches a druid monument while on her honeymoon in Scotland and is transported back to the 18th century, where she’s kidnapped by Highlanders and meets the sensitive hunk Jamie (Sam Heughan) in this new series, adapted from the novels by Diana Gabaldon. “The ‘Outlander’ books date to 1991, but it seems likely that TV executives looked at them and thought, oh, ‘Game of Thrones’ meets ‘Downton Abbey,’\xa0” Mike Hale wrote in The New York Times. “Ms. Balfe, Mr. Heughan and Tobias Menzies as the modern husband (who also pops up, inconveniently, in 1743) acquit themselves well, sharing the screen with the scenery and costumes and keeping straight faces through all the fantasy-romance conceits. They seem to be having a good time, and if you have a weakness for muskets, accents and the occasional roll in the heather, you probably will too.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/b486fa75-fb5e-5375-b4d9-896088fe36bf', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b486fa75-fb5e-5375-b4d9-896088fe36bf'}, {'abstract': 'Elizabeth Green’s article on Americans’ struggles with math received more than 940 comments online. Here’s what readers said.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/analytics-common-denominators/', 'snippet': 'Elizabeth Green’s article on Americans’ struggles with math received more than 940 comments online. Here’s what readers said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following Analytics appears on the Reply All page in the Aug. 10 issue of the magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/magazine/10analyticsbox/10analyticsbox-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 279, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/10/magazine/10analyticsbox/10analyticsbox-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 279}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/magazine/10analyticsbo