e', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9f1dd5c-fee4-50d4-ae2a-aa60892aa2b4', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9f1dd5c-fee4-50d4-ae2a-aa60892aa2b4'}, {'abstract': 'Carmine Gangone’s birds mattered to him not because they were a substitute for human companionship but because they connected him to a new community.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/the-pigeon-fliers-of-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Carmine Gangone’s birds mattered to him not because they were a substitute for human companionship but because they connected him to a new community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A decade ago, when I lived in Bushwick, Brooklyn, I used to watch the sunset from my rooftop. All around me were large flocks of pigeons, their white wingtips glittering as they swirled in the sun’s golden hour. These were not street pigeons. Their movements were too choreographed, and they hovered above particular tenements as if attached by marionette strings. Atop the buildings, I could just make out the silhouettes of men whistling at the birds while waving jerry-built flags. These were the puppeteers.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/sunday-review/10SUBPIGEON/10SUBPIGEON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/10/sunday-review/10SUBPIGEON/10SUBPIGEON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/sunday-review/10SUBPIGEON/10SUBPIGEON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/sunday-review/10SUBPIGEON/10SUBPIGEON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1384, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/sunday-review/10SUBPIGEON/10SUBPIGEON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/10/sunday-review/10SUBPIGEON/10SUBPIGEON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/sunday-review/10SUBPIGEON/10SUBPIGEON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pigeon Fliers of New York', 'kicker': 'Menagerie', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Pigeon Fliers of New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pigeons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T18:35:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Jerolmack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jerolmack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f09b4e84-b6cb-5335-a968-a3bcd181324b', 'word_count': 1438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f09b4e84-b6cb-5335-a968-a3bcd181324b'}, {'abstract': 'Protesters initially planned to march across the bridge, but will instead begin on Staten Island, where a man died last month after an encounter with the police.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/nyregion/protest-march-in-chokehold-case-is-moved-from-verrazano-bridge-to-staten-island.html', 'snippet': 'Protesters initially planned to march across the bridge, but will instead begin on Staten Island, where a man died last month after an encounter with the police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rev. Al Sharpton, seeking to defuse political and logistical concerns over his proposal to lead a protest march across the Verrazano-Narrows Bridge, said on Saturday that the march against aggressive policing would instead be held on Staten Island, where a man died last month after an encounter with the police. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protest March in Chokehold Case Is Moved From Verrazano Bridge to Staten Island', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protest in Chokehold Case Is Moved to Staten Island', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Verrazano-Narrows Bridge (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Action Network', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpton, Al', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T18:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/524a99fa-47e6-5d1c-aaef-b41afbcd867f', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/524a99fa-47e6-5d1c-aaef-b41afbcd867f'}, {'abstract': 'It’s looking pretty Keynesian out there.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/the-opposite-of-stagflation/', 'snippet': 'It’s looking pretty Keynesian out there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the truly amazing (and disheartening) things about the Great Recession and its aftermath has been the continuing insistence of many economists that it’s somehow a supply-side slump, driven by the evils of Obamacare or something. This tends to come from people who view stagflation in the 1970s as having permanently refuted all things Keynes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Opposite of Stagflation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T18:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e41f3f94-18c1-5fe5-b21c-632fe83161aa', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e41f3f94-18c1-5fe5-b21c-632fe83161aa'}, {'abstract': 'Not that bad. Really.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/09/in-praise-of-the-dmv/', 'snippet': 'Not that bad. Really.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, not exactly. But I see that some of the commenters on my libertarian piece invoke the old “horrors of the DMV” line to claim that government never works.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Praise of the DMV', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'se