: 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cce1de67-40f1-521c-aef6-a974588ff833', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cce1de67-40f1-521c-aef6-a974588ff833'}, {'abstract': 'The Drive East festival is back with another week of exceptional programming.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/arts/dance/drive-east-festival-returns-to-la-mama.html', 'snippet': 'The Drive East festival is back with another week of exceptional programming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'August is typically dance’s hibernation period. But last year, some extraordinary sights and sounds filled La MaMa’s intimate East Village theater when it was transformed into a haven for classical Indian music and dance. Beginning Monday, the Drive East festival is back with another week of exceptional programming, organized by Navatman, the South Asian performing arts group, and devoted to the dance styles of Bharatanatyam, Kathak and Kuchipudi, as well as a rarer form: Sattriya, originally practiced by celibate monks. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE1/10GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE1/10GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE1/10GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE1/10GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy'