ival, where he performed with the soprano Diana Damrau and impressed with his musicality, muscular technique and imaginative flair. Mr. de Maistre, the former principal harpist of the Vienna Philharmonic, has carved out a career as an orchestral soloist, chamber musician and recitalist and has expanded the repertory for harp with commissions and his own arrangements. He will perform some of them at 10 p.m. Thursday in the intimate, candlelit series A Little Night Music, part of Mostly Mozart, at Lincoln Center’s Stanley H. Kaplan Penthouse. That program includes his arrangements of pieces by Mozart, Liszt, Fauré and Smetana. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 496, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 496}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1692, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE6/10GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing the Harp to Center Stage', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical: Bringing the Harp to Center Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-09T20:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e7a5b67-f86d-59f9-b81d-54942f2e6681', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e7a5b67-f86d-59f9-b81d-54942f2e6681'}, {'abstract': 'The Wallace Line swerves among the islands of Indonesia from just west of Bali to the seas south of the Philippines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/arts/design/east-of-the-wallace-line-opens-at-the-yale-university-art-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'The Wallace Line swerves among the islands of Indonesia from just west of Bali to the seas south of the Philippines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Wallace Line swerves among the islands of Indonesia from just west of Bali to the seas south of the Philippines. It’s named after the British naturalist Alfred Russel Wallace, who discovered in the mid-19th century that different species of flora and fauna grew on either side. “East of the Wallace Line: Monumental Art From Indonesia and New Guinea,” opening Friday at the Yale University Art Gallery, will present more than 120 works of art and craft from the 17th to the 19th century made by people living east of that line. These habitats include the islands of Timor, Flores and the Moluccas of eastern Indonesia and, in western New Guinea, the Raja Ampat Islands and Cenderawasih Bay. Drawn from the gallery’s Indo-Pacific art collection, the exhibition will include large, ritual and ancestral statues carved from wood; small, intricately carved ceremonial and utilitarian objects made of wood, ivory, and brass; richly patterned textiles; and wooden shields inlaid with mother-of-pearl. (1111 Chapel Street, New Haven; artgallery.yale.edu.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE3/10GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE3/10GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE3/10GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE3/10GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1317, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE3/10GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE3/10GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/10/arts/10GUIDE3/10GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': '