11:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9877d614-d4d9-5a26-be97-67e2394a0c53', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9877d614-d4d9-5a26-be97-67e2394a0c53'}, {'abstract': 'TV listings for Sunday, Aug. 10.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/arts/10tvcol.html', 'snippet': 'TV listings for Sunday, Aug. 10.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (Discovery) AIR JAWS: FINS OF FURY Shark Week 2014, the 27th annual version of this programming sensation, presents 12 new shows, starting with this special, above, in which the filmmaker Jeff Kurr uses high-tech cameras and underwater gadgetry to track down the huge great white known as Colossus. “Shark of Darkness: Wrath of Submarine,” at 9, hunts for a 30-foot great white that locals believe has terrorized the coastline of South Africa for decades. And the actors Jake Johnson and Damon Wayans Jr., the director Robert Rodriguez and the extreme eater Chris Schewe are guests on “Shark After Dark,” a talk show hosted by Jonah Wolf, at 11. Meanwhile, Nat Geo Wild kicks off its second annual SharkFest with “Shark Kill Zone,” which tracks 10 shark species as they hunt for prey, at 8.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-10T12:53:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/47953f0f-82d5-5571-8aa9-00fcdcfdf44a', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47953f0f-82d5-5571-8aa9-00fcdcfdf44a'}, {'abstract': 'My husband and I consider our family progressive. We’re all for boys in pink playing with dolls. But progressive really means letting your children choose what to love, and my son loves football.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/if-my-son-loves-football-can-he-still-love-me/', 'snippet': 'My husband and I consider our family progressive. We’re all for boys in pink playing with dolls. But progressive really means letting your children choose what to love, and my son loves football.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s Thanksgiving and I should be inside watching the parade in my jammies, timing the marshmallow placement on the sweet potato casserole and deciding how soon is too soon for red wine. Instead, I am in 20-degree weather on an elementary school playground strapping flags on fourth graders and their parents. There’s no way I am joining this football game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/30/us/motherlode-pop-warner/motherlode-pop-warner-jumbo.png', 'height': 210, 'width': 325, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/30/us/motherlode-pop-warner/motherlode-pop-warner-superJumbo.png', 'height': 210, 'width': 325, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/30/us/motherlode-pop-warner/motherlode-pop-warner-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_