ce and music premieres. The season also includes a six-month residency, from January through June, by the International Contemporary Ensemble, which will feature new works by Christian Wolff, George Lewis, John Zorn, Cory Smythe and Forrest Pierce.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abrons Announces Theater, Dance and Music Premieres', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Premieres at Abrons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breuer, Lee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dendy, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenspan, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sontag, Susan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Tennessee', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABRONS ARTS CENTER', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Henry Street Settlement', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Contemporary Ensemble', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mabou Mines', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-10T13:27:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0024b71-eac0-5e1f-9f13-70ecf0d549ad', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0024b71-eac0-5e1f-9f13-70ecf0d549ad'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State John Kerry, on the final day of a trip to Myanmar, pushed for further progress in what many perceive to be slowing political and legal overhauls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/world/asia/kerry-citing-bumps-urges-myanmar-to-stay-on-path-to-democracy.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State John Kerry, on the final day of a trip to Myanmar, pushed for further progress in what many perceive to be slowing political and legal overhauls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YANGON, Myanmar — Secretary of State John Kerry called on Myanmar’s leaders on Sunday to move ahead with fundamental reforms amid concerns that the nation is stumbling on its path to democracy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 248, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/11/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 248}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/11/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/world/DIPLO/DIPLO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kerry Urges Myanmar to Stay on Path to Democracy, Despite Stumbles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kerry Urges Myanmar to Stay on Path to Democracy, Despite Stumbles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thein Sein', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-10T13:39:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6782e73d-c1ed-51fd-bcd9-a5c133b7ad65', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6782e73d-c1ed-51fd-bcd9-a5c133b7ad65'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers have developed a mathematical model for happiness, and it suggests that how you feel depends in large part on your anticipation.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/use-this-equation-to-stop-robbing-yourself-of-happiness/', 'snippet': 'Researchers have developed a mathematical model for happiness, and it suggests that how you feel depends in large part on your anticipation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The researchers who developed the above equation call it a “computational model of momentary subjective well-being.” And while it may look and sound complicated to most non-mathematicians, its gist is pretty simple: How happy you are depends in large part on your expectations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/opinion/nyto-happiness/nyto-happiness-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/07/opinion/nyto-happiness/nyto-happiness-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/opinion/nyto-happiness/nyto-happiness-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/opinion/nyto-happiness/nyto-happiness-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/opinion/nyto-happiness/nyto-happiness-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/07/opinion/nyto-happiness/nyto-happiness-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/07/opinion/nyto-happiness/nyto-happiness-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Use This Equation to Stop Robbing Yourself of Happiness', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 's