zation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa01893f-8ba3-5d5e-b537-be5fccf01512', 'word_count': 1276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa01893f-8ba3-5d5e-b537-be5fccf01512'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: An American delegation travels to the World Zionist Congress in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/1939-u-s-zionist-delegation-to-geneva-in-quest-of-solution-to-palestine/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: An American delegation travels to the World Zionist Congress in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To work out a solution to the Palestine problem which will satisfy the Arabs as well as the Jews will be the principal concern of the World Zionist Congress meeting in Geneva on August 18, according to Herman P. Kopplemann, former Congressman for three terms from Connecticut and member of the large American delegation to the meeting in Switzerland. “Outside influences have been creating discords which are unfortunate and unfair to both Arab and Jew in Palestine. We are far from satisfied with the British White Paper, which nullifies the Balfour Declaration, but we are going to do the best in our power to settle the controversy — particularly unfortunate at this time of racial discrimination — in a fair and peaceful way,” said Mr. Kopplemann. Mr. Kopplemann is one of the members of the American delegation which is meeting in Paris before the start of the congress to act as a steering committee for the delegation as a whole, which numbers some thirty-two persons. “We Americans feel that we have done a major part of the work of building up the wastelands and draining the swamps of Palestine, making that land, in fact, one of the most productive parts of the world. We have raised the standard of living there, not only of the Jew but also of the Arab. We feel that the American delegation should therefore participate in the congress to the fullest degree.” — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 11, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/blogs/11iht-oldaug11/11iht-oldaug11-articleLarge.png', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/11/blogs/11iht-oldaug11/11iht-oldaug11-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/blogs/11iht-oldaug11/11iht-oldaug11-jumbo.png', 'height': 639, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/blogs/11iht-oldaug11/11iht-oldaug11-superJumbo.png', 'height': 639, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/blogs/11iht-oldaug11/11iht-oldaug11-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/11/blogs/11iht-oldaug11/11iht-oldaug11-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/blogs/11iht-oldaug11/11iht-oldaug11-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1939: U.S. Zionist Delegation to Geneva in Quest of Solution to Palestine', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arabs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 