url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/ninja-turtles-reboot-tops-weekend-box-office/', 'snippet': '“Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles” took in an estimated $65 million at North American theaters, at least 30 percent more than analysts had projected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A five-year plan to resuscitate one of the quirkier entertainment franchises of the 1980s culminated in impressive form over the weekend, as “Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles” took in an estimated $65 million at North American theaters – at least 30 percent more than box-office analysts had projected. On Sunday, Paramount Pictures announced a sequel. (It must be said: Cowabunga.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Ninja Turtles’ Reboot Tops Weekend Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moviegoers Shell Out $65 Million for ‘Ninja Turtles’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paramount Pictures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-10T17:34:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/816e74ee-c6e8-594b-b7aa-603fd1cbfbc2', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/816e74ee-c6e8-594b-b7aa-603fd1cbfbc2'}, {'abstract': 'The search for extraterrestrial life should start in our own solar system, says Bill Nye, the Science Guy, in a video interview.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/how-to-look-for-alien-life-in-space-geysers/', 'snippet': 'The search for extraterrestrial life should start in our own solar system, says Bill Nye, the Science Guy, in a video interview.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What we at the Planetary Society do is to do our best to explain the space sciences,” says Bill Nye, “the Science Guy,” in an interview with Big Think. “We strongly believe that the search for life is worthy because it would change the world.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Look for Alien Life in Space Geysers', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Europa (Moon of Jupiter)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extraterrestrial Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jupiter (Planet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nye, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-10T18:01:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbe61be1-454c-5dab-810d-04427b91a0bd', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbe61be1-454c-5dab-810d-04427b91a0bd'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Turkey attacks Cyprus despite cease-fire agreement in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/1964-turkish-jets-again-raid-cyprus-despite-truce/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Turkey attacks Cyprus despite cease-fire agreement in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NICOSIA — Turkish fighter planes today [Aug. 10] attacked Cyprus for the fourth consecutive day despite a cease-fire agreement. The strafing attack was made against the northwestern village of Polis, but it was believed to have been launched in error by pilots who had not yet received their cease-fire orders from Ankara. Throughout the rest of the island, the situation eased somewhat when it was learned that Turkish troops had not invaded the island as alleged last night by the Greek Cypriot government. The government had charged that four Turkish destroyers were unloading men and material at Kokkina, the last major stronghold of the Turkish Cypriots on the northwestern coast. But the UN found no evidence to support the allegation. Col. Johnas Waern, commander of the UN Swedish contingent on Cyprus, inspected the area and reported seeing only a ‘‘very small ship’’ offshore which was not unloading anything. There was a brief flareup of shooting in Nicosia tonight, but there were no reports of any casualties. Firing also continued sporadically throughout the day between Greek and Turkish Cypriots in the Kokkina area, according to reliable reports reaching Nicosia tonight. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 11, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Turkish Jets Again Raid Cyprus Despite Truce', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-10T19:40:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a47a809-dfc6-5427-bb65-c08bcc50f64d', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a47a809-dfc6-5427-bb65-c08bcc50f64d'}, {'abstract': 'I even forgive the haircut.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/a-night-in-brooklyn-personal-and-trivial/', 'snippet': 'I even forgive the haircut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That’s San Fermin. Also St. Vincent, not my sort of thing, but clearly excellent of its kind. And free!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Night in Brooklyn (Personal and Trivial)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-10T19:42:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db354451-4bf4-5c27-9368-ee9408c671c1', 'word_count': 19, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db354451-4bf4-5c27-9368-ee9408c671c1'}, {'abstract': 'This is looking pretty bleak.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/10/meanwhile-in-europe-2/', 'snippet': 'This is looking pretty bleak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Japanification is well underway. Not quite deflation yet, but headline at 0.4 percent, core at 0.8 percent. In the U.S. the Fed is, rightly in my view, focused on slow wage growth as an indication of slack; in the euro area annual growth in labor costs is sliding:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meanwhile, in Europe', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-10T19:50:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aafdcbc0-846d-5a73-ae0f-19a9c14ec56a', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aafdcbc0-846d-5a73-ae0f-19a9c14ec56a'}, {'abstract': 'A test batch of small stuffed toys called Tsum Tsum, already a hit in Japan, has sold out in Disney Stores in the United States, and the company wonders if it has found the next Beanie Baby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/business/disney-rushes-to-build-a-tsum-tsum-collecting-craze.html', 'snippet': 'A test batch of small stuffed toys called Tsum Tsum, already a hit in Japan, has sold out in Disney Stores in the United States, and the company wonders if it has found the next Beanie Baby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Has Disney stumbled across the new Beanie Baby?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/business/11BeanieSUB/11BeanieSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/11/business/11BeanieSUB/11BeanieSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/business/11BeanieSUB/11BeanieSUB-jumbo.j