ts of animal exploitation is to draw an analogy between human and animal suffering. Marjorie Spiegel’s “The Dreaded Comparison: Human and Animal Slavery” finds parallels between white oppression of African slaves in America and human exploitation of nonhumans. Spiegel asserts that like human slaves, nonhuman animals are subjected to branding, restraints, beatings, auctions, the separation of offspring from their parents and forced voyages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Enigma of Animal Suffering', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-10T23:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rhys Southan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rhys', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e23beb54-790a-532e-a413-395b807f8d77', 'word_count': 1505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e23beb54-790a-532e-a413-395b807f8d77'}, {'abstract': 'Evidence-based sentencing is unfair and probably unconstitutional.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/opinion/sentencing-by-the-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'Evidence-based sentencing is unfair and probably unconstitutional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANN ARBOR, Mich. — IN a recent letter to the United States Sentencing Commission, Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. sharply criticized the growing trend of evidence-based sentencing, in which courts use data-driven predictions of defendants’ future crime risk to shape sentences. Mr. Holder is swimming against a powerful current. At least 20 states have implemented this practice, including some that require risk scores to be considered in every sentencing decision. Many more are considering it, as is Congress, in pending sentencing-reform bills.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/opinion/0811OPEDmunday/0811OPEDmunday-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 920, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/11/opinion/0811OPEDmunday/0811OPEDmunday-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 920}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/opinion/0811OPEDmunday/0811OPEDmunday-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/opinion/0811OPEDmunday/0811OPEDmunday-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1336, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/opinion/0811OPEDmunday/0811OPEDmunday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/11/opinion/0811OPEDmunday/0811OPEDmunday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/opinion/0811OPEDmunday/0811OPEDmunday-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sentencing, by the Numbers', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sentencing, by the Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': 