_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/994e4c77-8065-5ee3-8f4d-cd7a1b7b603e', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/994e4c77-8065-5ee3-8f4d-cd7a1b7b603e'}, {'abstract': 'It is the vividness of a perceived threat, rather than the threat’s true potency, that plays the bigger role in the potential to spread through social media, researchers find.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/world/ebola-may-pose-little-threat-to-us-but-it-looms-large-on-twitter.html', 'snippet': 'It is the vividness of a perceived threat, rather than the threat’s true potency, that plays the bigger role in the potential to spread through social media, researchers find.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the shadow of the deadly Ebola virus looms over Africa, its danger clear and present, a lesser kind of contagion, diffuse but persistent, has infected social media feeds in the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ebola May Pose Little Threat to U.S., but It Looms Large on Twitter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ebola May Pose Little Threat to U.S., but It Looms Large on Twitter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T00:54:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua A. Krisch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Krisch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d21bb4c1-e0e7-5cef-bd66-40b702f0c4a2', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d21bb4c1-e0e7-5cef-bd66-40b702f0c4a2'}, {'abstract': 'A landmark summit meeting was a splashy event that advertised the continent’s economic potential. But major follow-through is necessary to achieve results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/opinion/president-obama-s-africa-push.html', 'snippet': 'A landmark summit meeting was a splashy event that advertised the continent’s economic potential. But major follow-through is necessary to achieve results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One major purpose of President Obama’s landmark White House summit meeting on Africa last week was to advertise this often underrated continent’s economic potential and ensure it a brighter future. But determined follow-through will be required if the aspirations of the president and more than 40 African heads of state who were his guests are to be realized and Africa is to satisfy its promise as the world’s last big economic frontier.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama’s Africa Push', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Obama’s Africa Push', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T00:55:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a546bf4-eb90-5225-9c3b-eb933d8c01c5', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a546bf4-eb90-5225-9c3b-eb933d8c01c5'}, {'abstract': 'A law that restricts access to abortion — the admitting-privileges requirement — was blocked by a federal judge. His opinion should serve as a model for other courts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/opinion/a-judge-rules-for-alabama-women-on-abortion.html', 'snippet': 'A law that restricts access to abortion — the admitting-privileges requirement — was blocked by a federal judge. His opinion should serve as a model for other courts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In large parts of the country, women’s access to safe and legal abortion care is increasingly coming to depend on the willingness of judges to rigorously examine and reject new (and medically unnecessary) restrictions imposed by Republican legislatures. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Judge Rules for Alabama Women on Abortion', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Judge Rules for Alabama Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T00:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d564dc03-b6d7-5491-a900-2d1c1a3daacf', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d564dc03-b6d7-5491-a900-2d1c1a3daacf'}, {'abstract': 'The virus’s spread is showing how unprepared America and other advanced countries are to help protect and treat thousands of Africans threatened by a disease for which there is no cure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/opinion/controlling-the-ebola-epidemic.html', 'snippet': 'The virus’s spread is showing how unprepared America and other advanced countries are to help protect and treat thousands of Africans threatened by a disease for which there is no cure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, the World Health Organization formally declared an international public health emergency in response to what its director general, Dr. Margaret Chan, called “the largest, most severe, most complex outbreak” of the deadly Ebola virus “in the nearly four-decade history of the disease.” And what has the world done in those 40 years to defend against the disease? Not much. Apart from inflicting a staggering human toll, the spread of the Ebola virus in West Africa has laid bare how unprepared the United States and other advanced countries are to protect and treat thousands of Africans whose lives are threatened by an extremely dangerous virus for which there is no cure.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Controlling the Ebola Epidemic', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Controlling the Ebola Epidemic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T00:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0faf5152-bada-5b94-b1c0-733116679b00', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0faf5152-bada-5b94-b1c0-733116679b00'}, {'abstract': 'The viral media site will use a $50 million investment to diversify its content, expand its video arm and create an in-house incubator for new technology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/technology/a-move-to-go-beyond-lists-for-content-at-buzzfeed.html', 'snippet': 'The viral media site will use a $50 million investment to diversify its content, expand its video arm and create an in-house incubator for new technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are three completely crazy insights about BuzzFeed, the viral content start-up:', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/business/11Buzzfeedjp1/11Buzzfeedjp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/11/business/11Buzzfeedjp1/11Buzzfeedjp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub