}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T10:57:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Vavreck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vavreck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce75fafc-faec-54d6-8145-9d78ba56638a', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce75fafc-faec-54d6-8145-9d78ba56638a'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes medical advances are accomplished not through scientific breakthroughs, but through education and persuasion. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/upshot/lessons-from-the-low-tech-defeat-of-the-guinea-worm-.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes medical advances are accomplished not through scientific breakthroughs, but through education and persuasion. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given all the talk about the hepatitis C drug Sovaldi in recent weeks, as well as the high prices on many other recent innovations, you might think that we’re entering a time when leaps forward happen only at great cost. That misses the point. It also strengthens the false notion that we can move forward only through advances in technology. As I said in another column not long ago, people are more important than technology.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/upshot/12up-worm/12up-worm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/12/upshot/12up-worm/12up-worm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/upshot/12up-worm/12up-worm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/upshot/12up-worm/12up-worm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/upshot/12up-worm/12up-worm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/12/upshot/12up-worm/12up-worm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/upshot/12up-worm/12up-worm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons From the Low-Tech Defeat of the Guinea Worm', 'kicker': 'The New Health Care', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guinea Worm Disease', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preventive Medicine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T10:57:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron E. Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/808cedcf-075a-509b-bbfe-27b57fc59f09', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/808cedcf-075a-509b-bbfe-27b57fc59f09'}, {'abstract': 'The Congressional Budget Office recently estimated that if the federal minimum wage were to rise to $10.10, a total of 16.5 million workers would make more money.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/trying-to-understand-the-impact-of-minimum-wage-hikes-on-small-businesses/', 'snippet': 'The Congressional Budget Office recently estimated that if the federal minimum wage were to rise to $10.10, a total of 16.5 million workers would make more money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Does the battle over the minimum wage pit employees against small-business owners? That was the notion put forth on the Real Clear Politics website recently. In an essay titled “Living the Wage? Try Living the Small Business,” Tom Bevan, a co-founder of the site, ridiculed Democratic politicians who had embarked on an effort to understand how people subsist on minimum wage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Understand the Impact of a Higher Minimum Wage on Small Businesses', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T11:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dab5f80-5936-565e-8e96-90e1ecf59d91', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dab5f80-5936-565e-8e96-90e1ecf59d91'}, {'abstract': 'The Mariinsky Ballet is dancing mixed bills of Balanchine, Fokine, Ashton and Ratmansky -- a chance to see its dancers in varying styles, techniques and aesthetics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/arts/dance/a-taste-of-russian-dance-in-london.html', 'snippet': 'The Mariinsky Ballet is dancing mixed bills of Balanchine, Fokine, Ashton and Ratmansky -- a chance to see its dancers in varying styles, techniques and aesthetics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Russia’s two great ballet companies have been on the road of late. The Bolshoi, based in Moscow, just ended a two-week tour of New York, and the Mariinsky Ballet from St. Petersburg is in the middle of a substantial season here. Despite laments of cultural homogeneity, Russian ballet is clearly still a powerful cultural export with its own audience-luring mystique.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/arts/dance/12iht-mariinsky12/12iht-mariinsky12-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/12/arts/dance/12iht-mariinsky12/12iht-mariinsky12-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/arts/dance/12iht-mariinsky12/12iht-mariinsky12-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/arts/dance/12iht-mariinsky12/12iht-mariinsky12-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit