n wonders what caused the spiraling downward of his friend, Castro, an Afghan soldier. The P.T.S.D.? Or anti-American radicalization?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recent green on blue attack that claimed the life of Gen. Harold J. Greene, the deputy commander for the Combined Security Transition Command–Afghanistan, has, for good reason, caused a fury of questions in the media about these attacks and what they meant. Who are the Afghans that carry them out? Why do they seem to suddenly turn on the Americans that have been fighting with them for years and years, struggling to help Afghanistan build something from the ruins of three decades of war. The answers, it seems, are complex, but also nuanced. And the questions reminded me of the worst case of post-traumatic stress syndrome that I’ve ever seen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Hero to Hateful: Recalling an Afghan Soldier’s Descent', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGER (EMOTION)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greene, Harold J (1959-2014)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T13:05:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'bylin