 'uri': 'nyt://article/94d88808-a7dc-576d-87de-33235caabb64'}, {'abstract': 'Melissa Clark shows how to grill and slice skirt steak, which she first marinates in a mixture of garlic and herbs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/dining/100000003049781/grilled-skirt-steak-with-herbs.html', 'snippet': 'Melissa Clark shows how to grill and slice skirt steak, which she first marinates in a mixture of garlic and herbs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Melissa Clark shows how to grill and slice skirt steak, which she first marinates in a mixture of garlic and herbs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/multimedia/clark-skirt-steak/clark-skirt-steak-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/05/multimedia/clark-skirt-steak/clark-skirt-steak-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/multimedia/clark-skirt-steak/clark-skirt-steak-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/multimedia/clark-skirt-steak/clark-skirt-steak-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/multimedia/clark-skirt-steak/clark-skirt-steak-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/05/multimedia/clark-skirt-steak/clark-skirt-steak-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/05/multimedia/clark-skirt-steak/clark-skirt-steak-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grilled Skirt Steak With Herbs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T17:12:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'Jenny Woodward', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woodward', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/ad2f14a3-be75-51f6-935d-2c0dafd7c3aa', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/ad2f14a3-be75-51f6-935d-2c0dafd7c3aa'}, {'abstract': 'Skirt steak defies its awkward appearance to become a go-to for throwing on the grill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/dining/skirt-steak-works-great-for-grilling.html', 'snippet': 'Skirt steak defies its awkward appearance to become a go-to for throwing on the grill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Skirt steak isn’t winning any beauty pageants. It’s a long, lanky, awkward contender for your grill. You won’t be able to give it those pronounced crosshatched grill lines, and its flat shape gives you thin, squiggly slices rather than nice, wide planks. If you want pretty and iconic, splurge on a rib or strip steak.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Skirt Steak Works Great for Grilling', 'kicker': 'A Good Appetite', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '... But It Has a Nice Personality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-11T17:16:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56e93ab1-993f-5ab1-8638-538121efe71e', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56e93ab1-993f-5ab1-8638-538121efe71e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Swanson’s new book, “Blood Aces,” tells the story of the Dallas crime boss who moved to Vegas and started the World Series of Poker.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/an-unusual-gangster-doug-j-swanson-talks-about-benny-binion/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Swanson’s new book, “Blood Aces,” tells the story of the Dallas crime boss who moved to Vegas and started the World Series of Poker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doug J. Swanson’s “Blood Aces” documents the colorful, violent life of Benny Binion, the gangster who made his bones in Depression-era Dallas before moving to Las Vegas (with the law in hot pursuit). In the desert, he opened the Horseshoe casino and introduced the World Series of Poker. The book also tells the story of Binion’s rivals, like Herbert Noble, nicknamed the Cat because he survived 11 attempts on his life — but alas, not the 12th. In a recent email interview, Mr. Swanson discussed Binion’s penchant for danger, the difficulties in researching his life and more. Below are edited excerpts from the conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/books/11swanson/11swanson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'wid