ospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/1964-paris-studying-les-halles-area/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Parisians debated plans to rebuild Les Halles in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The Paris Municipal Council said today [Aug. 11] that it has appropriated $300,000 to study what to do with the tradition-cloaked Les Halles market area once the market moves out two years hence. The cramped wholesale food market, which has tied up traffic near the center of the city for years, will be replaced by a new complex in the suburban town of Rungis. One of the most controversial plans for the Halles area would raze completely a 750-acre slice of land. Out of the rubble a business center would rise with Paris’s first real skyscrapers. The war against a “Brasilia-on-the-Seine” has been mounting in the Paris press. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, August 12, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-halles/12iht-oldaug12-halles-articleLarge.png', 'height': 282, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-halles/12iht-oldaug12-halles-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 282}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-halles/12iht-oldaug12-halles-jumbo.png', 'height': 481, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/blogs/12iht-oldaug12-halles/12iht-oldaug12-halles-superJumbo.png', 'height': 962, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i