er limited partnerships still make sense for other companies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/11/kinder-morgans-reorganization-puts-master-limited-partnerships-in-question/', 'snippet': 'With Kinder Morgan restructuring, some are asking whether master limited partnerships still make sense for other companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What happens when the pioneer of an industry abandons its own legacy?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kinder Morgan’s Reorganization Puts Master Limited Partnerships in Question', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restructuring Puts a Popular Type of Partnership in Question', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kinder Morgan Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T01:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gelles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fde912e-6da6-510d-8536-dd0633a411ac', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fde912e-6da6-510d-8536-dd0633a411ac'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of political bullying, Governor Cuomo should welcome a primary challenge from Zephyr Teachout and give New York State voters a choice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/opinion/gov-cuomo-should-welcome-zephyr-teachout.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of political bullying, Governor Cuomo should welcome a primary challenge from Zephyr Teachout and give New York State voters a choice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York State voters rarely have enough real choice on their ballots, and Gov. Andrew Cuomo seems determined to keep it that way. Ever since another Democratic candidate for governor, Zephyr Teachout, arose on his left, Mr. Cuomo has tried to throw her off the primary ballot on the shaky grounds that she hasn’t met the state’s five-year residency requirement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Teachout Moment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Teachout Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teachout, Zephyr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Edgar G', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T01:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/442fe5f5-8dbd-5837-b66e-b187469b882c', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/442fe5f5-8dbd-5837-b66e-b187469b882c'}, {'abstract': 'More than a dozen states have expanded democracy, but voter ID laws and other restrictions continue to pop up all over the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/opinion/where-voting-is-now-easier.html', 'snippet': 'More than a dozen states have expanded democracy, but voter ID laws and other restrictions continue to pop up all over the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a time when many states are making it harder to vote, 16 states have provided some good news over the last year by deciding to go in the opposite direction. In various ways, they have expanded access to the polls, allowing more people to register or to vote more conveniently. The list, compiled by the Brennan Center for Justice, includes these states:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Voting Is Now Easier', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Voting Is Now Easier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brennan Center for Justice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T01:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9655a5a4-64ea-520f-a983-3e9bf7cc33d9', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9655a5a4-64ea-520f-a983-3e9bf7cc33d9'}, {'abstract': 'More than 60 people have died from the virus in a tiny village in Sierra Leone, and now people there worry that a quarantine will cut off their food and supplies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/world/africa/at-heart-of-ebola-outbreak-a-village-frozen-by-fear-and-death.html', 'snippet': 'More than 60 people have died from the virus in a tiny village in Sierra Leone, and now people there worry that a quarantine will cut off their food and supplies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NJALA NGIEMA, Sierra Leone — The signs of a deadly struggle remain: Scattered around the houses of the Ebola dead lie empty pill packages, their plastic casings punched through. Nearby in the mud are used packets of oral rehydration salts. The pills did not work, and the hurried trip to the hospital, if there was one, came too late.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Heart of Ebola Outbreak, a Village Frozen by Fear and Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Heart of Ebola Outbreak, a Village Frozen by Fear and Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T01:16:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df1efbde-88b3-5184-9ed2-0a7129c96a49', 'word_count': 1364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df1efbde-88b3-5184-9ed2-0a7129c96a49'}, {'abstract': 'The opera and its unions will resume negotiations this week, and must come to an agreement by Sunday night to avert a looming lockout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/nyregion/new-deadline-set-for-the-metropolitan-operas-labor-talks.html', 'snippet': 'The opera and its unions will resume negotiations this week, and must come to an agreement by Sunday night to avert a looming lockout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Opera, which has been threatening to lock out its workers if they do not agree to concessions, has set a new deadline for reaching an agreement with its unions: Sunday night, a little more than a month before the opera season is set to open.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Deadline Set for the Metropolitan Opera’s Labor Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Deadline Set for the Met’s Labor Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF MUSICIANS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN GUILD OF MUSICAL ARTISTS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T01:18:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7d313d2-4be5-5f03-a802-a4124fa2f690', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7d313d2-4be5-5f03-a802-a4124fa2f690'}, {'abstract': 'With a potential constitutional crisis and military coup being added to the danger already posed by jihadists, Iraq is desperate for a unifying hand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/opinion/iraq-needs-a-new-prime-minister.html', 'snippet': 'With a potential constitutional crisis and military coup being added to the danger already posed by jihadists, Iraq is desperate for a unifying hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nuri Kamal al-Maliki emerged from relative obscurity in 2006 when he was elected prime minister of the first government in Iraq formed after a period of caretaker rule. The best service he could perform now for his country would be to return to that obscurity as soon and as peacefully as possible.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq Needs a New Prime Minister', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq Needs a New Prime Minister', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abadi, Haider al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Massoum, Fouad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T01:21:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 's