in response to the weekend shooting of Michael Brown, was captured on social media as police officers used tear gas and rubber bullets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/us/protests-near-st-louis-seen-on-social-media.html', 'snippet': 'A chaotic night in Ferguson, Mo., in response to the weekend shooting of Michael Brown, was captured on social media as police officers used tear gas and rubber bullets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday night, protests continued in Ferguson, Mo., a St. Louis suburb, in response to the weekend shooting of Michael Brown, 18, who was killed by a police officer. The chaotic night was captured on social media as police officers used tear gas and rubber bullets to try to disperse the crowds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protests Near St. Louis, Seen on Social Media', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T04:52:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/001bf238-7b72-5167-90da-1a8dcc5b6c98', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/001bf238-7b72-5167-90da-1a8dcc5b6c98'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (HBO Signature) ROCK OF AGES (2012) Tom Cruise, above, bares his torso to play Stacee Jaxx, an Axl Rose-like rocker, and Catherine Zeta-Jones is the neo-puritanical Patricia Whitmore, who has vowed to clean up the Sunset Strip to get her husband (Bryan Cranston) elected mayor of Los Angeles, in this jukebox musical turned big-screen attraction, directed by Adam Shankman. Diego Boneta and Julianne Hough are impressionable youths who dream of making it big in 1987 Hollywood. And Alec Baldwin and Russell Brand play a nightclub impresario and his sidekick. “They make their stale buddy routine and romance amusing and, as with the rest of the adults, make the movie bearable,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “A whispering and writhing Mr. Cruise makes it watchable.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/06d4e733-9994-55b8-bcaa-3e802eac3dbb', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06d4e733-9994-55b8-bcaa-3e802eac3dbb'}, {'abstract': 'A gift horse or a Trojan horse? That about summed up the latest, almost farcical encounter between Moscow and Kiev.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/world/europe/russian-convoy-leaves-moscow-for-ukraine-bearing-aid.html', 'snippet': 'A gift horse or a Trojan horse? That about summed up the latest, almost farcical encounter betwe