e': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T08:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbfa4d16-5d7b-5311-b350-023d5da45efe', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbfa4d16-5d7b-5311-b350-023d5da45efe'}, {'abstract': 'A leak from a Georgia Senate campaign reminds us just how broken our political system is.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/magazine/memo-to-self-do-not-run-for-office.html', 'snippet': 'A leak from a Georgia Senate campaign reminds us just how broken our political system is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, Eliana Johnson of National Review gained access to a 144-page memo that was prepared by a team of political strategists working for the senate campaign of Michelle Nunn, the Georgia Democrat. Nunn, the daughter of Sam Nunn, the state’s longtime senator, is running against David Perdue, a Republican, to succeed Saxby Chambliss, who is retiring. While I am obviously not smart enough to be a “political strategist” — otherwise I would be paid more — it strikes me as advisable to keep a document like this under wraps, especially when it is so brutally self-critical in places (saying, among other things, that voters might dismiss Michelle Nunn as being a “lightweight,” “too liberal” and “not a ‘real’ Georgian”). Already the document has become fodder for Twitter ridicule and at least one attack ad.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17politics/mag-17Politics-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17politics/mag-17Politics-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17politics/mag-17Politics-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17politics/mag-17Politics-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1290, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17politics/mag-17Politics-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17politics/mag-17Politics-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17politics/mag-17Politics-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Memo to Self: Do Not Run for Office', 'kicker': 'Your Fellow Americans', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Memo to Self: Do Not Run for Office', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leibovich, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nunn, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Leibovich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leibovich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1531e938-d17a-5877-9179-677181cbc97c', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1531e938-d17a-5877-9179-677181cbc97c'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Ferguson has been covering the refugee crisis in northern Iraq, where a persecuted minority has been trapped on a mountaintop.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/a-mountain-of-uncertainty-in-iraq/', 'snippet': 'Adam Ferguson has been covering the refugee crisis in northern Iraq, where a persecuted minority has been trapped on a mountaintop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last four days, Adam Ferguson has photographed members of Iraq’s Yazidi minority religious group who had been surrounded on a mountaintop without water or food as a result of battlefield advances made by Sunni militants. As the refugee crisis continues, some have been able to escape into Syria this weekend. Mr. Ferguson, 35, freelances extensively for The New York Times as well as for National Geographic and Time magazine, and he spoke to James Estrin on Monday morning by phone from northern Iraq. Their conversation has been edited. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/blogs/20140811-lens-ferguson-slide-XLF1/20140811-lens-ferguson-slide-XLF1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/1