r.” We have dropped a word in each paragraph. Can you choose the best word for each blank?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Below, the first six paragraphs of “Inside Man’s Best Friend, Study Says, May Lurk a Green-Eyed Monster.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/science/24dogs-LN/24dogs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/24/science/24dogs-LN/24dogs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/science/24dogs-LN/24dogs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/science/24dogs-LN/24dogs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 919, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/science/24dogs-LN/24dogs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/07/24/science/24dogs-LN/24dogs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/science/24dogs-LN/24dogs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Dogs and Jealousy', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T10:26:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec8f10f2-5d69-58a8-bba4-75dcc5716ca1', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec8f10f2-5d69-58a8-bba4-75dcc5716ca1'}, {'abstract': 'Opinions on a leadership crisis in Iraq, abuse of Rikers juveniles, an anti-marijuana campaign for teenagers in Colorado and Turkey’s new president.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/morning-views-56/', 'snippet': 'Opinions on a leadership crisis in Iraq, abuse of Rikers juveniles, an anti-marijuana campaign for teenagers in Colorado and Turkey’s new president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki of\xa0Iraq\xa0“emerged from relative obscurity” in 2006, a New York Times editorial begins. “The best service he could perform now for his country would be to return to that obscurity as soon and as peacefully as possible.” The country is in “mortal danger” from Islamist militants and “needs a unifying hand at the helm,” which Mr. Maliki “emphatically” is not. “He bears heavy responsibility for the current crisis by alienating Sunni, Kurdish and other minority groups and undermining the Army and other national institutions through cronyism and corruption.”\xa0Iraq’s president named a more universally accepted candidate Monday, but Mr. Maliki refused to resign.\xa0“Adding a constitutional crisis and a potential military coup to the great danger already posed by the jihadists is madness,” the editorial board writes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T10:41:51+0000', 'docume