e to talk about your business, but there may also be questions about your personal life, your opinions about the government, and your overall experience in China. You may eve...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Radio shows, TV appearances and print interviews are all part of a chief executive’s job, whether in China or the United States. But journalists work very differently in China, where editors typically give them a list of questions to ask — and very little leeway to go “off script.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dealing With the Press in China: Be Prepared to Sing!', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Translation and Interpreters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T11:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Weidenhamer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weidenhamer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d50be081-98c8-5ded-b612-40641cebc2f0', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d50be081-98c8-5ded-b612-40641cebc2f0'}, {'abstract': 'Marc-André Dalbavie’s “Charlotte Salomon,” which had its premiere at the Salzburg Festival, is a reminder that beautiful, thoughtful music does not equal an opera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/arts/music/salzburg-festivals-charlotte-salomon-falls-short-on-drama.html', 'snippet': 'Marc-André Dalbavie’s “Charlotte Salomon,” which had its premiere at the Salzburg Festival, is a reminder that beautiful, thoughtful music does not equal an opera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALZBURG, Austria — Marc-André Dalbavie has long been a master of haze. “Seuils” (“Thresholds”), which this French composer wrote in 1991, the year he turned 30, opens with a ghostly, enveloping shimmer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/music/13dalbavieC/13dalbavieC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/music/13dalbavieC/13dalbavieC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/music/13dalbavieC/13dalbavieC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/music/13dalbavieC/13dalbavieC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1272, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/music/13dalbavieC/13dalbavieC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/music/13dalbavieC/13dalbavieC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/music/13dalbavieC/13dalbavieC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Salzburg Festival’s