 that transports much of America’s oil and natural gas, announced on Sunday that it was abandoning the master limited partnership it helped popularize, questions emerged about what would happen to the many other such structures, DealBook’s David Gelles writes. Largely because of Kinder Morgan’s success, the partnerships have become increasingly popular for energy companies. The structure allows them to pass all profits along to their investors as dividends and pay no corporate taxes, though the investors are subject to taxes on the distributions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Uncertainty Over Master Limited Partnerships', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T11:35:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59403e9f-a8cb-5319-90fe-4b5bae1009da', 'word_count': 1782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59403e9f-a8cb-5319-90fe-4b5bae1009da'}, {'abstract': 'An extra-large grab bag of grammar, style and other missteps, compiled — as always — with help from colleagues and readers.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/in-a-word-3/', 'snippet': 'An extra-large grab bag of grammar, style and other missteps, compiled — as always — with help from colleagues and readers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s an extra-large grab bag of grammar, style and other missteps, compiled with help from colleagues and readers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Word', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T12:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f9bdc5b-4c97-5511-971a-abe8f6fa54f9', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f9bdc5b-4c97-5511-971a-abe8f6fa54f9'}, {'abstract': 'The actor sings and plays the banjo on the number “Bring Him Home.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/in-performance-ramin-karimloo-of-les-miserables/', 'snippet': 'The actor sings and plays the banjo on the number “Bring Him Home.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, as several theater critics of The New York Times revisit some long-running Broadway shows, our In Performance video is from the new Broadway revival of the musical “Les Misérables,” a show that originally opened on Broadway in 1987 and ran for over 16 years. The video features the number “Bring Him Home” sung by the actor Ramin Karimloo on banjo, with Sergio Ortega on guitar. Mr. Karimloo, in his Broadway debut, was nominated for a Tony Award for his performance as Jean Valjean. The show is at the Imperial Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Performance: Ramin Karimloo of ‘Les Misérables’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karimloo, Ramin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T12:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ad43cb5-e51a-539f-93ae-7d40935cf383', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ad43cb5-e51a-539f-93ae-7d40935cf383'}, {'abstract': 'Former Maj. Gen. Jovito Palparan, who spent nearly three years as a fugitive, was wanted in connection with the disappearance of two students in 2006.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/world/asia/philippine-ex-general-wanted-in-activists-disappearance-is-arrested.html', 'snippet': 'Former Maj. Gen. Jovito Palparan, who spent nearly three years as a fugitive, was wanted in connection with the disappearance of two students in 2006.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANILA — The Philippine military on Tuesday captured a former army general wanted in connection with the disappearance of two students in 2006, a case that human rights groups say has come to symbolize the country’s legacy of abductions and abuses of leftist activists by members of the security forces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/world/asia/13PHILIPPINES1/13PHILIPPINES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/12/world/asia/13PHILIPPINES1/13PHILIPPINES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/world/asia/13PHILIPPINES1/13PHILIPPINES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/world/asia/13PHILIPPINES1/13PHILIPPINES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1