a0Tuesday\xa0evening performance on “The Tonight Show” – so will the band. Mr. Followill’s ribs were broken in a traffic accident on Saturday night, when the band’s tour bus stopped suddenly to avoid hitting a pedestrian. The group canceled its\xa0Sunday\xa0evening show in Saratoga Springs, N.Y., and posted a message about the accident\xa0on its Facebook page, but held off on announcing further cancellations until Mr. Followill’s doctors weighed in. On Monday, they did.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drummer’s Injury Sidelines Kings of Leon', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drummer’s Injury Sidelines Kings of Leon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fallon, Jimmy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Followill, Nathan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Ahmir (Questlove)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kings of Leon (Music Group)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wantagh (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T13:34:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efe4433b-ee3f-5c75-ba75-5825aa4bf697', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efe4433b-ee3f-5c75-ba75-5825aa4bf697'}, {'abstract': 'A Times article on Rick Perlstein’s Reagan book draws criticism for amplifying an accusation unfairly.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/was-an-accusation-of-plagiarism-really-a-political-attack/', 'snippet': 'A Times article on Rick Perlstein’s Reagan book draws criticism for amplifying an accusation unfairly.', 'lead_paragraph': ' There aren’t too many worse things you can suggest about an author than that his or her work is plagiarized. It’s the book-world equivalent of spreading the word that a financial adviser has cooked the books or that the parish priest has designs on the altar boys. By its nature, even the suggestion is tarnishing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was an Accusation of Plagiarism Really a Political Attack?', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plagiarism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perlstein, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shirley, Craig (1956- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toobin, Jeffrey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Invisible Bridge: The Fall of Nixon and the Rise of Reagan (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T13:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e86da855-2e08-50d9-affb-00a06e0e2d45', 'word_count': 1112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e86da855-2e08-50d9-affb-00a06e0e2d45'}, {'abstract': 'For Robin Williams, television was his start and, in some ways, perfect for his talents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/arts/television/on-tv-a-super-sized-performer-breaking-out-of-a-small-box.html', 'snippet': 'For Robin Williams, television was his start and, in some ways, perfect for his talents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1978, when “Saturday Night Live” still had almost all of its original cast, and prime time offered “All in The Family,” “M*A*S*H,” “WKRP in Cincinnati,” “Taxi” and “Rhoda,” there didn’t seem to be any room — or need — for something fresh and different on television.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/13williams-tv/13williams-tv-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/13williams-tv/13williams-tv-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/13williams-tv/13williams-tv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/13williams-tv/13williams-tv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/13williams-tv/13williams-tv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/13williams-tv/13williams-tv-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/arts/13williams-tv/13williams-tv-thum