713b'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The creator of James Bond, Ian Fleming, dies in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/1964-creator-of-james-bond-dies/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The creator of James Bond, Ian Fleming, dies in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': ' CANTERBURY, England — Ian Fleming, 58, creator of the James Bond novels, died today [Aug. 12] following a heart attack. Mr. Fleming, a World War II naval intelligence commander, often was identified by Bond fans with the fictional hero. But the dapper former newspaperman scoffed at the idea, although some of those who served under him during World War II speculated that several of his exploits still might be cloaked by official secrecy. Mr. Fleming had been on vacation at Sandwich Bay, Kent, with his wife and son when he was taken ill suddenly last night, a friend of the family said. He died about 2:30 a.m. in Canterbury Hospital. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 13, 1964', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-fleming/13iht-oldaug13-fleming-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-fleming/13iht-oldaug13-fleming-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 603}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-fleming/13iht-oldaug13-fleming-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-fleming/13iht-oldaug13-fleming-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-fleming/13iht-oldaug13-fleming-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-fleming/13iht-oldaug13-fleming-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/blogs/13iht-oldaug13-fleming/13iht-oldaug13-fleming-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Creator of James Bond Dies', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bond, James (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleming, Ian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T15:21:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ae54d9-ec91-55bb-9612-8ecfe5d9f0ad', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ae54d9-ec91-55bb-9612-8ecfe5d9f0ad'}, {'abstract': 'Capturing a shark breaching at night required a long-term commitment from the photographer.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/michael-muller-on-the-shark-photograph-that-took-one-year-to-get/', 'snippet': 'Capturing a shark breaching at night required a long-term commitment from the photographer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a photographer who specializes in celebrity portraiture, Michael Muller has photographed some of the most famous people in the world, including Manny Pacquiao, Joaquin Phoenix and Rihanna. But one subject proved particularly elusive: a great white shark breaching at night. After a failed first try, Muller finally got his shot one year later when he returned to False Bay, South Africa. The resulting photograph ran in the Aug. 10 magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/magazine/Shark1/Shark1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/11/magazine/Shark1/Shark1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/magazine/Shark1/Shark1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/magazine/Shark1/Shark1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/magazine/Shark1/Shark1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/11/magazine/Shark1/Shark1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/1