4/08/12/robin-williams-r-i-p/', 'snippet': 'Notes on a great comedian’s dramatic range.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Philip Seymour Hoffman died untimely earlier this year, my post on his legacy noted that he began to make his move as an actor – to make small roles big, to show that he deserved bigger chances still – around the time that I started to really pay attention to the movies, as a teenager in the late 1990s. So even if (like many people) I fully appreciated his place in the pantheon only after his death, there was never really a time when I didn’t associate Hoffman with great acting, and that greatness with the moviegoing experience writ large.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Robin Williams, R.I.P.', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrey, Jim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanks, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Philip Seymour', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Bill', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandler, Adam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Robin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T16:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/049d7da0-dee3-5dd8-949c-19cc537486a5', 'word_count