officer involved in the fatal shooting of an unarmed African-American teenager and would not do so because of concerns about the officer’s safety.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri Police Cite Threats in Deciding Not to Name Officer Who Shot Teenager', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Police Cite Threats in Deciding Not to Name Officer Who Shot Missouri Teenager', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Timothy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T18:19:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman and Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/954a5254-2687-5869-9e18-c958ec59c8bb', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/954a5254-2687-5869-9e18-c958ec59c8bb'}, {'abstract': 'After a spirited campaign that had him traveling round the world, Garry Kasparov lost his bid to become the president of the international chess federation.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/did-kasparovs-outspoken-nature-cost-him-the-election/', 'snippet': 'After a spirited campaign that had him traveling round the world, Garry Kasparov lost his bid to become the president of the international chess federation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a spirited campaign in which he traveled around the world,\xa0Garry Kasparov on Monday lost his bid to become the president of the international chess federation, bested by the eccentric incumbent, Kirsan Ilyumzhinov, who has held the office since 1995. The race turned into a cold-war-like struggle over the future of chess and of Vladimir Putin’s Russia, and in the end it was not as close as Kasparov and his supporters expected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/magazine/Kasparov1/Kasparov1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/12/magazine/Kasparov1/Kasparov1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/magazine/Kasparov1/Kasparov1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/magazine/Kasparov1/Kasparov1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/magazine/Kasparov1/Kasparov1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail',