'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Paynter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paynter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fd89ab1-27fc-5e9d-b090-0bf9c2d072fb', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fd89ab1-27fc-5e9d-b090-0bf9c2d072fb'}, {'abstract': 'The Smithsonian Institution is allowing members of the public to help decipher thousands of digitized pages that cannot be easily read by a computer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/smithsonian-turning-to-the-public-to-help-transcribe-documents/', 'snippet': 'The Smithsonian Institution is allowing members of the public to help decipher thousands of digitized pages that cannot be easily read by a computer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Smithsonian Institution has followed the crowdsourcing crowd, with the opening of an online transcription center allowing members of the public to help decipher thousands of digitized pages of Civil War diaries, botanical labels, correspondence and other documents that cannot be easily read by a computer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smithsonian Turning to the Public to Help Transcribe Documents', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smithsonian Asks Public for Transcription Help', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdsourcing (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian Institution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T19:28:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3cba986-6d8f-5c6f-a473-cdbdf72b74e7', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3cba986-6d8f-5c6f-a473-cdbdf72b74e7'}, {'abstract': 'This dish combines a recipe learned in Provençe with a recipe from Spain. The escabeche highlights sardines and saffron.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/health/sardines-in-vinegar-escabeche.html', 'snippet': 'This dish combines a recipe learned in Provençe with a recipe from Spain. The escabeche highlights sardines and saffron.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have eaten wonderful sardines in escabeche in Spain and in Provençe, where I first learned to make the dish from Lulu Peyraud, the doyenne of the famous winery Domaine Tempier in Bandol. She used to serve the sardines at the amazing lunches she made every day for the workers during the harvest. I am combining ingredients from Provençal and Spanish recipes, as I love the saffron in the Spanish version.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/science/14recipehealth/14recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/13/science/14recipehealth/14recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/science/14recipehealth/14recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/science/14recipehealt