ered attacks by Lyft with some of its own, including an implication that Lyft is airing accusations because Uber will not buy the company.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/accusations-fly-between-uber-and-lyft/', 'snippet': 'Uber has countered attacks by Lyft with some of its own, including an implication that Lyft is airing accusations because Uber will not buy the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | All is fair, they say, in love and war. And Uber and Lyft, two smartphone-based car services, are most certainly at war. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/business/12bits-lyft/12bits-lyft-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/12/business/12bits-lyft/12bits-lyft-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/business/12bits-lyft/12bits-lyft-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/business/12bits-lyft/12bits-lyft-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/business/12bits-lyft/12bits-lyft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/12/business/12bits-lyft/12bits-lyft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/business/12bits-lyft/12bits-lyft-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Accusations Fly Between Uber and Lyft', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lyft Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T19:36:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Isaac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isaac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab103004-96ff-520a-9acf-508f9e63c8ac', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab103004-96ff-520a-9acf-508f9e63c8ac'}, {'abstract': 'When not intervening threatens greater instability than intervention.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/iraq-and-the-risks-of-inaction/', 'snippet': 'When not intervening threatens greater instability than intervention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having used my Sunday column to make what you might call the war-skeptic’s case for our ongoing intervention against ISIS in northern Iraq, let me address the arguments from a writer more skeptical of military intervention than myself, Noah Millman of The American Conservative, who wrote late last week in opposition to the course the administration is taking:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq and the Risks of Inaction', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Erbil (Iraq)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T19:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c572609-26bb-569b-84b0-22be1e8022e6', 'word_count': 1363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c572609-26bb-569b-84b0-22be1e8022e6'}, {'abstract': 'The cuisine of the state of Veracruz in Mexico has much in common with Spain’s, including this spicy cousin of the Spanish escabeche. The dish calls for a mild vinegar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/health/veracruzana-vinegar-bathed-shrimp.html', 'snippet': 'The cuisine of the state of Veracruz in Mexico has much in common with Spain’s, including this spicy cousin of the Spanish escabeche. The dish calls for a mild vinegar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state of Veracruz in Mexico is home to many wonderful fish dishes. It’s also a region where olive oil is used, a legacy of its once close trade ties to Spain. Many of the signature dishes of this region have much in common with Spanish cooking, with a widespread use of olives, capers and almonds, and indeed, this is a spicy cousin of Spanish escabeche. Vinegar is widely used in Veracruz, but it is a milder vinegar than our wine vinegars. The vinegar traditionally used in this dish is pineapple vinegar, something I saw being sold in fruit stands all over the state of Veracruz when I traveled there. I use rice vinegar instead, because it’s mild like the pineapple vinegar. If you want a smoky, spicy flavor, use chipotles. Either choice is typical of the region.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/13/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/13/science/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i