alestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T19:49:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/166bc1d5-ce21-5647-9162-6d193f993a44', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/166bc1d5-ce21-5647-9162-6d193f993a44'}, {'abstract': 'More than a dozen reporters, editors and producers moved quickly to post the unexpected obituary on the web and to prepare it for the print edition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/08/12/robin-williamss-death-a-note-from-the-night-desk/', 'snippet': 'More than a dozen reporters, editors and producers moved quickly to post the unexpected obituary on the web and to prepare it for the print edition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first report of Robin Williams’s death was at 6:54 p.m. Eastern time. Twenty-four minutes later, The Times posted its first article. A Times news team — including more than a dozen reporters, the Obituary, National and Metro desks and video producers — was quickly in gear reporting the obituary and related stories that ran in today’s paper. The night note from Tom Jolly, the assistant managing editor, to staff editors provides an inside look at how the unexpected obituary came together. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/insider-williams/insider-williams-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/insider-williams/insider-williams-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/insider-williams/insider-williams-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/insider-williams/insider-williams-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/insider-williams/WILLIAMSOBIT-slide-GQB5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/insider-williams/WILLIAMSOBIT-slide-GQB5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/11/arts/artsspecial/insider-williams/WILLIAMSOBIT-slide-GQB5-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robin Williams’s Death: A Note From the Night Desk', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-12T19:56:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99f833d5-ae21-5d11-b0c9-865e52be59fa', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99f833d5-ae21-5d11-b0c9-865e52be59fa'}, {'abstract': 'A large new study suggests that doctors should take abnormal heart rhythms known as atrial fibrillation, or A-fib, that arise after surgery more seriously.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/12/a-new-surgery-risk/', 'snippet': 'A large new study suggests that doctors should take abnormal heart rhythms known as atrial fibrillation, or A-fib, that arise after surgery more seriously.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thousands of Americans every year develop an abnormal heart rhythm after having major surgery. These episodes have long been considered a fleeting phenomenon that is generally not a cause for concern.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/23/health/well_heart/well_heart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/10/23/health/well_heart/well_heart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/23/health/well_heart/well_heart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 780, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/23/health/well_heart/well_heart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 780, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/23/health/well_heart/well_heart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/10/23/health/well_heart/well_heart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/23/health/well_heart/we