artners, that allegedly lost $140 million of investors’ principal. Prosecutors said the former associate dean, Gabriel Bitran, 69, and his son Marco, 39, a money manager with degrees from M.I.T. and Harvard, falsely told clients they would invest their money using a mathematical model based on the elder Mr. Bitran’s research at M.I.T. that had earned returns between 16 percent and 23 percent, and later lied to investigators seeking to verify their claims. If their pleas are accepted, the Bitrans will each face between two and five years in prison. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Former Associate Dean to Plead Guilty in Case on Investments', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Former Associate Dean to Plead Guilty in Case on Investments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sloan School of Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bitran, Gabriel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bitran, Marco', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T00:41:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3379ae02-2fdf-54ca-b01b-5c3bc91b7edc', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3379ae02-2fdf-54ca-b01b-5c3bc91b7edc'}, {'abstract': 'Despite modest investments and a few visible improvements, American passenger trains still lag behind other nations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/opinion/making-the-case-for-high-speed-rail.html', 'snippet': 'Despite modest investments and a few visible improvements, American passenger trains still lag behind other nations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most American passenger trains, including Amtrak’s popular Acela service, run at speeds that are far slower than the superfast European and Japanese trains that can zip along at 200 miles per hour or more. The main reason is that, despite modest investments, American lawmakers have not given high-speed rail the priority it deserves. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the Case for High-Speed Rail', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making the Case for High-Speed Rail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Speed Rail Projects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMTRAK', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T00:42:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/384cc69b-70a9-58c1-be6a-913fd5295a18', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/384cc69b-70a9-58c1-be6a-913fd5295a18'}, {'abstract': 'A development plan for Brooklyn Bridge Park has set off a fierce debate, but the city’s need for affordable housing should be a priority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/opinion/battle-on-the-brooklyn-waterfront.html', 'snippet': 'A development plan for Brooklyn Bridge Park has set off a fierce debate, but the city’s need for affordable housing should be a priority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would not be New York if a disagreement involving two of its most precious things — green space and housing — did not end up as a ferocious debate, with fiery public meetings, petition drives, accusations of elitism and racism and the specter of doom for The City as We Know It. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Battle on the Brooklyn Waterfront', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Battle on the Brooklyn Waterfront', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bridge Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bridge Park Development Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T00:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fa78f8d-3a45-5fee-8981-56b4c8c7c822', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fa78f8d-3a45-5fee-8981-56b4c8c7c822'}, {'abstract': 'A police shooting in a St. Louis suburb is a reminder of a toxic racial legacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/opinion/racial-history-behind-the-ferguson-protests.html', 'snippet': 'A police shooting in a St. Louis suburb is a reminder of a toxic racial legacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The F.B.I. may be able to answer the many questions surrounding the death of Michael Brown, an 18-year-old black student from Ferguson, Mo., who was a few days from heading off to college when he was shot by a police officer on Saturday. The shooting of Mr. Brown, who was unarmed, led to three days of protest, some of it violent, and several tense confrontations between residents of the St. Louis suburban town of 21,000 and the police.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Death of Michael Brown', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Death of Michael Brown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Segregation