t://video/b48f600e-488c-5f5b-af74-6204bc4f7cef'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/arts/television/whats-on-tv-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:45 P.M. (HBO2) ARGO (2012) Ben Affleck, above, directed and stars in this Oscar winner for best film, which covers a little-known chapter of the Iranian hostage crisis, in which Antonio J. Mendez, a Central Intelligence Agency officer and a wizard of disguise, was tapped to help free six State Department employees stranded in Tehran after revolutionary forces seized the United States Embassy on Nov. 4, 1979. His plan: to have them pose as a Canadian movie crew filming a science-fiction flick called “Argo.” John Goodman and Alan Arkin play the Hollywood makeup artist and producer who help him. Bryan Cranston, his neck tendons popping, is one of his bosses; and Clea DuVall, Tate Donovan, Scoot McNairy, Rory Cochrane, Christopher Denham and Kerry Bishé are the escapees. After setting your pulse racing, Mr. Affleck “smoothly downshifts, easing from the high anxiety of the opener — which evokes 1970s political thrillers like Sydney Pollack’s ‘Three Days of the Condor’ — into something looser, mellower and funny,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Sched