': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/6-qs-about-the-news-robin-williams-oscar-winning-comedian-dies-at-63-in-suspected-suicide/', 'snippet': 'What was your reaction to the announcement that Robin Williams had died?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Robin Williams, Oscar-Winning Comedian, Dies at 63 in Suspected Suicide,” Dave Itzkoff reports on the death of the “surprisingly nuanced, Academy Award-winning actor.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | Robin Williams, Oscar-Winning Comedian, Dies at 63 in Suspected Suicide', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T08:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a46e4ee2-dac2-5c92-a168-e5baff37d239', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a46e4ee2-dac2-5c92-a168-e5baff37d239'}, {'abstract': 'Diamond Dallas Page, a former W.W.E. wrestler, created a new form of healing for broken-down macho guys like himself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/magazine/the-rise-of-beefcake-yoga.html', 'snippet': 'Diamond Dallas Page, a former W.W.E. wrestler, created a new form of healing for broken-down macho guys like himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A horde of screaming middle-aged wrestling fans gathered one Saturday evening in April at the Smoothie King Center in New Orleans to celebrate professional wrestling’s Hall of Fame induction ceremony. The world’s most popular fake-sport organization, World Wrestling Entertainment doesn’t maintain a brick-and-mortar Hall of Fame — no bronze plaques to commemorate its greats (the Ultimate Warrior, Superfly Jimmy Snuka), no interactive widgets to teach young fans storied techniques (“the camel clutch,” “the piledriver”). Instead, once a year, W.W.E.’s former stars relive their glory together, on a stage, face to face with thousands of their most fervent admirers. Throughout the preceding week, these fans traipsed up and down Bourbon Street until 2 a.m., screaming the names of their favorite wrestlers into the night. Now they wore fake championship belts and chanted ecstatically as retired stars strutted by in big ‘n’ tall tuxedos and sequined gowns. A deafening “hoooe!” greeted (Hacksaw) Jim Duggan; (Nature Boy) Ric Flair earned a high-pitched “woooo!” Hulk Hogan, who arrived in a black suit, black bandanna and yellow wraparound shades, sent hundreds of so-called Hulkamaniacs into a fit of rapture.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17page1/mag-17Page-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17page1/mag-17Page-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17page1/mag-17Page-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17page1/mag-17Page-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/magazine/17page1/17page1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType'