te/liberal/secular rebels that, it’s argued, would have prevented more radical groups from getting traction in that conflict, and thus forestalled the rise of ISIS to its current bad eminence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria and the Risks of Intervention', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T16:23:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ffa671a-5c31-5c89-886a-ae64ecdc2f82', 'word_count': 1413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ffa671a-5c31-5c89-886a-ae64ecdc2f82'}, {'abstract': 'What was wrong with the Ryan budget?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/fiscal-flimflam-revisited/', 'snippet': 'What was wrong with the Ryan budget?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong reminds us of the original Ryan budget plan — or actually “plan”, as I’ll explain — and emphasizes its dire warnings about a looming debt crisis that wasn’t. But pointing out that the debt panic was unjustified only gets at part of what was wrong with that Ryan budget (and all his subsequent proposals). For the fact is that it wasn’t a proposal made in good faith.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiscal Flimflam, Revisited', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T16:23:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbddaec5-53ad-5396-9c3c-71e8f5dfe47a', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbddaec5-53ad-5396-9c3c-71e8f5dfe47a'}, {'abstract': 'A new study reports that caffeine intake is associated with a reduced risk for tinnitus — ringing or buzzing in the ears.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/caffeine-may-reduce-tinnitus-risk/', 'snippet': 'A new study reports that caffeine intake is associated with a reduced risk for tinnitus — ringing or buzzing in the ears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study reports that caffeine intake is associated with a reduced risk for tinnitus — ringing or buzzing in the ears.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/health/well_perceptions/well_perceptions-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 219, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/health/well_perceptions/well_perceptions-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 219, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/health/well_perceptions/well_perceptions-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/24/health/well_perceptions/well_perceptions-thumbStanda