etter suit their needs. The swap was announced by the Nederlander Organization, which operates both theaters.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Love Letters’ and ‘Honeymoon in Vegas’ Swap Broadway Theaters', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater Swapping on Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurney, A R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nederlander Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T16:29:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cc9b243-5806-532f-a908-b99fc40d81a1', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cc9b243-5806-532f-a908-b99fc40d81a1'}, {'abstract': 'Her attack on President Obama’s policies shows that she doesn’t have an internal braking mechanism.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/hillary-clinton-doesnt-know-when-to-stop/', 'snippet': 'Her attack on President Obama’s policies shows that she doesn’t have an internal braking mechanism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to dispute that Hillary Clinton is the smartest person in most rooms. That’s why The Times editorial board endorsed her in the Democratic primary in 2008 over Barack Obama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hillary Clinton Doesn’t Know When to Stop', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T16:33:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/954e4372-7e50-5b8b-b5c2-e8fcbdccb1a7', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/954e4372-7e50-5b8b-b5c2-e8fcbdccb1a7'}, {'abstract': 'Couples could start marrying by next week as a federal appeals court panel denied a request to delay its ruling striking down Virginia’s ban on same-sex marriages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/us/virginia-same-sex-marriages.html', 'snippet': 'Couples could start marrying by next week as a federal appeals court panel denied a request to delay its ruling striking down Virginia’s ban on same-sex marriages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal appeals court that last month struck down Virginia’s ban on same-sex unions refused Wednesday to delay the effects of its ruling. State officials said that unless the United States Supreme Court interceded, Virginia counties could begin issuing marriage licenses to gay couples next week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Refuses to Stay Its Decision Striking Down Virginia’s Same-Sex Marriage Ban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Refuses to Stay Its Decision Striking Down Virginia’s Same-Sex Marriage Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blinder, Alan S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organi