ame': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dab39b45-e960-56c1-aeec-fdaca972e0d3', 'word_count': 1435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dab39b45-e960-56c1-aeec-fdaca972e0d3'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A stone from the Bastille prison is found in a house of the Sens region in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/1939-bastille-stone-found-in-house/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A stone from the Bastille prison is found in a house of the Sens region in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SENS — Set in the wall of an old house in Saint-Julien-du-Sault is a stone from the Bastille, one of the few authentic relics of the grim fortress of which no vestige exists in Paris since its destruction in 1789 by the revolutionary masses. The stone bears the following inscription in Latin and French: ‘‘This stone has been taken from the ruins of the Bastille. Patriotism has dedicated it to a better use by placing it here to give to this square the sweet name of Liberty. In the second year of French liberty.’’ For several years, stones from the Bastille were very fashionable. Small fragments of them were set like jewels and worn by women in rings and necklaces.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, August 14, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Bastille Stone Found in House', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War and Revolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T17:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70e9f3eb-dc1d-5cbe-8872-587ea58925c5', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70e9f3eb-dc1d-5cbe-8872-587ea58925c5'}, {'abstract': 'The police said the man had lunged for an officer’s weapon, but family members contended he had been lying on the ground when he was shot three times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/us/man-shot-and-killed-by-los-angeles-police-officer.html', 'snippet': 'The police said the man had lunged for an officer’s weapon, but family members contended he had been lying on the ground when he was shot three times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The police shot and killed an unarmed black man in South Los Angeles on Monday night, the Los Angeles Police Department said. The police said that the man, whom the department did not identify, had tackled an officer and lunged for the weapon in his holster before being shot at by both the officer and his partner.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Is Shot and Killed by the Police in California', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Is Shot and Killed by the Police in California', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Ezell Earl (1988-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Police Department', 'rank