news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7483556e-49fe-55aa-98e6-d06dc8bd8591', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7483556e-49fe-55aa-98e6-d06dc8bd8591'}, {'abstract': 'Nickelodeon held an open call for new cartoon ideas at Comic-Con and will turn the proposal for “Cupcakery of Doom,” pitched by a 28-year-old journalist, into an animated short.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/business/media/nickelodeon-cartoon-pitches-at-comic-con-turn-up-a-winner.html', 'snippet': 'Nickelodeon held an open call for new cartoon ideas at Comic-Con and will turn the proposal for “Cupcakery of Doom,” pitched by a 28-year-old journalist, into an animated short.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Nickelodeon said on Wednesday that an unusual open call for new cartoon ideas had produced a surprisingly strong result: “Cupcakery of Doom.” A 28-year-old newspaper employee pitched the idea, and it will be developed into an animated short with the potential to turn into a television series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nickelodeon Cartoon Pitches at Comic-Con Turn Up a Winner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nickelodeon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic-Con (Conventions)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Press Democrat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T18:35:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45ffa4b3-9330-5d72-83f3-42eb2595ac53', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45ffa4b3-9330-5d72-83f3-42eb2595ac53'}, {'abstract': 'The reunited group will tour the United States and Britain this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/culture-club-to-tour-with-original-lineup/', 'snippet': 'The reunited group will tour the United States and Britain this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British band Culture Club will reconvene with its original lineup – the flamboyant singer Boy George, the guitarist and keyboardist Roy Hay, the bassist Mikey Craig and the drummer Jon Moss – for an American tour in November and a British tour in December, Boy George announced on his webpage. Reports of a reunion had been circulating since May, but the posting is the first official confirmation that the Culture Club has reunited and plans to tour.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-boy/13artsbeat-boy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-boy/13artsbeat-boy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-boy/13artsbeat-boy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-boy/13artsbeat-boy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-boy/13artsbeat-boy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-boy/13artsbeat-boy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-boy/13artsbeat-boy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Culture Club to Tour With Original Lineup', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Culture Club to Reunite', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Craig, Mikey (1960- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'George, Boy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hay, Roy (1961- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Jonathan A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Culture Club (Music Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T18:35:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ab51317-53a0-52a8-881e-7eae074554e1', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ab51317-53a0-52a8-881e-7eae074554e1'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/classical-playlist-bruckner-richard-reed-parry-brahms-and-more/', 'snippet': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUCKNER: Symphony No. 7Budapest Festival Orchestra, Ivan Fischer, conductor(Channel Classics CCS SA 33714)For more than 30 years the conductor Ivan Fischer has been drawing inspired, fresh and intelligent performances from the impressive Budapest Festival Orchestra, an ensemble he co-founded and still conducts. Some Bruckner-lovers may find this account of the great Seventh Symphony lacking in mysticism and gravity. I suspect that most listeners, like me, will be drawn into the vibrant, glowing and revitalized performance Mr. Fischer draws from his excellent players. The sound of the orchestra is lush and rich, yet wondrously lucid. (Anthony Tommasini)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/classical-fischer/classical-fischer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/classical-fischer/classical-fischer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/classical-fischer/classical-fischer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/classical-fischer/classical-fischer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/classical-fischer/classical-fischer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/classical-fischer/classical-fischer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/classical-fischer/classical-fischer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Playlist: Bruckner, Richard Reed Parry, Brahms and More', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T18:54:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccaec32e-3e52-594f-8a17-da00e6f53a1b', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccaec32e-3e52-594f-8a17-da00e6f53a1b'}, {'abstract': 'It’s part of an overall strategy of embracing the surreal for the pop star, best known for the hit single she recorded with Gotye. Her sophomore album is out this week.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/kimbra-90s-music-video-new-zealand-songstress-who-moved-to-a-sheep-farm-in-l-a/', 'snippet': 'It’s part of an overall strategy of embracing the surreal for the pop star, best known for the hit single she recorded with Gotye. Her sophomore album is out this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Zealand–born pop singer Kimbra is full of surprises. She’s a Prince fanatic who studies the way the Purple One’s backing vocals “jump into your face, so loud and invasive, like they’re characters themselves, or a gang.” She’s an armchair philosopher who muses, “There’s a rousing frequency in the universe that could be divine, or primal, or human, but it’s a sound that calls you outward to where you feel unbound by time and space.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/t-magazine/13kimbra-bobb/13kimbra-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/13/t-magazine/13kimbra-bobb/13kimbra-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/t-magazine/13kimbra-bobb/13kimbra-bobb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/t-magazine/13kimbra-bobb/13kimbra-bobb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/t-magazine/13kimbra-bobb/13kimbra-bobb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/13/t-magazine/13kimbra-bobb/13kimbra-bobb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/t-magazine/13kimbra-bobb/13kimbra-bobb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kimbra, the New Zealand Songstress Who Moved to a Sheep Farm in L.A.', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimbra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T19:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Dorris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dorris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/124704f3-fa4e-54f7-aa5b-bdd77f8a4d91', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/124704f3-fa4e-54f7-aa5b-bdd77f8a4d91'}, {'abstract': 'A new musical, based on the 2004 film about J. M. Barrie, will begin performances in March.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/finding-neverland-to-come-to-broadway-in-march/', 'snippet': 'A new musical, based on the 2004 film about J. M. Barrie, will begin performances in March.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Finding Neverland,” a new musical based on the 2004 film about the “Peter Pan” playwright J. M. Barrie, will begin performances on Broadway in March, a spokesman for the show’s producer, Harvey Weinstein, said on Wednesday. A tryout production of the musical is underway at the American Repertory Theater in Cambridge, Mass., where it will officially open on Wednesday night. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-finding/13artsbeat-finding-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-finding/13artsbeat-finding-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-finding/13artsbeat-finding-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-finding/13artsbeat-finding-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1180, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-finding/13artsbeat-finding-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-finding/13artsbeat-finding-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/arts/13artsbeat-finding/13artsbeat-finding-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Finding Neverland’ to Come to Broadway in March', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Finding Neverland’ Is Headed to Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Laura Michelle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T19:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0360d2df-9448-5236-9bed-f41128d07a4b', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0360d2df-9448-5236-9bed-f41128d07a4b'}, {'abstract': 'Publicity about suicides, especially those of celebrities, has been linked to an increase in suicides, especially among young people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/upshot/the-science-behind-suicide-contagion.html', 'snippet': 'Publicity about suicides, especially those of celebrities, has been linked to an increase in suicides, especially among young people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Marilyn Monroe died in August 1962, with the cause listed as probable suicide, the nation reacted. In the months afterward, there was extensive news coverage, widespread sorrow and a spate of suicides. According to one study, the suicide rate in the United States jumped by 12 percent compared with the same months in the previous year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/14UP-Suicide/14UP-Suicide-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/14UP-Suicide/14UP-Suicide-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/14UP-Suicide/14UP-Suicide-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/14UP-Suicide/14UP-Suicide-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/14UP-Suicide/14UP-Suicide-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/14UP-Suicide/14UP-Suicide-thumbStan