 {'abstract': 'An uncompromising youthquake revitalized the fall runways with collegiate starter jackets, short skirts and nubby sweaters that inspire a coltish confidence.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/fashion-report-fall-runways-college-style/', 'snippet': 'An uncompromising youthquake revitalized the fall runways with collegiate starter jackets, short skirts and nubby sweaters that inspire a coltish confidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An uncompromising youthquake revitalized the fall runways with collegiate starter jackets, short skirts and nubby sweaters that inspire a coltish confidence.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '168', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Fashion | City Girl', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Girl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T22:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99942144-9ff1-52c5-bfe3-7f4440a0fa99', 'word_count': 21, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99942144-9ff1-52c5-bfe3-7f4440a0fa99'}, {'abstract': 'At least one of the leaders of a civil disobedience movement seeking universal suffrage in Hong Kong has received threats that reflect the tensions between those who want a democratic city, and those who want a semi-authoritarian one, at best.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/fighting-for-hong-kongs-political-future/', 'snippet': 'At least one of the leaders of a civil disobedience movement seeking universal suffrage in Hong Kong has received threats that reflect the tensions between those who want a democratic city, and those who want a semi-authoritarian one, at best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chan Kin-man, a prominent Hong Kong democracy activist, receives many anonymous threats. He has gotten a razor blade in the mail and messages like: ‘‘Hunt and Kill Traitors!’’ Sophisticated hacking attempts occur daily, often from email addresses belonging to friends or students. Some threats are unprintable, about what the sender would like to do to Mr. Chan’s mother.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/world/15sino-letter01/15sino-letter01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/12/world/15sino-letter01/15sino-letter01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/world/15sino-letter01/15sino-letter01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/world/15sino-letter01/15sino-letter01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/world/15sino-letter01/15sino-letter01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/12/world/15sino-letter01/15sino-letter01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/12/world/15sino-letter01/15sino-letter01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Laughing Off Threats in the Fight Against ‘Fake Democracy’', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chan Kin-man', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chu Yiu-ming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tai Yiu-ting, Benny', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Central', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T22:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94d988ca-579b-56ce-a5a4-aaefaa96669e', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94d988ca-579b-56ce-a5a4-aaefaa96669e'}, {'abstract': 'Like so many spectacularly successful comic playwrights from the first half of the 20th century, George Kelly (the uncle of Grace) is mostly forgotten.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/theater/a-betrayed-wife-clinging-to-hope.html', 'snippet': 'Like so many spectacularly successful comic playwrights from the first half of the 20th century, George Kelly (the uncle of Grace) is mostly forgotten.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like so many spectacularly successful comic playwrights from the first half of the 20th century, George Kelly (the uncle of Grace) is mostly forgotten. The interest that he does occasionally draw from contemporary producers is for his early satires. In 2000 Dylan Baker directed a droll and flamboyant production of “The Torch-Bearers,” Kelly’s 1922 sendup of community theater, which featured a memorably bravura performance by Marian Seldes. “The Show-Off,” which Kelly wrote two years later, is also periodically remounted. But the Mint Theater is not content with producing an ignored writer. Drawn to obscurity like a certain kind of obsessed indie music fan, it searches out the ignored works of ignored writers. So this month, the Mint mounts a rare production of one of Kelly’s later plays, “The Fatal Weakness” (1946), about a woman in a 28-year marriage who discovers that her husband is having an affair. Her fatal weakness is that she’s a hopeless romantic. (“The Fatal Weakness” starts previews on Tuesday at the Mint, 311 West 43rd Street, Clinton; minttheater.org, 866-811-4111.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/arts/17GUIDE5/17GUIDE5-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1342, 'width': 2046, 'subType'