 between art and commodity, has effectively opened a gift shop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I bought some art the other day — nothing too crazy, nothing too expensive, nothing made by an ex-graffiti artist going legit and now giddily bilking rappers out of their piles of new money. Just something beautiful, something I had an emotional response to, something that I perceived as having value independent of its function or cost of production.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCRITICAL1/14zCRITICAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCRITICAL1/14zCRITICAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCRITICAL1/14zCRITICAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCRITICAL1/14zCRITICAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCRITICAL1/14zCRITICAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCRITICAL1/14zCRITICAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCRITICAL1/14zCRITICAL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art That’s in the Hands of the Buyer', 'kicker': 'Critical Shopper', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art That’s in the Hands of the Buyer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Other Criteria (Manhattan, NY, Retail Store)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Damien', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T23:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21ad4fe6-01b3-57c4-b360-b1042ebcd054', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21ad4fe6-01b3-57c4-b360-b1042ebcd054'}, {'abstract': "Paul Schatz's recent additions to his Miraflores Collection are intricate (but user-friendly) patterns of jewel glass, shell and 24-karat gold.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/garden/a-marriage-of-design-and-application.html', 'snippet': "Paul Schatz's recent additions to his Miraflores Collection are intricate (but user-friendly) patterns of jewel glass, shell and 24-karat gold.", 'lead_paragraph': 'The bridge between design and real-life application can sometimes be shaky. So when Paul Schatz, an interior designer, teamed with New Ravenna Mosaics to develop glass tiles, he said he wanted tiles that were easy on the eyes and on the user as well.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ran