tz, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-13T23:09:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d97c7d2d-a151-5cbc-a524-2e60f51465e1', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d97c7d2d-a151-5cbc-a524-2e60f51465e1'}, {'abstract': "The new brass toys from James Klein and David Reid of KleinReid were inspired by the Eameses' classic wooden tops.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/garden/putting-a-shiny-spin-on-childrens-tops.html', 'snippet': "The new brass toys from James Klein and David Reid of KleinReid were inspired by the Eameses' classic wooden tops.", 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years ago, the ceramics artists James Klein and David Reid of KleinReid began creating limited-edition wood tops — inspired by the Eameses’ collection of the toys — for Herman Miller. “Tops called out to us because they’re about form, a poised shape, and they are about spinning, which is what we do on a potter’s wheel,” Mr. Reid said.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/garden/14CURRGOODS/0814CURRENTS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 516, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/garden/14CURRGOODS/0814CURRENTS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 516}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/garden/14CURRGOODS/0814CURRENTS2-jumbo.jpg