nst Humanity, a card game that rewards the absurd, the offensive and the hilarious, has become popular, popping up at birthdays and bachelorette parties, happy hours and celebrations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/fashion/for-a-well-played-hand-far-from-pc.html', 'snippet': 'Cards Against Humanity, a card game that rewards the absurd, the offensive and the hilarious, has become popular, popping up at birthdays and bachelorette parties, happy hours and celebrations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an age where honesty is often reserved for anonymity, and social media accounts are scraped for off-color content, a deck of cards with the slogan “a party game for horrible people” on its box has, for many young people, an undeniable allure. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCARDS/14zCARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCARDS/14zCARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCARDS/14zCARDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCARDS/14zCARDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCARDS/14zCARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCARDS/14zCARDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/fashion/14ZCARDS/14zCARDS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Well-Played Hand, Far From P.C.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Well-Played Hand, Far From P.C.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marikar, Sheila', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Temkin, Max', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T00:01:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Marikar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marikar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a954a986-68a6-5171-ac4c-176eff3cf28e', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a954a986-68a6-5171-ac4c-176eff3cf28e'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Casely-Hayford and his son, Charlie, produce a men’s wear line that represents a collaboration of generations and points of view.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/fashion/casely-hayford-a-father-and-son-design-team-represents-a-collaboration-of-generations.html', 'snippet': 'Joe Casely-Hayford and his son, Charlie, produce a men’s wear line that represents a collaboration of generations and points of view.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thirty years ago, before the East End of London was a hive of hipsterdom, home to an Ace Hotel and an Opening Ceremony outpost, the first Casely-Hayford studio sat there, roughly the size of a football field. It was the creative home of the designer Joe Casely-Hayford, whose family home was just down the road. “You couldn’t buy a cappuccino here,” said Mr. Casely-Hayford, speaking recently at what may pass for a tableau of Times Have Changed: the Ace Hotel’s thrumming lobby coffee bar. “You’d be shot if you asked for a cappuccino.”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/08/fashion/14ZCASELY/14zCASELY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/01/08/fashion/14ZCASELY/14zCASELY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/08/fashion/14ZCASELY/14zCASELY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/08/fashion/14ZCASELY/14zCASELY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/08/fashion/14ZCASELY/14zCASELY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/01/08/fashion/14ZCASELY/14zCASELY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/08/fashion/14ZCASELY/14zCASELY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They Meet in the Middle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They Meet in the Middle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneier, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Casely-Hayford (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casely-Hayford, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casely-Hayford, Charlie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits (Apparel)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Men's Fashion Week", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T00:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca13b5d0-debf-56c6-8534-92135ef6394f', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca13b5d0-debf-56c6-8534-92135ef6394f'}, {'abstract': 'Timepieces and other artifacts help tell the story at the 9/11 museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/fashion/a-moment-in-time-captured-in-pieces.html', 'snippet': 'Timepieces and other artifacts help tell the story at the 9/11 museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The instrument itself is a two-tone Oyster Perpetual Datejust, with a 41-millimeter case, an unusual grooved dial of 18-karat gold, a gold-and-silver Jubilee bracelet and a signature flip-lock clasp. It is a chronometer, which is to say a precision watch that enables its wearer to measure elapsed time, not in the way a stopwatch might, but with great accuracy. It is a Rolex, one of millions of wristwatches produced over the decades by this notable producer of high-end timepieces, and when originally sold it cost roughly $7,700. ', 'print_section': 'E'