, 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Souvenir of Venice', 'kicker': 'Intersection', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Souvenir of Venice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ridgewood (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T01:37:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oresti Tsonopoulos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oresti', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tsonopoulos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcda29ab-0947-5ed8-9e3a-e4ae7982e0cc', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcda29ab-0947-5ed8-9e3a-e4ae7982e0cc'}, {'abstract': 'In a letter to Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr., the representatives urged him to intervene immediately in the case of the Staten Island man who died in police custody.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/nyregion/six-members-of-congress-ask-holder-to-open-federal-inquiry-in-chokehold-case.html', 'snippet': 'In a letter to Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr., the representatives urged him to intervene immediately in the case of the Staten Island man who died in police custody.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six members of Congress have asked Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr. to open a federal investigation into the circumstances surrounding the death of a Staten Island man in police custody, and to extend the inquiry into other possible civil-rights violations committed by the Police Department through its “broken windows” approach to fighting crime.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Six Members of Congress Ask Holder to Open Federal Inquiry in Chokehold Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Six Members of Congress Ask Holder to Open Federal Inquiry in Chokehold Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T01:44:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d973a786-652c-5371-b340-a20ac1ab4e8c', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d973a786-652c-5371-b340-a20ac1ab4e8c'}, {'abstract': 'Mexico’s conservative opposition party has removed one of its congressional whips after a video emerged showing him and other legislators at a party with table dancers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/world/americas/mexico-lawmaker-punished-in-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'Mexico’s conservative opposition party has removed one of its congressional whips after a video emerged showing him and other legislators at a party with table dancers.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Mexico’s conservative opposition party has removed one of its congressional whips after a video emerged showing him and other legislators at a party with table dancers. The National Action Party, whose members often talk of maintaining wholesome family values, removed Luis Alberto Villarreal on Wednesday as coordinator of its legislators in the lower house as well as Mr. Villarreal’s deputy, Jorge Villalobos, who also appears in the video. It was taken earlier this year at a party at a beach resort but was disclosed this week on ReporteIndigo.com, a news website. Former President Felipe Calderón, a member of the party, said Wednesday in a radio interview that the video showed the “moral decomposition” of the party. Mr. Villarreal said in a statement that the video was illegally recorded at a private party for which no public funds were spent. The episode was the latest example of electronic eavesdropping that often propels political scandals here. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Lawmaker Punished in Scandal', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Lawmaker Punished in Scandal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Villalobos, Jorge', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Villarreal, Luis Alberto', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T01:48:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2fe0a2e-cebb-51e9-843d-7aad9b51ea6c', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2fe0a2e-cebb-51e9-843d-7aad9b51ea6c'}, {'abstract': 'In which I give you directions to get through Jason Flinn’s puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/13/doctors-advocate/', 'snippet': 'In which I give you directions to get through Jason Flinn’s puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — Interesting-looking grid, isn’t it? I will confess that I didn’t quite know what to make of the design before I started solving this second time at bat by Jason Flinn. But I will tell you what gave it away for me.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doctor’s Advocate', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T02:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a88191df-b2b2-5ea1-b45e-f7ace6ca70c1', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a88191df-b2b2-5ea1-b45e-f7ace6ca70c1'}, {'abstract': 'Increasing numbers of low-income mothers and fathers are at the center of a new collision that pits workplace scheduling technology against the routines of parenting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytim