act': 'Earlier this year, John Napier Tie, a former State Department official who worked on Internet issues, filed an inspector general whistleblower complaint alleging that the National Security Agency’s collection and storage of American communications abroad under Executive Order 12333 violates the Fourth Amendment. He also took his concerns to the House and Senate Intelligence Committees. He received these two letters back; he did not hear back from the Senate panel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2014/08/14/us/14whistleblower.html', 'snippet': 'Earlier this year, John Napier Tie, a former State Department official who worked on Internet issues, filed an inspector general whistleblower complaint alleging that the National Security Agency’s collection and storage of American communications...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this year, John Napier Tie, a former State Department official who worked on Internet issues, filed an inspector general whistleblower complaint alleging that the National Security Agency’s collection and storage of American communications abroad under Executive Order 12333 violates the Fourth Amendment. He also took his concerns to the House and Senate Intelligence Committees. He received these two letters back; he did not hear back from the Senate panel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14whistleblower-1407985895270/14whistleblower-1407985895270-articleLarge.png', 'height': 488, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14whistleblower-1407985895270/14whistleblower-1407985895270-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 488}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14whistleblower-1407985895270/14whistleblower-1407985895270-jumbo.png', 'height': 492, 'w