25ba1-410b-597e-8350-bb4f5912c68a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/98325ba1-410b-597e-8350-bb4f5912c68a'}, {'abstract': 'After Manager Joe Girardi was ejected for arguing an interference call, the Orioles crushed two home runs to secure a comeback victory and move eight games ahead of the Yankees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/sports/baseball/pineda-is-bright-spot-in-his-return-but-yankees-offense-only-flickers.html', 'snippet': 'After Manager Joe Girardi was ejected for arguing an interference call, the Orioles crushed two home runs to secure a comeback victory and move eight games ahead of the Yankees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — One of the more vivid signs of the Yankees’ recent frustrations materialized in the seventh inning Wednesday night. The Yankees were clinging to a 2-1 lead when Stephen Drew chopped a ball in front of the plate and sprinted toward first base. The throw to the bag from Nick Hundley, the Orioles’ catcher, deflected off Drew and dribbled into right field.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/sports/CITY-YANKEES/CITY-YANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'