 to map, monitor and safeguard Peru’s many endangered archaeological sites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/arts/design/drones-are-used-to-patrol-endangered-archaeological-sites.html', 'snippet': 'A drone air force has been created to map, monitor and safeguard Peru’s many endangered archaeological sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHEPÉN, Peru — A small remote-controlled helicopter buzzed over ancient hilltop ruins here, snapping hundreds of photographs. Below, stone walls built more than a thousand years ago by the Moche civilization gave way to a grid of adobe walls put up only recently by what officials said were land speculators.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New to the Archaeologist’s Tool Kit: The Drone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New to the Archaeologist’s Tool Kit: The Drone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peru', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blumenthal, Ralph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castillo Butters, Luis Jaime', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T03:58:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman and Ralph Blumenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ralph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blumenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ea2c1b2-8444-5a3e-a5d7-d5a7a5511297', 'word_count': 1359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ea2c1b2-8444-5a3e-a5d7-d5a7a5511297'}, {'abstract': 'The CFDA award-winning designers have launched two carryalls in collaboration with the L.A. leathergoods brand Killspencer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/t-magazine/public-school-kill-spencer-collaboration-a-brand-new-bag.html', 'snippet': 'The CFDA award-winning designers have launched two carryalls in collaboration with the L.A. leathergoods brand Killspencer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maxwell Osborne and Dao-Yi Chow of the CFDA-award-winning line Public School have been shaking up the men’s fashion scene with their streetwear-inspired styles since they launched in 2008. On the fall/winter 2014 runway, they debuted their first women’s collection; now they’ve added accessories. Tomorrow, the duo will launch two limited-edition unisex bags — a weekender ($850) and a backpack ($575) — in collaboration with Killspencer, the L.A. leather goods brand run by Spencer Nikosey, a former industrial designer. Both styles are made from the same pressed Italian matte leather that was used in Public School’s fall collection and feature waterproof interiors and quilted topstitching details. The bags are “intricate and functional,” says Osborne. “We wanted to make that type of bag for a guy — durable but still clean, sharp and exact.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/t-magazine/14school-bobb/14school-bobb-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/t-magazine/14school-bobb/14school-bobb-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600