recounted in real time on Twitter and other platforms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/us/protest-in-missouri-at-police-killing-of-teenager-is-chronicled-on-social-media.html', 'snippet': 'The police dispersed demonstrators in Ferguson, Mo., by force on Wednesday night. The developments were recounted in real time on Twitter and other platforms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Demonstrators in Ferguson, Mo. gathered on Wednesday for another round of protests over the death of Michael Brown, an unarmed teenager who was killed over the weekend by a police officer. Mr. Brown’s death has triggered days of protests that have brought national attention to racial tension between the police and the African-American community in the St. Louis suburb.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protest in Missouri at Police Killing of Teenager Is Chronicled on Social Media', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T09:04:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce320cea-02bb-559a-a632-085e16754f3b', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce320cea-02bb-559a-a632-085e16754f3b'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of the 27th annual Shark Week, some history about how it all began — even though, according to one analysis, your chances of being bitten by a shark are much slimmer than your chances of being bitten by the Uruguay striker Luis Suárez.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/throwback-thursday-1916-new-jersey-shark-attacks/', 'snippet': 'In honor of the 27th annual Shark Week, some history about how it all began — even though, according to one analysis, your chances of being bitten by a shark are much slimmer than your chances of being bitten by the Uruguay striker Luis Suárez.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In honor of the 27th annual Shark Week, some history about how pop culture’s shark mania first began, and a terrifying photo of a great white — even though, according to this analysis, your chances of being bitten by a shark are considerably slimmer than your chances of being bitten by the Uruguay striker Luis Suárez:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Throwback Thursday | 1916 New Jersey Shark Attacks', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T09:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9764276-710e-5468-aed9-81f4679008fe', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9764276-710e-5468-aed9-81f4679008fe'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/us/your-thursday-briefing.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to the Morning Briefing on NYT Now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14stlouis1_now/14stlouis1_now-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14stlouis1_now/14stlouis1_now-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14stlouis1_now/14stlouis1_now-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14stlouis1_now/14stlouis1_now-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14stlouis1_now/14stlouis1_now-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14stlouis1_now/14stlouis1_now-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/14stlouis1_now/14stlouis1_now-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Thursday Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T09:56:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adeel Hassan and Victoria Shannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adeel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hassan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21f267e9-0836-5d5b-83d7-a2e69e147bb2', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21f267e9-0836-5d5b-83d7-a2e69e147bb2'}, {'abstract': 'Opinions on college sports, Ferguson, Ebola, plastic bags and more.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/morning-views-58/', 'snippet': 'Opinions on college sports, Ferguson, Ebola, plastic bags and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Claudia Wilken, a federal judge, handed down a decision meaning “college athletes will almost certainly be better off financially,” according to an editorial in The New York Times. “And the notion that these athletes are pure amateurs – ‘students first, athletes second’ – will be impossible to sustain.” Judge Wilken issued an injunction against a ban on payments to players for “the commercial use of their names, images and likenesses,” which she claims was in violation of antitrust law. “She also ruled that college sports’ governing body, the National Collegiate Athletic Association, may not prohibit universities from offering cost-of-living stipends in addition to scholarships.” The O’Bannon Ruling, as it’s known, is named for Ed O’Bannon, “a former basketball player for the University of California, Los Angeles,” and “other plays like him who until now have been unable to share in the considerable wealth generated by their skill and hard work.” The N.C.A.A. “built a lucrative commercial enterprise that depended in large part on unpaid labor.” Judge Wilken’s decision is a step toward righting those decades of exploitation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05f5d69e-d1d7-58c8-8962-2b638cd5caf7', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05f5d69e-d1d7-58c8-8962-2b638cd5caf7'}, {'abstract': "A state that was once the nation's most populous is now fourth, as residents seek opportunity elsewhere.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/upshot/a-leading-export-of-new-york-state-people.html', 'snippet': "A state that was once the nation's most populous is now fourth, as residents seek opportunity elsewhere.", 'lead_paragraph': 'New York was once the nation’s most populous state. Now it’s fourth. That’s in part because millions of New Yorkers have left the Empire State for opportunities elsewhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Leading Export of New York State: People', 'kicker': 'Migrations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T10:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b28a4c25-652c-54fb-8a79-56a463ed6469', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b28a4c25-