louse-Lautrec,” MoMA’s exhibition of 100 works by the artist, depicts the vibrant, louche and often sympathetic denizens of a late-19th-century demimonde.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henri de Toulouse-Lautrec’s aristocratic parents were first cousins, and his numerous  genetic defects, including bone abnormalities, are attributed to a family history of inbreeding. At 13, he fell and broke a thigh bone, and at 14, the other. The breaks didn’t heal properly, and his legs stopped growing. As an adult he stood 4 feet 11 inches. He had the body of a grown man but walked on childlike legs with the help of a cane. His lips and nose outgrew the rest of his face, causing him to lisp and drool and suffer from chronic sinus problems.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/TOULOUSE/TOULOUSE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/TOULOUSE/TOULOUSE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/TOULOUSE/TOULOUSE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/TOULOUSE/TOULOUSE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1302, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/TOULOUSE/TOULOUSE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/TOULOUSE/TOULOUSE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbn