zation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb1d19a8-ce39-58bb-9920-1ae089d1b9a7', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb1d19a8-ce39-58bb-9920-1ae089d1b9a7'}, {'abstract': 'A full-page obituary in the Chinese-language Oriental Daily claimed that the owner of a rival newspaper, Apple Daily, had died.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/hong-kong-newspaper-prints-fake-obituary-of-rivals-owner/', 'snippet': 'A full-page obituary in the Chinese-language Oriental Daily claimed that the owner of a rival newspaper, Apple Daily, had died.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the journalistic equivalent of putting a horse’s head in your rival’s bed. Lai Chee-ying, 65, also known as Fatty Lai and a native of Shunde in the southern Chinese province of Guangdong, had died of AIDS and cancer on Aug. 7. Since his family members were also sick, there would be no funeral.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hong Kong Newspaper Prints Fake Obituary of Rival’s Owner', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lai, Jimmy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APPLE DAILY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HSBC Holdings PLC.', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ming Pao Daily News', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Next Media Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reporters Without Borders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Chartered Bank PLC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub