ub team, Barcelona, until the end of October.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/sports/15suarez/15suarez-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/15/sports/15suarez/15suarez-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/sports/15suarez/15suarez-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/sports/15suarez/15suarez-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1519, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/sports/15suarez/15suarez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/15/sports/15suarez/15suarez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/sports/15suarez/15suarez-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Luis Suárez’s Ban for Bite Is Altered but Upheld', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suárez’s Ban for Bite Is Altered but Upheld', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borden, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suarez, Luis (1987- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T13:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a876149-c55f-50c1-a19d-f32e63018c6d', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a876149-c55f-50c1-a19d-f32e63018c6d'}, {'abstract': 'As the local police prepared to release the name of the officer who fatally shot an unarmed teenager, the Missouri State Highway Patrol took over security in Ferguson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/us/ferguson-missouri-police-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'As the local police prepared to release the name of the officer who fatally shot an unarmed teenager, the Missouri State Highway Patrol took over security in Ferguson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FERGUSON, Mo. — President Obama on Thursday called for an end to the violence here, denouncing actions both by the police and by protesters. Hours later, the Missouri governor, Jay Nixon, ordered the state highway patrol to take over security operations from local law enforcement.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Tack on Unrest Eases Tension in Missouri', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Tack on Unrest Eases Tension in Missouri', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Ronald S', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T13:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz, Michael D. Shear and Michael Paulson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/471f3f34-16f0-5cb3-8820-13a75f096d91', 'word_count': 1506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/471f3f34-16f0-5cb3-8820-13a75f096d91'}, {'abstract': '“Frank” centers on a highly eccentric musical group whose equilibrium is disturbed when it is joined by an admiring outsider.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/movies/frank-about-an-offbeat-band-and-its-eccentric-leader.html', 'snippet': '“Frank” centers on a highly eccentric musical group whose equilibrium is disturbed when it is joined by an admiring outsider.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Popular music has always had a place for eccentrics and visionaries, artists whose inventions sometimes take them to the borderlands of madness. “Frank,” a captivatingly low-key new film directed by Lenny Abrahamson, was inspired by the life and work of one such musician, a singer known as Frank Sidebottom, who flourished in Britain in the 1990s. At one point, Mr. Sidebottom hired a keyboard player named Jon Ronson — though “hired” may suggest too conventional an arrangement — who later embellished, edited and updated his experience into the screenplay for this movie, which takes place in the present-day world of social media and South by Southwest. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Music for Its Own Sake, Until a Dreamer Intrudes', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Music for Its Own Sake, Until a Dreamer Intrudes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Frank (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abrahamson, Lenny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fassbender, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNairy, Scoot', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gyllenhaal, Maggie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ronson, Jon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T14:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa8b3110-cd55-566c-9779-1c656ce7cadb', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa8b3110-cd55-566c-9779-1c656ce7cadb'}, {'abstract': 'Some Southern states are becoming more Democratic-leaning as new arrivals from the North move in. But this is not true in every state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/upshot/changing-south-is-at-intersection-of-demographics-and-politics.html', 'snippet': 'Some Southern states are becoming more Democratic-leaning as new arrivals from the North move in. But this is not true in every state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The South is the fastest-growing region of the country, and Democrats are hoping that a flood of Northern expats and demographic change will allow them to turn red states to blue at a fast enough pace to counter the region’s growing share of the Electoral College.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Changing South Is at Intersection of Demographics and Politics', 'kicker': 'Migrations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T14:04:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0022fd0-f7e3-5c2d-b919-27ee76722353', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0022fd0-f7e3-5c2d-b919-27ee76722353'}, {'abstract': 'Armored vehicles aren’t themselves the problem.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/in-ferguson-focus-on-police-action-not-police-gear/', 'snippet': 'Armored vehicles aren’t themselves the problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The web is full of ridicule at the dark armor and military weaponry of the suburban St. Louis police officers, who have been confronting unarmed protesters over the last few days as if they were ISIS militants. The anger, however, is misplaced. The focus should not be on police gear, but on police conduct, which is increasingly appalling. The vast amount of tear gas fired just last night seemed wholly unjustified.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Ferguson, Focus on Police Action, Not Police Gear', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T14:09:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35aa1a0a-7ace-5a68-b24a-cbb52e6fadf6', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35aa1a0a-7ace-5a68-b24a-cbb52e6fadf6'}, {'abstract': 'What would children learn if we made them give away some of their favorite toys after a month? Maybe that ownership and appreciation aren’t linked.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/rent-a-toy-learn-a-lesson/', 'snippet': 'What would children learn if we made them give away some of their favorite toys after a month? Maybe that ownership and appreciation aren’t linked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What would children learn if we made them give away some of their favorite toys after a month?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/us/motherlode-pley/motherlode-pley-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarg