, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/10HUNT-MAIN/10HUNT-MAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/10HUNT-MAIN/10HUNT-MAIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suburbs: Been There, Done That.', 'kicker': 'The Hunt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suburbs: Been There, Done That.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Joyce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Columbus Circle (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7781b54c-4042-5172-b7c0-4e0f8bbd8639', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7781b54c-4042-5172-b7c0-4e0f8bbd8639'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty years ago, the Boston Globe journalist Farah Stockman worked at a camp for inner-city kids in Boston. Now she tracks some of her former campers down to see what their lives are like and what impact, if any, the camp made.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/checking-in-20-years-after-an-experiment-with-the-american-dream/', 'snippet': 'Twenty years ago, the Boston Globe journalist Farah Stockman worked at a camp for inner-city kids in Boston. Now she tracks some of her former campers down to see what their lives are like and what impact, if any, the camp made.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty years ago, a group of classmates from Harvard started a summer camp for children from Mission Hill, Boston. Farah Stockman, now a writer at The Boston Globe, was one of the students. “We didn’t know it at the time, but we were watching an experiment that tested the validity of the American dream for Boston’s poorest children.”\xa0Now Ms. Stockman has written a series, with a video, exploring what happened to the kids who attended the camp:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Checking In 20 Years After an Experiment With the American Dream', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T15:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Altman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8bcb3b9-dac6-5f29-aabd-c1c87b3226d6', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8bcb3b9-dac6-5f29-aabd-c1c87b3226d6'}, {'abstract': 'Two advertising campaigns use different marketing strategies. Is it better to make your audience feel empowered or inadequate?', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/what-sells-better-sexy-or-empowered/', 'snippet': 'Two advertising campaigns use different marketing strategies. Is it better to make your audience feel empowered or inadequate?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consider two advertising campaigns for women’s clothing: In one