d/middleeast/gaza-conflict-is-just-the-latest-round-in-a-long-war.html', 'snippet': 'Israel’s real problem is the instability from the failure to negotiate a sovereign Palestinian state and finally fix its borders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — As another round of warfare between Israel and Hamas may be ending, Israelis can feel as stuck, in different ways, as the Palestinians themselves. Because of course this is really just another round in the unresolved Arab-Israeli war of 1948-49.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/world/SUB-17GAZA/SUB-17GAZA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/world/SUB-17GAZA/SUB-17GAZA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/world/SUB-17GAZA/SUB-17GAZA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/world/SUB-17GAZA/SUB-17GAZA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/world/SUB-17GAZA/SUB-17GAZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/world/SUB-17GAZA/SUB-17GAZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/world/SUB-17GAZA/SUB-17GAZA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaza Conflict Is Just the Latest Round in a Long War', 'kicker': 'Letter From the Mideast', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Is Trapped in a War That Never Ended as Instability Persists at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T15:58:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c73370c5-083d-5ee2-8417-2c88e8668796', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c73370c5-083d-5ee2-8417-2c88e8668796'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to the Internet, exposing students to global issues and to experts who work on them has never been easier, and it frequently leads to learning that extends far beyond the classroom.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/engaging-in-global-issues-in-the-classroom-and-beyond/', 'snippet': 'Thanks to the Internet, exposing students to global issues and to experts who work on them has never been easier, and it frequently leads to learning that extends far beyond the classroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of the more than 8,000 class periods that I have taught, one stands out as my favorite\xa0— not only for what happened in the class but also for how it transformed my teaching. The class took place in the fall of 2004 and what strikes me about it now is how primitive it was by today’s technological standards. Indeed, the entire class consisted of the students sitting in a circle, staring at a speakerphone, and engaging in a dialogue about global health with a guest on the other end of the line. Fortunately for us, the guest was Dr. Paul Farmer, a path-breaking physician who co-founded the organization Partners in Health and who is the subject of a book the class had read, “Mountains Beyond Mountains.” For forty minutes, the students peppered Farmer with questions about Haiti, about how to best use one’s talents to address global health issues, and about how he had worked with Republicans and Democrats to ramp up global health funding.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/opinion/13kristof_jimkim/13kristof_jimkim-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/13/opinion/13kristof_jimkim/13kristof_jimkim-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/opinion/13kristof_jimkim/13kristof_jimkim-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/opinion/13kristof_jimkim/13kristof_jimkim-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1093, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/opinion/13kristof_jimkim/13kristof_jimkim-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/13/opinion/13kristof_jimkim/13kristof_jimkim-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/13/opinion/13kristof_jimkim/13kristof_jimkim-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Engaging in Global Issues in the Classroom and Beyond', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristof, Nicholas D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T16:21:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Cone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91bb102d-7959-51c2-bea5-2a1df17cb734', 'word_count': 1622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91bb102d-7959-51c2-bea5-2a1df17cb734'}, {'abstract': 'A state that grew rapidly for much its history is now finding that many of its residents are picking up and moving on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/upshot/the-california-exodus.html', 'snippet': 'A state that grew rapidly for much its history is now finding that many of its residents are picking up and moving on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'California has experienced rapid population growth for most of its history, but that trend has come to an end. California’s population grew by 2.9 percent over the last three years, only slightly above the nation’s 2.4 percent increase. Over the last few decades, millions of Californians have left the Golden State for opportunities elsewhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/upshot/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257-articleLarge.png', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/15/upshot/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/upshot/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257-jumbo.png', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/upshot/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1046, 'width': 1679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/upshot/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/15/upshot/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/upshot/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257/15up-california-chart1-1407873591257-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The California Exodus', 'kicker': 'Nation on the Move', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T16:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d2d6f8e-84af-50ba-b310-ddc0bc88019c', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d2d6f8e-84af-50ba-b310-ddc0bc88019c'}, {'abstract': 'A box set of music and an anniversary concert in Brooklyn will mark the label’s 30th anniversary.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/celebrating-30-years-of-def-jam/', 'snippet': 'A box set of music and an anniversary concert in Brooklyn will mark the label’s 30th anniversary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lots of college-age music fans dream about starting their own record labels, and a few make a go of it. Rick Rubin was one: in 1984, he and Russell Simmons started Def Jam Recordings in Mr. Rubin’s dorm room at New York University, and it quickly became an influential hip-hop and urban music imprint. This fall, the label – now part of the sprawling Universal Music Group – is celebrating its three-decade run with a limited-edition retrospective box, “Def Jam 30,” to be released on LP and CD on Sept. 16, and a concert that will bring together some of the label’s stars, past and present, at the Barclays Center, in Brooklyn, on Oct. 16.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating 30 Years of Def Jam', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrating 30 Years Of the Def Jam Label', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Def Jam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T16:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/834e2b4f-c035-589d-8a84-b13d8ba9279e', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/834e2b4f-c035-589d-8a84-b13d8ba9279e'}, {'abstract': 'Paired with other seasonal ingredients —\xa0Jonah crabs and corn — okra makes for a delicious summery taco filling.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/a-chef-in-the-field-okra/', 'snippet': 'Paired with other seasonal ingredients —\xa0Jonah crabs and corn — okra makes for a delicious summery taco filling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This series by the chef Jeff Schwarz and the photographer Greg Kessler traces the trajectory of seasonal food — from its original source to a place on your table.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chef in the Field | Okra', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAGANSETT (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T16:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Schwarz and Greg Kessler', 'person': [{