 in Inwood, there is scant evidence of the grating strain of foodie consciousness that has infiltrated American culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I moved to New York from the West Coast 20 years ago, but only this summer was I introduced to a little-known fact about the island of Manhattan: If you take the A train all the way to its northern terminus, you wind up in Seattle. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Emerald Atop Manhattan', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Emerald Atop Manhattan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Inwood (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian Road Cafe (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T18:04:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfe944fe-c0b7-5099-b626-025b75a078e5', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfe944fe-c0b7-5099-b626-025b75a078e5'}, {'abstract': 'Students who read and discussed a scene from Harry Potter in which the cruel Draco Malfoy calls Hermione a “filthy little Mudblood,” and her friends react with outrage reported more positive feelings about immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/14/harry-potter-casts-a-spell-for-tolerance/', 'snippet': 'Students who read and discussed a scene from Harry Potter in which the cruel Draco Malfoy calls Hermione a “filthy little Mudblood,” and her friends react with outrage reported more positive feelings about immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parents often seek diversity in their children’s classmates and playmates, and with good reason: The most direct way to discover that members of other groups are people just like us is to spend time learning, playing and talking with them. But there’s an additional, more subtle way of getting the same message across, by cultivating what might be called a diversity of the imagination. We do it whenever we read the Harry Potter novels with our kids.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/motherlode-hermione/motherlode-hermione-jumbo.png', 'height': 525, 'width': 431, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/motherlode-hermione/motherlode-hermione-superJumbo.png', 'height': 525, 'width': 431, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/motherlode-hermione/motherlode-hermione-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/14/us/motherlode-hermione/motherlode-hermione-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/us/motherlode-hermione/motherlode-hermione-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Harry Potter Casts a Spell for Tolerance', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {