ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a300b34-67f5-5a68-941e-11cad3601b05', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a300b34-67f5-5a68-941e-11cad3601b05'}, {'abstract': 'A doctor tells the Haggler that he spent 3 hours, 17 minutes trying to have AT&T adjust one month’s charges to his practice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/your-money/when-your-longest-call-is-the-one-to-correct-the-bill.html', 'snippet': 'A doctor tells the Haggler that he spent 3 hours, 17 minutes trying to have AT&T adjust one month’s charges to his practice.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Sorry,” Elton John sang years ago, “seems to be the hardest word.” The Haggler has always found this sentiment mystifying. “Sherbet.” Now there is a hard word. Everyone pronounces it “sherbert.” “Dilate” is a toughie. We all prefer “dialate” for some reason.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/business/17-HAGGLER/17-HAGGLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/business/17-HAGGLER/17-HAGGLER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/business/17-HAGGLER/17-HAGGLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/business/17-HAGGLER/17-HAGGLER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1193, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/business/17-HAGGLER/17-HAGGLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75,