’ Julius Thomas have given fantasy owners three difference-making options (along with existing stud Jimmy Graham of the New Orleans Saints) to choose from at the tight end position. While the Big 3 get most of the attention, the position, in fantasy terms, has gotten much deeper, thanks to the same N.F.L. passing trends that have expanded the field of quality quarterbacks and wide receivers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Football: Tight End Primer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gronkowski, Rob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Jimmy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Julius (1988- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T20:19:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Sablich and Justin Sablich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d6bc36d-cfb3-5777-9c96-94c1e986fde4', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d6bc36d-cfb3-5777-9c96-94c1e986fde4'}, {'abstract': 'In Ferguson, Mo., Police Chief Thomas Jackson called the city a “powder keg” as he appealed for calm amid ongoing protests over the police shooting death of Michael Brown, a black, unarmed teenager.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000003056419/ferguson-