 home to exhibitions like “Phoenix,” winged beasts from the artist Xu Bing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miser still remembers turning the corner at Broadway and 112th Street, near Columbia, years ago and being stunned by his first glimpse of the Cathedral Church of St. John the Divine. In a city full of massive and historic structures, the building’s sheer scale and neo-medieval aura manage to stand out. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cathedral of St. John the Divine Is a Gallery, Too', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cathedral of St. John the Divine Is a Gallery, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cathedral Church of St John the Divine (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xu Bing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T20:25:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49633c4c-cb28-5393-a53a-280f91481cc6', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49633c4c-cb28-5393-a53a-280f91481cc6'}, {'abstract': 'Who said friends have to be supportive of each other? The truth can have a bracing clarity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/fashion/have-i-told-you-lately-that-youre-crazy.html', 'snippet': 'Who said friends have to be supportive of each other? The truth can have a bracing clarity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some years ago a woman I knew told me she could levitate. She had been doing a good deal of meditation, and this was something you could supposedly work up to if you were really good, like throwing someone over your shoulder in the Lindy Hop.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MISINFORMED/17MISINFORMED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MISINFORMED/17MISINFORMED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MISINFORMED/17MISINFORMED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MISINFORMED/17MISINFORMED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MISINFORMED/17MISINFORMED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MISINFORMED/17MISINFORMED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MISINFORMED/17MISINFORMED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Have I Told You Lately That You’re Crazy?', 'kicker': 'I Was Misinformed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Have I Told You Lately That You’re Crazy?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wadler, Joyce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T20:33:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f1bc74c-0ff9-53bc-bded-3215982b4334', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f1bc74c-0ff9-53bc-bded-3215982b4334'}, {'abstract': 'Thom Andersen and Noël Burch’s film “Red Hollywood” makes a case for the quality of work by blacklisted filmmakers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/movies/red-hollywood-looks-at-work-by-blacklisted-filmmakers.html', 'snippet': 'Thom Andersen and Noël Burch’s film “Red Hollywood” makes a case for the quality of work by blacklisted filmmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Red Hollywood” may suggest the rivers of blood that flood our screens. But the red in the title of this fascinating essaylike movie refers to the home-front Communists and other American radicals — actual and accused — who once upon a Hollywood time made socially conscious movies that took on the world and its woes. These were true believers, like the fiery Abraham Polonsky who, with films like “Force of Evil” (1948), challenged reigning ideologies and at times cast pitch-black shadows over the scene to make class, race and sexual inequality all part of the big picture.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15REDHOLLYWOOD/15REDHOLLYWOOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy':