date': '2014-08-14T21:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b8e5cbb-adc1-53b7-aef6-70e5cd11bb89', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b8e5cbb-adc1-53b7-aef6-70e5cd11bb89'}, {'abstract': 'Answers to those pesky questions about social manners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/fashion/Social-Qs-a-fib-will-do.html', 'snippet': 'Answers to those pesky questions about social manners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My wife and I retired to a beautiful town on the coast of Maine. Many friends ask to visit, and most of their visits have been great. But one couple who came began negotiating with us as soon as they walked in the door: over dinner menus, the days’ activities, even our music selection. When they left, I told my wife: “Never again!” Now they’ve started asking for a return visit. I think we should tell them the truth: They were terrible guests. She disagrees. Any advice?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType':