er': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/835480c7-dc22-5d70-8e6a-1bc46a8da31d', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/835480c7-dc22-5d70-8e6a-1bc46a8da31d'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Fabian Almazan took his “Rhizome” project to the Village Vanguard, explaining how all music, like people, has commonalities under the surface.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/arts/music/fabian-almazan-takes-rhizome-project-to-village-vanguard.html', 'snippet': 'The pianist Fabian Almazan took his “Rhizome” project to the Village Vanguard, explaining how all music, like people, has commonalities under the surface.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around the midpoint of his first set at the Village Vanguard on Wednesday night, the pianist Fabian Almazan paused to explain the title of his most recent album, “Rhizome.” He touched on the botanical definition of the word, a rootstock from which multiple shoots typically emerge. Then he drew a parallel to humankind, saying that for all our differences, and “the violence in the world,” a core commonality lurks under the surface. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15FABIN1/15FABIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15FABIN1/15FABIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15FABIN1/15FABIN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15FABIN1/15FABIN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15FABIN1/15FABIN1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15FABIN1/15FABIN1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15FABIN1/15FABIN1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Worldly Music Branching Out From a Single Root', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Worldly Music Branching Out From a Single Root', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Village Vanguard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almazan, Fabian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-14T21:43:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c35663fe-545c-573a-a77c-232aa7cfce7c', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c35663fe-545c-573a-a77c-232aa7cfce7c'}, {'abstract': 'Data shows that extensions of unemployment benefits helped prevent mortgage defaults more than government programs focused on reducing monthly payments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/realestate/helping-prevent-foreclosures.html', 'snippet': 'Data shows that extensions of unemployment benefits helped prevent mortgage defaults more than government programs focused on reducing monthly payments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study finds that the emergency extensions of unemployment benefits during the recession went a long way toward preventing mortgage defaults, even more than government programs meant to prevent foreclosures by focusing only on reducing monthly payments. Researchers from the Federal Reserve Board of Governors, in Washington, and the Kellogg School of Management, at Northwestern University, estimate that between July 2008 and December 2012, the $250 billion paid out in federally funded unemployment benefits helped prevent an estimated 1.4 million foreclosures. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17mort/17mort-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17mort/17mort-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 298}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17mort/17mort-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 509, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17mort/17mort-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1439, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17mort/17mort-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandar