 that’s unleashed all too rarely in her role as a lovable misanthrope on “Parks and Recreation.” Sadly, playing a lusty, undead girlfriend in “Life After Beth” gives her even fewer opportunities to beam, but when she does, the whole film seems to slow down and soften.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15LIFE/15LIFE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15LIFE/15LIFE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 770}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15LIFE/15LIFE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15LIFE/15LIFE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15LIFE/15LIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15LIFE/15LIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/arts/15LIFE/15LIFE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'His Girlfriend Is Dead (Shh, Don’t Tell Her)', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life After Beth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywo