 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loprest, Frank James Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T02:08:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/091ba5fb-d5c0-5eaf-8e8b-9cefa3fa46a8', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/091ba5fb-d5c0-5eaf-8e8b-9cefa3fa46a8'}, {'abstract': 'The family of Ezell Ford, an unarmed black man who was shot and killed by Los Angeles police officers on Monday evening, plans to file a wrongful-death lawsuit against the Police Department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/us/california-police-to-face-suit-over-killing-of-unarmed-man.html', 'snippet': 'The family of Ezell Ford, an unarmed black man who was shot and killed by Los Angeles police officers on Monday evening, plans to file a wrongful-death lawsuit against the Police Department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The family of Ezell Ford, an unarmed black man who was shot and killed by Los Angeles police officers\xa0on Monday\xa0evening, plans to file a wrongful-death lawsuit against the Police Department, a lawyer for the family said\xa0Thursday. The lawyer, Steven A. Lerman, who also represented Rodney G. King after he was beaten by Los Angeles police in the 1990s, said that he expected to file a complaint this week, and that the circumstances surrounding the shooting in South Los Angeles remained unclear. Police officials have said that Mr. Ford tackled an officer who had stopped him and lunged for the officer’s gun, which was secured in his holster. The officer’s partner then shot Mr. Ford and the first officer reached for a backup weapon to shoot as well. Mr. Lerman said that the police could have easily used less lethal options on Mr. Ford, whose family said he had a mental illness. “They could have used a Taser, they could have wrestled him to the ground, they did not have to shoot right away,” Mr. Lerman said. Cmdr. Andrew Smith, a police spokesman, said that Mr. Ford had continued to walk as the police tried to stop him and tried to conceal his hands. Residents who said they witnessed the shooting told local news media that they had seen no sign that Mr. Ford put up a struggle. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Police to Face Suit Over Killing of Unarmed Man', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Police to Face Suit Over Killing of Unarmed Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Ezell Earl (1988-2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T02:17:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcdd0d0a-2aed-5af2-b82a-56c3314314cd', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcdd0d0a-2aed-5af2-b82a-56c3314314cd'}, {'abstract': 'A large rat has appeared around the Chelsea building for several months. But the creature, a common sight at union protests, is not against the search engine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/nyregion/ou