2014-08-15T10:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af700482-702d-585a-9252-78345a8fa450', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af700482-702d-585a-9252-78345a8fa450'}, {'abstract': 'Opinions on abusive police tactics in Ferguson, the U.S. strategy against ISIS, the “death tax” in Washington state, Saudi Arabia’s commitment to fighting terrorism and Airbnb in Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/morning-views-59/', 'snippet': 'Opinions on abusive police tactics in Ferguson, the U.S. strategy against ISIS, the “death tax” in Washington state, Saudi Arabia’s commitment to fighting terrorism and Airbnb in Canada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a “night that startled the nation with images of police overkill,” higher authorities “wisely stepped into” Ferguson, Missouri, says an editorial in The New York Times. The St. Louis suburb was rocked by an incident last Saturday, when a police officer shot Michael Brown, an unarmed 18-year-old. Residents held protests since the shooting, and were \xa0“countered by aggressive street policing by officers outfitted in war gear who too often veered toward provocation more than protection.” The local authorities have refused to identify the police officer who shot the teenager. “Residents have a right to know whether the officer has a record of reckless behavior,” and whether the officer lives in the community. Missouri Governor Jay Nixon said the protesters should be given the right to demonstrate, and that Ferguson “would become known ‘as a community that pulled together to overcome’ violence.” Bringing back a “sense of justice” will not be easy in the town where the majority of residents are black while the leadership is white, the editorial says. The authorities are warranted in responding “forcefully” to violence, but the “unyielding use of military tactics and abusive behavior” have widened the gap between them and the town’s residents. “Once the tear gas has dissipated, Mr. Nixon and Mr. Obama have an obligation to ensure that a real dialogue begins in Ferguson and other racially segregated areas, in hopes of keeping armored vehicles off the streets of America.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Views', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T10:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hanna Kozlowska', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozlowska', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d66aed4c-8c26-51ca-b992-eb55c3386e48', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d66aed4c-8c26-51ca-b992-eb55c3386e48'}, {'abstract': 'NATO and Ukraine said vehicles crossed into Ukraine and were destroyed by Ukrainian artillery fire, but it was unclear whether they were carrying separatists or Russian soldiers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/world/europe/ukraine-russia.html', 'snippet': 'NATO and Ukraine said vehicles crossed into Ukraine and were destroyed by Ukrainian artillery fire, but it was unclear whether they were carrying separatists or Russian soldiers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine — The government of Ukraine, pushing to oust pro-Russian rebels from their last enclaves in the east while nervously eyeing a stalled Russian aid convoy, said on Friday that its force had destroyed a number of Russian military vehicles that it said crossed into Ukraine late Thursday through a border area controlled by the separatists.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/world/16SUBUKRAINE/16SUBUKRAINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/16/world/16SUBUKRAINE/16SUBUKRAINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/world/16SUBUKRAINE/16SUBUKRAINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/world/16SUBUKRAINE/16SUBUKRAINE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/world/16SUBUKRAINE/16SUBUKRAINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/16/world/16SUBUKRAINE/16SUBUKRAINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/world/16SUBUKRAINE/16SUBUKRAINE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine, Eye on Convoy, Says It Hit Military Vehicles Coming From Russia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukraine, Eye on Convoy, Says It Hit Military Vehicles Coming From Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Higgins, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Vehicles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T10:16:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6758e562-5451-5963-a130-2c8ea36554a1', 'word_count': 1298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6758e562-5451-5963-a130-2c8ea36554a1'}, {'abstract': 'Tens of thousands of opposition supporters converged on the capital in an attempt to force Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif to resign after just 14 months in office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/world/asia/pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'Tens of thousands of opposition supporters converged on the capital in an attempt to force Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif to resign after just 14 months in office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Tens of thousands of opposition supporters, led by a former cricket star, Imran Khan, and a cleric, Muhammad Tahir-ul Qadri, converged on the Pakistani capital late Friday for what they billed as an extended protest movement to oust Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' Opposition in Pakistan Is Drenched but Not Doused ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opposition in Pakistan Is Drenched but Not Doused', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major'