esse Wegman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wegman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acfefe09-a899-56fa-9268-5affae4fd30e', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acfefe09-a899-56fa-9268-5affae4fd30e'}, {'abstract': 'After the discovery of suspicious accounting at a film affiliate, investors in Alibaba’s initial public offering may be less confident about the company’s investment binge, writes John Foley of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/alibabas-deal-spree-turns-from-romance-to-thriller/', 'snippet': 'After the discovery of suspicious accounting at a film affiliate, investors in Alibaba’s initial public offering may be less confident about the company’s investment binge, writes John Foley of Reuters Breakingviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alibaba’s investment story has turned from romance to thriller. Its Hong Kong movie-making affiliate has uncovered “possibly noncompliant” accounting just four months after the Chinese e-commerce giant bought a 60 percent stake. It’s not clear whether Alibaba’s controls were flawed, but it certainly raises questions about the value of the company’s recent investment binge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/business/dbpix-alibaba2/dbpix-alibaba2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/15/business/dbpix-alibaba2/dbpix-alibaba2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/business/dbpix-alibaba2/dbpix-alibaba2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/business/dbpix-alibaba2/dbpix-alibaba2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1052, 'width': 1578, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/business/dbpix-alibaba2/dbpix-alibaba2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/15/business/dbpix-alibaba2/dbpix-alibaba2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/business/dbpix-alibaba2/dbpix-alibaba2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alibaba’s Deal Spree Turns From Romance to Thriller', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ma, Jack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alibaba Group Holding Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T14:08:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Foley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Foley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00f5c2af-0faa-5353-a59f-3400f