iew', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/241214d0-4c40-53ac-a068-6671ce28fd9d', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/241214d0-4c40-53ac-a068-6671ce28fd9d'}, {'abstract': 'In their exploration of mortality and desire, William T. Vollmann’s stories often inhabit supernatural realms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/books/review/william-t-vollmanns-last-stories-and-other-stories.html', 'snippet': 'In their exploration of mortality and desire, William T. Vollmann’s stories often inhabit supernatural realms.', 'lead_paragraph': '“This is my final book.” So begins “Last Stories and Other Stories,” by William T. Vollmann, and, if you take the claim at face value — since Vollmann offers no reason not to — so ends the miraculous career of a leading fabulist.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-BERNHEIMER/0817-bks-BERNHEIMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-BERNHEIMER/0817-bks-BERNHEIMER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 685}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-BERNHEIMER/0817-bks-BERNHEIMER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 897, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-BERNHEIMER/081