 companies have a new proposition: Let them track every second of your driving in exchange for an annual discount that can reach into the hundreds of dollars if you behave yourself on the road.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/your-money/16money-illo/16money-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/16/your-money/16money-illo/16money-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/your-money/16money-illo/16money-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/your-money/16money-illo/16money-illo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1458, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/your-money/16money-illo/16money-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/16/your-money/16money-illo/16money-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/your-money/16money-illo/16money-illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lower Your Car Insurance Bill, at the Price of Some Privacy', 'kicker': 'Your Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Safety Spies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieber, Ron', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Progressive Casualty Insurance Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Farm Insurance Cos', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALLSTATE CORP', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T14:56:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Insurance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/400a6e89-c208-56c9-b3c0-7f516b954cc0', 'word_count': 1546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/400a6e89-c208-56c9-b3c0-7f516b954cc0'}, {'abstract': 'In 1928, two brothers head to Africa to collect film footage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/books/review/o-africa-by-andrew-lewis-conn.html', 'snippet': 'In 1928, two brothers head to Africa to collect film footage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Bogle’s seminal history of African-Americans in film, “Toms, Coons, Mulattoes, Mammies, and Bucks,” starts like this: “In the beginning, there was an Uncle Tom. A former mechanic photographed him in a motion picture that ran no longer than 12 minutes. And a new dimension was added to American movies. . . . Uncle Tom himself. He was the American movies’ first black character.” Thus the fraught, complex and sometimes heartbreaking relationship between blacks, whites and moviemaking began.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-Southgate/0817-bks-Southgate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-Southgate/0817-bks-Southgate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 743}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-Southgate/0817-bks-Southgate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 654, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-Southgate/0817-bks-Southgate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 654, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-Southgate/0817-bks-Southgate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-Southgate/0817-bks-Southgate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/review/0817-bks-Southgate/0817-bks-Southgate-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Black and White', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Black and White', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'O, Africa! (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conn, Andrew Lewis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T14:58:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Southgate', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southgate', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/91552788-16b7-536f-839b-ff0f7d4fc683', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91552788-16b7-536f-839b-ff0f7d4fc683'}, {'abstract': 'An unfaithful artist attempts to win back his wife’s affection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/books/review/courtney-maums-i-am-having-so-much-fun-here-without-you.html', 'snippet': 'An unfaithful artist attempts to win back his wife’s affection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The protagonist of Courtney Maum’s debut novel, “I Am Having So Much Fun Here Without You,” is really, truly hard to like. Richard Haddon is a British artist living in Paris, and when we meet him we learn quickly that he has just compromised his artistic principles to sell palatable, décor-friendly paintings, and that he has recently cheated on his beautiful French wife, Anne-Laure, with whom he has a relatively happy marriage and a young daughter. Richard’s affair — not a one-off drunken mistake, but rather a serious monthslong “I wish I could leave my wife for you” kind of thing — ended only because she left him.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cheat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cheat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'I Am Having So Much Fun Here Without You (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maum, Courtney', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T14:58:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Haley Tanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Haley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0535c499-5d91-59ae-afcc-86a18ba99ed8', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0535c499-5d91-59ae-afcc-86a18ba99ed8'}, {'abstract': 'A study of Winston Churchill’s contradictions and passions and his long relationship with empire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/books/review/churchill-and-empire-by-lawrence-james.html', 'snippet': 'A study of Winston Churchill’s contradictions and passions and his long relationship with empire.', 'lead_paragraph': '“To paraphrase Winston Churchill,” Ronald Reagan said in his first Inaugural Address, “I did not take the oath I’ve just taken with the intention of presiding over the dissolution of the world’s strongest economy.” If it was curious that an American president should cite an English politician, what made it odder was the line he chose to adapt.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17WHEATCROFT/17WHEATCROFT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 856, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17WHEATCROFT/17WHEATCROFT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 856}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17WHEATCROFT/17WHEATCROFT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 718, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17WHEATCROFT/17WHEATCROFT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1436, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17WHEATCROFT/17WHEATCROFT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17WHEATCROFT/17WHEATCROFT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17WHEATCROFT/17WHEATCROFT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Imperial Son', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Imperial Son', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Churchill and Empire: A Portrait of an Imperialist (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheatcroft, Geoffrey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Lawrence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Churchill, Winston Leonard Spencer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T14:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoffrey Wheatcroft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheatcroft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a051c12b-f31b-519b-b879-50056888e6b5', 'word_count': 1273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a051c12b-f31b-519b-b879-50056888e6b5'}, {'abstract': 'An attempt to save a marriage proves fatal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/books/review/life-drawing-by-robin-black.html', 'snippet': 'An attempt to save a marriage proves fatal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Punishment and penance for marital infidelity can take many forms, and on the face of it, the means by which a painter named Gus (short for Augusta) Edelman, the narrator of Robin Black’s first novel, is paying for the sin of cheating on her husband — a retreat to an isolated house in the country — has a certain amount of appeal, at least to creative types like them. It’s Yaddo with no company but their own.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17POLS/17POLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17POLS/17POLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 858}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17POLS/17POLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 717, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17POLS/17POLS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1433, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/books/17POLS/17POLS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width