': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/16UP-Beschloss/16UP-Beschloss-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/16UP-Beschloss/16UP-Beschloss-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 475}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/16UP-Beschloss/16UP-Beschloss-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 810, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/16UP-Beschloss/16UP-Beschloss-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1620, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/16UP-Beschloss/16UP-Beschloss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/16UP-Beschloss/16UP-Beschloss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/14/upshot/16UP-Beschloss/16UP-Beschloss-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kennedy, L.B.J. and a Disputed Deer Hunt', 'kicker': 'HistorySource', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kennedy, Johnson and a Dispute After a Deer Hunt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beschloss, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manchester, William', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deer', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Beschloss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beschloss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Web Log', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a4fd8fc-2b56-543a-b7d1-e097e6705447', 'word_count': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a4fd8fc-2b56-543a-b7d1-e097e6705447'}, {'abstract': 'As a Ukrainian family adapts to life in Brooklyn, memories of the old country linger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/books/review/panic-in-a-suitcase-by-yelena-akhtiorskaya.html', 'snippet': 'As a Ukrainian family adapts to life in Brooklyn, memories of the old country linger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yelena Akhtiorskaya’s impressive debut novel, “Panic in a Suitcase,” considers the precarious position of émigrés \xadtrying to build a life in America — specifically, Ukrainian émigrés trying to build a life in Brooklyn’s Brighton Beach. Set there and in Odessa, Ukraine, the novel spans 15 years in the lives of the Nasmertov family. It opens in 1993 as Pasha, the only remaining family member in Odessa, visits Brighton Beach to see his cancer-stricken mother, the matriarch of the family. Pasha — sometimes called “the greatest poet not just in Odessa and not in all of Ukraine but in all of Russia” — is a beacon for his family, much to the curiosity of his young niece, Frida. Though the first half of the novel centers on the family’s attempt to coerce Pasha into moving to America, this beautifully drawn portrait of a splintered \xadimmigrant family is also about young \xadFrida and her struggle to assimilate. Akhtiorskaya layers the novel with equal parts humor and anxiety, and expertly highlights the unease of having one foot in and one foot out of the old country. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Assimilation Required', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some Assimilation Required', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Panic in a Suitcase (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akhtiorskaya, Yelena', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T15:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karolina Waclawiak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karolina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waclawiak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/35eb251c-e7fd-5a01-8dfe-aebdcc03b5cb', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35eb251c-e7fd-5a01-8dfe-aebdcc03b5cb'}, {'abstract': 'For some New Yorkers, sharing an apartment with others is a choice, not a necessity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/realestate/sharing-a-new-york-apartment-by-choice.html', 'snippet': 'For some New Yorkers, sharing an apartment with others is a choice, not a necessity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the eight years that she was based in Chicago, Katie Kirby happily lived by herself. When she moved to Manhattan three years ago, there didn’t seem to be any reason for a different domestic arrangement, and she contentedly signed on for a one-bedroom on the Upper West Side.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17COVER1SUB/17COVER1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17COVER1SUB/17COVER1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17COVER1SUB/17COVER1SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17COVER1SUB/17COVER1SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17COVER1SUB/17COVER1SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17COVER1SUB/17COVER1SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/realestate/17COVER1SUB/17COVER1SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Buddy System', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Buddy System', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': N