 None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f924497e-ef06-5d87-ad45-b75a502e2ccc', 'word_count': 1551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f924497e-ef06-5d87-ad45-b75a502e2ccc'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking to patch holes in her family history, the author travels to Aruba, her father’s childhood home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/travel/on-an-island-hunt-for-pieces-of-my-history.html', 'snippet': 'Seeking to patch holes in her family history, the author travels to Aruba, her father’s childhood home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We had been in the lobby of our hotel in Oranjestad, Aruba’s capital, for only a few minutes when the Dutch territory’s Arcadian “One Happy Island” front was shattered by a desk clerk whose petulance hit me like a left hook straight to the temple. As she delivered the rules and regulations like a stern lecture, scolding my daughter and me for the simple offense of standing before her, my mind drifted back home to New York City. There I was, at Mendez Boxing gym, and there she was, standing in place of my favorite heavy bag. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/travel/17-personal-top/17-personal-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/travel/17-personal-top/17-personal-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 456}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/travel/17-personal-top/17-personal-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/t