b8-5d8b-8686-5882ddf22622'}, {'abstract': 'Despite changing ownership and locations several times since its opening in 1932, Egger’s Ice Cream Parlor, on Staten Island’s north shore, remains a great beacon of the classic cone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/nyregion/a-one-shake-two-straws-kind-of-place.html', 'snippet': 'Despite changing ownership and locations several times since its opening in 1932, Egger’s Ice Cream Parlor, on Staten Island’s north shore, remains a great beacon of the classic cone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most summer afternoons at Egger’s Ice Cream Parlor on Staten Island’s north shore unfold in the same way. Spoons clank against ice cream bowls, customers chat about birthday parties and coming T-ball games, and the heady scent of hot fudge perfumes the place. In a city of $7 milkshakes and extravagant flavors like black sesame seaweed or tarragon pink pepper, Egger’s remains a great beacon of the classic cone.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A One-Shake, Two-Straws Kind of Place', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A One-Shake, Two-Straws Kind of Place', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Egger's Ice Cream Parlor (Staten Island, NY)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koenig, Leah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Cream and Frozen Desserts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Port Richmond (Staten Island, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T17:16:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Koenig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koenig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff04951e-98d9-5bd8-9cfd-f080f5de0395', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff04951e-98d9-5bd8-9cfd-f080f5de0395'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s randomly generated Senate election simulation, some surprises along the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/upshot/taking-a-spin-how-democrats-could-keep-their-majority.html', 'snippet': 'In this week’s randomly generated Senate election simulation, some surprises along the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democrats hold on to the Senate by the skin of their teeth by winning Arkansas in this week’s spin of Leo’s Senate wheels. Every week we generate random election scenarios based on the probabilities from the Upshot’s Senate elections forecasting model.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/upshot/16up-spin-image/16up-spin-image-articleLarge.png', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/16/upshot/16up-spin-image/16up-spin-image-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/upshot/16up-spin-image/16up-spin-image-jumbo.png', 'height': 639, 'width': 1016, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/upshot/16up-spin-image/16up-spin-image-superJumbo.png', 'height': 639, 'width': 1016, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/upshot/16up-spin-image/16up-spin-image-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType'