are best held at arm’s length.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/nyregion/an-education-in-keeping-new-york-clean-and-keeping-themselves-safe.html', 'snippet': 'A new class of sanitation workers learns how to drive garbage trucks and grapple with snow chains, and why trash bags are best held at arm’s length.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rose-gold light was falling onto Jamaica Bay and sea gulls passed overhead on another beautiful morning at Floyd Bennett Field in Brooklyn, a far reach of New York City mostly devoid of New Yorkers and cars.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At This Academy, the Curriculum Is Garbage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At This Academy, the Curriculum Is Garbage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanitation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schlossberg, Tatiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vocational Training', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T18:34:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tatiana Schlossberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tatiana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schlossberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cf37515-4c77-5d47-a642-ce6a0f6b8c75', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cf37515-4c77-5d47-a642-ce6a0f6b8c75'}, {'abstract': 'Buying a piece of Monster is a capitulation of sorts, though Coca-Cola hasn’t caved in financially, Kevin Allison of Reuters Breakingviews writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/coke-finds-right-formula-in-monster-deal/', 'snippet': 'Buying a piece of Monster is a capitulation of sorts, though Coca-Cola hasn’t caved in financially, Kevin Allison of Reuters Breakingviews writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coca-Cola, the $180 billion soda giant, is paying $2.2 billion for 17 percent of Monster Beverage, a maker of trendy energy drinks. It goes to show how even a global powerhouse with significant distribution and marketing advantages can struggle to keep ahead of upstart rivals. At least Coke got the deal formula right.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/business/dbpix-monster/dbpix-monster-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/16/business/dbpix-monster/dbpix-monster-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/business/dbpix-monster/dbpix-monster-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/business/dbpix-monster/dbpix-monster-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/business/dbpix-monster/dbpix-monster-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/16/business/dbpix-monster/dbpix-monster-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u