mes.com/2014/08/16/upshot/mapping-migration-in-the-united-states-since-1900.html', 'snippet': 'An interactive map showing nationwide migration patterns in the United States since 1900.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, we published a series of interactive charts showing how Americans have moved between states since 1900. The charts show striking patterns for many states: You can trace the rise of migrant and immigrant populations all along the Southwest, particularly in Texas and Arizona; the influx of New Yorkers and other Northeasterners into Florida starting in the 1970s; and the growth in the Southern share of the Illinois population during the Great Migration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mapping Migration in the United States', 'kicker': 'Nation on the Move', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T18:51:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregor Aisch and Robert Gebeloff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aisch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gebeloff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0070c87d-1616-546f-a6d9-dc9a391a6779', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0070c87d-1616-546f-a6d9-dc9a391a6779'}, {'abstract': 'Because A