ct', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sharks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discovery Channel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T19:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Flanagin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flanagin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e243a1c-3c5e-58d3-be90-a2f3e01107d7', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e243a1c-3c5e-58d3-be90-a2f3e01107d7'}, {'abstract': 'The online dictionary added new terms inspired by popular culture and online usage.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/oxford-dictionary-recognizes-yolo-amazeballs-and-hot-mess/', 'snippet': 'The online dictionary added new terms inspired by popular culture and online usage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Oxford Dictionaries will include YOLO – an acronym for “you only live once,” popularized by Drake in his 2011 song, “The Motto” – in the quarterly update of its online dictionary, released this week. And though the list is heavy with science and technology terms – clickbait, listicle and pharmacovigilance (monitoring drugs after they are approved for use) – several entries are arguably arts-related.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oxford Dictionary Recognizes: YOLO, Amazeballs and Hot Mess', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dictionaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oxford University Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T19:03:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdab12d2-82f4-5fca-bc40-3cb0bcbb528e', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdab12d2-82f4-5fca-bc40-3cb0bcbb528e'}, {'abstract': 'Valerie and Clark Tate’s wedding took place in 2000, and while they “unhitched” in 2007, they remain legally married, share a home and are raising their son together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/fashion/weddings/together-on-the-road-to-divorce.html', 'snippet': 'Valerie and Clark Tate’s wedding took place in 2000, and while they “unhitched” in 2007, they remain legally married, share a home and are raising their son together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Valerie and Clark Tate’s wedding took place in 2000, and although they “unhitched” in 2007, they remain legally married, share a home and are raising their son, Jonah, together. Both have other romantic relationships. With their rabbi, they are preparing for a Jewish divorce in the fall that they view as a “spiritual divorce.” Both acknowledge a legally binding divorce may be ahead. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17UNHITCHED/0817-UNHITCHED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17UNHITCHED/0817-UNHITCHED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17UNHITCHED/0817-UNHITCHED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17UNHITCHED/0817-UNHITCHED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17UNHITCHED/0817-UNHITCHED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17UNHITCHED/0817-UNHITCHED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17UNHITCHED/0817-UNHITCHED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Together on the Road to Divorce', 'kicker': 'Unhitched', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Together on the Road to Divorce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rafkin, Louise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T19:04:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Louise Rafkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Louise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rafkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/377ff2eb-0e67-502d-82c2-fec6fe29c6a1', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/377ff2eb-0e67-502d-82c2-fec6fe29c6a1'}, {'abstract': 'The dispute between Amazon and Hachette has caused the usually reticent retailer start talking but made the publisher shut up. Some of the best commentary is coming from authors in the middle.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/amazon-its-friends-and-critics/', 'snippet': 'The dispute between Amazon and Hachette has caused the usually reticent retailer start talking but made the publisher shut up. Some of the best commentary is coming from authors in the middle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The exact nature of the conflict between Amazon and Hachette is somewhat veiled. The parties confirm that it is over e-book prices, and Amazon obviously wants more money from the sale of e-books than Hachette is willing to give. But Hachette has been circumspect, while Amazon has been forceful if not always accurate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/business/15bits-amazon/15bits-amazon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/15/business/15bits-amazon/15bits-amazon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/business/15bits-amazon/15bits-amazon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 627, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/business/15bits-amazon/15bits-amazon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1253, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'su