n.html', 'snippet': 'Mike Bindra and Laura de Palma, who run the festival, where two attendees died in drug-related episodes last year, are in the middle of a discussion within the world of electronic dance music about how to stem the tide of drugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With three weeks left until thousands of raver babies dressed in neon spandex descend on Electric Zoo, New York’s largest dance music festival, Mike Bindra and Laura de Palma were running through their checklists in a state of high anxiety. The load-in for their giant show was about to begin. In a few days’ time, six performance stages — the biggest serving 30,000 fans — would spring up in a field on Randalls Island. Crates of pyrotechnics, trucks of LED screens and a stadium’s worth of subwoofers would soon be coming in.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ELECTRIC2ALT/17ELECTRIC2ALT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ELECTRIC2ALT/17ELECTRIC2ALT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 477}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ELECTRIC2ALT/17ELECTRIC2ALT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ELECTRIC2ALT/17ELECTRIC2ALT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 1719, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ELECTRIC2ALT/17ELECTRIC2ALT-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ELECTRIC2ALT/17ELECTRIC2ALT-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ELECTRIC2ALT/17ELECTRIC2ALT-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Year After Drug Deaths, the Electric Zoo Music Festival Tries Again', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zookeepers of the Rave', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Zoo Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feuer, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bindra, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Palma, Laura', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ecstasy (Drug)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Randalls Island (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T19:09:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12046d8-7f94-5a87-9016-49318bd4545d', 'word_count': 2560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12046d8-7f94-5a87-9016-49318bd4545d'}, {'abstract': 'The stylist and owner of the Amagansett boutique Tiina is debuting limited editions of four of the knitwear brand’s styles in striated shades of natural indigo.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/tiina-laakkonen-elder-statesman-collaboration/', 'snippet': 'The stylist and owner of the Amagansett boutique Tiina is debuting limited editions of four of the knitwear brand’s styles in striated shades of natural indigo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As anyone familiar with her styling work, her Amagansett, N.Y.,\xa0boutique, Tiina, or her\xa0nearby home already knows, Tiina Laakkonen really, really loves indigo. “Blue is my favorite color and indigo is the most natural, alive version of it,” she says. “I used to live in black clothes when I lived in New York, but they seem too hard in both the light and the life out East.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/t-magazine/15tiina-hartman/15tiina-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/15/t-magazine/15tiina-hartman/15tiina-hartman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/t-magazine/15tiina-hartman/15tiina-hartman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/t-magazine/15tiina-hartman/15tiina-hartman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/t-magazine/15tiina-hartman/15tiina-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/15/t-magazine/15tiina-hartman/15tiina-hartman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/15/t-magazine/15tiina-hartman/15tiina-hartman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Tiina Laakkonen and the Elder Statesman, Blue Is the Warmest Color', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chait, Greg', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laakkonen, Tiina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elder Statesman', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAGANSETT (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T19:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48a752e2-a26b-539c-9902-4761462ce197', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48a752e2-a26b-539c-9902-4761462ce197'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re thinking about helping with the finances of a Broadway production, here are some rules to keep in mind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/theater/rules-for-investing-in-a-broadway-production.html', 'snippet': 'If you’re thinking about helping with the finances of a Broadway production, here are some rules to keep in mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Broadway shows often