type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46e04373-583b-5823-8814-be5f1fd8029f', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46e04373-583b-5823-8814-be5f1fd8029f'}, {'abstract': 'When he was 13, the first record Benjamin Booker ever bought was “Elephant” by the White Stripes. The singer-guitarist, now 25, is the opening act on Jack White’s current tour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/arts/music/benjamin-booker-on-opening-for-jack-white.html', 'snippet': 'When he was 13, the first record Benjamin Booker ever bought was “Elephant” by the White Stripes. The singer-guitarist, now 25, is the opening act on Jack White’s current tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first record Benjamin Booker ever bought was “Elephant” by the White Stripes, which came out when he was in eighth grade. “When I was 13 it was, like, the coolest,” he recalled. Now 25, Mr. Booker, the singer-guitarist, was recently plucked to be the opening act on Jack White’s current tour, though he had only written 12 songs in his entire life. It’s just part of the dizzying whirlwind that’s enveloped Mr. Booker this summer — from TV appearances with David Letterman and Conan O’Brien to being named one of the “most refreshing” rock acts at Lollapalooza by Rolling Stone — ahead of the release of his self-titled debut album, due out Tuesday on ATO Records.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/arts/17SNAPSHOT/17SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1318, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/arts/17SNAPSHOT/17SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1318}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/arts/17SNAPSHOT/17SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 