urs early. It also allows for more listening — car windows that would be rolled up to protect against frigid weather are cracked, the music playing on dashboard radios or from phones connected to speakers turned up just loud enough to float into the street. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sunday-review/0817MUSIC/0817MUSIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/sunday-review/0817MUSIC/0817MUSIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 598}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sunday-review/0817MUSIC/0817MUSIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sunday-review/0817MUSIC/0817MUSIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2040, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sunday-review/0817MUSIC/0817MUSIC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/sunday-review/0817MUSIC/0817MUSIC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sunday-review/0817MUSIC/0817MUSIC-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Real Song of the Summer', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Real Song of the Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnston, Maura', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T20:54:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maura Johnston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e92f46f-e701-5411-a934-20e6246f1130', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e92f46f-e701-5411-a934-20e6246f1130'}, {'abstract': 'Great Muscadet can be a complex treat, offering an almost tactile expression of the earth in which the grapes were grown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/dining/muscadet-a-great-value-isnt-getting-its-due.html', 'snippet': 'Great Muscadet can be a complex treat, offering an almost tactile expression of the earth in which the grapes were grown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GORGES, France — The gently rolling green hills paint a picture of pastoral simplicity here in Muscadet country, about 15 miles southeast of the city of Nantes, near to where the Loire empties into the Atlantic. The placid surface belies the complex clash of soils underneath, where multiple forms of granite, clay, schist and metamorphic descendants of granite (like gneiss and orthogneiss) turn most discussions with grape growers into detailed geology lessons. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/dining/20POUR1/20POUR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/20/dining/20POUR1/20POUR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/dining/20POUR1/20POUR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/dining/20POUR1/20POUR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1341, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/dining/20POUR1/20POUR1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/20/dining/20POUR1/20POUR1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/dining/20POUR1/20POUR1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Muscadet Just Doesn’t Get Its Due', 'kicker': 'The Pour', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Muscadet Just Doesn’t Get Its Due', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T20:59:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'ran