material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f5b8a32-c16c-50d0-ae8e-a2e401f36114', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f5b8a32-c16c-50d0-ae8e-a2e401f36114'}, {'abstract': 'The millennials are emerging as a dominant demographic force. What does that mean for the rest of us?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/fashion/the-millennials-are-generation-nice.html', 'snippet': 'The millennials are emerging as a dominant demographic force. What does that mean for the rest of us?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suddenly, as you may have noticed, millennials are everywhere. Not that this group of people born after 1980 and before 2000 — a giant cohort now estimated to number at least 80 million Americans, more than the baby boom generation — was ever invisible. What’s changed is their status. Coddled and helicoptered, catered to by 24-hour TV cable networks, fussed over by marketers and college recruiters, dissected by psychologists, demographers and trend-spotters, the millennial generation has come fully into its own. The word “millennial,” whether as noun or adjective, has monopolized the nonstop cultural conversation, invariably freighted with zeitgeisty import.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-copy/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-copy/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 669}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-copy/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 919, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-copy/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1838, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-copy/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-copy/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-copy/17MILLENNIALS_COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Generation Nice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Generation Nice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanenhaus, Sam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T21:08:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Tanenhaus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanenhaus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7bbf884-7bdc-59e3-890d-018add7651dc', 'word_count': 1759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7bbf884-7bdc-59e3-890d-018add7651dc'}, {'abstract': 'For American children, team sports have become an untamed behemoth, gradually colonizing weeknights, weekends, religious holidays and now vacations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/fashion/team-sports-are-taking-over-kids-lives.html', 'snippet': 'For American children, team sports have become an untamed behemoth, gradually colonizing weeknights, weekends, religious holidays and now vacations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my daughters were young, they had a book we all loved called “Jump into January.” Every month was illustrated with a search-and-find painting filled with seasonal items. August’s was “Sail into August / come along with me / That sand is soft, the sea is warm / What can you see?” Items included a sailboat, shovel, crab, hammock, surfboard and sand castle.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17THISLIFE/17THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 203, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17THISLIFE/17THISLIFE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 203}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17THISLIFE/17THISLIFE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17THISLIFE/17THISLIFE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1950, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17THISLIFE/17THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17THISLIFE/17THISLIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/fashion/17THISLIFE/17THISLIFE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s No Off in This Season', 'kicker': 'This Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'There’s No Off in This Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feiler, Bruce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T21:10:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Feiler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feiler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d21f99b3-6209-541f-8a96-25d7b0c2191d', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d21f99b3-6209-541f-8a96-25d7b0c2191d'}, {'abstract': 'Porter Robinson, a 22-year-old D.J. from Chapel Hill, N.C., is reaching past electronic dance music in his first full-length album.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/arts/music/porter-robinson-releases-worlds-his-first-album.html', 'snippet': 'Porter Robinson, a 22-year-old D.J. from Chapel Hill, N.C., is reaching past electronic dance music in his first full-length album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2010 an 18-year-old unknown named Porter Robinson began turning heads on the electronic dance scene for his spastic, high-octane production. Now Mr. Robinson is a star of electronic dance music, or E.D.M., but the sounds that appear on his first full-length album, “Worlds” (Astralwerks), released on Tuesday, would no doubt be puzzling to many of his fist-pumping boosters. After several years of performing at bacchanalian festivals like Ultra and Electric Daisy Carnival, Mr. Robinson has rejected that mind-set and the head rush of adrenaline that currently dominates the scene. On “Worlds,” he has opted instead for washes of gorgeous textures, contemplative storytelling and remarkably sharp melodies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16PORTER/16PORTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16PORTER/16PORTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16PORTER/16PORTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16PORTER/16PORTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16PORTER/16PORTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 7