nk': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barneys New York', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BeachMint', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lucky Magazine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ModCloth Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opening Ceremony LLC', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T22:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Gregory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gregory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d2109ce-0612-56c3-a3ae-a3c13fd66f99', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d2109ce-0612-56c3-a3ae-a3c13fd66f99'}, {'abstract': 'The food retailer, based in Minnesota, said that it had been able to prevent the breach from affecting all its locations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/technology/food-retailer-discloses-a-data-breach.html', 'snippet': 'The food retailer, based in Minnesota, said that it had been able to prevent the breach from affecting all its locations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Supervalu, a food retailer based in Minnesota, said on Thursday that its cash register system had been breached by hackers, possibly resulting in the theft of credit and debit card information from its supermarkets and liquor stores, as well as from an array of stores it sold last year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supervalu Discloses a Data Breach', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Food Retailer Discloses a Data Breach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SUPERVALU INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identity Theft', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T22:12:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fbd667b-550e-5f7a-8e17-557649a177fb', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fbd667b-550e-5f7a-8e17-557649a177fb'}, {'abstract': 'The Stratford Festival presents an opportunity to relate the themes of Shakespeare’s seldom-staged history play “King John” to those of “King Lear.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/theater/king-john-and-king-lear-at-the-stratford-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Stratford Festival presents an opportunity to relate the themes of Shakespeare’s seldom-staged history play “King John” to those of “King Lear.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'STRATFORD, Ontario — “King Lear” and “King John” reside at opposite ends of the Shakespeare canon. One is at the pinnacle, considered by many his greatest masterwork and produced about as frequently as any of his plays. The other scuttles around furtively somewhere far beneath, poking its oddly shaped head up for public consideration only rarely. (I probably don’t need to tell you which is which.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16STRATFORD2/16STRATFORD2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16STRATFORD2/16STRATFORD2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16STRATFORD2/16STRATFORD2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16STRATFORD2/16STRATFORD2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16STRATFORD2/16STRATFORD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16STRATFORD2/16STRATFORD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/arts/16STRATFORD2/16STRATFORD2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Contrast of Kings: Ubiquitous and Rare', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Contrast of Kings: Ubiquitous and Rare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stratford Shakespeare Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'King John (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'King Lear (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T22:14:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c871f804-8ee9-5bed-ac00-fcf4dd6afaa4', 'word_count': 1142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c871f804-8ee9-5bed-ac00-fcf4dd6afaa4'}, {'abstract': 'On Sundays, Ms. Monk, the composer, singer, director and choreographer, spends some time rehearsing, but also makes time for family and her box tortoise. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/nyregion/meredith-monk-tune-body-and-voice-feed-the-tortoise.html', 'snippet': 'On Sundays, Ms. Monk, the composer, singer, director and choreographer, spends some time rehearsing, but also makes time for family and her box tortoise. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Meredith Monk, the composer, singer, director, choreographer, Buddhist practitioner and inveterate boundary pusher, will celebrate the 50th anniversary of her career this fall with performances at the Brooklyn Academy of Music and Carnegie Hall. A taste of what’s to come is offered on Aug. 23 at Guild Hall in East Hampton, Long Island, where she will perform with her Grammy-nominated Vocal Ensemble. When Ms. Monk, 71, moved into her West Broadway loft 42 years ago, visitors had to call from a pay phone, after which she would toss down a sock with a key in it. These days she has a buzzer and an elevator.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE3/17ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE3/17ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE3/17ROUTINE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE3/17ROUTINE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE3/17ROUTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE3/17ROUTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/nyregion/17ROUTINE3/17ROUTINE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Meredith Monk: Tune Body and Voice. Feed the Tortoise.', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tune Body and Voice. Feed the Tortoise.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monk, Meredith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shattuck, Kathryn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T22:14:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbb3adfc-ffa0-5b6b-aba6-c1f0793b2e79', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbb3adfc-ffa0-5b6b-aba6-c1f0793b2e79'}, {'abstract': 'The remodeled First World War galleries at the Imperial War Museum in London prefer to convey the experience of the conflict rather than explain the forces behind it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/arts/design/first-world-war-galleries-reopen-at-imperial-war-museum.html', 'snippet': 'The remodeled First World War galleries at the Imperial War Museum in London prefer to convey the experience of the conflict rather than explain the forces behind it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A moonscape of craters, mud and shattered stumps fills a wall-sized video screen; you can hear shrieking shells and shattering blasts; an enormous British howitzer, meant to pulverize the enemy’s defenses, points toward the fields. The only thing missing in this gallery, devoted to the Battle of the Somme at the Imperial War Museum here, is the ability to conceive of 20,000 British dead and 37,000 wounded or missing in the first day of fighting, and more than a million casualties over all during five months. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting the Nightmares of World War I', 'kicker': 'Museum Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revisiting the Nightmares of World War I', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Imperial War Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothstein, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T22:17:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Rothstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a91428a-f975-55e0-94dd-b8cd91e9cc55', 'word_count': 1284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a91428a-f975-55e0-94dd-b8cd91e9cc55'}, {'abstract': 'All participants in the first phase of the trial developed antibodies that lasted at least six months, suggesting the vaccine may provide long-term protection against the chikungunya virus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/science/new-vaccine-shows-promise-against-mosquito-borne-virus.html', 'snippet': 'All participants in the first phase of the trial developed antibodies that lasted at least six months, suggesting the vaccine may provide long-term protection against the chikungunya virus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new vaccine in its first human trials may offer protection against the chikungunya virus, a mosquito-borne infection that causes fever and severe joint pain, researchers reported Thursday in The Lancet. \xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Vaccine Shows Promise Against Mosquito-Borne Virus', 'kicker': 'Global Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Possible Vaccine to Fight Spread of Chikungunya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saint Louis, Catherine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chikungunya Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosquitoes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizat