 'uri': 'nyt://article/45e64cfc-e32d-5ab7-95fd-908a73ddc2e4'}, {'abstract': 'The Pennsylvania legislature is considering a cigarette tax for the city that would make the budget reductions temporary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/us/philadelphia-schools-to-open-on-time-amid-millions-in-budget-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'The Pennsylvania legislature is considering a cigarette tax for the city that would make the budget reductions temporary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After having warned that schools might not open on time in Philadelphia, Superintendent William R. Hite Jr. said Friday that a series of temporary spending cuts would help administrators to close an $81 million budget deficit and that classes would start as scheduled next month.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philadelphia Schools to Open on Time Amid Millions in Budget Cuts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Philadelphia Schools to Open on Time Amid Millions in Budget Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hite, William R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurdle, Jon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-15T23:59:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich and Jon Hurdle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hurdle', 'qualifie