': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/fashion/bill-cunningham-nature-rules.html', 'snippet': 'The beautiful and rustic nature of Nahant, Mass., welcomed the vintage customs of the Nahant Vintage Dance participants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After last Sunday’s festivities at Nahant Victorian Dance Weekend in Nahant, Mass., guests promenaded to Lodge Park on East Point, the highest point of the tied island, in open fields with 360-degree ocean views and Queen Anne’s lace five feet tall, in their turn-of-the-century finest. The site was the former Nahant Hotel, where wealthy Bostonians vacationed before the Civil War. It burned down in 1860, and Newport, R.I., became the summer destination of choice.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Nature Rules', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nature Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T00:06:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7ff12ef-98a2-5571-9e17-f657774c729f', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7ff12ef-98a2-5571-9e17-f657774c729f'}, {'abstract': 'Plus, how to consolidate online address books. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/15/technology/personaltech/quicker-ways-to-digitize-old-photographs.html', 'snippet': 'Plus, how to consolidate online address books. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. Flatbed scanners are good but can be slow and bulky. Are there any such things as photo scanners with automatic feeders, or a faster way to scan many prints without paying someone else to do it?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quicker Ways to Digitize Old Photographs', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fujitsu Limited', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eastman Kodak Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T00:09:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/e98b9d9a-065e-5d1a-9af5-7b72f8857fbf', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e98b9d9a-065e-5d1a-9af5-7b72f8857fbf'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s itinerary on the first international trip of his administration, did little to curb speculation he might be considering a run for the presidency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/nyregion/israel-offered-cuomo-a-new-stage-and-a-rehearsal-for-a-bigger-role.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s itinerary on the first international trip of his administration, did little to curb speculation he might be considering a run for the presidency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — At times, he seemed like a tour guide leading a study-abroad trip. At others, he was afforded all the trappings of a visiting head of state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/nyregion/NOTEBOOK-web/NOTEBOOK-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/16/nyregion/NOTEBOOK-web/NOTEBOOK-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/nyregion/NOTEBOOK-web/NOTEBOOK-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/nyregion/NOTEBOOK-web/NOTEBOOK-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/nyregion/NOTEBOOK-web/NOTEBOOK-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/16/nyregion/NOTEBOOK-web/NOTEBOOK-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/16/nyregion/NOTEBOOK-web/NOTEBOOK-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Offered Cuomo a New Stage and a Rehearsal for a Bigger Role', 'kicker': "Reporter's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Gave Cuomo a New Stage, and a Rehearsal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jerusalem (Israel)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T00:15:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0710456-580e-5bfe-acfb-dd632870552b', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0710456-580e-5bfe-acfb-dd632870552b'}, {'abstract': 'Iraq has devolved into a combination of Lebanon and Nigeria — a toxic brew of sectarian politics and oil-fueled kleptocracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/opinion/sunday/iraqs-last-chance.html', 'snippet': 'Iraq has devolved into a combination of Lebanon and Nigeria — a toxic brew of sectarian politics and oil-fueled kleptocracy.', 'lead_paragraph': '“THE country is in your hands,” whispered Iraq’s president, Fuad Masum, on Aug. 11 as he charged the newly designated prime minister, Haider al-Abadi, with forming a cabinet. “May God help you,” another lawmaker added. Indeed, after last week’s sidelining of the country’s long-serving prime minister, Nuri Kamal al-Maliki, Mr. Abadi will need all the divine intervention he can get if Iraq is to be spared a descent into all-out civil war.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sunday-review/0817COVER/0817COVER-articleLarge-