': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T01:43:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a04bb03-16d4-5cc4-8e12-34c387eef57a', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a04bb03-16d4-5cc4-8e12-34c387eef57a'}, {'abstract': 'New Jersey’s current pretrial system is rigged against the poor, but two new reform bills offer some hope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/opinion/gov-christie-takes-on-the-bail-bondsmen.html', 'snippet': 'New Jersey’s current pretrial system is rigged against the poor, but two new reform bills offer some hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie, who often likens New Jersey’s pretrial system to “debtors’ prisons,” signed two bills this week that offer hope for something a lot fairer. One bill would remake the system so it more nearly resembles the federal system — allowing judges to keep suspects in jail if they are a flight risk or a threat to society, but not because they can’t post bail. The second bill authorizes a vote in November on a constitutional amendment that must be approved before Mr. Christie’s proposed reforms can take effect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gov. Christie Takes On the Bail Bondsmen', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gov. Christie Takes On the Bail Bondsmen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutional Amendments', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T01:47:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f286d2a0-9cde-5227-b073-96ded9696086', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f286d2a0-9cde-5227-b073-96ded9696086'}, {'abstract': 'With the outbreak in West Africa appearing more out of control than ever, help is finally arriving to assist the local governments in fighting the epidemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/opinion/a-painfully-slow-ebola-response.html', 'snippet': 'With the outbreak in West Africa appearing more out of control than ever, help is finally arriving to assist the local governments in fighting the epidemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The outbreak of the Ebola virus in West Africa appears more out of control than ever. By Friday, the virus had infected more than 2,000 people in four countries and had killed more than half of them. The World Health Organization, which snoozed on the sidelines for months after the outbreak was first identified in March, has issued increasingly frantic warnings in recent days. On Aug. 8, it declared the spread of the virus “a public health emergency of international concern.” On Thursday, it warned that the reported numbers of people killed or sickened by the virus may “vastly underestimate the magnitude of the outbreak” because many sick people escape detection. The next day, it said that patients flooding into newly opened treatment centers were filling beds faster than they could be provided.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Painfully Slow Ebola Response', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Painfully Slow Ebola Response', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Samaritan's Purse", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Agency for International Development', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T01:53:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e493f2a-f82c-559f-9dbe-4dcf569b8a5