}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7fcb902-416b-5555-9023-20292af55529', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7fcb902-416b-5555-9023-20292af55529'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, work can be confining — even stifling. But within a creative mind, it can spin into endless possibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/business/a-menagerie-of-ideas-unlocked-in-odd-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'Yes, work can be confining — even stifling. But within a creative mind, it can spin into endless possibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the ages of 18 to 36 — when I began to teach creative writing — I worked variously as a house cleaner, house painter, landscaper, masseuse, editor and secretary. I worked as a tree planter in Zambia for a half-year when I was 19, then as a produce worker at a co-op grocery store in San Francisco, where I grew up. My first salaried job was going door to door, raising money for Salvadoran refugees fleeing civil conflict and death squads. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/business/17-ONWORK/17-ONWORK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/business/17-ONWORK/17-ONWORK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/business/17-ONWORK/17-ONWORK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/business/17-ONWORK/17-ONWORK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1064, 'width': 1622, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum