lorie disclosure. (At the risk of sounding whiny, they aren’t exactly “coming after” your popcorn; you’d be free to buy it, it’s just that the cinema would have to tell you how many calories you’re about to consume.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steps and the City (Fairly Trivial)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T15:08:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f8cd24d-411e-559c-aad4-e16680f04f57', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f8cd24d-411e-559c-aad4-e16680f04f57'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Rick Perry and Senator Ted Cruz spoke at the RedState Gathering in Fort Worth this month and both received enthusiastic support from attendees, highlighting a growing tension in Texas politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/us/tug-of-war-between-republicans-gov-rick-perry-and-sen-ted-cruz-seeking-same-base-support.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Rick Perry and Senator Ted Cruz spoke at the RedState Gathering in Fort Worth this month and both received enthusiastic support from attendees, highlighting a growing tension in Texas politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT WORTH — One week before a grand jury in liberal Travis County indicted Gov. Rick Perry on two felony counts, he and United States Sen. Ted Cruz were in friendlier territory, speaking at a conference hosted by a conservative blog here in the largest reliably Republican community in Texas.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None,