t://article/9238c053-7fb7-5c97-a0a6-f75fe68dbbfe'}, {'abstract': 'Come groan and get mixed up with Mel Taub’s Puns and Anagrams.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/16/variety-puns-and-anagrams-5/', 'snippet': 'Come groan and get mixed up with Mel Taub’s Puns and Anagrams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — Puns and Anagrams, or PandAs as they are affectionately called by some, are the reward we get for a sturdy week of straight crossword puzzle-solving. Yes, it’s still basically a crossword puzzle, but when was the last time you guffawed or slapped your forehead and groaned out loud while doing a Saturday crossword puzzle? PandAs are silly, and they’re a nice relief after the tough, late-week puzzles. At least I think so.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Puns and Anagrams', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T16:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2ce1bde-2fb8-5e2f-8800-ca5eaf48c454', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2ce1bde-2fb8-5e2f-8800-ca5eaf48c454'}, {'abstract': 'Missy Franklin and Katie Ledecky will lead the United States women’s team at the Pan Pacific Swimming Championships this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/sports/missy-franklin-and-katie-ledecky-adjust-to-life-as-swimmings-royalty.html', 'snippet': 'Missy Franklin and Katie Ledecky will lead the United States women’s team at the Pan Pacific Swimming Championships this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IRVINE, Calif. — They are USA Swimming’s dynamic duo, but there is one competition that neither Missy Franklin nor Katie Ledecky can win: the popularity contest to anoint a single chlorine queen. It is a losing proposition for both Franklin, a six-time gold medalist at last summer’s world championships, and Ledecky, who will go into this week’s Pan Pacific Swimming Championships poised to win as many as five gold medals.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sports/swimming/swimming-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/17/sports/swimming/swimming-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 983}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sports/swimming/swimming-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 625, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sports/swimming/swimming-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1250, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sports/swimming/swimming-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/17/sports/swimming/swimming-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/17/sports/swimming/swimming-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As (Very) Fast Friends, Two Young Americans Balance at Sport’s Peak', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As (Very) Fast Friends, Two Young Americans Balance at Sport’s Peak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Missy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ledecky, Katie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pan Pacific Swimming Championships', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Swimming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T16:01:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b7e4f26-2102-537f-9301-ca593b57d330', 'word_count': 1997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b7e4f26-2102-537f-9301-ca593b57d330'}, {'abstract': 'Workers are their own bosses in the so-called sharing economy, but that flexibility also brings much uncertainty — and few of the protections of full-time work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/technology/in-the-sharing-economy-workers-find-both-freedom-and-uncertainty.html', 'snippet': 'Workers are their own bosses in the so-called sharing economy, but that flexibility also brings much uncertainty — and few of the protections of full-time work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just after 4 a.m. on a recent Friday, while most of the neighbors in her leafy Boston suburb were still asleep, Jennifer Guidry was in the driveway of her rental apartment, her blond hair pulled back in a tidy French braid, vacuuming the inside