on/sunday/china-confronts-its-coal-problem.html', 'snippet': 'If done right, Beijing’s strategy could have a meaningful effect on local air quality and the planet as a whole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chinese government has indicated a strong desire — and made some specific proposals — to reduce its reliance on coal, a step that would be a welcome development for the Chinese people and the planet as a whole. But there is a lot we don’t know yet about Beijing’s strategy and whether it will be bold enough to have a meaningful effect on local air quality and climate change. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Confronts Its Coal Problem', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Confronts Its Coal Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T18:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/76d498b5-55dc-5b91-ad3d-a3615dee0c14', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76d498b5-55dc-5b91-ad3d-a3615dee0c14'}, {'abstract': 'The comeback of the wild turkey appears to be complete.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/opinion/sunday/strutting-back-with-a-vengeance.html', 'snippet': 'The comeback of the wild turkey appears to be complete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whatever happened to Giuliani? No, not the ex-mayor with the comb-over. Giuliani the urbane wild turkey, the bold bird that drew raves from shocked city dwellers when she arrived at Manhattan’s Riverside Park 11 years ago to strut imperiously, residing in plain sight, deigning to tolerate handouts and a nickname. Giuliani was studied like an extraterrestrial by crowds more mindful of wild turkey as a libation — not the dominant roaming bird of colonial days that was nearly driven to extinction as settlers fed off the flocks and urban landscapes exploded.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strutting Back With a Vengeance', 'kicker': 'Editorial Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strutting Back With a Vengeance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turkeys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T18:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5ee169d-c1e1-511f-a20c-b79bd2e85b34', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5ee169d-c1e1-511f-a20c-b79bd2e85b34'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of investigating and mocking nuns, we’d be better off if we spent more time emulating them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/opinion/sunday/nicholas-kristof-sister-acts.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of investigating and mocking nuns, we’d be better off if we spent more time emulating them.', 