Ebola has further weakened the region’s decrepit, understaffed health systems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/world/africa/with-aid-doctors-gone-ebola-fight-grows-harder.html', 'snippet': 'The departure of many Western development workers from the West African countries hit hardest by Ebola has further weakened the region’s decrepit, understaffed health systems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When people started dying of Ebola in Liberia, Clarine Vaughn faced a wrenching choice: Should she send home, for their own health and safety, four American doctors working for Heartt, the aid group she led there? Or should she keep them in the country without proper supplies or training to fight the virulent, contagious disease, which was already spreading panic?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Aid Doctors Gone, Ebola Fight Grows Harder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Many Doctors Retreat, Ebola Fight Grows Harder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fink, Sheri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ZMapp (Drug)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nabarro, David', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T18:49:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheri Fink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03b930c3-f2c7-5d5c-bda3-1d78728561b8', 'word_count': 2153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03b930c3-f2c7-5d5c-bda3-1d78728561b8'}, {'abstract': 'Starting in January, Medicare will pay monthly fees to doctors who manage care for patients with two or more chronic conditions like heart disease, diabetes and depression.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/17/us/medicare-to-start-paying-doctors-who-coordinate-needs-of-chronically-ill-patients.html', 'snippet': 'Starting in January, Medicare will pay monthly fees to doctors who manage care for patients with two or more chronic conditions like heart disease, diabetes and depression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a policy change, the Obama administration is planning to pay doctors to coordinate the care of Medicare beneficiaries, amid growing evidence that patients with chronic illnesses suffer from disjointed, fragmented care.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare to Start Paying Doctors Who Coordinate Needs of Chronically Ill Patients', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Medicare to Start Paying Doctors Who Coordinate Needs of Chronically Ill Patients', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-16T18:51:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname'