en to,” explains Ahmed Gallab, the singer and multi-instrumentalist known as Sinkane. “Then, as you grow as an artist, you get bored and start making abstract art music. Everyone from the Beatles to Radiohead did that. Me, I’ve kind of constructed my career backwards.” Following two arty, largely instrumental releases, Sinkane’s 2012 album “Mars” (its first on the tastemaking DFA imprint) was a breakthrough, combining African-inflected rhythms, complex melodic textures and Gallab’s seductively tuneful voice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/18/t-magazine/18sinkane-diehl/18sinkane-diehl-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/18/t-magazine/18sinkane-diehl/18sinkane-diehl-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/18/t-magazine/18sinkane-diehl/18sinkane-diehl-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/18/t-magazine/18sinkane-diehl/18sinkane-diehl-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/18/t-magazine/18sinkane-diehl/18sinkane-diehl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/18/t-magazine/18sinkane-diehl/18sinkane-diehl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/18