es.com/2014/08/18/jewish-film-festival-to-return-to-london-theater/', 'snippet': 'The UK Jewish Film Festival and the Tricycle Theater in London have resolved their dispute over funding, so the festival can return to that space next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tricycle Theater in London and the UK Jewish Film Festival have resolved their dispute over funding and the conflict in Gaza that led to the festival’s not being held at that theater this year, according to a joint statement posted on the festival’s website. The theater and the festival, the statement said, have had lengthy discussions and have “agreed to work together to rebuild their relationship.” But the 2014 festival, to be held in November, will not take place at the Tricycle.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jewish Film Festival to Return to London Theater', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jewish Film Festival And Theater Make Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tricycle Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-18T17:25:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c113bf7c-e736-5822-92eb-3a7f45b34bd2', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c113bf7c-e736-5822-92eb-3a7f45b34bd2'}, {'abstract': 'What makes CrossFit appealing to members and confusing to outsiders is that it’s more than a workout — it’s a cultural identity. A new book on the subject may also only appeal to the initiated.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/18/crossfit-book-breathe-fire/', 'snippet': 'What makes CrossFit appealing to members and confusing to outsiders is that it’s more than a workout — it’s a cultural identity. A new book on the subject may also only appeal to the initiated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the video, Nicole Carroll is grimacing, tears welling in her eyes. She’s in the final set of a workout — three rounds of 50 squats, seven “muscle-ups” (pull-ups on two overhead gymnastic rings) and 10 lifts of a 95-pound weight from hip to shoulder level.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19scibookalt/19scibookalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19scibookalt/19scibookalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19scibookalt/19scibookalt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19scibookalt/19scibookalt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1517, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19scibookalt/19scibookalt-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19scibookalt/19scibookalt-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19scibookalt/19scibookalt-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Insider’s Guide to CrossFit', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'True Believers at Fitnessu2019s Limits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herz, J C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CrossFit Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-18T17:29:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christie Aschwanden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aschwanden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29dd3fac-d870-5006-b985-c025cd87565a', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29dd3fac-d870-5006-b985-c025cd87565a'}, {'abstract': 'Some argue that with billions of stars in our galaxy, there must be other civilizations. But others say intelligence is so rare on Earth; why would we expect to find it elsewhere?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/science/in-search-for-intelligent-life-consider-the-lottery.html', 'snippet': 'Some argue that with billions of stars in our galaxy, there must be other civilizations. But others say intelligence is so rare on Earth; why would we expect to find it elsewhere?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost 20 years ago, in the pages of an obscure publication called Bioastronomy News, two giants in the world of science argued over whether SETI — the Search for Extraterrestrial Intelligence — had a chance of succeeding. Carl Sagan, as eloquent as ever, gave his standard answer. With billions of stars in our galaxy, there must be other civilizations capable of transmitting electromagnetic waves. By scouring the sky with radio telescopes, we just might intercept a signal.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19JOHN/19JOHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19JOHN/19JOHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 729}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19JOHN/19JOHN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 844, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19JOHN/19JOHN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1494, 'width': 1230, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19JOHN/19JOHN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19JOHN/19JOHN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19JOHN/19JOHN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Intelligent-Life Lottery ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Intelligent-Life Lottery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extraterrestrial Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SETI Institute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sagan, Carl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayr, Ernst', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gould, Stephen Jay', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drake, Frank', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-18T17:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c92fef6d-d6c9-54ca-b80b-f5e5f8b39f63', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c92fef6d-d6c9-54ca-b80b-f5e5f8b39f63'}, {'abstract': '“The Great Society,” at the Oregon Shakespeare Festival, is the second installment in Robert Schenkkan’s Lyndon B. Johnson saga.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/theater/in-the-great-society-jack-willis-stars-as-johnson.html', 'snippet': '“The Great Society,” at the Oregon Shakespeare Festival, is the second installment in Robert Schenkkan’s Lyndon B. Johnson saga.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASHLAND, Ore. — “Christ, I feel like a catfish that’s bit a big juicy worm only to find a right sharp hook in the middle of it,” says Lyndon B. Johnson in “The Great Society,” the second part of Robert Schenkkan’s sprawling dramatization of Johnson’s tumultuous years in the White House. As the play opens, Johnson has just been elected to a full presidential term, but there’s no time for a celebratory fishing trip, because he’s already facing a full slate of problems.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/arts/GREAT/GREAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 889, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/19/arts/GREAT/GREAT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 889}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/arts/GREAT/GREAT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 692, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/arts/GREAT/GREAT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1383, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/arts/GREAT/GREAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/19/arts/GREAT/GREAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/arts/GREAT/GREAT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flawed President Who Dared to Dream', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flawed President Who Dared to Dream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oregon Shakespeare Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schenkkan, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson