blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/18/heather-graham-bows-out-of-new-labute-play/', 'snippet': 'Neil LaBute’s new play “The Money Shot” is still set to begin performances in two weeks, with Elizabeth Reaser taking over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late last month MCC Theater announced with some fanfare that it would open its season with “The Money Shot,” a new dark comedy by its resident playwright, Neil LaBute, with Heather Graham in one of the starring roles. But over the weekend, barely two and a half weeks before the production was scheduled to open for previews, Deadline first reported that Ms. Graham had bowed out to concentrate on the film “Half Magic,” which she wrote and will direct and star in. The television and film actress Elizabeth Reaser (“True Detective” and “The Good Wife”) will replace her, a spokesman for the production said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/theater/24graham/24graham-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/24/theater/24graham/24graham-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/theater/24graham/24graham-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/theater/24graham/24graham-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/theater/24graham/24graham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'c