aragraph': 'For most pop stars, the announcement of a new album is a pretty routine affair. But most pop stars are not Taylor Swift.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taylor Swift Maximizes Use of Social Media in Release of New Album', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Release, Taylor Swift Maximizes Social Media', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Taylor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Releases (Entertainment)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-19T01:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/212ab148-ff61-5610-995f-3e45baf11ffc', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/212ab148-ff61-5610-995f-3e45baf11ffc'}, {'abstract': 'When the S.E.C. announced it was awarding $400,000 to a whistle-blower, it didn’t name the recipient per the Dodd-Frank law. His name is Bill Lloyd, and this is his story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/opinion/joe-nocera-the-man-who-blew-the-whistle.html', 'snippet': 'When the S.E.C. announced it was awarding $400,000 to a whistle-blower, it didn’t name the recipient per the Dodd-Frank law. His name is Bill Lloyd, and this is his story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late last month, the Securities and Exchange Commission issued an oblique press release announcing that it was awarding an unnamed whistle-blower $400,000 for helping expose a financial fraud at an unnamed company. The money was the latest whistle-blower award — there have been 13 so far — paid as part of the Dodd-Frank financial reform law, which includes both protections for whistle-blowers and financial awards when their information leads to fines of more than $1 million. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man Who Blew the Whistle', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Man Who Blew the Whistle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MassMutual Financial Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-19T01:20:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7776d08-03e3-570b-b5c2-d05c152c9fc0', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7776d08-03e3-570b-b5c2-d05c152c9fc0'}, {'abstract': 'An academic paper argues that the American tax code’s loopholes result in effective rates that make United States corporations more competitive than their competitors based overseas, not less.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/18/tax-burden-in-u-s-not-as-heavy-as-it-looks-study-finds/', 'snippet': 'An academic paper argues that the American tax code’s loopholes result in effective rates that make United States corporations more competitive than their competitors based overseas, not less.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, chief executives have complained bitterly about the United States corporate tax code, arguing that it is too complicated and that rates are too high. The issue has reached a near boiling point this summer as many large American companies have sought to buy smaller foreign rivals so they can renounce their United States corporate citizenship and reincorporate overseas to lower their tax bills. Others are considering the move, known as an inversion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/business/Sorkin/Sorkin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/19/business/Sorkin/Sorkin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/business/Sorkin/Sorkin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/business/Sorkin/Sorkin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/business/Sorkin/Sorkin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/19/business/Sorkin/Sorkin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/business/Sorkin/Sorkin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tax Burden in U.S. Not as Heavy as It Looks, Report Says', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tax Burden Not as Heavy as It Looks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-19T01:20:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ceb900a9-cd7a-530d-9e95-adf120165305', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ceb900a9-cd7a-530d-9e95-adf120165305'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama made clear that he was not issuing a blanket indictment of either the protesting crowds or the law enforcement officers responding to the demonstrations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/us/calling-for-calm-in-ferguson-obama-cites-need-for-improved-race-relations.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama made clear that he was not issuing a blanket indictment of either the protesting crowds or the law enforcement officers responding to the demonstrations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama called for calm and healing in Ferguson, Mo., on Monday even as he acknowledged the deep racial divisions that continue to plague not only that St. Louis suburb but cities across the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calling for Calm in Ferguson, Obama Cites Need for Improved Race Relations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Calling for Calm in Ferguson, Obama Cites Need for Improved Race Relations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirschfeld Davis, Julie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subje