ly endangered.” These languages preserve priceless cultural heritage, and some hold unexpected value — nuances in these languages convey unparalleled knowledge of the natural world. Many of these at-risk languages are found in my home state of California. Now for some, only a few fluent speakers remain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Who Speaks Wukchumni?’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dictionaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-19T01:40:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmanuel Vaughan-Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmanuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vaughan-Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/eace6737-5afd-56a9-9063-5f840889b548', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eace6737-5afd-56a9-9063-5f840889b548'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama appears remarkably distant from his own party on Capitol Hill, Democrats there say, leaving him with few loyalists as issues erupt abroad and at home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/us/aloof-obama-is-frustrating-his-own-party.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama appears remarkably distant from his own party on Capitol Hill, Democrats there say, leaving him with few loyalists as issues erupt abroad and at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The meeting in the Oval Office in late June was called to give President Obama and the four top members of Congress a chance to discuss the unravelin