}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce3d9ab5-fa40-59d1-a6d5-514fd1a3a8ab', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce3d9ab5-fa40-59d1-a6d5-514fd1a3a8ab'}, {'abstract': 'The unusually floral gin The Botanist, produced on Islay, the Scottish island famed for its peaty Scotches, is perfect for this special twist on the Negroni.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/t-magazine/scottish-gin-islay-botanist-negroni-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'The unusually floral gin The Botanist, produced on Islay, the Scottish island famed for its peaty Scotches, is perfect for this special twist on the Negroni.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Off the western coast of the Scottish mainland lies Islay, an island three times the size of Martha’s Vineyard. It’s a place rich in whisky lore, thanks to its eight distilleries, all of which make a product with an unmistakably peaty flavor. But the Botanist, introduced by the whisky distillery Bruichladdich (pronounced “brook-laddie”) in 2010, is the island’s only gin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/t-magazine/19gin-nichols-recipe/19gin-nichols-recipe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/19/t-magazine/19gin-nichols-recipe/19gin-nichols-recipe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/t-magazine/19gin-nichols-recipe/19gin-nichols-recipe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/t-magazine/19gin-nichols-recipe/19gin-nichols-recipe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_