act': 'An announcer whose career began with radio and grew with popular game shows like “The Price Is Right,” Mr. Pardo was best known for decades of introducing stars on the sketch comedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/nyregion/don-pardo-the-voice-of-saturday-night-live-dies-at-96.html', 'snippet': 'An announcer whose career began with radio and grew with popular game shows like “The Price Is Right,” Mr. Pardo was best known for decades of introducing stars on the sketch comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don Pardo, who literally introduced television viewers to some of America’s biggest stars and soon-to-be-stars as the longtime announcer for “Saturday Night Live,” died on Monday in Tucson. He was 96.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/arts/PARDO-obit/PARDO-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 474, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/20/arts/PARDO-obit/PARDO-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 474}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/arts/PARDO-obit/PARDO-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/arts/PARDO-obit/PARDO-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1543, 'width': 1955, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/arts/PARDO-obit/PARDO-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/20/arts/PARDO-obit/PARDO-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/arts/PARDO-obit/PARDO-obit-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don Pardo, the Voice of ‘SNL,’ Is Dead at 96', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don Pardo, the Voice of ‘SNL,’ Is Dead at 96', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Saturday Night Live (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pardo, Don (1918-2014)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-19T04:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c36991a-0ab7-51ed-a6a7-d37086900fef', 'word_count': 1235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c36991a-0ab7-51ed-a6a7-d37086900fef'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:30 A.M. (HBO2) MOONRISE KINGDOM (2012) In this sweet, dreamy feature from the director Wes Anderson, 12-year-old Suzy (Kara Hayward, above) meets her soul mate, an orphan boy at scout camp named Sam (Jared Gilman). They exchange letters and plot an escape from their dreary worlds. In her case, it’s a house headed by a joyless mom and dad (Frances McDormand and Bill Murray), lawyers who call each other “counselor” in bed; in his case, it’s camp and a series of foster homes. “\xa0‘Moonrise Kingdom’ breezes along with a beautifully coordinated admixture of droll humor, deadpan and slapstick,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “Like all of Mr. Anderson’s films, though, there’s a deep, pervasive melancholia here too.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-19T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandon K. Thorp', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandon', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Thorp', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/05719d43-6302-5919-bc77-0f241f12c0f9', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05719d43-6302-5919-bc77-0f241f12c0f9'}, {'abstract': 'Violence erupted in Ferguson, Mo., once more overnight, even as National Guard troops arrived in the latest in a series of attempts to quell the chaos after a police officer fatally shot an unarmed teenager.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/us/ferguson-missouri-protests.html', 'snippet': 'Violence erupted in Ferguson, Mo., once more overnight, even as National Guard troops arrived in the latest in a series of attempts to quell the chaos after a police officer fatally shot an unarmed teenager.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FERGUSON, Mo. — Violence erupted here once more overnight, even as Missouri National Guard troops arrived, the latest in a series of quickly shifting attempts to quell the chaos that has upended this St. Loui