 crashed in Ryhope in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDERLAND — The Leeds express met with a serious accident to-night [Aug. 19] at about eight o’clock on the North Eastern Railway at Ryhope station, about three miles from here. This train travels from Newcastle and calls at Sunderland on its journey. To-night the train seems to have run harder and faster than usual, indeed passengers were alarmed some minutes before the smash took place. All the coaches, except the last one, were thrown off the metals, and soon a scene of great confusion ensued. Strange to say, there was but one death, that of a child; but there were several injured severely.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, August 20, 1889', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20iht-oldaug20-leeds/20iht-oldaug20-leeds-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20iht-oldaug20-leeds/20iht-oldaug20-leeds-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20iht-oldaug20-leeds/20iht-oldaug20-leeds-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20iht-oldaug20-leeds/20iht-oldaug20-leeds-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20iht-oldaug20-leeds/20iht-oldaug20-leeds-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/20/bl