ance at a brother or sister’s sports or other events part of being a supportive family, or “dragging them along?”', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/weekly-quandary-should-siblings-spectate/', 'snippet': 'Is sibling attendance at a brother or sister’s sports or other events part of being a supportive family, or “dragging them along?”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Weekly Quandary, we pull a question from the comments, the weekly open thread or email that we know (or at least suspect) plagues more than one parent. You — the readers — provide the advice: How have you made this work better in your family? This week’s quandary comes from a comment that surprised me on a recent blog post, “When Sports and Family Time Conflict, Speak Up.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/us/motherlode-hockey-skates/motherlode-hockey-skates-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/19/us/motherlode-hockey-skates/motherlode-hockey-skates-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/us/motherlode-hockey-skates/motherlode-hockey-skates-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/us/motherlode-hockey-skates/motherlode-hockey-skates-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 1632, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/us/motherlode-hockey-skates/motherlode-hockey-skates-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/19/us/motherlode-hockey-skates/motherlode-hockey-skates-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/us/motherlode-hockey-skates/motherlode-hockey-skates-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekly Quandary: Should Siblings Spectate?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-19T17:18:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29a8dec5-990e-58f1-b67e-afacd5b6765d', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29a8dec5-990e-58f1-b67e-afacd5b6765d'}, {'abstract': 'The costumed characters of Times Square held a news conference.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/19/monsters-inc-organizes/', 'snippet': 'The costumed characters of Times Square held a news conference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you belong to a lowly regarded, often abused, all-but-anonymous segment of New York City society, how do you assert your rights and dignity? You\xa0organize and demand them. In Times Square at noon on Tuesday, a couple dozen costumed characters held a news conference to defend themselves and their right to work (posing for photos with tourists and soliciting tips), and to denounce what they said was routine police harassment. The group calls itself NYC Artists United for a Smile, a jaunty name that matched the performers’ mood as they cheered and applauded themselves and yelled “Si, se puede,” the yes-we-can chant of immigrants and the working poor.\xa0Except for Batman, who glowered as usual as he passed out handbills at the edge of the crowd.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monsters, Inc.', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-19T17:44:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffe699eb-d241-52b3-83fc-cce0fd260886', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffe699eb-d241-52b3-83fc-cce0fd260886'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Plouffe, who ran President Obama’s 2008 campaign, will be in charge of policy and strategy for the car service start-up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/technology/uber-picks-a-political-insider-to-wage-its-regulatory-battles.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Plouffe, who ran President Obama’s 2008 campaign, will be in charge of policy and strategy for the car service start-up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uber wants your vote of support. And it has hired a campaign manager to win you over.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/bu