-taylor-schilling-to-star-in-a-month-in-the-country/', 'snippet': 'The two 2014 Emmy Award nominees will star in the Classic Stage revival of Turgenev’s play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Swords and shivs will give way to lovelorn prose next year when the 2014 Emmy Award nominees Peter Dinklage (“Game of Thrones”) and Taylor Schilling (“Orange Is the New Black”) star as Rakitin and Natalya in the Classic Stage revival of Turgenev’s “A Month in the Country,” the company announced on Tuesday. Erica Schmidt, Mr. Dinklage’s wife, will direct the play, which is set at a Russian country estate in the 1840s. The show is to run Jan. 9 through Feb. 15, 2015, at Classic Stage’s East Village home on East 13th Street. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/theater/19dinklage/19dinklage-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/19/theater/19dinklage/19dinklage-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 694}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/theater/19dinklage/19dinklage-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 886, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/theater/19dinklage/19dinklage-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 1167, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/theater/19dinklage/19dinklage-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/19/theater/19dinklage/19dinklage-thumbStandard.jpg', '