 amounts of data to save money and solve problems, makes such intuitive sense. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Better Governing Through Data', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Better Governing Through Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of the Comptroller (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T01:10:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/00b6fde5-e196-5cc3-b49d-c98a97ae8c8b', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00b6fde5-e196-5cc3-b49d-c98a97ae8c8b'}, {'abstract': 'The rock-star candidate who got elected on his electrifying promise has become a bored bird in a gilded cage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/opinion/maureen-dowd-alone-again-naturally.html', 'snippet': 'The rock-star candidate who got elected on his electrifying promise has become a bored bird in a gilded cage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Affectations can be dangerous, as Gertrude Stein said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/dowd-circular/dowd-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'su