//article/c8d0187a-73ca-585e-b5b7-00fbd5273781', 'word_count': 1606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8d0187a-73ca-585e-b5b7-00fbd5273781'}, {'abstract': 'Louis Segna is charged with 11 counts of falsely reporting an incident, but his lawyer told jurors that the tips were just hard to substantiate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/nyregion/brooklyn-man-on-trial-on-charges-of-making-false-reports-to-911.html', 'snippet': 'Louis Segna is charged with 11 counts of falsely reporting an incident, but his lawyer told jurors that the tips were just hard to substantiate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stream of calls came into the 911 system from an unknown person in Brooklyn, each one describing an emergency in the heart of Williamsburg: a sound like an explosion in an L train tunnel; a man displaying a pistol; someone wielding a knife and issuing threats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Caller Said Something; Had He Seen Something?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Caller Said Something; Had He Seen Something?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Segna, Louis (1961- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nine-One-One (911) (Emergency Phone Number)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T01:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbf5a6d1-513e-5f9b-b32d-74e795a822c5', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbf5a6d1-513e-5f9b-b32d-74e795a822c5'}, {'abstract': 'RadioShack’s ubiquitous stores flourished when consumers fixed their own gadgets. Now, the chain is trying out brighter, more inviting stores to lure shoppers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/business/a-supplier-to-tinkerers-radioshack-struggles-in-a-wireless-world.html', 'snippet': 'RadioShack’s ubiquitous stores flourished when consumers fixed their own gadgets. Now, the chain is trying out brighter, more inviting stores to lure shoppers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1971, Steve Jobs and Steve Wozniak hawked tiny machines called Blue Boxes that allowed long-distance phone calls to be made free by mimicking certain tones.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/business/JP-RADIO-01/JP-RADIO-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/20/business/JP-RADIO-01/JP-RADIO-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/business/JP-RADIO-01/JP-RADIO-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/business/JP-RADIO-01/JP-RADIO-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1295, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/business/JP-RADIO-01/JP-RADIO-01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/20/business/JP-RADIO-01/JP-RAD