e company to go ahead with its coming season of performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Opera and the union representing its stagehands reached a contract deal early Wednesday morning, clearing the last major hurdle before the company could go ahead with its coming season of operas featuring murderously jealous lovers, dying sopranos and a fellow named Figaro — both before and after his marriage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Metropolitan Opera Clears Last Major Hurdle in Labor Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Metropolitan Opera Clears Last Major Hurdle in Labor Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gelb, Peter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T08:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4d8f520-89cc-577a-9a08-069daafb6381', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4d8f520-89cc-577a-9a08-069daafb6381'}, {'abstract': 'The archrivals Chris Evert and Martina Navratilova talk about their legendary 1984 match, which might have changed the course of women’s tennis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/magazine/a-us-open-to-remember-navratilova-and-evert-look-back.html', 'snippet': 'The archrivals Chris Evert and Martina Navratilova talk about their legendary 1984 match, which might have changed the course of women’s tennis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Within the bounds of a singles tennis court, Chris Evert and Martina Navratilova knew each other very well. Between 1973 and 1988, the two 18-time Grand Slam champs faced each other 80 times, with Navratilova holding a slight advantage, 43 to 37. Yet remarkably, despite their monumental rivalry, they were close friends off the court. Having so frequently found themselves alone together at the end of a tournament, Evert and Navratilova formed a bond that is difficult to imagine today between champions: They practiced together, helped tune each other’s strokes and hung out regularly. They even won Wimbledon and the French Open as doubles partners.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/magazine/24navrat-evert1/mag-24Navrat-Evert-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/magazine/24navrat-evert1/mag-24Navrat-Evert-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/magazine/24navrat-evert1/mag-24Navrat-Evert-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/magazine/24navrat-evert1/mag-24Navrat-Evert-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {