ernational Herald Tribune archives: A famous cricketer died in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — Charles A. Absolom’s wasted life is ended. The famous Cambridge cricketer’s body lies at the port of Spain, Trinidad, far from the land he loved so well. For upwards of ten years he had lived in America. When he broke loose from associations which bound him to England he bought a rifle and dog and buried himself in the heart of the Rocky Mountains. The reasons for this he never gave. Some said it was a love affair, and that explanation was generally accepted. Wherever he was known, there is deep regret that a life began under such favourable auspices should have ended so sadly. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Aug. 21, 1889', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1889: Wandering Cricketer Dies', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cricket (Game)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T10:39:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7ca4666-43d4-522f-bad5-edd3faf34192', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7ca4666-43d4-522f-bad5-edd3faf34192'}, {'abstract': 'The dissenting voices came after the governor of the central bank, Mark J. Carney, was accused of sending mixed signals to the market about the timing of any future rate increases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/business/ec