: 'nyt://article/fcdb82ed-918f-5491-b08f-35f57791bf9b'}, {'abstract': 'Daily Clip Report is a collection of articles about the media and The Times that is emailed each day to senior executives and newsroom managers here.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/08/20/daily-clip-report-2/', 'snippet': 'Daily Clip Report is a collection of articles about the media and The Times that is emailed each day to senior executives and newsroom managers here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daily Clip Report is a collection of articles about The Times and the media sent by email each morning to senior executives and newsroom editors. The email is produced by the Corporate Communications Department at The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Clip Report', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T11:33:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jordan Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jordan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc4edab7-5838-5353-815e-a2bab8de2e50', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc4edab7-5838-5353-815e-a2bab8de2e50'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Sullivan won the Republican primary and will face off against Mark Begich. Republicans have dominated federal offices in Alaska since it became a state in 1960.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/upshot/alaska-might-be-more-friendly-to-democrats-than-it-appears.html', 'snippet': 'Dan Sullivan won the Republican primary and will face off against Mark Begich. Republicans have dominated federal offices in Alaska since it became a state in 1960.', 'lead_paragraph': "Republicans need to win six seats to retake the Senate, and, at first glance, Alaska looks as if it ought to be one of the G.O.P.'s best opportunities. In presidential elections, it’s one of the most dependably Republican states, and the Democratic incumbent, Mark Begich, won his Senate seat in large part because his opponent was convicted of seven counts of corruption one week before the election. Mr. Begich still only won by less than 2 percentage points.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/upshot/21up-akprimer/21up-akprimer-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/21/upshot/21up-akprimer/21up-akprimer-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/upshot/21up-akprimer/21up-akprimer-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/upshot/21up-akprimer/21up-akprimer-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/upshot/21up-akprimer/21up-akprimer-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/21/upshot/21up-akprimer/21up-akprimer-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/upshot/21up-akprimer/21up-akprimer-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alaska Might Be More Friendly to Democrats Than It Appears', 'kicker': 'Midterm Calculus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2014)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Begich, Mark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T11:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ebbf4e4-6e8f-53d4-8f08-6f065200de4e', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ebbf4e4-6e8f-53d4-8f08-6f065200de4e'}, {'abstract': 'Standard Chartered to will pay a $300 million fine for backsliding. | A default swaps association has postponed a payout auction on Argentine bonds. | Grappling with the cost of corporate gadflies. | Bank of America has a sole chief operating officer.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/morning-agenda-standard-chartereds-backsliding-woes/', 'snippet': 'Standard Chartered to will pay a $300 million fine for backsliding. | A default swaps association has postponed a payout auction on Argentine bonds. | Grappling with the cost of corporate gadflies. | Bank of America has a sole chief operating offi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a settlement announced on Tuesday by New York State’s financial regulator, the British bank Standard Chartered will pay a $300 million fine and suspend its dollar-clearing activities because of its failure to weed out transactions prone to money-laundering, Ben Protess and Chad Bray write in DealBook. The deal comes two years after the bank paid a combined $667 million to state and federal authorities over similar accusations. Those settlements resolved accusations that Standard Chartered, in part through its New York branch, processed transactions for Iran and other countries blacklisted by the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Standard Chartered’s Backsliding Woes', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T11:36:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0492773d-6ba9-56b1-a0eb-448974f37205', 'word_count': 1949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0492773d-6ba9-56b1-a0eb-448974f37205'}, {'abstract': 'The Islanders said the team would be sold to a former Washington Capitals co-owner and a London-based investor.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/islanders-owner-announces-he-will-sell-n-h-l-team-to-an-investment-group/', 'snippet': 'The Islanders said the team would be sold to a former Washington Capitals co-owner and a London-based investor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Islanders said the team would be sold to a former Washington Capitals co-owner and a London-based investor, Richard Sandomir reports in The New York Times. Read more »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Islanders’ Owner Announces He Will Sell N.H.L. Team to an Investment Group', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T11:56:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a97deff-67a1-5aa7-9469-f3f824501d23', 'word_count': 29, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a97deff-67a1-5aa7-9469-f3f824501d23'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Iyengar, who practiced his asanas, or postures, well into his 90s, established yoga institutes on six continents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/world/asia/bks-iyengar-who-helped-bring-yoga-to-west-dies-at-95.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Iyengar, who practiced his asanas, or postures, well into his 90s, established yoga institutes on six continents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — B. K. S. Iyengar, who helped introduce the practice of yoga to a Western world awakening to the notion of an inner life, died on Wednesday in the southern Indian city of Pune. He was 95.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'B. K. S. Iyengar, Who Helped Bring Yoga to the West, Dies at 95', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'B. K. S. Iyengar, Who Helped Bring Yoga to the West, Dies at 95', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iyengar, B K S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T11:58:48