ticle/cd8609c1-97a3-527a-a616-c9112c802656', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd8609c1-97a3-527a-a616-c9112c802656'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Pope Pius X died in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/1914-pope-pius-x-dies-after-illness/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Pope Pius X died in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Pope Pius X. died at 1.35 this morning [Aug. 20], and the discussion as to his probable successor is already open. On Tuesday his Holiness passed an uneasy night, which was much troubled by fits of coughing, and his condition became seriously worse yesterday morning. Mgr. Zampini administered the extreme unction. Pius X. then said : ‘‘May God’s will be done: it is the end.’’ At 1.22 a.m. the Pope murmured some incomprehensible words, and thirteen minutes later Mgr. Bressan leaned over his bed and saw that he was dead. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Aug. 21, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/blogs/21iht-oldaug21/21iht-oldaug21-articleLarge.png', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/21/blogs/21iht-oldaug21/21iht-oldaug21-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/blogs/21iht-oldaug21/21iht-oldaug21-jumbo.png', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/blogs/21iht-oldaug21/21iht-oldaug21-superJumbo.png', 'height': 898, 'width': 1204, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': No