the most interesting division has\xa0opened within American conservatism, where a large group of conservative and libertarian writers have been much less\xa0inclined than perhaps they/we would have been thirty years ago to give the police the benefit of the doubt. More interesting still is the breadth and diversity of this group: It’s not only the predictable police skeptics, the Cato Institute and Reason types; you also have elite-media squishes like myself, fiercer polemicists\xa0like\xa0Kevin Williamson and Mark Steyn, and the populist crew at RedState (Erick Erickson, Leon Wolf) raising similar questions about police conduct, along with many\xa0other writers\xa0(and, of course, Rand Paul) as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Conservative Divide Over Ferguson', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erickson, Erick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steyn, Mark', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williamson, Kevin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drudge Report', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T16:38:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'se