e, a four-year-old company that makes software that helps sales teams by eliminating the need for sales representatives to spend time on data entry. To his dismay,\xa0Matthew Bellows, founder and chief executive of Yesware, saw his 10-person sales team fall far short of the sales goals he’d set. And that was with 100,000 known leads — current users of the software’s free version — seemingly primed to be converted into paying customers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Yesware Need to Hire a Vice President of Sales?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T17:54:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Grossmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grossmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ca177ea-4130-57ce-807b-7201baede97d', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ca177ea-4130-57ce-807b-7201baede97d'}, {'abstract': 'A New York Times correspondent, Jodi Kantor, spoke with Malala Yousafzai, an education activist, about her mother learning to read as an adult.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/asia/100000003065530/malalas-mother-learns-to-read.html', 'snippet': 'A New York Times correspondent, Jodi Kantor, spoke with Malala Yousafzai, an education activist, about her mother learning to read as an adult.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A New York Times correspondent, Jodi Kantor, spoke with Malala Yousafzai, an education activist, about her mother learning to read as an ad