n game, then brought a real-life version to Pebble Beach last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Auto designers have a new place to show off their concept cars, beyond auto shows. Video games are now providing a venue where dream cars can not only be seen but also driven. And those video game cars are making their way into real life as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/automobiles/21ASTON-image-1/21ASTON-image-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/21/automobiles/21ASTON-image-1/21ASTON-image-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/automobiles/21ASTON-image-1/21ASTON-image-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/automobiles/21ASTON-image-1/21ASTON-image-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/automobiles/21ASTON-image-1/21ASTON-image-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/21/automobiles/21ASTON-image-1/21ASTON-image-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/automobiles/21ASTON-image-1/21ASTON-image-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The DP-100 Is Aston Martin’s Real-Life Interpretation of a Video Game Sports Car', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PlayStation (Video Game System)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Pebble Beach Concours D'Elegance (Car Show)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aston Martin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pebble Beach (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T18:16:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/848f3830-468b-5f67-8057-c8193efeddc1', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/848f3830-468b-5f67-8057-c8193efeddc1'}, {'abstract': 'Hiring a political heavyweight, like David Plouffe, makes good business sense.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/uber-hires-an-obama-alum/', 'snippet': 'Hiring a political heavyweight, like David Plouffe, makes good business sense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There appears to be a time in the life of every young technology company when its executives realize that they don’t understand politics, public policy or public relations and must hire somebody who does. Uber just hit that milestone: On Tuesday it announced that it was hiring David Plouffe, who ran President Obama’s 2008 election campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uber Hires an Obama Alum', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plouffe, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T18:28:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23258609-3099-5d4c-8ad9-1a395fa96a9f', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23258609-3099-5d4c-8ad9-1a395fa96a9f'}, {'abstract': '', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2014/08/20/opinion/20op-talk-lapham.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lewis Lapham', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T18:28:51+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/b45203ef-a484-5532-92a7-7e2f701f931f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/b45203ef-a484-5532-92a7-7e2f701f931f'}, {'abstract': 'The soundtrack, essentially an oldies compilation, topped Billboard’s album chart for a second week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/guardians-of-the-galaxy-soundtrack-holds-at-no-1/', 'snippet': 'The soundtrack, essentially an oldies compilation, topped Billboard’s album chart for a second week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The top three places on the Billboard album chart this week are multiple-artist projects or soundtracks, a phenomenon that happened last in April 2009. Holding the top place for its second week is the “Guardians of the Galaxy” soundtrack, which, Nielsen SoundScan reports, sold 93,000 copies in the week ending Sunday, a 15 percent drop from the week before, to grab the No. 1 position. “Guardians” is, however, essentially an oldies album that revives songs like Marvin Gaye and Tammi Terrell’s “Ain’t No Mountain High Enough,” Norman Greenbaum’s ubiquitous “Spirit in the Sky,” David Bowie’s “Moonage Daydream” and Blue Swede’s “Hooked on a Feeling,” all of which sold heftily in their day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Guardians of the Galaxy’ Soundtrack Holds at No. 1', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T18:34:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/193be531-e739-559f-b244-b6f68c54caae', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/193be531-e739-559f-b244-b6f68c54caae'}, {'abstract': 'The capital city, Vilnius, is steadily becoming a more international market, though the vast majority of buyers are still Lithuanian, according to brokers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/greathomesanddestinations/real-estate-in-lithuania.html', 'snippet': 'The capital city, Vilnius, is steadily becoming a more international market, though the vast majority of buyers are still Lithuanian, according to brokers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A RENOVATED THREE-BEDROOM APARTMENT IN VILNIUS', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Hunting in ... Lithuania', 'kicker': 'International Real Estate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Hunting in ... Lithuania', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lithuania', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vilnius (Lithuania)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T18:34:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Sigal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sigal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df120b55-35d9-5023-a8a1-116d6b383f6f', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df120b55-35d9-5023-a8a1-116d6b383f6f'}, {'abstract': 'Fashion’s big names, like those in music, sports and entertainment, have eagerly accepted the challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/anna-wintour-takes-ice-bucket-challenge/', 'snippet': 'Fashion’s big names, like those in music, sports and entertainment, have eagerly accepted the challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In fashion, the words “ice bucket” tend to be closely followed by “chilled Champagne.” But this week, buckets have been more often emptied than filled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bucket A List: Anna Wintour Takes the Challenge', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T18:38:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b68a49f7-14c7-5f51-9e8c-daf5e1820073', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b68a49f7-14c7-5f51-9e8c-daf5e1820073'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/classical-playlist-mozart-schubert-goffredo-petrassi-and-more/', 'snippet': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOZART: Piano Concertos No. 25 in C (K. 503) and No. 20 in D minor (K. 466)Martha Argerich, pianist; Claudio Abbado, conductor; Orchestra Mozart(Deutsche Grammophon 4379 1033)The only problem with the artistry of Martha Argerich, one of the most brilliant pianists of modern times, is her occasional wild streak, something that has come out especially in solo repertory. But with the right colleagues in chamber music and the right conductor in concertos, reined in just a bit, Ms. Argerich is often incomparable. She has an ideal colleague in the conductor Claudio Abbado, who recorded two Mozart concertos with her live last March at the Lucerne Festival, now issued as a recording. The performances of the Concerto No. 25 in C and No. 20 in D minor are phenomenal, with Ms. Argerich’s vibrant, colorful, imaginative playing held in check just enough by the masterly conducting of Abbado, who draws exciting playing from the festival’s Orchestra Mozart. That Abbado died in January makes the recording even more special. (Anthony Tommasini) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/arts/classical-agerich/classical-agerich-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy'