, star player and team psychologist are wrapped into one powerful presence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — One day last week, over the course of about an hour at the famed Oval cricket ground here, Alastair Cook looked at a weather report, examined the condition of the grass, decided whether his team would bat first or second, altered the positioning of some players in the field, made an inquiry with the umpire, gave a pep talk to an important cog in the team and, when necessary, stomped around near a few pigeons that were loitering in the middle of the action. (The pigeons duly flew away.)', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/sports/21cricket2/21cricket2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/21/sports/21cricket2/21cricket2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/sports/21cricket2/21cricket2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/sports/21cricket2/21cricket2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1123, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/sports/21cricket2/21cricket2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/21/sports/21cricket2/21cricket2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '