on, Mo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/opinion/a-fair-inquiry-for-michael-brown.html', 'snippet': 'Justice is a process, but there can be no hint of bias in the investigations into the shooting in Ferguson, Mo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The violence on the streets of Ferguson, Mo., abated on Tuesday night, but hundreds of peaceful protesters continue to gather each day to demand justice in the case of Michael Brown, the unarmed black teenager who was shot by a white police officer on Aug. 9. Now it’s up to local and federal officials to show that they are aggressively pursuing that demand. They have a long way to go.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fair Inquiry for Michael Brown', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Fair Inquiry for Michael Brown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCulloch, Robert P (1951- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Jay', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Darren (1986- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Prosecutors (Independent Counsel)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Louis (Mo)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T22:06:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e36561f-7f55-5e94-bb47-8c9d2f4aac4e', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e36561f-7f55-5e94-bb47-8c9d2f4aac4e'}, {'abstract': 'Laid-back style in Glasgow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/fashion/sunny-in-scotland.html', 'snippet': 'Laid-back style in Glasgow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sitting in the shadow of the University of Glasgow’s spire, the West End is home to lively bars, restaurants and premier art museums. But it’s the vast selection of affordable vintage clothing stores that drew Blossom Mccuaig to Byres Road for a day of shopping. Ms. Mccuaig indulged in the uncharacteristically sunny weather by pairing a white children’s tank top (admittedly borrowed from her little sister) and a black pencil skirt with flowers embroidered on the waist. She cites her grandparents’ wardrobe, old movies and local street style as her main inspirations. This interview has been edited and condensed.\xa0', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunny in Scotland', 'kicker': 'Intersection', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sunny in Scotland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Glasgow (Scotland)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T22:07:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fritzie Andrade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fritzie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Andrade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd6316cd-9a2f-574a-b6e6-5cd8fd71653a', 'word_count'