ct', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T22:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Labdza and Bon Duke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Labdza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Duke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/934c6310-b183-52ac-8107-fafd07481845', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/934c6310-b183-52ac-8107-fafd07481845'}, {'abstract': 'A Special Operations team failed to rescue the journalist James Foley and other Americans held in Syria during a secret mission earlier this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/world/middleeast/us-commandos-tried-to-rescue-foley-and-other-hostages.html', 'snippet': 'A Special Operations team failed to rescue the journalist James Foley and other Americans held in Syria during a secret mission earlier this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EDGARTOWN, Mass. — A secret nighttime military mission authorized by President Obama to rescue Americans held captive in Syria failed early this summer when a team of two dozen Delta Force commandos raided an oil refinery in the northern part of the country but found after a firefight with Islamic militants that there were no hostages to be saved, administration officials said Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Raid to Save Foley and Other Hostages, U.S. Found None', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a U.S. Raid, Forces Found No Hostages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foley, James (1973-2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T22:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d02422c6-beed-57ea-9b01-3020a21f07fd', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d02422c6-beed-57ea-9b01-3020a21f07fd'}, {'abstract': 'During the week of Sept. 8, we’ll be coaching a real family through real family dinners in real time – seven new meals in seven days – and we hope that you’ll cook along with us.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/casting-call-rethink-family-dinner-with-jenny-rosenstrach/', 'snippet': 'During the week of Sept. 8, we’ll be coaching a real family through real family dinners in real time – seven new meals in seven days – and we hope that you’ll cook along with us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My friend Sarah is what you might call capable. She’s an emergency room surgeon in Salt Lake City; she’s the mother of a 5-year-old; and she has just completed her ninth marathon in as many years. On a Friday last February, while my husband and I sat in her ridiculously organized kitchen, she poured each of us a glass of wine as we asked her a million questions about her day. She seemed shocked that we were so interested in hearing her E.R. stories. Removing appendixes, stabilizing car accident victims, saving lives — all in a day’s work. She put up with all of our questions, and then said something I’ll never forget.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/us/motherlode-dinner-playbook/motherlode-dinner-playbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/21/us/motherlode-dinner-playbook/motherlode-dinner-playbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/us/motherlode-dinner-playbook/motherlode-dinner-playbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/us/motherlode-dinner-playbook/motherlode-dinner-playbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1224, 'width': 1632, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/us/motherlode-dinner-playbook/motherlode-dinner-playbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/21/us/motherlode-dinner-playbook/motherlode-dinner-playbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/us/motherlode-dinner-playbook/motherlode-dinner-playbook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'lega