, 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keenan, Sandy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gers (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-20T23:22:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandy Keenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e906688a-af22-510f-a575-f9ec3a6e5773', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e906688a-af22-510f-a575-f9ec3a6e5773'}, {'abstract': 'Stories were my way in. Those figures in the cards became characters and plot points.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/20/the-tarot-card-reader/', 'snippet': 'Stories were my way in. Those figures in the cards became characters and plot points.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I thought I could hold it together, that if I was broadcasting crazy it was at least in a glamorous silent-film-star kind of way. Perfect eyeliner surrounding a glint of madness. But obviously I wasn’t pulling it off. A friend intervened: “You’re freaking me out. I’m going to take you to a woman who has helped me out of tough times before.” She set up the appointment and I washed up at her tarot card reader’s Manhattan apartment.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/opinion/0821PRIVATELIVES/0821PRIVATELIVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy