he American diplomatic mission in Benghazi, Libya, has chosen Lt. Gen. Dana K. Chipman as its chief counsel, a spokeswoman for the panel’s chairman said Wednesday. General Chipman retired in 2013 after four years as the Army’s judge advocate general under President Obama, capping a 33-year career with the military. The House voted in May to form the committee to investigate whether the Obama administration misled Congress regarding its response to the attack and its aftermath, and Representative Trey Gowdy, Republican of South Carolina, was named chairman. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Panel on Benghazi Hires General for Legal Team', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Panel on Benghazi Hires General for Legal Team', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huetteman, Emmarie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chipman, Dana K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T00:10:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/953a7a71-86d5-556e-962f-e41cbc485226', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/953a7a71-86d5-556e-962f-e41cbc485226'}, {'abstract': '“Phanto