k': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/356089a3-df63-524a-b342-126776286611', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/356089a3-df63-524a-b342-126776286611'}, {'abstract': 'Reporters, editors and those who monitor the freedom of the press describe a harsh environment for reporters, in the United States and abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/world/middleeast/from-arrests-to-beheadings-conflict-reporting-takes-harsh-toll-on-journalists.html', 'snippet': 'Reporters, editors and those who monitor the freedom of the press describe a harsh environment for reporters, in the United States and abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Islamic extremist fighters forced a freelance reporter, James Foley, to read propaganda celebrating their cause, and then beheaded him in a Middle Eastern desert. Another American journalist is next, they warned. In Iran, Jason Rezaian, a reporter for The Washington Post, was snatched by men waving an arrest warrant in late July. He has not been heard from since. In Afghanistan, Matthew Rosenberg, a reporter for The New York Times, was ordered expelled from the country because government officials did not like his stories.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Missouri to Syria, Journalists Are Becoming Targets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Missouri to Syria, Journalists in Troubled Areas Are Becoming Targets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haughney, Christine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', '