': 'Of the 103 people taken into custody during overnight protests on Monday and Tuesday, 23 were from out of state, and the influx has bothered some residents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, Mikki Kendall was in her Chicago home, watching live streams on her laptop as protesters and the police played out a 10th straight day of confrontation in the streets of Ferguson, Mo. On Wednesday, she was on the road, headed 300 miles to offer demonstrators her services as a former Army medic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Started as a Local Protest in Missouri Grows Into a Center of National Activism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Started as a Local Protest in Missouri Grows Into a Center of National Activism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzsimmons, Emma G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anonymous (Internet Group)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T01:44:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines and Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78b69140-b41a-5f27-9175-a41c71dc401a', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78b69140-b41a-5f27-9175-a41c71dc401a'}, {'abstract': 'The militants had pressed the United States to provide several million dollars for the release of James Foley, an American journalist killed in retaliation for recent airstrikes in Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/world/middleeast/isis-pressed-for-ransom-before-killing-james-foley.html', 'snippet': 'The militants had pressed the United States to provide several million dollars for the release of James Foley, an American journalist killed in retaliation for recent airstrikes in Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kneeling in the dirt in a desert somewhere in the Middle East, James Foley lost his life this week at the hands of the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria. Before pulling out the knife used to decapitate him, his masked executioner explained that he was killing the 40-year-old American journalist in retaliation for the recent United States’ airstrikes against the terrorist group in Iraq.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/world/21FOLEY/21FOLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/21/world/21FOLEY/21FOLEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/world/21FOLEY/21FOLEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy