ator, he has forged a career doing rooms that are relaxed to the point of being hard to categorize as decorated; this is the idea, an observation he would take as a high compliment. There is a Scheerer style, involving limed pecky cypress, Saarinen tables and Thonet bentwood chairs, but it is actually more of a philosophy than a style. “Elegance,” he says, “is really about economy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great American Designs of Tom Scheerer', 'kicker': 'Profile in Style', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Netto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Netto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a15443d-83aa-5279-b6f0-af90fd395f8e', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a15443d-83aa-5279-b6f0-af90fd395f8e'}, {'abstract': 'A romantic inclination toward portrait necklines and cinched waists is giving classical tailoring a more feminine spirit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/t-magazine/fashion-classic-tailored-suits-for-women.html', 'snippet': 'A romantic inclination toward portrait necklines and cinched waists is giving classical tailoring a more feminine spirit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A romantic inclination toward portrait necklines and cinched waists is giving classical tailoring a more feminine spirit.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '256', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Romantic Inclination', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Romantic Inclination Toward Portrait Necklines and Cinched Waists Is Giving Classical Tailoring a More Feminine Spirit',