iginal': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2658f906-5f2a-52d1-ad40-1618fdedcf56', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2658f906-5f2a-52d1-ad40-1618fdedcf56'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:45 P.M. (Showtime 2) KIDNAPPED FOR CHRIST (2014) Kate Logan was a young evangelical when she traveled to the Dominican Republic to document life at a Christian boarding school, now defunct, called Escuela Caribe, one of hundreds of small schools to which American parents send their supposedly troubled teenagers. Once there, Ms. Logan (above right, with Tai, a student) hoped to make a record of young lives changing for the better. Instead, she met Beth, a 15-year-old who was punished with beatings and stints in solitary confinement, and a gay teenager named David, whose parents arranged for his midnight abduction from his home in Colorado and his relocation to the school, where they hoped strict discipline and aggressive Christianity might change his sexual orientation. The resulting documentary is important, if imperfect, Neil Genzlinger wrote in The New York Times. “Ms. Logan makes the young-filmmaker mistake of injecting herself into the story,” he said. “It’s not necessary; the students’ tales are what’s important.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandon K. Thorp', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandon', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Thorp', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/c954f4b2-91e0-58b4-be07-3ed69e42d481', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c954f4b2-91e0-58b4-be07-3ed69e42d481'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 21, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/pageoneplus/corrections-august-21-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on August 21, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: August 21, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T05:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5dabf34-2e65-5b59-9fb3-cbf6fb51b7ab', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5dabf34-2e65-5b59-9fb3-cbf6fb51b7ab'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, August 21, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-thursday-august-21-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, August 21, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The United States of America will continue to do what we must do to protect our people. We will be vigilant, and we will be relentless.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, August 21, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name