rl': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/chinese-group-calls-on-japan-to-hand-over-tang-era-stele/', 'snippet': 'A Chinese organization seeks the return of a nine-ton Tang dynasty stele that was taken by the Japanese military in the early 1900s. The stone also has historical significance to Koreans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At some point between 1906 and 1908 — no one is sure precisely when — the Japanese military removed a nine-ton Tang dynasty stele from Lushun, the northeastern city also known then as Port Arthur, and shipped it to Tokyo, a trophy of Japan’s victory over the Russians in 1905.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20sino-stele01/20sino-stele01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20sino-stele01/20sino-stele01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20sino-stele01/20sino-stele01-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20sino-stele01/20sino-stele01-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 876, 'width': 1235, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20sino-stele01/20sino-stele01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/20/blogs/20sino-stele01/20sino-stele01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption