int_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T11:01:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/095a6140-5cb9-586f-9bee-860ad4243b56', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/095a6140-5cb9-586f-9bee-860ad4243b56'}, {'abstract': 'Members of the Church of Almighty God, an offshoot of Christianity, are accused of beating and kicking a woman to death after she resisted recruitment in a McDonald’s restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/world/asia/5-sect-members-go-on-trial-in-killing-at-mcdonalds-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'Members of the Church of Almighty God, an offshoot of Christianity, are accused of beating and kicking a woman to death after she resisted recruitment in a McDonald’s restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Five defendants went on trial in eastern China on Thursday, accused of beating and kicking a woman to death in a McDonald’s restaurant after she resisted their attempt to recruit her into a sect that has been condemned by the government as a malignant cult.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Says 5 in Sect Killed Woman Who Wouldn’t Join', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Says 5 in Sect Killed Woman Who Wouldn’t Join', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Church of Almighty God (Eastern Lighting)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wu Shuoyan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Lidong', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religious Cults', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T11:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a92b8f4-e512-54ba-8e51-dfe0d30f8110', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a92b8f4-e512-54ba-8e51-dfe0d30f8110'}, {'abstract': 'A $16.65 billion mortgage settlement with Bank of America is set to be announced. |Scrutiny is shifting to subprime auto loans. | Dollar General questions the motives of Family Dollar’s chief executive. | Argentina has introduced a bill to sidestep a U.S. court ruling.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/morning-agenda-bank-of-america-nears-huge-settlement/', 'snippet': 'A $16.65 billion mortgage settlement with Bank of America is set to be announced. |Scrutiny is shifting to subprime auto loans. | Dollar General questions the motives of Family Dollar’s chief executive. | Argentina has introduced a bill to sideste...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department is set to announce a $16.65 billion settlement with Bank of America over accusations that it duped investors into buying troubled mortgage securities, DealBook’s Ben Protess, Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Michael Corkery write, according to people briefed on the matter. The accord would be the biggest government settlement by a company in American history. Prosecutors are also preparing a separate civil case against Angelo Mozilo, the man who came to embody the risk-taking for which Bank of America is now paying dearly, a rare move against a senior executive at the center of the financial crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Bank of America Nears Huge Settlement', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T11:33:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b66aaea6-2db7-5400-9090-7135c00b8232', 'word_count': 2045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b66aaea6-2db7-5400-9090-7135c00b8232'}, {'abstract': 'John Lithgow and Alfred Molina star in “Love Is Strange” as Manhattan men who marry but are forced to live separately.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/movies/love-is-strange-stars-john-lithgow-and-alfred-molina.html', 'snippet': 'John Lithgow and Alfred Molina star in “Love Is Strange” as Manhattan men who marry but are forced to live separately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the first moments we see them together — waking, washing and dressing in the Manhattan apartment they have shared for decades — it is clear that Ben (John Lithgow) and George (Alfred Molina) are a walking illustration of the phrase “old married couple.” They know each other so well and have adapted, graciously and sometimes a little fractiously, to each other’s peculiarities. State law, at long last, has caught up with the reality of their relationship: The first scenes in Ira Sachs’s “Love Is Strange” take place on the morning of George and Ben’s marriage, which is solemnized in an alfresco ceremony followed by a relaxed and lively party at home. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/movies/22LOVEIS/22LOVEIS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/movies/22LOVEIS/22LOVEIS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/movies/22LOVEIS/22LOVEIS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/movies/22LOVEIS/22LOVEIS-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/movies/22LOVEIS/22LOVEIS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/22/movies/22LOVEIS/22LOVEIS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/movies/22LOVEIS/22LOVEIS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Till Real Estate Do You Part ', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Till Real Estate Do You Part', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lithgow, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Molina, Alfred', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Ira', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomei, Marisa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Love Is Strange (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T12:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1006c8fc-1527-5954-8614-64dc794cbd58', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1006c8fc-1527-5954-8614-64dc794cbd58'}, {'abstract': 'With business getting better, the stress level from working overtime has increased, and I am starting to experience something I might call “value conflict.” We want to give the customers great service, but we also don’t want to burn out our people.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/the-true-price-of-customer-service/', 'snippet': 'With business getting better, the stress level from working overtime has increased, and I am starting to experience something I might call “value conflict.” We want to give the customers great service, but we also don’t want to burn out our people...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I started my custom picture framing company 36 years ago, I was one of the first to offer a one-week turnaround in an industry that was used to making people wait anywhere from weeks to months for their framing to be completed. This required carrying a good inventory, having a flexible staff, and maintaining the systems and commitment to do so.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The True Price of Customer Service