eaves for vacation in 1889.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/1889-president-carnot-leaves-paris/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: French president is waved goodbye as he leaves for vacation in 1889.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Carnot left Paris for Fontainebleau yesterday afternoon by the Gare de Lyon, where a few hundred persons were waiting in the drenching rain to wish him and his wife bon voyage and a pleasant fortnight’s holiday. The directors of the railway company had a waiting room specially arranged, and presented to Mme. Carnot a magnificent bouquet. President Carnot, on his way to the station, happened to come across a large body of English tourists. The Britishers, who heard that the President was coming, raised a real English ‘‘Hip, hip, hip, hurrah!’’ that nearly raised the roof off the Presidential carriage.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Aug. 22, 1889', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/blogs/22ih-oldaug22-carnot/22ih-oldaug22-carnot-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/blogs/22ih-oldaug22-carnot/22ih-oldaug22-carnot-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 814}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/blogs/22ih-oldaug22-carnot/22ih-oldaug22-carnot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 755, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/blogs/22ih-oldaug22-carnot/22ih-oldaug22-carnot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1390, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio