d', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ubha, Ravi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Becker, Boris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T17:14:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Ubha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ubha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e963d721-04e4-5b71-9bd0-466ba0506bc7', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e963d721-04e4-5b71-9bd0-466ba0506bc7'}, {'abstract': 'One second. That’s all it took to lose my vision. And my world changed.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/one-moment-you-see-then-you-dont/', 'snippet': 'One second. That’s all it took to lose my vision. And my world changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was watching Diane Sawyer on the evening news, wondering how she manages year after year to look so young, when suddenly her face disappeared. Now you see. Now you don’t. One second. That’s all it took. A dense black inkblot shaped like a map of England and southern Norway suddenly blocked my view of Diane so that all I could see was her blond hair and shoulders. At first, I thought it was the television set. Changing channels didn’t bring her face back, nor did rubbing my eyes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/07/24/health/well_seeing/well_seeing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/07/24/health/well_see