, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39c210ab-d210-5d58-842f-5cd67b380707', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39c210ab-d210-5d58-842f-5cd67b380707'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: In 1939, floods in China leave thousands of people dead.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/1939-rising-china-flood-engulfs-city/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: In 1939, floods in China leave thousands of people dead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TIENTSIN — Thousands of persons are believed to have perished in Tientsin and the surrounding country as the waters of the Haiho River continued today to pour over the greater portion of the city. Officials estimated that the inundation was one of the worst in the history of North China. Most of the casualties are believed to be in villages along the Haiho, near the city. The only spots above water are a small section of the French Concession, most of the Italian Concession, the international bridge and the railway station.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug.\xa022, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Rising China Flood Engulfs City', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tianjin (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T17:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reporte