s wife.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — An Iranian-American woman with dual citizenship, who had been working in Iran as a photojournalist officially accredited by the authorities, was released on Thursday after having been held at an unidentified location since July 22, her relatives said. They refused to reveal her identity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Frees Photojournalist', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Detained Photojournalist Freed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rezaian, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salehi, Yeganeh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iranian-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T17:53:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71c7b1c5-a9f7-5c36-b8b0-4bab3f0db55b', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71c7b1c5-a9f7-5c36-b8b0-4bab3f0db55b'}, {'abstract': 'The boy, Shakie Kamara, 15, died of bleeding and hypothermic shock after being shot in the legs when soldiers fired into a crowd trying to leave a quarantined area in Monrovia, Liberia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/world/africa/liberian-boy-dies-after-being-shot-during-clash-over-ebola-quarantine.html', 'snippet': 'The boy, Shakie Kamara, 15, died of bleeding and hypothermic shock after being shot in the legs when soldiers fired into a crowd trying to leave a quarantined area in Monrovia, Liberia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONROVIA, Liberia — A teenage boy who was wounded on Wednesday during clashes at an Ebola-stricken neighborhood in Monrovia, Liberia, died of hypovolemic shock after being shot in his legs, said Dr. Mohammed Sankoh, the medical director of Redemption Hospital.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberian Boy Dies After Being Shot During Clash Over Ebola Quarantine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liberia: Boy Dies From Wounds After Clash Over Ebola Quarantine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Onishi, Norimitsu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T17:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norimitsu Onishi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Norimitsu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Onishi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97e6a0a1-553d-579d-b25b-62c8d826f231', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97e6a0a1-553d-579d-b25b-62c8d826f231'}, {'abstract': 'On Ariana Grande’s new album, “My Everything,” the young pop star strikes a balance between sweet and sultry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/arts/music/ariana-grande-prepares-my-everything.html', 'snippet': 'On Ariana Grande’s new album, “My Everything,” the young pop star strikes a balance between sweet and sultry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The building on the quiet Los Angeles block with a plate on the door that reads “Believe” — here are the offices of Scooter Braun, Svengali to Justin Bieber. Upstairs in the back is a room filled with old arcade games and the full gamut of Bieber accolades, including a piece of paper taped to the wall identifying him as Gossip Bang Chinese Fans’ Choice Male Hottie 2013, whatever that might be.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GRANDE1/24JPGRANDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GRANDE1/24JPGRANDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GRANDE1/24JPGRANDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GRANDE1/24JPGRANDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GRANDE1/24JPGRANDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GRANDE1/24JPGRANDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GRANDE1/24JPGRANDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Staying Safe, Exploring Sassy', 'kicker':