bsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/939883ca-7f23-5c94-90a1-3b16e56084ea', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/939883ca-7f23-5c94-90a1-3b16e56084ea'}, {'abstract': 'The minority leader gave the country a glimpse of confrontations to come.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/how-mitch-mcconnell-would-rule-the-senate/', 'snippet': 'The minority leader gave the country a glimpse of confrontations to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Mitch McConnell gave the country a glimpse this week of what Republican control of the Senate would look like. If it produces a familiar depression, it’s because we’ve seen what happens when Republican leaders in the House have used the identical tactics, and most people have little interest in seeing Washington return to battle stations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Mitch McConnell Would Rule the Senate', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T20:53:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bbad1c6-e1ad-531c-aec1-4f702308a62d', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bbad1c6-e1ad-531c-aec1-4f70230