up working with an assassin’s blind sister in the Italian film “Salvo.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/movies/a-mobsters-tale-in-salvo-with-saleh-bakri.html', 'snippet': 'A criminal enforcer ends up working with an assassin’s blind sister in the Italian film “Salvo.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A soulful romance, an existential action flick and something of a miracle movie — the appealing slow-burner “Salvo” hovers at the crossroads of genre. Its story pulls in all directions, and its mood, tone and backdrop are as serious as a Mafia hit. Yet its setup has the makings of a comedy sketch: A Sicilian mobster, Salvo (Saleh Bakri, holding every inch of screen), meets a blind woman, Rita (Sara Serraiocco), who soon after begins to see the light. It’s a moment that summons the New Testament prophecy about the blind seeing, but it’s also old-fashioned movie-made hokum. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22SALVO/22SALVO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22SALVO/22SALVO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22SALVO/22SALVO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22SALVO/22SALVO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22SALVO/22SALVO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22SALVO/22SALVO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22SALVO/22SALVO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Shadows, With Their Physical and Moral Impairments', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Shadows, With Their Physical and Moral Impairments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grassadonia, Fabio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piazza, Antonio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Serraiocco, Sara', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bakri, Saleh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Salvo (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T21:07:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/568dcba4-156c-5a39-8f88-20a87552c02c', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/568dcba4-156c-5a39-8f88-20a87552c02c'}, {'abstract': 'Matthew Thomas’s devastating debut novel, “We Are Not Ourselves,” is a starkly honest, intimate family story with the power to rock you to your core.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/books/we-are-not-ourselves-an-intense-family-story.html', 'snippet': 'Matthew Thomas’s devastating debut novel, “We Are Not Ourselves,” is a starkly honest, intimate family story with the power to rock you to your core.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matthew Thomas’s devastating debut novel, “We Are Not Ourselves,” does not trumpet the fact that it’s an honest, intimate family story with the power to rock you to your core. It begins on a modest note. “Instead of going to the priest,” its opening sentence says, “the men who gathered at Doherty’s Bar after work went to Eileen Tumulty’s father.” But if Eileen, the book’s wrenchingly credible main character, had not been raised by such a secular Irish-born strongman (and an alcoholic mother as tender as an ice cube), her life would never have followed the path it did.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22BOOK/22BOOK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22BOOK/22BOOK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 937}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22BOOK/22BOOK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 656, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22BOOK/22BOOK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1817, 'width': 1164, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22BOOK/22BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22BOOK/22BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'ca