], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b1f0ca3-67eb-5d9c-bf4d-da9100b572e6', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b1f0ca3-67eb-5d9c-bf4d-da9100b572e6'}, {'abstract': 'There is an opening for an ambitious candidate to push the party on issues like police abuses and racial injustice, but it hasn’t happened yet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/23/upshot/where-are-the-national-democrats-on-ferguson.html', 'snippet': 'There is an opening for an ambitious candidate to push the party on issues like police abuses and racial injustice, but it hasn’t happened yet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is something very strange about the national political reaction to the protests in Ferguson, Mo., (and nationally) over Michael Brown’s shooting. The protesters are angry, and they’re not aimlessly angry. They have a specific set of policy grievances about policing and criminal justice that are shared by a large slice of the electorate, particularly the Democratic primary electorate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/upshot/20up-democrats/20up-democrats-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/20/upshot/20up-democrats/20up-democrats-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/upshot/20up-democrats/20up-democrats-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/upshot/20up-democrats/20up-democrats-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/upshot/20up-democrats/20up-democrats-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/20/upshot/20up-democrats/20up-democrats-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/20/upshot/20up-democrats/20up-democrats-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Are the National Democrats on Ferguson?', 'kicker': 'Quiet on Criminal Justice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T21:23:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Barro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e083492a-cc80-523c-975b-68874f5f4121', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e083492a-cc80-523c-975b-68874f5f4121'}, {'abstract': 'In “Men in Armor” at the Frick Collection, a portrait by El Greco and another by Scipione Pulzone hang side by side, creating a discussion about competing views of art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/arts/design/men-in-armor-el-greco-and-pulzone-at-the-frick-collection.html', 'snippet': 'In “Men in Armor” at the Frick Collection, a portrait by El Greco and another by Scipione Pulzone hang side by side, creating a discussion about competing views of art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The\xa0quadricentennial celebration of the death of El Greco, the great painter of the Spanish Renaissance, will eventually include six East Coast museums this fall, but it is already off to a roaring start with a mouse-size exhibition at the Frick Collection. “Men in Armor” brings together only two canvases, both portraits of bearded Italian gentlemen wearing gleaming cuirasses, as upper-body armor has been called since the time of the Romans. One is a stalwart of the Frick’s collection by El Greco, purchased in 1913, when Henry Clay Frick was building the Fifth Avenue mansion that was ultimately intended to become a museum for his extensive collection. The other painting, on loan from a private collection and rarely exhibited, is by El Greco’s Roman contemporary, Scipione Pulzone.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ELGRECO/22ELGRECO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ELGRECO/22ELGRECO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ELGRECO/22ELGRECO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ELGRECO/22ELGRECO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ELGRECO/22ELGRECO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ELGRECO/22ELGRECO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ELGRECO/22ELGRECO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Silent Men, Deep in Conversation', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Silent Men, Deep in Conversation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMOR', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frick Collection', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'El Greco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pulzone, Scipione', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T21:25:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/393357d9-6893-58cf-86a8-31493988d44d', 'word_count': 1319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/393357d9-6893-58cf-86a8-31493988d44d'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes staying together is just about pragmatism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/fashion/we-pledge-allegiance.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes staying together is just about pragmatism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A friend of mine believes a king-size bed leads to a divorce. Her parents had a king-size bed, and when she was in college her father confessed to having an affair. He blamed the ensuing divorce on a lack of intimacy, but my friend blamed it on her parents’ too-big bed. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/fashion/24MODERNLOVE/24MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/fashion/24MODERNLOVE/24MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 789}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/fashion/24MODERNLOVE/24MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 779, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/fashion/24MODERNLOVE/24MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1557, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/fashion/24MODERNLOVE/24MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/24/fashion/24MODERNLOVE/24MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/fashion/24MODERNLOVE/24MODERNLOVE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Pledge Allegiance ... ’', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘We Pledge Allegiance ... ’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T21:29:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Debby Greene', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Debby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greene', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af922961-bbd8-59ae-aacb-f75011a54f55', 'word_count': 1500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af922961-bbd8-59ae-aacb-f75011a54f55'}, {'abstract': '“If I Stay” hits the audience with a series of tragedies that ripple out from a car accident on a snowy Oregon road.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/movies/if-i-stay-weighs-teenagers-prospects-after-horrific-crash.html', 'snippet': '“If I Stay” hits the audience with a series of tragedies that ripple out from a car accident on a snowy Oregon road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This summer has been bookended by two movies, both based on young adult best sellers and starring gifted and ambitious actresses, about smart, independent-minded teenage girls finding love in the shadow of death. It is hard to avoid comparing “If I Stay,” which opens on Friday, with “The Fault in Our Stars,” but there is also no reason to choose between them. Each one is a cleanly directed, credibly acted machine for the production of tears.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Limbo, and in Love', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Limbo, and in Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutler, R J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moretz, Chloe Grace', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forman, Gayle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blackley, Jamie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'If I Stay (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T21:32:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1f451ab-6a8f-5cb6-b937-586b719b03cd', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1f451ab-6a8f-5cb6-b937-586b719b03cd'}, {'abstract': 'Seven classic forms of Indian dance were performed at the Erasing Borders Festival in Battery Park City Wednesday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/arts/dance/erasing-borders-festival-focuses-on-indian-dance.html', 'snippet': 'Seven classic forms of Indian dance were performed at the Erasing Borders Festival in Battery Park City Wednesday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Krishna was evoked, Ganesha was praised, the 10 avatars of Vishnu were illustrated, seven of the eight classical dance forms of India were demonstrated — and the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island were on the horizon throughout. Passing runners and cyclists slowed down to gawp at the costumes, steps and gestures. Even yachts in the harbor veered in their course to get a better view.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ERASINGSUB/SUB22ERASING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ERASINGSUB/SUB22ERASING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ERASINGSUB/SUB22ERASING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ERASINGSUB/SUB22ERASING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ERASINGSUB/SUB22ERASING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ERASINGSUB/SUB22ERASING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22ERASINGSUB/SUB22ERASING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Praise of Hindu Gods, With Sharp Turns and Barefoot Rhythms', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Praise of Hindu Gods, With Sharp Turns and Barefoot Rhythms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Downtown Dance Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Battery Dance Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indo-America