 against Allergan, which was hoping its lawsuit against Valeant and Pershing Square Capital Management might prevent its shareholders from calling a special meeting until the case was resolved.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/21/botox-maker-allergans-suit-against-valeant-wont-delay-special-meeting/', 'snippet': 'A federal judge in California ruled against Allergan, which was hoping its lawsuit against Valeant and Pershing Square Capital Management might prevent its shareholders from calling a special meeting until the case was resolved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 7:00 p.m. | When Allergan, the maker of Botox, sued Valeant Pharmaceuticals and Pershing Square Capital Management this month in a federal court in California, claiming insider trading, its opponents said the suit was an attempt to prevent shareholders from calling a special meeting until the case was resolved. Pershing Square, Allergan’s largest shareholder, is pressing for a special meeting as it pursues a hostile takeover of the company with its partner, Valeant. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/business/dbpix-botox/dbpix-botox-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/business/dbpix-botox/dbpix-botox-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/business/dbpix-botox/dbpix-botox-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/business/dbpix-botox/dbpix-botox-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1002, 'width': 1399, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/business/dbpix-botox/dbpix-botox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/22/business/dbpix-botox/dbpix-botox-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/business/dbpix-botox/dbpix-botox-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Botox Maker Allergan’s Suit Against Valeant Won’t Delay Special Meeting', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALLERGAN INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pershing Square Capital Management', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Valeant Pharmaceuticals International Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T22:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gelles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c63a2176-b9c0-5ac2-80ef-3abe6f01eb47', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c63a2176-b9c0-5ac2-80ef-3abe6f01eb47'}, {'abstract': 'The Mei Lanfang Jingju troupe celebrates the 120th anniversary of the birth of the genre’s master, Mei Lanfang, at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/arts/music/mei-lanfang-jingju-troupe-begins-a-rare-tour.html', 'snippet': 'The Mei Lanfang Jingju troupe celebrates the 120th anniversary of the birth of the genre’s master, Mei Lanfang, at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the climactic episode of “Farewell My Concubine,” one of the seminal works of Mei Lanfang, the acknowledged master of the genre of Peking Opera, the beloved concubine of the King of Western Chu entertains her man with a dizzying sword dance. On Wednesday night at the David H. Koch Theater, to open a four-day run of performances to commemorate the 120th anniversary of Mei’s birth, a theater troupe from Beijing performed a trimmed version of this work, starring the captivating Shang Wei as the devoted concubine. During that sword dance, a delighted audience kept breaking into applause as Ms. Shang twirled around in her stunningly colorful costume and headdress, thrusting her sword, tossing it skyward, catching it behind her back, never losing composure, always the picture of stoic, stylized beauty.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22JPPEKING1/22JPPEKING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22JPPEKING1/22JPPEKING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22JPPEKING1/22JPPEKING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22JPPEKING1/22JPPEKING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1318, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22JPPEKING1/22JPPEKING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22JPPEKING1/22JPPEKING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22JPPEKING1/22JPPEKING1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mighty Women Wielding Words (and Swords)', 'kicker': 'Opera Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mighty Women Wielding Words (and Swords)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mei Lanfang', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mei Lanfang Jingju Troupe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peking Opera', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Farewell My Concubine (Opera)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-21T22:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5c9affc-c312-5762-a9f1-317307daed68', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5c9affc-c312-5762-a9f1-317307daed68'}, {'abstract': 'The MTV Video Music Awards’ video of the year nominees have revealing moments about their identities in their work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/arts/television/vma-contenders-include-beyonce-miley-cyrus-and-pharrell-williams.html', 'snippet': 'The MTV Video Music Awards’ video of the year nominees have revealing moments about their identities in their work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A LTHOUGH MTV years ago abandoned music videos for reality shows, its annual Video Music Awards remains a barometer of mainstream pop. This year, Beyoncé leads the field with eight nominations, followed by Eminem and Iggy Azalea with seven each. The show, now in its 30th year, will be broadcast from the Forum in Inglewood, Calif., on Sunday at 9 p.m. and will feature performances by Beyoncé, Taylor Swift and Maroon 5. Spontaneous moments in the show have often upstaged the videos. Remember Kanye West interrupting Ms. Swift in 2009 or Miley Cyrus gyrating on Robin Thicke last year? But the five nominees for video of the year (four feature women) each have moments that subtly reveal the musicians’ larger artistic identities.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22VMA2/22VMA2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22VMA2/22VMA2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22VMA2/22VMA2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/arts/22VMA2/22VMA2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1183, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {