onal Herald Tribune archives: In 1914, France vows to defend Belgians against Germany.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/1914-france-plans-to-free-brussels/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: In 1914, France vows to defend Belgians against Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Official communiqué from the French Ministry of War: The entry of the Germans into Brussels is a bitter experience for the Belgians and is also deeply felt by every Frenchman. The Government of the Republic has deemed it right to affirm that the sufferings of the Belgians are also our own. From the day when German soldiers entered Belgian territory, when Belgian blood was shed to resist their passage, the causes of the two countries became indissolubly associated and henceforward they are one and the same. France is resolved to do her utmost to liberate the territory of her ally. She considers that her duty will not be entirely accomplished until there is not a single German soldier left in Belgium.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Aug. 23, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/blogs/23iht-oldaug23-belgium/23iht-oldaug23-belgium-jumbo.png', 'height': 514, 'width': 580, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/blogs/23iht-oldaug23-belgium/23iht-oldaug23-belgium-superJumbo.png', 'height': 514, 'width': 580, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/blogs/23iht-oldaug23-belgium/23iht-oldaug23-belgium-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/