r': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T14:44:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35e1ab8a-86f1-5944-bef2-0f2fafb52430', 'word_count': 1528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35e1ab8a-86f1-5944-bef2-0f2fafb52430'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: General Franco tries to reassemble Spanish art.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/1939-franco-gathers-spanish-art/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: General Franco tries to reassemble Spanish art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Art lovers the world over, and especially in France, are watching the progress of one of the biggest jobs the Spanish war left for General Franco to tackle: the reassembling of the dispersed Spanish art treasures. During the war, both sides made efforts to prevent the destruction of works of art in churches, museums and private collections. During the early phases of the struggle, anarchist fanatics defaced many sacred paintings, such as “Jesus and the Virgin,” by Roger Van der Weiden, in the St. Cruz Hospital in Toledo. The Republican authorities took pains to stop this destruction. As Franco’s troops occupied the country’s territory, the authorities immediately organized a service for the protection and reassembling of works of art. These services, directed by Eugenio d’Ors, now are engaged in checking losses and putting together the famous collections which have been dispersed. Some priceless antiques and works of art are definitely lost. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 23, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Franco Gathers Spanish Art', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Civil War (1936-39)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franco, Francisco', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T14:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b9fb264-10a3-5cb1-8add-72699814516a', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b9fb264-10a3-5cb1-8add-72699814516a'}, {'abstract': 'The worshipers were killed in a mosque in a mixed Sunni-Shiite area in what appeared to be a revenge attack for bombings targeting Shiites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/23/world/middleeast/gunmen-massacre-more-than-50-sunni-worshipers-in-central-iraq.html', 'snippet': 'The worshipers were killed in a mosque in a mixed Sunni-Shiite area in what appeared to be a revenge attack for bombings targeting Shiites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Dozens of Sunni worshipers were killed during a militant raid on a rural mosque in central Iraq on Friday, an attack that security officials said had followed the attempted assassination of a local Shiite leader.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dozens Kill