 younger workers to share more publicly are challenging views of what is private.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEXT time you’re lunching with your colleagues, try this: Ask everyone their salary. You might end up dining alone in the future.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Secrecy About Salaries May Be on the Wane', 'kicker': 'Shortcuts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Secrecy About Salaries May Be on the Wane', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tugend, Alina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T15:47:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alina Tugend', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tugend', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/757ede12-33fd-5042-91f2-f9cd63a25c12', 'word_count': 1212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/757ede12-33fd-5042-91f2-f9cd63a25c12'}, {'abstract': 'Summer produce and corn tortillas combine for a bounty of meatless tacos.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/recipes-for-health-vegetarian-tacos/', 'snippet': 'Summer produce and corn tortillas combine for a bounty of meatless tacos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taco night is nothing new, but over the last five days, we’ve had taco week. The markets are piled high with irresistible produce — summer squash, tomatoes, green beans, corn, peppers and chiles, greens and herbs – and corn tortillas are a great vehicle for them.We’ve seen enough taco trucks, especially here in Los Angeles, the home of the Korean taco, to know that you can wrap a warm tortilla around just about anything and call it a taco. I leave the kimchi out of my own (though I did make one unconventional filling with tofu, a sort of picadillo cooked and mashed in a salsa ranchera that proved to be irresistible) and stick to the Mexican seasonings I love: chiles and cilantro, cumin and chili powder and salsas. Vegetables were the focus of each filling, and all of this week’s tacos are vegetarian. I combined sweet corn and green beans in one, and roasted peppers, squash and potatoes seasoned with cumin and chile powder in another. I grabbed chard from my garden for a few of the fillings, and made use of this summer’s bounty of squash.I love the flavor of corn tortillas, and they’re a godsend for friends who have trouble with gluten. I buy them in packs of three dozen, then divide the packages so I can freeze them by the dozen because I usually don’t use 36 tortillas in a week (though this week, I did). As for how much filling to count on for each taco, I follow Rick Bayless’s advice and use about a quarter cup. As he says, tacos are as much about the tortilla as they are about the filling, and you wouldn’t want to overwhelm the tortilla any more than you’d want to overwhelm pasta with too much sauce.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19recipehealthalt/19recipehealthalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19recipehealthalt/19recipehealthalt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19recipehealthalt/19recipehealthalt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19recipehealthalt/19recipehealthalt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/19/science/19recipehealthalt/19recipehealthalt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name