7f-2dd3dce7db05'}, {'abstract': 'The Leslie Lohman Museum of Gay and Lesbian Art in SoHo, established in 2011, exhibits and preserves gay and lesbian art, and fosters those who create it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/arts/design/permanency-displays-gay-and-lesbian-art.html', 'snippet': 'The Leslie Lohman Museum of Gay and Lesbian Art in SoHo, established in 2011, exhibits and preserves gay and lesbian art, and fosters those who create it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Portraits of lesbians from the artistic circle of the photographer Berenice Abbott, who moved to Paris in 1921 and apprenticed with Man Ray; homoerotic prints by David Hockney; a sketchbook by Larry Stanton, featuring images of Greenwich Village faces in the 1970s, before AIDS: These are some of the works featured in the exhibition “Permanency: Selections from the Permanent Collection” at the Leslie Lohman Museum of Gay and Lesbian Art in SoHo. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GUIDE4/24GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GUIDE4/24GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 769}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GUIDE4/24GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GUIDE4/24GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1599, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24GUIDE4/24GUIDE4-thum