 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manziel, Johnny', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Browns', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T17:16:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90d12f88-e6b2-5a12-a0f2-7d444a9ace1f', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90d12f88-e6b2-5a12-a0f2-7d444a9ace1f'}, {'abstract': 'The Internet abounds with sites offering dance on video. Four critics for The New York Times pick their favorites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/arts/dance/dance-on-video-from-many-corners-of-the-web.html', 'snippet': 'The Internet abounds with sites offering dance on video. Four critics for The New York Times pick their favorites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dancegoer of the 21st century no longer needs to go to the dance. Thanks to YouTube, Vimeo and other websites, we have dazzling access — at the touch of fingers or thumbs, on screens held in the palm, on the lap or at the desk — to performances that were unavailable, and to technological treatments that transform dance. No, it’s not the same as being in the same space and moment: The camera’s single eye reduces the spatial complexity of movement, and separate takes chop up its continuity. Here, the dance critics of The New York Times write about a few of the many performances captured in videos.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24VIDEOS1/24VIDEOS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 319, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24VIDEOS1/24VIDEOS1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 319}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24VIDEOS1/24VIDEOS1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 545, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24VIDEOS1/24VIDEOS1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1090, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24VIDEOS1/24VIDEOS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24VIDEOS1/24VIDEOS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/arts/24VIDEOS1/24VIDEOS1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pirouettes at the Tap of a Keyboard', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pirouettes at the Tap of a Keyboard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T17:17:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74245903-df07-5f67-b882-87f7367bf3e3', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74245903-df07-5f67-b882-87f7367bf3e3'}, {'abstract': 'The Industrial Revolution left an economic giant in the dust. Today, trade shocks could do the same to some Western countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/upshot/lesson-from-old-india-when-an-economy-just-doesnt-get-better.html', 'snippet': 'The Industrial Revolution left an economic giant in the dust. Today, trade shocks could do the same to some Western countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Commentators have often compared the recent Great Recession of the United States and Europe to the Great Depression of the 1930s. In both cases, asset prices tumbled, financial systems turned insolvent and demand plummeted. One difference is that in the recent case, we mounted a swifter rescue effort than we did in the 1930s; for instance, Ben S. Bernanke, as chairman of the Federal Reserve in the recent crisis, drew upon his academic research in supporting bailouts and reflating the economy.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/upshot/22up-india-1/22up-india-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/upshot/22up-india-1/22up-india-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 494}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/upshot/22up-india-1/22up-india-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cred