mbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/books/review/25BLACKALL1/0825-bks-Blackall-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/books/review/25BLACKALL1/25BLACKALL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/25/books/review/25BLACKALL1/25BLACKALL1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/books/review/25BLACKALL1/25BLACKALL1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Must Love Dogs', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Must Love Dogs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiPucchio, Kelly', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stein, David Ezra', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gall, Chris', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Christian', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T17:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophie Blackall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blackall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d60b66a-3777-5a1f-a09c-5201cf0f08f1', 'word_count': 1029, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d60b66a-3777-5a1f-a09c-5201cf0f08f1'}, {'abstract': 'Two girls (one rich, one poor) trade places on their way to visit the czar in St. Petersburg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/books/review/egg-spoon-by-gregory-maguire.html', 'snippet': 'Two girls (one rich, one poor) trade places on their way to visit the czar in St. Petersburg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the many magical or potentially magical objects in Gregory Maguire’s latest novel, “Egg & Spoon,” is a Fabergé egg. Look at one side of the egg and you see the hut of Baba Yaga. Give it a turn and an ancient ice dragon comes into view. Turn it once more and the legendary Firebird is revealed. Each rotation requires a shift in focus, and one story can be viewed only at the exclusion of the others.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-Bardugo/0824-bks-Bardugo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 313, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-Bardugo/0824-bks-Bardugo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 313}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-Bardugo/0824-bks-Bardugo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 534, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-Bardugo/0824-bks-Bardugo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-Bardugo/0824-bks-Bardugo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-Bardugo/0824-bks-Bardugo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-Bardugo/0824-bks-Bardugo-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Wicked Things Are', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where the Wicked Things Are', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maguire, Gregory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T17:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leigh Bardugo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leigh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bardugo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/db4e05f3-464d-5c02-abec-d8b27ff533fd', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db4e05f3-464d-5c02-abec-d8b27ff533fd'}, {'abstract': 'In three picture books, dancers who prefer to practice alone learn to share their talents with others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/books/review/frances-dean-who-loved-to-dance-and-dance-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'In three picture books, dancers who prefer to practice alone learn to share their talents with others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some people are natural performers. Give them a wedding D.J. or a karaoke mike and brace yourself, bystanders: It’s “Love Shack” to the max. Other people, even if they’re secretly talented, need coaxing. The bathroom-shower soprano clams up in public. The dude who rocks the funky chicken behind closed doors folds up his wings and refuses to boogie. The risk of humiliation is simply too great: People may judge. People may laugh. And how do we know that? Because at some point along the way, perhaps when we were very young, someone did judge, or did laugh — and the reflexive urge we felt to shake, rattle and roll? Poof! Extinguished.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-McDonald-1/0824-bks-McDonald-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-McDonald-1/0824-bks-McDonald-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-McDonald-1/0824-bks-McDonald-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-McDonald-1/0824-bks-McDonald-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1286, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-McDonald-1/0824-bks-McDonald-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/24/books/review/0824-bks-McDonald-1/0824-bks-McDonald-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': N