, 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bay of Bengal', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T18:42:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75f36d32-1b7f-5dab-86fd-ed533fe63b2c', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75f36d32-1b7f-5dab-86fd-ed533fe63b2c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Farel, a hairstylist who is running a pop-up salon for athletes at the United States Open, spends his Sundays with his wife and daughters at their East Hampton home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/nyregion/julien-farel-hair-today-hair-tomorrow.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Farel, a hairstylist who is running a pop-up salon for athletes at the United States Open, spends his Sundays with his wife and daughters at their East Hampton home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hairstylist and entrepreneur Julien Farel owns four salons, including the 10,000-square-foot flagship at the Loews Regency Hotel on Park Avenue, which opened in April. For the United States Open, which begins tournament play on Monday, there is a fifth salon, albeit temporary, at Arthur Ashe Stadium, where participants can have their hair cut, braided, pulled back or trimmed — whatever they need to be court- and camera-ready. Boldface names like Novak Djokovic and Victoria Azarenka are tended to personally by Mr. Farel. When New York’s Grand Slam event is not in session, Mr. Farel, 45, a native of France, and his wife, Suelyn, 45, the chief executive of the Julien Farel Group, retreat on weekends to their East Hampton home with their daughters, Chloe, 8, and Manon, 6.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Julien Farel: Hair Today, Hair Tomorrow', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hair Today, Hair Tomorrow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farel, Julien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barbers and Barbering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Hampton (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farel, Suelyn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T18:50:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd369d0-3aa1-5f0d-9677-e518e0b50052', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd369d0-3aa1-5f0d-9677-e518e0b50052'}, {'abstract': 'President Enrique Peña Nieto announced the new unit, aiming to stamp out violent crime and reassure business interests, but his was not the first such effort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/23/world/americas/familiar-flaws-seen-in-mexicos-new-elite-police-force.html', 'snippet': 'President Enrique Peña Nieto announced the new unit, aiming to stamp out violent crime and reassure business interests, but his was not the first such effort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — More than