the back-to-school issue, themed “The Way We Learn.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/08/22/behind-the-book-review-cover/', 'snippet': 'The Book Review editor, Pamela Paul, explained how her team came up with the art for the back-to-school issue, themed “The Way We Learn.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week features our third annual back-to-school issue, this year themed “The Way We Learn.” We introduced the back-to-school issue in 2012 centered on a new children’s book feature to supplement our spring children’s books special, which runs in May, and our biggest children’s book section of the year, in November, when we announce the winners of the New York Times Best Illustrated Awards. The end of the summer seemed an ideal time to cover the big fall children’s books, as well as address those sticky issues that children, parents and educators face at the beginning of the school year — from separation for toddlers to social media bullying for teenagers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/blogs/Book-Review-Image/Book-Review-Image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 562, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/blogs/Book-Review-Image/Book-Review-Image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 562}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/blogs/Book-Review-Image/Book-Review-Image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 959, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/blogs/Book-Review-Image/Book-Review-Image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1918, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 