employer, Penske Media Corporation, try to reach a legal settlement, according to a person with knowledge of the negotiations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nikki Finke Goes Silent in Reported Legal Dispute With Penske Media', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nikki Finke Goes Silent in Reported Legal Dispute With Penske Media', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finke, Nikki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penske Media Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T23:26:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9716f13-08f7-5cde-97d6-3d1a3ca2ffad', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9716f13-08f7-5cde-97d6-3d1a3ca2ffad'}, {'abstract': 'How pro-Confederate conspiracies in the 1864 Midwest helped win the elections for the Republicans.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/unrest-in-the-midwest/', 'snippet': 'How pro-Confederate conspiracies in the 1864 Midwest helped win the elections for the Republicans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 20, 1864, Oliver P. Morton, the governor of Indiana, received an anonymous letter in his Indianapolis office. The letter, postmarked from Buffalo, tipped him off to the arrival of arms and ammunition shipped secretly from the East Coast. The guns were intended, it said, for “antagonists of our Govt” who planned to foment unrest before the coming presidential election. The informer gave details about the whereabouts of shipments from a New York City arms dealer in boxes marked “stationary” [sic].', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unrest in the Midwest', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T23:29:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen E. Towne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Towne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a32f445-f8f6-5a95-b164-8d02ea972c9b', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a32f445-f8f6-5a95-b164-8d02ea972c9b'}, {'abstract': 'Arvind Subramanian, a United States-based economist, has criticized the government of Prime Minister Narendra Modi for policies that seem unfriendly to investors and markets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/23/business/international/us-economist-is-top-pick-for-indias-chief-adviser.html', 'snippet': 'Arvind Subramanian, a United States-based economist, has criticized the government of Prime Minister Narendra Modi for policies that seem unfriendly to investors and markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — With Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s new government promising to ramp up economic growth, an economist based in the United States has emerged as the most likely candidate to serve as its chief economic adviser.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Modi/Modi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Modi/Modi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Modi/Modi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Modi/Modi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1476, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Modi/Modi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Modi/Modi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/23/business/Modi/Modi-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arvind Subramanian Said to Be Top Pick for India’s Chief Economic Adviser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Economist Top Pick for India’s Chief Adviser', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Subramanian, Arvind', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-22T23:35:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ab5d081-52e4-5697-af37-e4036483d144', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ab5d081-52e4-5697-af37-e4036483d144'}, {'abstract': 'In our fall women’s fashion issue, T celebrates the quiet rebels leading the way in fashion and the culture at large.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/now-online-t-womens-fall-fashion-issue/', 'snippet': 'In our fall women’s fashion issue, T celebrates the quiet rebels leading the way in fashion and the culture at large.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our fall women’s fashion issue, T celebrates the quiet rebels leading the way in fashion and the culture at large. We start with Sarah Burton, the shy and unassuming designer who is embracing her independent streak four years after the death of her mentor and close friend, Alexander McQueen. We remember the French icon Loulou de la Falaise, whose effervescent personality and inimitable style brought out the best in her close collaborator Yves Saint Laurent, and manifested in her own designs too.\xa0We visit Federico Forquet at home in Tuscany, where the former couturier long ago put fashion in the rearview to focus on a career in interior design and gardening. And in Elena Ferrante, a novelist so elusive that no one knows what she — or he, as the case may be — even looks like, we examine the nature of literary stardom and the value of unbiased self-reflection. Elsewhere, Claire Messud visits the provocative South African-born painter Marlene Dumas at her studio in Amsterdam; T’s critic-at-large Jody Rosen heads into the Mojave Desert to investigate the Integratron, a U.F.O.-like structure that serves as a Mecca for spiritual seekers; Jenna Lyons and Courtney Love rock out to Beats and try on the latest Dior heels; and a new generation of female directors step out from behind the camera, revealing the personal experiences and passion for original filmmaking that led them to take on the Hollywood status quo. See all stories from the issue >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/t-magazine/Tfallwomenfashion-cover/Tfallwomenfashion-cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/21/t-magazine/Tfallwomenfashion-cover/Tfallwomenfashion-cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 747}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/21/t-magazine/Tfallwomenfashion-cover/Tfallwomenfashion-cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 823, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo