': 'I’m by no means the only person, or even pundit, who sometimes (often) feels that centrists are the craziest people in our political life. Liberals these days rarely stake out really extreme positions (more on that in a minute); conservatives may denounce Obama as a Muslim atheist communist, but at least they know what they want. The really strange people are those who insist that there is symmetry between left and right, that both are equally far out and equally at fault for polarization, and make up all kinds of strange stories to justify this claim.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attack of the Crazy Centrists', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-23T15:10:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae1e6a49-590d-5725-812f-f53e6276d892', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae1e6a49-590d-5725-812f-f53e6276d892'}, {'abstract': 'Ledecky, a 17-year-old American, clocked a 3:58.37 at the Pan Pacific Championships in Australia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/sports/katie-ledecky-improves-on-her-world-record-in-the-400-freestyle.html', 'snippet': 'Ledecky, a 17-year-old American, clocked a 3:58.37 at the Pan Pacific Championships in Australia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOUTHPORT, Australia — Katie Ledecky broke her world record in the 400-meter freestyle on Saturday at the Pan Pacific Swimming Championships. With the Gold Coast Aquatic Centre crowd here cheering her on, Ledecky was timed in 3 minutes 58.37 seconds. Her United States teammate Cierra Runge finished second in 4:04.55.