jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-23T18:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Rosenbloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/348cbf56-9b31-5d18-964a-072821ff5bc8', 'word_count': 1590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/348cbf56-9b31-5d18-964a-072821ff5bc8'}, {'abstract': 'Only a very small percentage of insects are pests, and most are quite beneficial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/opinion/sunday/bug-love.html', 'snippet': 'Only a very small percentage of insects are pests, and most are quite beneficial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LARAMIE, Wyo. — IT’S summertime, the season of insects, and if you spend any time outdoors (or even indoors), you’ve probably been swatting and stomping your way toward fall. Mosquitoes and midges dance over ponds, butterflies and bumblebees tussle on daisies, crickets and katydids trill melodies, moths zigzag around lights leaving dusty trails.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824BUGS/0824BUGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 228, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824BUGS/0824BUGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 228}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824BUGS/0824BUGS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824BUGS/0824BUGS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824BUGS/0824BUGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824BUGS/0824BUGS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824BUGS/0824BUGS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bug Love', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bug Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pesticides', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-23T18:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott R. Shaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Shaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/54a4bc17-cc10-5106-8cf5-e3c36360333c', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54a4bc17-cc10-5106-8cf5-e3c36360333c'}, {'abstract': 'A rodent helped calm my teenager’s anxiety.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/23/my-daughter-her-rat/', 'snippet': 'A rodent helped calm my teenager’s anxiety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Somehow, we have to get Eden, my daughter’s pet rat, from Brooklyn to Portland, Ore., where Olivia will start college next month. Like E. B. White’s Stuart Little, Eden has become part of our family, a kind of miniature sibling to my only child, who is about to leave home. Eden is one of a klatch of pet rats we know (picture three young women and their animals at our kitchen table, eating tacos, our two cats asleep in a corner). According to Robert Sullivan’s book “Rats,” “fancy” descendants of the homely gray Rattus norvegicus had an earlier moment as women’s companions during the Victorian era. Is Eden part of a revival zeitgeist thing, a moment soon to be documented by pop culture media?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824RATS/0824RATS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 564, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824RATS/0824RATS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 564}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824RATS/0824RATS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 962, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824RATS/0824RATS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1409, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824RATS/0824RATS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824RATS/0824RATS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sunday-review/0824RATS/0824RATS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Daughter, Her Rat', 'kicker': 'Menagerie', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Daughter, Her Rat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rats', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-23T18:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Metz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Metz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0454e7a-c30c-5daf-a32d-ba2060cf99ca', 'word_count': 1187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0454e7a-c30c-5daf-a32d-ba2060cf99ca'}, {'abstract': 'The economy still doesn’t have the growth and jobs to justify a rate increase.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/opinion/sunday/why-interest-rates-need-to-stay-low.html', 'snippet': 'The economy still doesn’t have the growth and jobs to justify a rate increase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sharp debate within the Federal Reserve over when to raise interest rates was publicly aired last week at the annual central bankers’ conference in Jackson Hole, Wyo. On one side is a small yet vocal minority of Fed officials who want to head off inflation by raising rates sooner rather than later. On the other is a majority that thinks a near-term rate hike would stifle growth and, with it, any chance of restoring health to the labor market. That group includes Janet Yellen, the Fed’s chairwoman, and most members of the Fed’s policy committee. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Interest Rates Need to Stay Low', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Interest Rates Need to Stay Low', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-23T18:35:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f676f12-f315-52a8-b504-95d2f9b07907', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f676f12-f315-52a8-b504-95d2f9b07907'}, {'abstract': 'Just as the body needs time to rest, so too does an essay, or a book.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/23/on-not-writing/', 'snippet': 'Just as the body needs time to rest, so too does an essay, or a book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I started writing this essay five years ago, and then I stopped. That I was not able to finish the piece did not strike me at the time as ironic but as further proof that whatever I once had in me — juice, talent, will — was gone. In any case, completing it would have made moot the very point I was attempting to make: Not writing can be good for one’s writing; indeed, it can make one a better writer. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-draft/opinionator-pog-draft-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-draft/opinionator-pog-draft-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-draft/opinionator-pog-draft-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-draft/opinionator-pog-draft-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-draft/opinionator-pog-draft-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-draft/opinionator-pog-draft-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-draft/opinionator-pog-draft-thumbLarge-v2.png', '