': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpton, Al', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-23T20:44:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1fb4944-70d2-5987-81af-6f68db9948a2', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1fb4944-70d2-5987-81af-6f68db9948a2'}, {'abstract': 'Gay-themed sporting events were once considered political statements and occasionally drew protests, but they have now become a seasonal staple, particularly in baseball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/sports/gays-and-sports-intersect-more-easily-in-the-stands.html', 'snippet': 'Gay-themed sporting events were once considered political statements and occasionally drew protests, but they have now become a seasonal staple, particularly in baseball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Friday night was not much different from most others at Dodger Stadium. An actor, Jesse Tyler Ferguson, threw out the ceremonial first pitch. A recording artist, Mary Lambert, sang the national anthem. And there was not much more hand-holding than usual among couples during the postgame fireworks show.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/sports/PRIDE1/PRIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/sports/PRIDE1/PRIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xl