.html', 'snippet': 'Jean Paul Lourdes, who trained as a biochemist in France and then worked as a perfumer in Switzerland before he became a chef, is close to creating a world-class eating experience at Restaurant Latour in Sussex County, N.J.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About a half-mile away from a restaurant called “That Italian Joint,” and down the road from the disaster-courting Action Park, sits Restaurant Latour, a rarefied establishment where matcha green tea cocktails are served with yuzu bubbles and local pickled elderflowers grace buttermilk granita. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Challenging Dinner, Layer by Layer', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Challenging Dinner, Layer by Layer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Restaurant Latour (Hamburg, NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamburg (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lourdes, Jean Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-23T21:09:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marissa Rothkopf Bates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marissa', 'middlename': 'Rothkopf', 'lastname': 'Bates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/24de2cb1-1cab-5657-8ca7-0981bf035fbb', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24de2cb1-1cab-5657-8ca7-0981bf035fbb'}, {'abstract': 'Little Pub, which opened in June 2009 in Ridgefield, is true to its name in size and ambience, and its menu is full of flavorful surprises.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/nyregion/a-review-of-little-pub-in-ridgefield.html', 'snippet': 'Little Pub, which opened in June 2009 in Ridgefield, is true to its name in size and ambience, and its menu is full of flavorful surprises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Douglas and Daneen Grabe named their new restaurant Little Pub, they were not kidding about the size. This Ridgefield restaurant, which opened in June 2009, is tiny, seating a mere 25 to 35 diners inside, giving it a built-in noisiness. The good news is that an attached screened porch (seating 35 to 40) makes conversation possible while dining. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINECT3/24DINECT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINECT3/24DINECT3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 602}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINECT3/24DINECT3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1020, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINECT3/24DINECT3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2040, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINECT3/24DINECT3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINECT3/24DINECT3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24DINECT3/24DINECT3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venturing Beyond the Usual Bar Food', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venturing Beyond the Usual Bar Food', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ridgefield (Conn)', 'rank'