'}, {'abstract': 'The menu at Massa’ Coastal Italian Cuisine in Mamaroneck is organized in a way that pays homage to the Italian homeland of the co-owners and co-executive chefs, Pasquale Coli and his son Francesco Coli.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/nyregion/a-review-of-massa-coastal-italian-cuisine-in-mamaroneck.html', 'snippet': 'The menu at Massa’ Coastal Italian Cuisine in Mamaroneck is organized in a way that pays homage to the Italian homeland of the co-owners and co-executive chefs, Pasquale Coli and his son Francesco Coli.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s exciting to find an Italian restaurant with a menu that promises to deliver the rich flavors of Southern Italy, specifically Puglia’s Salentine Peninsula, the area at the heel of Italy’s “boot.” The kitchen of Massa’ Coastal Italian Cuisine in Mamaroneck is influenced by the produce from the peninsula’s inland farmsteads (or masserias) and by the plentiful seafood fished from the adjoining Adriatic and Ionian Seas. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24SUBDINEWE2/24SUBDINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24SUBDINEWE2/24SUBDINEWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24SUBDINEWE2/24SUBDINEWE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/24/nyregion/24SUBDINEWE2/24SUBDINEWE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype'