 earthquake damaged buildings, knocked out power to thousands and injured scores of residents. It was the largest quake to strike the Bay Area since 1989, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/us/strong-earthquake-shakes-bay-area-in-california.html', 'snippet': 'The magnitude-6.0 earthquake damaged buildings, knocked out power to thousands and injured scores of residents. It was the largest quake to strike the Bay Area since 1989, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAPA, Calif. — Early Sunday morning, Franz Oehler’s house blew apart.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Losses From California Quake Could Top $1 Billion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Earthquake Strikes in California’s Napa Valley', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco Bay Area (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Napa (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Geological Survey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-24T12:12:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy and Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ba16382-b148-563b-b8f9-9e104cd720e0', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ba16382-b148-563b-b8f9-9e104cd720e0'}, {'abstract': 'In my new husband’s family, what was “fair” in family life was governed by seniority. I preferred to rely on egalitarian turn taking. “Fair” turns out to be subject to interpretation.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/in-a-stepfamily-whose-fairness-wins-out/', 'snippet': 'In my new husband’s family, what was “fair” in family life was governed by seniority. I preferred to rely on egalitarian turn taking. “Fair” turns out to be subject to interpretation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Years ago, when Bob (now my husband) and I were cohabiting but not yet married, we started taking our children to Florida over April vacation to take advantage of my mother’s unused timeshare week. My daughter, Katy, was around 7 at the time, and Bob’s two youngest girls, Whit and Hilly, were teenagers. The layout of our condo featured, on the beach side, a spacious master suite with a king-size bed and a balcony. Its distinct Yin, at the other end of the unit, was a rayless chamber with twin beds and a view of the parking lot. Per my advance request, the housekeeping crew had stuffed a rollaway bed into the room before we arrived. The three girls were squeezed together like industrially farmed piglets. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/us/motherlode-house-sun/motherlode-house-sun-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/us/motherlode-house-sun/motherlode-house-sun-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/us/motherlode-house-sun/motherlode-house-sun-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/us/motherlode-house-sun/motherlode-house-s