elle made a surprise return here — and no one seemed more surprised than he. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/comedy/comedy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/comedy/comedy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 862}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/comedy/comedy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 713, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/comedy/comedy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2025, 'width': 1409, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/comedy/comedy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/comedy/comedy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/comedy/comedy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chappelle Returns to Hartford (All Is Forgiven)', 'kicker': 'On Comedy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chappelle Returns to Hartford (All Is Forgiven)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chappelle, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hartford (Conn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-24T17:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38846c07-481f-5de6-81e8-4ba3e2df3941', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38846c07-481f-5de6-81e8-4ba3e2df3941'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/24/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:30 P.M. (Starz) BLUE JASMINE (2013) Woody Allen’s film about a Manhattan socialite brought low is his “most sustained, satisfying and resonant film since ‘Match Point,’\xa0” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. The socialite is Jasmine (Cate Blanchett, whose performance won her an Oscar for best actress), an Upper East Sider whose husband, Hal (Alec Baldwin), had been sent to prison for financial crimes. Jasmine, suddenly penniless, seeks shelter and comfort with her sister (Sally Hawkins, above center, flanked by Ms. Blanchett and Andrew Dice Clay) in San Francisco. Slowly, in flashbacks, Mr. Allen reveals why Hal went to prison, what happened to him and who’s been most victimized. The more you learn about the people on screen, the worse you feel for them. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-24T17:06:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brand