ugh the Charlie Parker Jazz Festival in Harlem, no matter the age of the performers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The proposition that jazz is a continuum, with elders passing down knowledge, guildlike, to their successors, can be found almost anywhere the music manages to thrive. But it finds a special traction at the Charlie Parker Jazz Festival in Marcus Garvey Park in Harlem, where the audience comes with judicious expectations, implicitly on guard against posturing or pandering — but eager to be reached and to respond in turn.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'These Hand-Me-Downs Still Shine Like New', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'These Hand-Me-Downs Still Shine Like New', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parker, Charlie, Jazz Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aldana, Melissa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowers, Kris', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loueke, Lionel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roney, Wallace', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Garvey, Marcus, Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-24T20:45:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/566ad19c-ac3a-5480-824e-0db6b521f