as shuttered before the cinema doors were even open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/movies/beijing-film-festival-is-shuttered-again.html', 'snippet': 'The 11th edition of an independent film festival set to begin on Saturday in Beijing was shuttered before the cinema doors were even open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 11th edition of an independent film festival set to begin on Saturday in Beijing was shuttered before the cinema doors were even open. The Chinese authorities confiscated documents and films and briefly detained organizers of the Beijing Independent Film Festival, The Associated Press reported. The festival has faced numerous hurdles over the years, including a power failure in 2012 that organizers attributed to the government. This year, however, was different, Wang Hongwei, the festival’s artistic director, told The A.P. “In the past few years, when they forced us to cancel the festival, we just moved it to other places, or delayed the screenings,” he said. “But this year, we cannot carry on with the festival. It is completely forbidden.” Mr. Wang and Li Xianting, the founder of the festival’s organizing group, were arrested on Saturday night but later released.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beijing Film Festival Is Shuttered Again', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beijing Film Festival Is Shuttered Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-24T21:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c3dfca3-24b1-54fa-af95-43dff1a9ebaf', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c3dfca3-24b1-54fa-af95-43dff1a9ebaf'}, {'abstract': 'Architectural influences will provide the framework of the Martha Graham Dance Company’s 2014-15 season, organizers announced on Sunday', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/arts/dance/martha-graham-dance-announces-season.html', 'snippet': 'Architectural influences will provide the framework of the Martha Graham Dance Company’s 2014-15 season, organizers announced on Sunday', 'lead_paragraph': 'Architectural influences will provide the framework of the Martha Graham Dance Company’s 2014-15 season, organizers announced on Sunday. Titled “Shape&Design,” the company’s two-week season at the Joyce Theater (Feb. 10-22) will explore the structural aspects of works by Graham and others. Highlights include new commissions by Kyle Abraham, Michelle Dorrance, Liz Gerring and Sonya Tayeh. In honor of the 85th anniversary of Graham’s “Lamentation,” each choreographer will contribute a work for “Lamentation Variations,” a series that began in 2007 and features pieces inspired by Graham’s signature solo. The season also plans to feature works exemplifying Graham’s collaborations with the sculptor Isamu Noguchi. In addition to the Joyce season and a 20-city tour, the troupe is scheduling performances at various New York locations throughout the fall and winter. The Graham Deconstructed series, which takes audiences behind the scenes, begins with Peter Sparling’s look at the 1953 piece “Voyage” (Sept. 16 and 17), followed by a company performance of “Appalachian Spring” (Oct. 30) to celebrate the 70th anniversary of its premiere; both will be at the Martha Graham Studio Theater in the West Village. The Museum at the Fashion Institute of Technology will host a performance on Oct. 28 in conjunction with its “Dance and Fashion” exhibition, which includes several Graham Company costumes. And from Dec. 10 through 13, Hauser & Wirth will host the dancers as part of that Chelsea gallery’s Thomas Houseago exhibition. More information is at marthagraham.org.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Martha Graham Dance Announces Season', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Martha Graham Dance Announces Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Graham, Martha, Dance Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-24T21:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aa4257c-df0a-5cd7-a061-e32979999ad1', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aa4257c-df0a-5cd7-a061-e32979999ad1'}, {'abstract': 'All eyes will be on stars like Novak Djokovic and Serena Williams, but there are plenty of other intriguing players at this year’s Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/sports/tennis/players-to-watch-at-the-us-open.html', 'snippet': 'All eyes will be on stars like Novak Djokovic and Serena Williams, but there are plenty of other intriguing players at this year’s Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caroline Wozniacki ', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im