alue': 'San Francisco Bay Area (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T03:06:43+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/fb9cb4aa-9480-5f3c-8084-043d173df21b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/fb9cb4aa-9480-5f3c-8084-043d173df21b'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, August 25, 2014.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-monday-august-25-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, August 25, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“My girlfriend and I were thrown straight in the air, and the windows exploded.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, August 25, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T03:08:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc6b5ed9-f1dc-51a2-b343-63ed798260d5', 'word_count': 32, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc6b5ed9-f1dc-51a2-b343-63ed798260d5'}, {'abstract': 'Soho Rep will take audiences from a South African kitchen to a Brooklyn laundromat in its 2014-15 season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/theater/soho-rep-plans-varied-productions.html', 'snippet': 'Soho Rep will take audiences from a South African kitchen to a Brooklyn laundromat in its 2014-15 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soho Rep will take audiences from a South African kitchen to a Brooklyn laundromat in its 2014-15 season, the theater is to announce on Monday. The season will open with the United States premiere of Debbie Tucker Green’s “Generations” (Sept. 30-Oct. 26), a coproduction with the Play Company that centers on three generations of a South African family preparing a meal. The play will reunite Ms. Tucker and Leah C. Gardiner, the writing-directing team behind the Obie-winning 2011 production of “Born Bad.” The new year will begin with “Winners and Losers” (Jan. 2-Feb. 1), directed by Chris Abraham. The work is about two friends — portrayed by the play’s creators Marcus Youssef and James Long — who are forced to take a frank look at their lives through a made-up game. In May, Soho Rep will welcome the world premiere of Anne Washburn’s “10 Out of 12.” Directed by Les Waters, the production is about making a play and about how work shapes us. The season will wrap up with “Washeteria,” taking place in an unused storefront in South Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Created by Louisa Thompson, with Sarah Benson and Adrienne Kapstein, the play is a compilation of episodes created by cast members and a team of second-graders, with each story lasting about the length of a wash cycle. More information is at sohorep.org.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soho Rep Plans Varied Productions', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Soho Rep Plans Varied Productions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soho Rep', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Debbie Tucker', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washburn, Anne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, Les', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benson, Sarah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gardiner, Leah C', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abraham, Chris', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T04:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/146b5b54-9ac1-58fb-bf2a-7be97c30beb2', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/146b5b54-9ac1-58fb-bf2a-7be97c30beb2'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 28 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/word-of-the-day-lugubrious/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 28 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'lugubrious •\\lu̇-ˈgü-bre-əs also -ˈgyü-\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | lugubrious', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T04:02:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d43d1e21-874e-53c0-ba71-4cb080292863', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d43d1e21-874e-53c0-ba71-4cb080292863'}, {'abstract': 'Even with an excellent chance of being cured, teenagers with cancer face myriad emotional, educational and social concerns, especially missing out on activities and losing friends who can’t cope with cancer in a contemporary.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/healing-teenage-cancers-scars/', 'snippet': 'Even with an excellent chance of being cured, teenagers with cancer face myriad emotional, educational and social concerns, especially missing out on acti