[{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T04:09:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2832a63-b024-5f20-b536-e8e6c93193a5', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2832a63-b024-5f20-b536-e8e6c93193a5'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:15 P.M. (Showtime 2) MAD HOT BALLROOM (2005) This documentary, filmed in three New York City schools, finds fifth-graders of various backgrounds and ethnicities training for and participating in a ballroom dancing competition. The director, Marilyn Agrelo, sheds a little light on the city’s class differences without making a big deal about them. “The young sophisticates of TriBeCa seem not only materially better off than their counterparts uptown or in Brooklyn, but also confident of their superiority,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “In spite of their teacher’s concerns about foisting too much competition on them, they expect to win. The children of Washington Heights, on the other hand — or at least their passionate, dynamic teacher — feel as if they need to win.” (Above, the students Wilson and Jatnna.) ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T04:15:02+0000', 'doc