cleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/25artsbeat-true/25artsbeat-true-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/25artsbeat-true/25artsbeat-true-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/25artsbeat-true/25artsbeat-true-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/25artsbeat-true/25artsbeat-true-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/25artsbeat-true/25artsbeat-true-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/arts/25artsbeat-true/25artsbeat-true-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘True Blood’ Recap: Finale Says Farewell to Bad Things', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T11:48:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11de86c8-6650-5e1f-90c3-1ad4c8de4b28', 'word_count': 1785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11de86c8-6650-5e1f-90c3-1ad4c8de4b28'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Roosevelt insists he doesn’t consider the war imminent in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/1939-roosevelt-sends-peace-appeals/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Roosevelt insists he doesn’t consider the war imminent in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In an ultimate attempt to use his influence for peace, President Roosevelt addressed peace appeals early this morning [Aug. 25] to Chancellor Adolf Hitler and President Ignace Moscicki of Poland. The messages, which were not identical, suggested three possible methods of arriving at a peaceful solution of the dispute between the two countries: direct negotiation, submission of the dispute to neutral arbitration, agreement to solve the controversy through the procedure of conciliation. The President suggested that the parties select as conciliator or mediator a national of one of the traditionally neutral states of Europe or of the American republics. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 26, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/blogs/26iht-oldaug26/26iht-oldaug26-articleLarge.png', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/26/blogs/26iht-oldaug26/26iht-oldaug26-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/blogs/26iht-oldaug26/26iht-oldaug26-jumbo.png', 'height': 618, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/blogs/26iht-oldaug26/26iht-oldaug26-superJumbo.png', 'height': 729, 'width': 1207, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/blogs/26iht-oldaug26/26iht-oldaug26-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/26/blogs/26iht-oldaug26/26iht-oldaug26-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/blogs/26iht-oldaug26/26iht-oldaug26-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Roosevelt Sends Peace Appeals', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitler, Adolf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Franklin Delano', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T11:51:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68f6bfb6-652c-5659-b7dc-e791057e8cbe', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68f6bfb6-652c-5659-b7dc-e791057e8cbe'}, {'abstract': 'Burger King says it is in talks to buy Tim Hortons. | Roche has agreed to buy InterMune. | An unfinished chapter at Countrywide. | Central Bankers have a new gospel.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/morning-agenda-burger-kings-deal-talks/', 'snippet': 'Burger King says it is in talks to buy Tim Hortons. | Roche has agreed to buy InterMune. | An unfinished chapter at Countrywide. | Central Bankers have a new gospel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Burger King said on Sunday that it was in talks to buy Tim Hortons, the Canadian doughnut-and-coffee chain, in a potential deal that would create one of the world’s biggest fast-food chains, DealBook’s Michael J. de la Merced writes. Should the deal be completed, it would mean Burger King’s corporate headquarters would move to Canada, raising the prospect of yet another United States company switching its national citizenship to lower its tax bill. The two companies are expected to argue that a merger would bring a host of strategic benefits, but it would nevertheless count as a so-called corporate inversion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Burger King’s Deal Talks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T11:54:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3edcf09-d68e-5a11-8c96-3d15f2738356', 'word_count': 1951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3edcf09-d68e-5a11-8c96-3d15f2738356'}, {'abstract': 'Speakers at the teenager’s funeral service, addressing an overflowing crowd, exhorted mourners to work for justice, not just for Mr. Brown, but for others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/us/michael-brown-funeral.html', 'snippet': 'Speakers at the teenager’s funeral service, addressing an overflowing crowd, exhorted mourners to work for justice, not just for Mr. Brown, but for others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — His gold-and-black coffin was topped by a baseball cap — a palpable, personal reminder of the young man who was fatally shot by a police officer only weeks ago. But the calls from the pulpit were for Michael Brown’s memory to live on in a broad movement for justice, for voter participation, and for answers to vexing and unending questions about race and policing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Mourning for Michael Brown, Call for Change', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Mourning, Call for Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "My Brother's Keeper", 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpton, Al', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Louis (Mo)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T12:04:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff3d6d07-f8d5-57c3-bb04-0f0cc4e76575', 'word_count': 1400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff3d6d07-f8d5-57c3-bb04-0f0cc4e76575'}, {'abstract': 'A new report suggests that bear farms have not decreased the demand for wild bears and bear parts.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/researchers-find-illegal-bear-trade-expanding-in-asia/', 'snippet': 'A new report suggests that bear farms have not decreased the demand for wild bears and bear parts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The illegal traffic in bears nearly tripled in Asia between 2000 and 2011, according to a study by Traffic, the wildlife trade monitor, of trade data and customs seizures in 17 countries. That increase suggests that the establishment of bear farms, to meet the demand for bile and other bear products, has not shielded wild bears from poaching, the organization said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/world/25sino-bear01/25sino-bear01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/25/world/25sino-bear01/25sino-bear01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/world/25sino-bear01/25sino-bear01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/world/25sino-bear01/25sino-bear01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/25/world/25sino-bea