, 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/04/multimedia/technique-caramelize/technique-caramelize-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/04/multimedia/technique-caramelize/technique-caramelize-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooking Techniques: Caramelizing Onions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T17:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/04315789-b40b-5b90-bb69-91dfc10b0eca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/04315789-b40b-5b90-bb69-91dfc10b0eca'}, {'abstract': 'The fine-jewelry designer enlisted the artist and photographer for a new campaign, the result of winning a contest sponsored by the CFDA/Vogue Fashion Fund and Kate Spade New York.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/monique-pean-ryan-mcginley-video-liya-kebede/', 'snippet': 'The fine-jewelry designer enlisted the artist and photographer for a new campaign, the result of winning a contest sponsored by the CFDA/Vogue Fashion Fund and Kate Spade New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each season, the designer Monique Péan visits a different destination to source materials and ideas for her fine-jewelry collection. The latest line out this fall, titled “Lahnse,” had its genesis in Norway and Iceland, whose rugged landscapes provided both stones (such as labradorite) and inspiration for the pieces’ geometric shapes. When Péan won a CFDA/Vogue Fashion Fund contest — for which Kate Spade New York partnered with the designer to produce a campaign to appear in the September issue of Vogue — she enlisted the artist Ryan McGinley, who “is amazing at shooting in nature,” she says. “The sense of exploration captured in Ryan’s work aligns with my design process of traveling the world.” The black sand and rock formations at Iceland’s Vík Í Myrdal beach, one of the shoot locations, also made their way into an accompanying short film, which, like the campaign, features the model Liya Kebede. (The location also figured prominently in the recent indie film “Land Ho!,” whose directors shared a travel diary with T.) Here, a first look at the clip.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan McGinley Shoots a Short Film for Monique Péan', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kebede, Liya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGinley, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pean, Monique', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T18:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fbb6702-9fa5-5e7a-8b6d-87cddfdbac69', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fbb6702-9fa5-5e7a-8b6d-87cddfdbac69'}, {'abstract': 'Use steaming liquid to scrape the flavorful burnt bits off the bottom of the pan while cooking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/dining/100000003068657/cooking-techniques-deglazing-a-pan.html', 'snippet': 'Use steaming liquid to scrape the flavorful burnt bits off the bottom of the pan while cooking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Use steami