unt': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3e113357-9502-5ce6-9518-072986e8dcf2'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Baller remained committed even after his own accountant spoke to a lawyer, who came back vehemently opposed to the idea.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/a-business-owner-stands-by-zane-benefits-controversial-health-insurance-plan-for-now/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Baller remained committed even after his own accountant spoke to a lawyer, who came back vehemently opposed to the idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In June, we reported on the controversy surrounding Zane Benefits, a company that has won over many small businesses by promising them that they can cancel their group health insurance plan and still offer their employees a health benefit. Zane sells software that helps small businesses reimburse workers — with tax-free dollars! — when they buy their own individual insurance policies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Business Owner Stands By Zane Benefits’ Controversial Health Insurance Plan (for Now)', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zane Benefits Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T18:49:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelb