tion': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cf79913-e4a0-5a51-9f79-9bfe04d74268', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cf79913-e4a0-5a51-9f79-9bfe04d74268'}, {'abstract': 'Only 18 percent of women in early labor were given injections to help the child after birth and drugs to delay labor. A total of 42 percent received neither.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/health/premature-labor-drugs-underused-study-says.html', 'snippet': 'Only 18 percent of women in early labor were given injections to help the child after birth and drugs to delay labor. A total of 42 percent received neither.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each year, roughly 1 million children worldwide die after being born prematurely, yet two strategies that are effective in preventing these deaths are largely underused, researchers have found.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Premature Labor Drugs Underused, Study Says', 'kicker': 'Global Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Premature Labor Drugs Underused, Study Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saint Louis, Catherine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lancet, The (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T19:16:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/498f20af-f8d7-5200-adf0-5056c2bdbdbd', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/498f20af-f8d