: 'Appointment at Chinese Journalism School Highlights Growing Party Role', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Journalism Schools', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Propaganda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin Zhibo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beijing University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lanzhou University', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Daily", 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hubei Province (China)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T22:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damon Yi and Amy Qin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54d1b456-590d-5e69-bfbf-e3bfc47be322', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54d1b456-590d-5e69-bfbf-e3bfc47be322'}, {'abstract': 'A fungus uses the carpenter ants it kills to get at other potential victims in the colony.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/science/fungus-turns-ants-into-zombie-booby-traps.html', 'snippet': 'A fungus uses the carpenter ants it kills to get at other potential victims in the colony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A fungus compels infected ants to die near their colonies, ensuring access to a steady stream of new victims, researchers say in PLOS One. Before killing a carpenter ant, the fungal parasite prompts it to climb vegetation in rain forests. After the ant dies, it stays attached to the leaf, from where the fungus can drop spores on unsuspecting passers-by. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/science/FLOA/FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/26/science/FLOA/FLOA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/science/FLOA/FLOA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/science/FLOA/FLOA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/science/FLOA/FLOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/26/science/FLOA/FLOA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/science/FLOA/FLOA-thumbLarge.jpg', 