 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cf323ab-4763-5c95-9570-9c204df67ceb', 'word_count': 1579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cf323ab-4763-5c95-9570-9c204df67ceb'}, {'abstract': 'The artist hosted an event in Riverside Park in Manhattan that asked dancers to evoke seminal artistic periods, from the Renaissance to Abstract Expressionism.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/rashaad-newsome-king-of-arms-art-ball-riverside-park-photos/', 'snippet': 'The artist hosted an event in Riverside Park in Manhattan that asked dancers to evoke seminal artistic periods, from the Renaissance to Abstract Expressionism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday, the artist Rashaad Newsome hosted the second edition of the King of Arms Art Ball in Riverside Park in Manhattan. The event consisted of a series of performances that married the elements of a vogue ball with art historical moments. In one segment, dancers were asked to show their moves while wearing looks inspired by the drapery seen in Renaissance painting; in another, they were challenged to embody the qualities of Abstract Expressionism. An all-star jury that included ballroom legends like Meeka Prodigy and Héctor Xtravaganza awarded prizes. The photographer Dina Litovsky was on hand to capture the action.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rashaad Newsome Marries Voguing With Art History', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newsome, Rashaad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Riverside Park (