t': 'From the sounds to the faces to the clothes, diversity ruled the day at the Brooklyn music and arts event.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years ago, the first Afropunk Festival\xa0hosted a free concert to 100 or so revelers at BAMcafé in Fort Greene, Brooklyn. Now, the event has grown into one of New York’s biggest and most spirited summer happenings. This past weekend, acts such as SZA, Sharon Jones & the Dap-Kings and D’Angelo drew crowds in the tens of thousands to Commodore Barry Park, near the Navy Yard. Diversity ruled the day, from the sounds onstage to the faces in the crowd to the wildly styled looks on parade. As expected, fairgoers brought their fashion A game, sporting elements of Africana, hip-hop, punk rock and sportswear — often all together in a single outfit. The photographer Daniel Lord was on hand to capture the action.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Many Looks of Afropunk Festival 2014', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Sharon Lafaye (1956- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'SZA (Singer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dap-Kings (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Greene (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-25T22:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By daniel lord', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/201a62c0-ee7b-5ef0-9f98-cd39c2bbb3fb', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/201a62c0-ee7b-5ef0-9f98-cd39c2bbb3fb'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of hours of shows are becoming available