i organization with a murderous anti-Western ideology controls territory in Iraq and Syria, which are closer to Europe and the United States than Afghanistan is. It commands resources and camps and even a Syrian military base. It spreads its propaganda through social media. It has set the West on edge through the recorded beheading of the American journalist James Foley — with the promise of more to come.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-thumbLarge-v6.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making of a Disaster', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Making of a Disaster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Roger', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T01:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd645732-f0d5-5034-8990-caa924c01827', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd645732-f0d5-5034-8990-caa924c01827'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Ross Sorkin’s summer reading list on the meanderings of business, finance and technology.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/25/absorbing-events-past-in-a-summers-reading-list/', 'snippet': 'Andrew Ross Sorkin’s summer reading list on the meanderings of business, finance and technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the summer comes to an end, I’ve been trying to squeeze as much reading as I can into the final days. A benefit of this job is the opportunity to get sneak peeks at books before they are released, so I’ve been catching up on a pile of books that I missed earlier in the year as well as trying to get ahead by polishing off a couple that won’t be published until later this fall. So while Amazon’s Jeff Bezos continues to battle it out with Hachette (now that