': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T03:33:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17625aaf-e091-5f4c-8d61-98f2548947bc', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17625aaf-e091-5f4c-8d61-98f2548947bc'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s symposium asked “What is cooking?” — a question that may have proved too difficult to answer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/t-magazine/mad4-food-festival-copenhagen.html', 'snippet': 'This year’s symposium asked “What is cooking?” — a question that may have proved too difficult to answer.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What is cooking?” was the question posed by the organizers of this year’s MAD symposium. During the two-day festival in Copenhagen, which culminated yesterday, it was perhaps never fully answered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MAD4 Food Festival in Copenhagen: A Rallying Cry for Social Change', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TLiving', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Prior', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prior', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c8bfeb4-c4ff-557c-9fad-314f0e0a0a07', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c8bfeb4-c4ff-557c-9fad-314f0e0a0a07'}, {'abstract': 'The co-curator of this year’s symposium in Copenhagen reveals his hopes for the event and his special lunch plans for the festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/22/t-magazine/alex-atala-mad-symposium-copenhagen.html', 'snippet': 'The co-curator of this year’s symposium in Copenhagen reveals his hopes for the event and his special lunch plans for the festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This Sunday and Monday, under a big tent in a field in Copenhagen, many of the culinary world’s most influential figures will gather for the fourth MAD Symposium. Founded by the Noma chef Rene Redzepi and his team in 2011, the annual gathering has matured from a party for like-minded chefs to a themed conference that informs conversations in kitchens worldwide. Last year’s theme, “Guts,” was co-curated by Momofuku’s David Chang and saw a roster of international presenters speak, both metaphorically and literally, about the subject. This year, Atala, the Brazilian DJ-turned-chef and owner of acclaimed Sao Paulo restaurant D.O.M. (who controversially demonstrated the reality of working with meat by decapitating a live chicken onstage at last year’s festival), returns as co-curator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/t-magazine/22atala-prior/22atala-prior-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/22/t-magazine/22atala-prior/22atala-prior-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/t-magazine/22atala-prior/22atala-prior-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/22/t-magazine/22atala-prior/22atala-prior-