 the teenage friends Francis Doyle (Emile Hirsch) and Tim Sullivan (Kieran Culkin) cope with the anxieties of education, puberty and first love by writing a series of superhero comics. “The masterstroke of this small, heartfelt directorial debut,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times, “is its integration of animated sequences (by Todd McFarlane) in which action-adventure caricatures of the comic book characters parallel or comment on events in the boys’ lives.” Those lives are darkened as the film progresses, most affectingly by a story of familial abuse shared by Francis’s new girlfriend, Margie Flynn (Jena Malone). Jodie Foster plays Sister Assumpta, an especially reviled teacher at the boys’ Roman Catholic school. Mr. Holden wrote: “Ms. Foster, who seems to grow primmer with each film, locates the compassion beneath her character’s grim, authoritarian surface. Like tiny ripples on a pond, her face registers the concerns of a caring surrogate parent committed to practicing an austere form of tough love.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandon K. Thorp', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandon', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Thorp', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/753ac3bb-163d-548a-96eb-66c2ddf8ec1f', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/753ac3bb-163d-548a-96eb-66c2ddf8ec1f'}, {'abstract': 'A story about marijuana fields discovered in satellite images that went viral has been deleted, and a denial has been issued 