tions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T11:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e15cd4e-f8bf-58b7-b98c-d7d22b24dbdc', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e15cd4e-f8bf-58b7-b98c-d7d22b24dbdc'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Hundreds of Americans were stranded in Europe as war threatened to break out in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/1939-americans-stranded-in-europe/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Hundreds of Americans were stranded in Europe as war threatened to break out in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States liner President Roosevelt, the Italian Line’s Conte di Savoia and numerous other large trans-Atlantic craft have changed their schedules drastically as a result of the critical European situation. Thousands of American visitors to Europe, those successful in the scramble for berths on liners bound for the United States, were disappointed when their ships either returned to home ports in Europe or announced indefinite postponement of scheduled sailings pending the issue of the crisis. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 27, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/27iht-oldaug27/27iht-oldaug27-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/27iht-oldaug27/27iht-oldaug27-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/27iht-oldaug27/27iht-oldaug27-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 633, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/27iht-oldaug27/27iht-oldaug27-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 633, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/27iht-oldaug27/27iht-oldaug27-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/27iht-oldaug27/27iht-oldaug27-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/27iht-oldaug27/27iht-oldaug27-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Americans Stranded in Europe', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T11:10:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/447328ed-2f01-508d-8bc4-e41936fe8866', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447328ed-2f01-508d-8bc4-e41936fe8866'}, {'abstract': 'Ukraine released video of what it said were captured Russian soldiers, raising tensions as President Vladimir V. Putin met with his Ukrainian counterpart, Petro O. Poroshenko.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/world/europe/ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'Ukraine released video of what it said were captured Russian soldiers, raising tensions as President Vladimir V. Putin met with his Ukrainian counterpart, Petro O. Poroshenko.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINSK, Belarus — President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia held inconclusive talks late Tuesday with the president of Ukraine, extending a reluctant hand to a new leadership vilified in Russia’s state-run news media as the fruit of a fascist putsch. Hours earlier, Ukraine released videos of captured Russian soldiers that directly challenged Mr. Putin’s longstanding claim that his country has nothing to do with the conflict in eastern Ukraine. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/world/europe/26WATCHING2/26WATCHING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/26/world/europe/26WATCHING2/26WATCHING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/