ject', 'value': 'Stickball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bensonhurst (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T12:56:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Brozinsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brozinsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1d95405-f186-5eaa-91c2-7f0f76ee65ab', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1d95405-f186-5eaa-91c2-7f0f76ee65ab'}, {'abstract': 'The 19th-century city has spawned numerous 21st-century pleasures, from sumptuous design objects to gorgeous, laboriously produced rugs to a one-of-a-kind resort.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/jaipur-travel-and-shopping-guide-for-design-lovers/', 'snippet': 'The 19th-century city has spawned numerous 21st-century pleasures, from sumptuous design objects to gorgeous, laboriously produced rugs to a one-of-a-kind resort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jaipur is like the elusive mistress you can’t get enough of. Considered to be India’s first planned city, it was painted an autumnal shade of pink to coincide with the visit of the Prince of Wales (King Edward VII) in 1878. But time and traffic have turned the pink into a shade of sandstone orange, and today, the city straddles eras. Run-down palaces pop up at random street corners. Ornately carved domes rise up against glass monoliths. Global ideas mingle with generations-old handicrafts, from block printing to brass beating. A stroll around the 18th-century Palace of the Winds (Hawa Mahal), which overlooks the city’s main arterial road, gives you a sense of the throbbing cosmopolis Jaipur has become. Here, the top spots to visit in all directions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/t-magazine/26jaipur-dravid-1/26jaipur-dravid-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/26/t-magazine/26jaipur-dravid-1/26jaipur-dravid-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/t-magazine/26jaipur-dravid-1/26jaipur-dravid-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/t-magazine/26jaipur-dravid-1/26jaipur-dravid-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/t-magazine/26jaipur-dravid-1/26jaipur-dravid-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/26/t-magazine/26jaipur-dravid-1/26jaipur-dravid-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/t-magazine/26jaipur-dravid-1/26jaipur-dravid-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Design Lover’s Guide to the Modern Jaipur', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T13:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Supriya Dravid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Supriya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dravid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d103dfb-fe9c-5e10-a22e-2b927327ea15', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d103dfb-fe9c-5e10-a22e-2b927327ea15'}, {'abstract': 'Animators in the southern Chinese city of Shenzhen are creating a 104-episode animated series loosely based on a historical Qing Dynasty imperial consort, the Fragrant Concubine, who is shrouded in myth.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/fabled-uighur-princess-coming-to-chinese-television-as-a-cartoon/', 'snippet': 'Animators in the southern Chinese city of Shenzhen are creating a 104-episode animated series loosely based on a historical Qing Dynasty imperial consort, the Fragrant Concubine, who is shrouded in myth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chinese officials are embracing a wide range of tactics in trying to suppress surging ethnic violence in the western border region of Xinjiang. There are, for example, frequent police raids on homes of suspected Uighur insurgents and executions of those found guilty by courts of “terrorist activities.” There was also a recent proposal by President Xi Jinping to move more Uighurs to parts of China dominated by the Han, the nation’s main ethnic group, so the mostly Muslim Uighurs could be better assimilated into Chinese society.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/blogs/26sino-cartoon01/26sino-cartoon01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1030, 'width': 600, 'subTy