'pub_date': '2014-08-26T14:11:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/044a4571-dd0c-51fb-9ccf-18d8dd8012ff', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/044a4571-dd0c-51fb-9ccf-18d8dd8012ff'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Senator Goldwater took days off by the sea before entering the presidential race in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/1964-goldwater-fishing-in-pacific/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Senator Goldwater took days off by the sea before entering the presidential race in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWPORT BEACH, Calif. — Sen. Barry Goldwater arrived here last night [Aug. 26] for six days “to fish and not shave and have a good time.” Within two hours, the Republican presidential nominee, his wife and two other couples were at sea aboard the converted PT boat Sundance for a “no politics” pre-campaign holiday off the California coast. The senator was hardly at sea, however, before his boat returned to the harbor off Santa Catalina island for a waterborne news conference. Sen. Goldwater said that no peace negotiations which involve the United States “directly or indirectly” in Vietnam should be held until the military situation improves. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 27, 1964 ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1964: Goldwater Fishing in Pacific', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Elections (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldwater, Barry M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newport Beach (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T14:18:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5bdaa5b-c945-5e69-82dd-aac5fe1c8898', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5bdaa5b-c945-5e69-82dd-aac5fe1c8898'}, {'abstract': 'Governments should ban the use of e-cigarettes indoors and in public places, the organization said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/business/international/world-health-organization-urges-stronger-regulation-of-electronic-cigarettes.html', 'snippet': 'Governments should ban the use of e-cigarettes indoors and in public places, the organization said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Governments should ban the use of electronic cigarettes in public places and outlaw tactics to lure young users, the World Health Organization said in a report released on Tuesday that calls for some of the toughest measures yet proposed for the increasingly popular devices.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/business/27ecigs-pic1/27ecigs-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/27/business/27ecigs-pic1/27ecigs-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/business/27ecigs-pi