rs. And meet a business owner who loves air travel (even turbulence).', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/today-in-small-business-the-problem-with-passion/', 'snippet': 'Stanford offers a free online course on how to build a business. Some merchants use Bitcoin A.T.M.s to attract customers. And meet a business owner who loves air travel (even turbulence).', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Small Business: The Problem With Passion', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T16:55:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4917a2cc-44da-53d5-8223-3355fbfabc55', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4917a2cc-44da-53d5-8223-3355fbfabc55'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes a corporate merger is just a corporate merger, not a disguised attempt to escape U.S. taxes. Here’s one such case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/upshot/dont-get-mad-if-burger-king-gets-canadian.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes a corporate merger is just a corporate merger, not a disguised attempt to escape U.S. taxes. Here’s one such case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Burger King has agreed to buy Tim Hortons, and has announced its intent to locate the headquarters of the combined company in Canada. This sounds like another tax inversion: a transaction in which an American company combines with a smaller foreign competitor, allowing it to move its tax residency abroad while keeping the bulk of its operations in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/upshot/26up-inversion/26up-inversion-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/26/upshot/26up-inversion/26up-inversion-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/upshot/26up-inversion/26up-inversion-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/upshot/26up-inversion/26up-inversion-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/upshot/26up-inversion/26up-inversion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/26/upshot/26up-inversion/26up-inversion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/upshot/26up-inversion/26up-inversion-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Get Mad if Burger King Gets Canadian', 'kicker': 'Dollars and Doughnuts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tim Hortons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Burger King Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T16:59:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Barro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a44de41a-8dcb-594d-b03f-929ca305234c', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a44de41a-8dcb-594d-b03f-929ca305234c'}, {'abstract': 'We are expected to solve any and all problems with the parts we are given to finish — whether we caused the problem or not.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/responding-to-reader-questions-about-our-parts-fiasco/', 'snippet': 'We are expected to solve any and all problems with the parts we are given to finish — whether we caused the problem or not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several readers have asked for a more detailed explanation of how we solved our parts problem. Other readers wondered whether we figured out how to finish the problem parts for our customer through blind luck or whether we had a method, possibly one taught by W. Edwards Deming. I want to try to answer those questions along with a few others readers posed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Responding to Reader Questions About Our Parts Fiasco', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub'