 ensembles who stood out. Michelle Monaghan’s Giambattista Valli Couture dress was elegantly long-sleeved, while Kristen Wiig offered a nod to the\xa0’90s in her understated Vera Wang slip dress. The “House of Cards” star Robin Wright, meanwhile, took the look for an androgynous turn in a cream Ralph Lauren tuxedo-inspired jumpsuit. Here, our 10 favorite ivory looks of the night.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 10 Best White Looks From the 2014 Emmys', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Travel Diary: Roam Katmandu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monaghan, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Vera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Robin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T18:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malina Joseph Gilchrist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malina', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Gilchrist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7db665fe-ab87-5870-8681-bb562c86a3ea', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7db665fe-ab87-5870-8681-bb562c86a3ea'}, {'abstract': 'In videos and photographs, Doctors Without Borders has documented its work in and around Syria, illustrating the far-reaching medical needs of a bloody and long-lasting civil war.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/how-doctors-see-the-syrian-civil-war/', 'snippet': 'In videos and photographs, Doctors Without Borders has documented its work in and around Syria, illustrating the far-reaching medical needs of a bloody and long-lasting civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As if you didn’t already think Doctors Without Borders had its hands full with the Ebola crisis unfolding in West Africa, the organization recently released a series of videos and photographs covering the group’s work in and around Syria. The series, “The Reach of War: A Day in the Life of the Syrian Conflict,” offers a glimpse into the activities that the organization conducts on a daily basis to aid refugees and the war-wounded in Syria, Iraq, Lebanon and Jordan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/opinion/nyto-doctors/nyto-doctors-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/26/opinion/nyto-doctors/nyto-doctors-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/opinion/nyto-doctors/nyto-doctors-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/opinion/nyto-doctors/nyto-doctors-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 2020, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/opinion/nyto-doctors/nyto-doctors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/26/opinion/nyto-doctors/nyto-doctors-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/opinion/nyto-doctors/nyto-doctors-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Doctors See the Syrian Civil War', 'kicker': 'Op-Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physical Therapy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMMAN (JORDAN)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': "Dara'a (Syria)", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T18:34:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Altman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64c3dbd5-c115-5e13-9606-d4542abc6e79', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64c3dbd5-c115-5e13-9606-d4542abc6e79'}, {'abstract': 'At Bâtard in TriBeCa, Markus Glocker sends a clear message with memorable cooking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/dining/restaurant-review-batard-in-tribeca.html', 'snippet': 'At Bâtard in TriBeCa, Markus Glocker sends a clear message with memorable cooking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few minutes into my first dinner at Bâtard, it became obvious that the chef, Markus Glocker, has a sniper’s accuracy at the stove. Nothing on his gracefully composed plates was chewier or crunchier or softer or saltier than it wanted to be. Mr. Glocker’s kitchen chops were not exactly a surprise, given that he worked in Vienna for Heinz Reitbauer, in Chicago for Charlie Trotter and in London and New York for Gordon Ramsay, none of them ever known to have smiled indulgently at a young cook and said: “Don’t worry about burning those onions, kid. The customers won’t notice.” ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Expressing Himself With Joy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Expressing Himself With Joy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Batard (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'TriBeCa (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nieporent, Drew', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glocker, Marcus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winterman, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T18:39:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5e8b9f8-03ca-5846-9710-5aafecdbccd5', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5e8b9f8-03ca-5846-9710-5aafecdbccd5'}, {'abstract': 'Tax strategy does not appear to be the primary driver of the acquisition of Tim Hortons, Steven Davidoff Solomon writes in the Deal Professor column, and the reaction of investors in Burger King may be too optimistic.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/26/inversion-critics-and-investors-may-be-misjudging-burger-king-deal/', 'snippet': 'Tax strategy does not appear to be the primary driver of the acquisition of Tim Hortons, Steven Davidoff Solomon writes in the Deal Professor column, and the reaction of investors in Burger King may be too optimistic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that Burger King’s acquisition of the beloved Tim Hortons doughnut chain in Canada has been announced, one word sums up the initial investor and public reaction to the deal: silly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-dealprof-BK/dbpix-dealprof-BK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-dealprof-BK/dbpix-dealprof-BK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-dealprof-BK/dbpix-dealprof-BK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-dealprof-BK/dbpix-dealprof-BK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-dealprof-BK/dbpix-dealprof-BK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 7