ame': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T21:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1d9816c-4fb4-5e06-9e83-edd7b765d94b', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1d9816c-4fb4-5e06-9e83-edd7b765d94b'}, {'abstract': 'Alexandra Jacobs, recently promoted from features editor to deputy fashion critic, reported on the awards show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2014/08/26/covering-the-emmys-far-from-the-red-carpet/', 'snippet': 'Alexandra Jacobs, recently promoted from features editor to deputy fashion critic, reported on the awards show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alexandra Jacobs, recently promoted from features editor to deputy fashion critic, reported on the Emmys.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Covering the Emmys: Far From the Red Carpet', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Alexandra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T21:04:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Lehman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lehman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d77c1fe7-7424-554c-94f3-1ab7b849d898', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d77c1fe7-7424-554c-94f3-1ab7b849d898'}, {'abstract': '“Through a Lens Darkly,” a film on the history of African-American photography, is also a family memoir and a tribute to unsung artists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/movies/through-a-lens-darkly-on-african-american-photography.html', 'snippet': '“Through a Lens Darkly,” a film on the history of African-American photography, is also a family memoir and a tribute to unsung artists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To describe Thomas Allen Harris’s “Through a Lens Darkly: Black Photographers and the Emergence of a People” as a history of African-American photography would be accurate but incomplete. Inspired by the book “Reflections in Black” (2000), Deborah Willis’s groundbreaking and thorough excavation of a vital and neglected photographic tradition, Mr. Harris’s film is a family memoir, a tribute to unsung artists and a lyrical, at times heartbroken, meditation on imagery and identity. The film is always absorbing to watch, but only once it’s over do you begin to grasp the extent of its ambitions, and just how much it has done within a packed, compact hour and a half.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/arts/27THROUGH-REFER/27THROUGH-REFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/27/arts/27THROUGH-REFER/27THROUGH-REFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 624}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/arts/27THROUGH-REFER/27THROUGH-REFER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 985, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 