es, meetings related to Israel — have repeatedly been scheduled on major Jewish holidays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE emblem of the United Nations shows the planet brought together in the embrace of two olive branches. Its charter affirms the “equal rights” of “nations large and small.” But in the “family of nations,” some members are more equal than others. No example of this inequity is starker than that of Israel.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Declare Yom Kippur a U.N. Holiday', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Declare Yom Kippur a U.N. Holiday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mariaschin, Daniel S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michaels, David J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yom Kippur', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-26T22:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel S. Mariaschin and David J. Michaels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Mariaschin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Michaels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c44b4f6a-91e6-51c6-b25d-9fd00007df4c', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c44b4f6a-91e6-51c6-b25d-9fd00007df4c'}, {'abstract': 'N