: 'Kurdish separatists kidnapped three Chinese engineers in an area near a power plant in Turkey’s southeast, a regional government official said Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/world/europe/turkey-chinese-workers-abducted.html', 'snippet': 'Kurdish separatists kidnapped three Chinese engineers in an area near a power plant in Turkey’s southeast, a regional government official said Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Kurdish separatists kidnapped three Chinese engineers in an area near a power plant in Turkey’s southeast, a regional government official said Tuesday. The attackers were believed to belong to the Kurdistan Workers’ Party, a militant group known as the P.K.K. It has waged an insurgency for decades against the Turkish state but has more recently been engaged in peace talks with it. Xinhua, the Chinese state news agency, said the engineers appeared to have been working Sunday evening at a thermal power plant belonging to a private company in Sirnak Province, near the Iraqi border, when the attack occurred. The P.K.K., which the United States, Turkey and the European Union consider a terrorist group, is based in northern Iraq, and has recently joined forces with Kurdish pesh merga fighters in their struggle against extreme Islamic militants gaining ground in Iraq. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey: Chinese Workers Abducted', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey: Chinese Workers Abducted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arsu, Sebnem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Kurdistan Workers' Party", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}