/www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/world/asia/afghanistan-presidential-election.html', 'snippet': 'American officials hoped to persuade Abdullah Abdullah, who withdrew observers from a United Nations vote audit, to continue talks on a unity government with his rival, Ashraf Ghani.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — American and United Nations officials scrambled to salvage Afghanistan’s bitterly contested presidential election on Wednesday after one candidate, Abdullah Abdullah, decided to boycott the internationally brokered audit of the vote.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/world/asia/28AFGHANISTAN/28AFGHANISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/27/world/asia/28AFGHANISTAN/28AFGHANISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/world/asia/28AFGHANISTAN/28AFGHANISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/world/asia/28AFGHANISTAN/28AFGHANISTAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/world/asia/28AFGHANISTAN/28AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/27/world/asia/28AFGHANISTAN/28AFGHANISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/world/asia/28AFGHANISTAN/28AFGHANISTAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unity Government Effort in Doubt as Afghan Candidate Boycotts Election Audit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unity Government Effort in Doubt as Afghan Candidate Boycotts Election Audit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nordland, Rod', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABDULLAH, ABDULLAH', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghani, Ashraf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T09:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/670ffb3c-4440-5258-a23f-3361c266924a', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/670ffb3c-4440-5258-a23f-3361c266924a'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A German steamship is sunk off the West Coast of Africa in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/1914-britain-sinks-german-ship/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A German steamship is sunk off the West Coast of Africa in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The 14,000-ton North German Lloyd steamship Kaiser Wilhelm der Grosse, upon which many thousands of Americans have travelled to and from Europe, was sunk yesterday while in service as a German auxiliary cruiser, by a 5,000-ton British cruiser, after a chase lasting more than a week, off the West Coast of Africa. The cruiser had gone to the rescue of the Union-Castle liner Galician, from The Cape, which had been captured about ten days ago by the Kaiser Wilhelm der Grosse off Ferro, Canary Islands, as a result of a trick. \xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, Aug. 28, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/28iht-oldaug28-ship/28iht-oldaug28-ship-jumbo.png', 'height': 534, 'width': 588, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/28iht-oldaug28-ship/28iht-oldaug28-ship-superJumbo.png', 'height': 534, 'width': 588, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/28iht-oldaug28-ship/28iht-oldaug28-ship-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/28iht-oldaug28-ship/28iht-oldaug28-ship-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/28iht-oldaug28-ship/28iht-oldaug28-ship-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1914: Britain Sinks German Ship', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'maj