ph': 'TOKYO — Japan’s conservative prime minister, Shinzo Abe, sent a message of support earlier this year to a ceremony honoring more than 1,000 Japanese who died after convictions for war crimes, a government spokesman said on Wednesday. The move could worsen frictions between Japan and its neighbors, particularly China, over bitter memories of World War II in the region.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan’s Premier Supported Ceremony for War Criminals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan’s Premier Supported Ceremony for War Criminals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T11:22:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57724790-d701-5d3e-b56d-1debef47c174', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57724790-d701-5d3e-b56d-1debef47c174'}, {'abstract': 'Detroit is silent on a proposal to use its art as collateral. | Global financial connections in Burger King’s deal for Tim Hortons. | Companies are invoking their attorney-client privilege to shelter wrongdoing. | The S.&P. 500 closes above 2,000 for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/morning-agenda-unusual-offer-for-detroits-art/', 'snippet': 'Detroit is silent on a proposal to use its art as collateral. | Global financial connections in Burger King’s deal for Tim Hortons. | Companies are invoking their attorney-client privilege to shelter wrongdoing. | The S.&P. 500 closes above 2,000 ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Detroit prepares to defend its plan next week to exit bankruptcy, city leaders have received an unusual offer to mortgage all the artwork in the Detroit Institute of Arts, Mary Williams Walsh writes in DealBook. A company called Art Capital, which makes loans backed by artwork, has told the city it is willing to lend it up to $3 billion, roughly 10 times the exit financing Detroit is now contemplating, using the museum’s art as collateral. The city has responded to the proposal with silence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Unusual Offer for Detroit’s Art', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T11:36:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f596a9d6-9f7a-555c-98e7-531a861c3a0f', 'word_count': 2238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f596a9d6-9f7a-555c-98e7-531a861c3a0f'}, {'abstract': 'America has changed for the better.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/the-way-we-ate-personal/', 'snippet': 'America has changed for the better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time I had to cook for myself was the summer between my junior and senior years, when I was working for Bill Nordhaus on this paper (pdf); I shared a very beat-up apartment in New Haven, and tried, sort of, to do some of the cooking. To help, my mother bought me the Betty Crocker Good and Easy cookbook. And I have often told people about the, um, interesting recipes. But was my memory embellishing? Strangely, it never occurred to me to check it out on the intertubes. But I finally did — and no, I wasn’t making any of it up:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Way We Ate (Personal)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T12:25:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d94d3ad-8659-57e1-bc52-8dfaa9812e3c', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d94d3ad-8659-57e1-bc52-8dfaa9812e3c'}, {'abstract': 'Kit Eaton reviews three apps that will help you learn the basics of computer programming from your mobile device.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/technology/personaltech/100000003076466/app-smart-learn-to-code.html', 'snippet': 'Kit Eaton reviews three apps that will help you learn the basics of computer programming from your mobile device.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kit Eaton reviews three apps that will help you learn the basics of computer programming from your mobile device.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/multimedia/appsmart-coding/appsmart-coding-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/26/multimedia/appsmart-coding/appsmart-coding-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/multimedia/appsmart-coding/appsmart-coding-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/multimedia/appsmart-coding/appsmart-coding-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/multimedia/appsmart-coding/appsmart-coding-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/26/multimedia/appsmart-coding/appsmart-coding-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/26/multimedia/appsmart-coding/appsmart-coding-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart | Learn to Code', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T12:27:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Circuits', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'Dallas Jensen and Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dallas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname