reature.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/yohji-yamamoto-designs-a-game-jersey-for-real-madrid/', 'snippet': 'One of the Real Madrid game jerseys for 2014-2015 will be a Yamamoto-designed creation, complete with its own mythological creature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Finally, our post-World Cup prayers have been answered: A designer has linked up with a soccer team to make the players’ game jerseys. Yohji Yamamoto has designed 2014-15 uniforms for the European champion Real Madrid under the auspices of his Y-3 Adidas line. I have to say, they are pretty cool.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/fashion/27Runway/27Runway-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 543, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/27/fashion/27Runway/27Runway-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 543}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/fashion/27Runway/27Runway-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 927, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/fashion/27Runway/27Runway-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1854, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/fashion/27Runway/27Runway-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/27/fashion/27Runway/27Runway-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/fashion/27Runway/27Runway-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yohji Yamamoto Goes Where No Designer Has Gone Before', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uniforms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yamamoto, Yohji', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Madrid (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Y-3 (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T12:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5b05981-09a2-5290-9862-2009d17c9383', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5b05981-09a2-5290-9862-2009d17c9383'}, {'abstract': 'A project from the photography duo of Herring & Herring, the issue, titled “Framed,” aims to cast familiar figures in an entirely new light.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/fashion-photography-magazine-herring-and-herring-features-beyonce-elijah-wood-fred-armisen/', 'snippet': 'A project from the photography duo of Herring & Herring, the issue, titled “Framed,” aims to cast familiar figures in an entirely new light.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographers Dimitri Scheblanov and Jesper Carlsen forged a professional partnership under the moniker of Herring & Herring, a tribute to their shared love of the pickled fish. Under it, they produce provocative and modern images for commercial and editorial clients spanning from Gucci and DeBeers to Vice magazine. Last year the pair created their first issue of Herring & Herring magazine, a text-free monograph devoted to fashion photography, which they published under the title “Fit to Print” and sent out to industry colleagues and friends.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Art Magazine Featuring Beyoncé, Kelly Osbourne and Other Stars Like You’ve Never Seen Them Before', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Armisen, Fred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wood, Elijah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T13:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Neilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72bf27bb-a308-5a88-82f0-489654125274', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72bf27bb-a308-5a88-82f0-489654125274'}, {'abstract': 'Hollande takes a hard line against anyone questioning his subservience.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/stockholm-syndrome-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'Hollande takes a hard line against anyone questioning his subservience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure enough, President Hollande has finally shown some steel — moving forcefully to suppress critics of his slavish adherence to the austerity demanded by Germany and Brussels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stockholm Syndrome in Paris', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T13:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d74a4528-116c-511d-9844-91730e657b69', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d74a4528-116c-511d-9844-91730e657b69'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time, the quota for visas available to Chinese investors hoping to obtain permanent residency status in the United States has been filled before the end of the fiscal year.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/a-door-into-u-s-for-chinese-investors-closes-for-now/', 'snippet': 'For the first time, the quota for visas available to Chinese investors hoping to obtain permanent residency status in the United States has been filled before the end of the fiscal year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time, the quota for visas available to Chinese investors hoping to obtain permanent residency status in the United States has been filled before the end of the fiscal year, a United States State Department official has announced.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/world/27sino-visa01/27sino-visa01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/27/world/27sino-visa01/27sino-visa01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/world/27sino-visa01