 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d903e7c-09b3-55a9-a439-89d0b06e6a00', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d903e7c-09b3-55a9-a439-89d0b06e6a00'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy prepares for war in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/1939-lights-of-rome-darkened/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy prepares for war in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Dim lights on alternate lampposts and a sharp falling off in the number of private automobiles on the streets gave Rome this evening [Aug. 27] its first outward signs of war preparations. Apart from this, the Italian capital was still conspicuous among the great cities of Europe for the unchanged tempo of its life. Thousands of citizens are away for their annual month’s vacation and have not come back. Thousands of others passed the day sunning themselves on the beach of Ostia, Rome’s seaport and bathing resort. Beneath this tranquil surface, however, both military preparations and diplomatic activity are proceeding.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 28, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: Lights of Rome Darkened', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T14:53:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f56fbf5-6d81-541e-9bd5-211c10486051', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f56fbf5-6d81-541e-9bd5-211c10486051'}, {'abstract': 'The recession temporarily halted condo development in this once-industrial waterfront community, but new projects are now springing up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/realestate/greenpoint-brooklyn-flavored-with-a-dash-of-poland.html', 'snippet': 'The recession temporarily halted condo development in this once-industrial waterfront community, but new projects are now springing up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just before she found her dream fixer-upper in Greenpoint, Brooklyn, Antoinette Sneed left an open house in tears. Raised in an Italian-American family in Williamsburg, she had all but given up on finding an affordable place in Brooklyn.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greenpoint, Brooklyn: Flavored With a Dash of Poland', 'kicker': 'Living in', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flavored With a Dash of Poland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doyle, Rachel B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenpoint (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel B. Doyle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/317d23d4-f1e0-5a4e-99b4-272f27f0196e', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/317d23d4-f1e0-5a4e-99b4-272f27f0196e'}, {'abstract': 'The mother of Steven Sotloff, a freelance journalist being held by ISIS, broke her silence to appeal directly to the group’s leader in a video obtained by The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/world/middleeast/steven-sotloff-isis-hostage.html', 'snippet': 'The mother of Steven Sotloff, a freelance journalist being held by ISIS, broke her silence to appeal directly to the group’s leader in a video obtained by The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mother of an American hostage being held by the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria released an emotional video appeal to his captors on Wednesday. Shirley Sotloff, the mother of the 31-year-old freelance journalist Steven J. Sotloff, addressed her plea directly to Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi, the leader of ISIS and the self-declared caliph of the Muslim world.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/world/APPEAL/APPEAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 331, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/28/world/APPEAL/APPEAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 331}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/world/APPEAL/APPEAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 564, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/world/APPEAL/APPEAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1128, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/world/APPEAL/APPEAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'sub