how he came to profile a restaurateur named Sharky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Fuller reports on Southeast Asia. His work recently led him to Sharky, a restaurateur who produces European food in Myanmar, where whole-milk mozzarella cheese and bagels are novel. Here’s how he found him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/sharky1/sharky1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/sharky1/sharky1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/sharky1/sharky1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/sharky1/sharky1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/sharky1/sharky1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/sharky1/sharky1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/blogs/sharky1/sharky1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Bagels in Myanmar', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fuller, Thomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ye Htut Win', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yangon (Myanmar)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T16:05:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee3d94ec-e2be-56b0-85d0-1292d16191d0', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee3d94ec-e2be-56b0-85d0-1292d16191d0'}, {'abstract': 'Drury Street is just blocks from the city’s main shopping avenue, but the comparatively smaller strip has less congestion and a more authentic feel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/travel/in-dublin-shopping-away-from-the-crowds.html', 'snippet': 'Drury Street is just blocks from the city’s main shopping avenue, but the comparatively smaller strip has less congestion and a more authentic feel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Drury Street in the heart of Dublin is just a few short blocks from Grafton Street, the city’s main shopping avenue, but the comparatively smaller strip has a more authentic feel. Instead of international chain stores and tourist-heavy congestion, there are fewer crowds and a diverse mix of locally owned boutiques housed in low brick buildings and selling everything from home goods to Irish art. It’s a favorite destination for locals who come for the far from ho-hum finds.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't