avel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e1d2399-c6cb-59f4-9138-7b576506a739', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e1d2399-c6cb-59f4-9138-7b576506a739'}, {'abstract': 'In this southern Oregon town, which draws at least 300,000 visitors each year, some restaurants are focusing on the midday meal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/travel/a-taste-for-lunch-in-ashland-ore.html', 'snippet': 'In this southern Oregon town, which draws at least 300,000 visitors each year, some restaurants are focusing on the midday meal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent summer afternoon, it was a busy scene outside the Ashland Food Co-op, where the lunch menu is the biggest draw. On a small triangle of grass a barefooted young woman in a grass skirt did a rather frantic and awkward hip dance while her shirtless tattooed partner played the bongos. Two gray-haired men wearing button-downs ate salad at an outdoor table and argued about Richard Blanco, the Inaugural poet in 2013 who gave a reading here last year.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/travel/31HEADSUP1/31HEADSUP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/31/travel/31HEADSUP1/31HEADSUP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 736}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/travel/31HEADSUP1/31HEADSUP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 836, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's