cted to save taxpayers hundreds of billions of dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/upshot/medicare-not-such-a-budget-buster-anymore.html', 'snippet': 'Estimates of future medical spending keep falling. The changes are projected to save taxpayers hundreds of billions of dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’re looking at the biggest story involving the federal budget and a crucial one for the future of the American economy. Every year for the last six years in a row, the Congressional Budget Office has reduced its estimate for how much the federal government will need to spend on Medicare in coming years. The latest reduction came in a report from the budget office on Wednesday morning.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare: Not Such a Budget-Buster Anymore', 'kicker': 'Public Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Medicare: Not Such a Budget-Buster Anymore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanger-Katz, Margot', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quealy, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T16:18:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Sanger-Katz and Kevin Quealy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quealy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dba901c6-4658-5d70-852c-16bf56174f2b', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dba901c6-4658-5d70-852c-16bf56174f2b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Spacey is to give a pop concert with an orchestra in Washington to raise funds for his arts education foundation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/kevin-spacey-to-sing-in-benefit-concert/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Spacey is to give a pop concert with an orchestra in Washington to raise funds for his arts education foundation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You may have seen – and may have been impressed by – Kevin Spacey singing in the 2004 film “Beyond the Sea,” a biopic in which he played the singer Bobby Darin (he also directed the film, and wrote the script with Lewis Colick). You might also have caught his performance of “Mind Games” in “Come Together: A Night for John Lennon’s Words and Music,” a 2001 television tribute taped at Radio City Music Hall. There is, apparently, plenty more where that came from: Mr. Spacey plans to set aside his current Washington persona, as the nefarious Frank Underwood on “House of Cards,” and sing a full concert there on Sept. 29 at Shakespeare Theater’s Harman Hall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/arts/27artsbeat-spacey/27artsbeat-spacey-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 990, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/28/arts/27artsbeat-spacey/27artsbeat-spacey-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 990}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/arts/27artsbeat-spacey/27artsbeat-spacey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 621, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/arts/27artsbeat-space