ata crunching in a SUNY dormitory.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Last year, as a college freshman, Jack Fischer decided to put some casual observations to the test.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Teenager’s Study Suggests Public Colleges Get Less Times Attention', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T16:23:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd2624cd-f060-5126-a2d8-a266abcd9ed5', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd2624cd-f060-5126-a2d8-a266abcd9ed5'}, {'abstract': 'Tanks, artillery and infantry have crossed from Russia into an unbreached part of eastern Ukraine in recent days, in what Ukrainian and Western military officials are calling a stealth invasion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/world/europe/ukraine-russia-novoazovsk-crimea.html', 'snippet': 'Tanks, artillery and infantry have crossed from Russia into an unbreached part of eastern Ukraine in recent days, in what Ukrainian and Western military officials are calling a stealth invasion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DONETSK, Ukraine — Determined to preserve the pro-Russian revolt in eastern Ukraine, Russia reinforced what Western and Ukrainian officials described as a stealth invasion on Wednesday, sending armored troops across the border as it expanded the conflict to a new section of Ukrainian territory.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/0