ppers into buyers is low by comparing its performance to benchmark data for similar stores.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/bringing-digital-analytics-to-main-street-retailers/', 'snippet': 'Swarm might indicate that a store’s rate of converting shoppers into buyers is low by comparing its performance to benchmark data for similar stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2010, Rudd Davis helped start a business that developed a technology platform to let hotels deliver personalized content to guest phones. At the same time this was happening, Mr. Davis and his parents bought a century-old country store in their small Vermont town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bringing Digital Analytics to Main Street Retailers', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ShopperTrak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vermont', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T17:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eilene Zimmerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eilene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4a03fd0-7b03-5329-a07d-f250c4e3640f', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4a03fd0-7b03-5329-a07d-f250c4e3640f'}, {'abstract': 'Harare, designed by Caroline Fuss, is the latest fair-trade label to combine indigenous craft with contemporary design.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/caroline-fuss-harare-proenza-schouler-alum-fashion-line-made-from-traditional-guatemalan-textiles/', 'snippet': 'Harare, designed by Caroline Fuss, is the latest fair-trade label to combine indigenous craft with contemporary design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caroline Fuss had just completed a Proenza Schouler design internship when she visited Guatemala for the first time in 2011. Impressed by the quality and intricacy of the weavings in the village markets she visited, the Australian-born, New York-based designer set out to build a sustainable fashion line that would utilize and promote what she saw as an untapped textile resource. The result is Harare, named after the Zimbabwean town where Fuss’s mother and grandmother were raised. Almost every piece in the line is comprised of fabric woven by small groups of Guatemalan artisans, many of whom are the tenth generation to practice their trade; the garments are sewn or knitted in New York or Los Angeles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/t-magazine/27bobb-harare/27bobb-harare-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/27/t-magazine/27bobb-harare/27bobb-harare-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/t-magazine/27bobb-harare/27bobb-harare-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/t-magazine/27bobb-harare/27bobb-harare-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'super