ragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A former Iowa state senator pleaded guilty Wednesday to receiving and concealing payments in exchange for switching his support from one presidential candidate to another in the 2012 election, the Justice Department said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Iowa State Senator Admits Taking Cash to Switch Allegiance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorenson, Kent', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T18:57:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By David S. Joachim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Joachim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c42c1d72-53f1-5f68-97a2-0c125f666015', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c42c1d72-53f1-5f68-97a2-0c125f666015'}, {'abstract': 'Experts say kids are so sleep-deprived it’s hurting their health, and some argue that starting school later is the answer.', 'web_url': 'https://op-talk.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/how-students-can-get-more-sleep/', 'snippet': 'Experts say kids are so sleep-deprived it’s hurting their health, and some argue that starting school later is the answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was sitting in class, my freshman year of college, quietly taking notes, when suddenly something\xa0crawled up from underneath the seat in front of me. I recoiled in horror: It was a witch!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/opi