: 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T19:10:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b342d59-c758-551a-9cf5-b09d85c28551', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b342d59-c758-551a-9cf5-b09d85c28551'}, {'abstract': 'The race between State Senator Tony Avella and John C. Liu, a former New York City comptroller, could have ramifications for the balance of power in Albany.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/nyregion/as-primary-nears-democrats-are-watching-a-senate-battle-in-queens.html', 'snippet': 'The race between State Senator Tony Avella and John C. Liu, a former New York City comptroller, could have ramifications for the balance of power in Albany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the hilly streets of Whitestone, Queens, the Hamptons-bound helicopters buzzing overhead were ruining the afternoon quiet. A collapsed storm drain was a trap for unsuspecting children. And each dilapidated house was another sign of middle-class malaise amid the million-dollar properties.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/nyregion/SENATEweb1/SENATEweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/28/nyregion/SENATEweb1/SENATEweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/nyregion/SENATEweb1/SENATEweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/nyregion/SENATEweb1/SENATEweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/nyregion/SENATEweb1/SENATEweb1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/28/nyregion/SENATEweb1/SENATEweb1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/nyregion/SENATEweb1/SENATEweb1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Queens Primary, 2-Term Senator Faces Rival Seeking a Comeback', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Queens Primary, 2-Term Senator Faces Rival Seeking a Comeback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, State Legislature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Avella, Tony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu, John C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T19:15:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbae3d9d-9f5d-5533-a701-05349bd7c110', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbae3d9d-9f5d-5533-a701-05349bd7c110'}, {'abstract': 'Some say the editorial “wimped out” by not supporting Zephyr Teachout.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/readers-respond-to-the-andrew-cuomo-non-endorsement/', 'snippet': 'Some say the editorial “wimped out” by not supporting Zephyr Teachout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The editorial board’s decision not to endorse either candidate in the Democratic primary for governor was guaranteed to annoy partisans on both sides, and the comments on\xa0today’s editorial\xa0reflect that anger. The most frequently voiced criticism was: “You wimped out,” in\xa0the words of Nancy Fitz, from Greenwich, Conn. We should have made a choice, they said, just as voters must.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Respond to the Andrew Cuomo Non-Endorsement', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teachout, Zephyr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-27T19:17:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47fcac92-46ef-5a7a-b9ac-bf157b091b9d', 'word_count': 921, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47fcac92-46ef-5a7a-b9ac-bf157b091b9d'}, {'abstract': 'I have a 7-year-old and a 2-year-old whose seizures mean someone’s eyes have to be on her at every moment. Fortunately I have a great support system and a flexible work arrangement.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/27/how-nicole-zeitzer-johnson-communications-director-and-special-needs-parent-does-it/', 'snippet': 'I have a 7-year-old and a 2-year-old whose seizures mean someone’s eyes have to be on her at every moment. Fortunately I have a great support system and a flexible work arrangement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicole Zeitzer Johnson is the director of communications at Qello, a digital streaming service for full-length concerts and music documentaries, and the mother of two children, Tanner, 7, and Josie, 2. Josie has a rare genetic neurological condition called FoxG1, which is associated with impaired development. In the “How I Do It” series, Motherlode asks parents, from members of Congress to retail clerks, to share “how they do it” on one typical day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/us/motherlode-nicole-johnson/motherlode-nicole-johnson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 318, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/us/motherlode-nicole-johnson/motherlode-nicole-johnson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 318, 'width': 480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/27/us/motherlode-nicole-johnso