uld redress imbalances of power between corporations and small-business franchisees, and it would encourage reforms in other states.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/opinion/a-better-deal-for-franchisees-and-workers.html', 'snippet': 'A bill in California would redress imbalances of power between corporations and small-business franchisees, and it would encourage reforms in other states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fast-food workers, who have been striking regularly for higher pay and an unimpeded right to unionize, are not the only people fed up with powerful corporate bosses. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better Deal for Franchisees and Workers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Better Deal for Franchisees and Workers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Franchises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T01:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb8f3d5b-d11a-522f-b9c1-eebc0ebedc40', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb8f3d5b-d11a-522f-b9c1-eebc0ebedc40'}, {'abstract': 'A former Iowa state senator pleaded guilty to receiving and concealing payments in exchange for switching his support from one presidential candidate to another in the 2012 election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/us/iowa-guilty-plea-in-campaign-allegiance-deal.html', 'snippet': 'A former Iowa state senator pleaded guilty to receiving and concealing payments in exchange for switching his support from one presidential candidate to another in the 2012 election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A former Iowa state senator pleaded guilty on Wednesday to receiving and concealing payments in exchange for switching his support from one presidential candidate to another in the 2012 election, the Justice Department said. Kent Sorenson of Milo resigned from the Iowa Senate last year after an inquiry found that he had probably violated ethics rules by taking money from presidential campaigns. Mr. Sorenson, 42, had been the state chairman for the presidential campaign of Representative Michele Bachmann, Republican of Minnesota, but switched his support to former Representative Ron Paul of Texas days before the state’s caucus. In his plea agreement, Mr. Sorenson admitted that he had agreed to switch his allegiance in exchange for $73,000. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iowa: Guilty Plea in Campaign Allegiance Deal', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iowa: Guilty Plea in Campaign Allegiance Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joachim, David S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorenson, Kent', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T01:04:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original':