14.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-thursday-august-28-2014.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, August 28, 2014.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There was some resistance to awarding a Union soldier the congressional medal at Gettysburg even 150 years after the fact. They didn’t want us refighting the Civil War all over again. It’s still sensitive.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, August 28, 2014', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T04:32:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/4062d6c8-7aeb-5fe7-8132-4617de3e92f4', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4062d6c8-7aeb-5fe7-8132-4617de3e92f4'}, {'abstract': 'Jana Cepelova lost, 6-2, 6-1, to Simona Halep, and the main reasons appeared to be her deep court position and her tendency to hit shots that elite players like to dine on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/sports/tennis/simona-halep-brushes-aside-jana-cepelova-at-us-open.html', 'snippet': 'Jana Cepelova lost, 6-2, 6-1, to Simona Halep, and the main reasons appeared to be her deep court position and her tendency to hit shots that elite players like to dine on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jana Cepelova has essentially perfected one type of deep groundstroke: hard and flat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sitting Back, an Underdog Quickly Falls Behind', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halep, Simona', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cepelova, Jana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T04:59:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O'Shannessy", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shannessy", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa0fa963-2e4b-5c2a-8273-7fbf98d6dd03', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa0fa963-2e4b-5c2a-8273-7fbf98d6dd03'}, {'abstract': 'In all, 420 people in New York City fatally overdosed on heroin in 2013 out of a total of 782 drug overdoses, rising to a level not seen in a decade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/nyregion/heroins-death-toll-rising-in-new-york-amid-a-shift-in-who-uses-it.html', 'snippet': 'In all, 420 people in New York City fatally overdosed on heroin in 2013 out of a total of 782 drug overdoses, rising to a level not seen in a decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A heroin crisis gripping communities across the country deepened in New York last year, with more people in the city dying in overdoses from the drug than in any year since 2003. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heroin’s Death Toll Rising in New York, Amid a Shift in Who Uses It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heroin’s Death Toll Rising, City Data Show, Amid a Shift in Who Uses It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heroin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Mental Hygiene Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bassett, Mary T', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1cf99da-abb2-5ecb-9b4c-51f34160769a', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1cf99da-abb2-5ecb-9b4c-51f34160769a'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:20 P.M. (Showtime) SILVER LININGS PLAYBOOK (2012) Pat Solatano (Bradley Cooper) has returned to the home of his parents (Jacki Weaver and Robert De Niro) after eight months in a mental institution in this film from David O. Russell. Pat wants to tackle the world and reclaim his estranged wife, Nikki, who took out a restraining order against him, through a physical and psychological regimen he created while locked away. Then he meets Tiffany (Jennifer Lawrence, above with Mr. Cooper), a heartbreaker who persuades him that she can circumvent the law by passing a letter from him to Nikki, if only he’ll enter a dance contest with her. Soon, she is leading, and he is following. “For all its high-flying zaniness, the movie has the sting of life, and its humor feels dredged up from the same dark, boggy place from which Samuel Beckett extracted his yuks,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times about this best picture Oscar nominee, which also earned nominations for Mr. Cooper, Ms. Weaver and Mr. De Niro, and a win for Ms. Lawrence. “These are characters who get in one another’s faces and occasionally punch a loved one right in the kisser. They must go on, they can’t go on, but together they do.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f647945e-274d-5fd7-a6a2-4dfe04c0b5f0', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f647945e-274d-5fd7-a6a2-4dfe04c0b5f0'}, {'abstract': 'The mutual love affair between the former N.B.A. player and his adopted home of Beijing will reach a new milestone this fall when “I Am Stephon Marbury,” a musical about his life in China, opens in the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/stephon-marbury-the-musical-a-tale-of-making-it-in-beijing/', 'snippet': 'The mutual love affair between the former N.B.A. player and his adopted home of Beijing will reach a new milestone this fall when “I Am Stephon Marbury,” a musical about his life in China, opens in the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephon Marbury’s turbulent decade in the N.B.A. was marked by public feuds and lackluster teams, but in recent years he has found a better basketball life in China, where he has led the Beijing Ducks to two national championships.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'capti