ps transactions over a period of almost six years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deutsche Bank Fined $7.8 Million Over Faulty Reports on Swaps', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regulatory Penalty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Conduct Authority (Great Britain)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T11:02:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b12925a-facd-56be-bda3-1c0ce97f0053', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b12925a-facd-56be-bda3-1c0ce97f0053'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: France begins to censor the press and communications in 1939.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/1939-france-imposes-censorship/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: France begins to censor the press and communications in 1939.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — With Adolf Hitler greatly aggravating the crisis by raising his demands on Poland to include the Corridor as well as Danzig, France yesterday glided into a regime of war. A government censorship over the press, radio and cinema was set up. The eminent French dramatist, Jean Giraudoux, who was recently appointed French propaganda chief, was placed as the head of the censors’ bureau, which is being established at the Hotel Continental, near the Place Vendôme. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 29, 1939', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1939: France Imposes Censorship', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T11:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4b1e0ec-eb39-551b-b564-f4770713d92a', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4b1e0ec-eb39-551b-b564-f4770713d92a'}, {'abstract': 'JPMorgan Chase and other United States banks struck by cyberattack. | Alibaba’s profit soared. | Lending Club filed to go public. | Still work to be done to hold corporate malefactors accountable.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/morning-agenda-hackers-hit-u-s-banks/', 'snippet': 'JPMorgan Chase and other United States banks struck by cyberattack. | Alibaba’s profit soared. | Lending Club filed to go public. | Still work to be done to hold corporate malefactors accountable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A number of United States banks, including JPMorgan Chase and at least four others, were struck by hackers in a series of coordinated attacks this month, according to four people briefed on a continuing investigation into the crimes, Nicole Perlroth writes in The New York Times. The hackers infiltrated the banks’ networks, siphoning off gigabytes of data, including checking and savings account information, in what security experts described as a sophisticated cyberattack. The motivation and origin of the attacks are not yet clear, according to investigators.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Hackers Hit U.S. Banks', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T11:32:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e37ee9ae-3541-5245-8a9f-af36770efe79', 'word_count': 2047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e37ee9ae-3541-5245-8a9f-af36770efe79'}, {'abstract': 'This Reader Idea get students thinking, talking and writing about their own approaches to skills like brainstorming and collaboration.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/reader-idea-get-to-know-your-introverts-extroverts-and-ambiverts/', 'snippet': 'This Reader Idea get students thinking, talking and writing about their own approaches to skills like brainstorming and collaboration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All this week, we are featuring Great Ideas From Readers, lesson plans from teachers who teach with The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/learning/LN20140829f/LN20140829f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/29/learning/LN20140829f/LN20140829f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08