istorts birds’ songs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m catching up with Winged Warnings, a remarkable online series on birds as sentinels for (and victims of) environmental problems, which is unfolding over at Environmental Health News. The series launched in recent days with an introductory overview, a piece on how ospreys have recovered from the DDT era but face new ills, and a report on troubles with puffins and other northern seabirds facing disrupted food webs and a changing climate. Here’s a video summary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/dotwinged/dotwinged-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 177, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/dotwinged/dotwinged-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 177, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/dotwinged/dotwinged-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/dotwinged/dotwinged-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/blogs/dotwinged/dotwinged-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Winged Warning: Heavy Metal Song Distortion', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mercury (Metal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pesticides', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T12:34:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79a3219a-748c-5776-942d-7c1fd62fba33', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79a3219a-748c-5776-942d-7c1fd62fba33'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: On a 90-degree day, a bodega owner told a woman he was giving her a discount because he liked the way she was covered up.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/modesty-is-rewarded/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: On a 90-degree day, a bodega owner told a woman he was giving her a discount because he liked the way she was covered up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Modesty Is Rewarded', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Convenience Stores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discount Selling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T12:43:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellie Levi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e040ced-4dcb-5d65-b123-597245fa52a2', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e040ced-4dcb-5d65-b123-597245fa52a2'}, {'abstract': 'A new study suggests that Toxoplasma can turn its host’s genes on and off, influencing behavior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/science/parasites-practicing-mind-control.html', 'snippet': 'A new study suggests that Toxoplasma can turn its host’s genes on and off, influencing behavior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An unassuming single-celled organism called Toxoplasma gondii is one of the most successful parasites on Earth, infecting an estimated 11 percent of Americans and perhaps half of all people worldwide. It’s just as prevalent in many other species of mammals and birds. In a recent study in Ohio, scientists found the parasite in three-quarters of the white-tailed deer they studied.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/science/28zimmer/28zimmer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/28/science/28zimmer/28zimmer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/science/28zimmer/28zimmer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/science/28zimmer/28zimmer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's