95762-4a4d-581e-b4a3-3cb8976974b2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3cf95762-4a4d-581e-b4a3-3cb8976974b2'}, {'abstract': 'Some activists like Rebecca Gomperts are now imagining the unthinkable: a future where most abortions happen at home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/magazine/the-dawn-of-the-post-clinic-abortion.html', 'snippet': 'Some activists like Rebecca Gomperts are now imagining the unthinkable: a future where most abortions happen at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In June 2001, under a cloud-streaked sky, Rebecca Gomperts set out from the Dutch port of Scheveningen in a rented 110-foot ship bound for Ireland. Lashed to the deck was a shipping container, freshly painted light blue and stocked with packets of mifepristone (which used to be called RU-486) and misoprostol. The pills are given to women in the first trimester to induce a miscarriage. Medical abortion, as this procedure is called, had recently become available in the Netherlands. But use of misoprostol and mifepristone to end a pregnancy was illegal in Ireland, where abortion by any means remains against the law, with few exceptions.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dawn of the Post-Clinic Abortion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Post-Clinic Abortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bazelon, Emily', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gomperts, Rebecca', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Vessel (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mifeprex (RU-486)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Women on Web', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T14:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Bazelon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazelon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4631caee-1a4f-5235-9213-068eb6ee3128', 'word_count': 6822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4631caee-1a4f-5235-9213-068eb6ee3128'}, {'abstract': 'To illustrate Emily Bazelon’s cover story about activists working to give women access to abortions at home, we knew that we wanted to show a package of pills received by mail.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/under-cover-opening-up-the-abortion-by-mail-cover/', 'snippet': 'To illustrate Emily Bazelon’s cover story about activists working to give women access to abortions at home, we knew that we wanted to show a package of pills received by mail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To illustrate Emily Bazelon’s cover story about activists working to give women access to abortions at home, we knew that we wanted to show a package of pills received by mail. As Jake Silverstein, the magazine’s editor in chief, noted, what was new about Bazelon’s article was not that women could use pills to have an abortion, but that women who would otherwise be denied access to an abortion could get those pills through the mail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under Cover: Opening Up the ‘Abortion by Mail’ Cover', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T14:54:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'or