ument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilarie M. Sheets', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff105fbf-d8fc-53c6-ba7a-ef1fdcddb8aa', 'word_count': 1895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff105fbf-d8fc-53c6-ba7a-ef1fdcddb8aa'}, {'abstract': 'Dusty Hill fell on the band’s tour bus, and ZZ Top bowed out of concerts with Jeff Beck.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/zz-top-cancels-shows-after-bassist-is-injured/', 'snippet': 'Dusty Hill fell on the band’s tour bus, and ZZ Top bowed out of concerts with Jeff Beck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the second rock band tour bus accident of the summer, Dusty Hill, the bassist for ZZ Top, slipped and fell on the band’s bus on Tuesday evening, and sustained unspecified injuries that have forced the band to cancel some of its dates. The accident follows an accident in which Nick Followill, the drummer for the Kings of Leon, broke his ribs when the group’s tour bus stopped to avoid hitting a pedestrian, and canceled several weeks of concerts.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ZZ Top Cancels Shows After Bassist Is Injured', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ZZ Top Cancels Shows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ZZ Top', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T15:03:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': 