ndependence Party and will run for his old seat in Parliament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A British lawmaker with strongly anti-European views defected from the governing Conservative Party on Thursday to join the U.K. Independence Party, dealing an embarrassing blow to Prime Minister David Cameron.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conservative Party Lawmaker Defects to Anti-Europe Party in Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Tory Lawmaker Makes a Switch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erlanger, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carswell, Douglas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Kingdom Independence Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farage, Nigel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T17:28:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d87e13c-3e1e-5ca9-88bb-f3eecf66679a', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d87e13c-3e1e-5ca9-88bb-f3eecf66679a'}, {'abstract': 'A reader seeks the Haggler’s help in getting a refund on a $3,000 hair-removal treatment plan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/your-mo