hen', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lubben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51846c02-2621-5c9b-9c37-d675574fed49', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51846c02-2621-5c9b-9c37-d675574fed49'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time, parents and administrators can assess the effectiveness of teachers at the county, district and, in some cases, the school level.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/nyregion/new-york-state-releases-localized-teacher-evaluations.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time, parents and administrators can assess the effectiveness of teachers at the county, district and, in some cases, the school level.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York State released teacher and principal evaluations on Thursday that for the first time allow parents and administrators to assess the effectiveness of local teachers at the county, district and, in some cases, the school level.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critics Question High Ratings on New York State Teacher Evaluations Amid Poor Test Scores', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Critics Question High Ratings on Teacher Evaluations While Students Test Poorly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Evaluations (Labor)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T19:51:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de8e2ceb-0857-53c9-8c0a-b77355a7eb65', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de8e2ceb-0857-53c9-8c0a-b77355a7eb65'}, {'abstract': '“Theresa Bernstein: A Century in Art” aims to make a case for this artist’s place in a history dominated by male painters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/arts/design/a-theresa-bernstein-retrospective-in-philadelphia.html', 'snippet': '“Theresa Bernstein: A Century in Art” aims to make a case for this artist’s place in a history dominated by male painters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — Since the publication of Linda Nochlin’s groundbreaking 1971 essay, “Why Have There Been No Great Women Artists?,” feminist art historians have worked hard to rescue forgotten female figures from oblivion. One interesting candidate for recovery is offered by a traveling exhibition now at the Woodmere Art Museum here. “Theresa Bernstein: A Century in Art” presents more than 50 paintings dating from 1912 to 1972. It’s the first retrospective ever dedicated to Ms. Bernstein (1890-2002), who came of age during the heyday of early-20th-century American realism. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/ALT229BERNSTEIN/ALT229BERNSTEIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/ALT229BERNSTEIN/ALT229BERNSTEIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/ALT229BERNSTEIN/ALT229BERNSTEIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'r