 into the mystery of a neighbor’s missing husband.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chief Inspector Armand Gamache, the brooding, wounded protagonist in Louise Penny’s splendid series of mystery novels, has officially shed his professional title in her latest book, “The Long Way Home.” He has left the Montreal police force after an (almost literally) explosive confrontation with corrupt elements that had been poisoning the force from within. Gamache emerged triumphant, but not unbloodied, in Ms. Penny’s last book, “How the Light Gets In,” which was perhaps her most sensationally plotted, reaching its climax in the foiling of a terrorist act that would have claimed thousands of lives.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BOOK/29BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BOOK/29BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 802}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BOOK/29BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BOOK/29BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1873, 'width': 1402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BOOK/29BOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BOOK/29BOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'cap