mes'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/434fad19-aa21-51b5-8ca7-a4883343419f', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/434fad19-aa21-51b5-8ca7-a4883343419f'}, {'abstract': '“Bruce Davidson/Paul Caponigro: Two American Photographers in Britain and Ireland,” at the Yale Center for British Art, is a strange but memorable pairing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/arts/design/bruce-davidson-and-paul-caponigro-images-at-yale.html', 'snippet': '“Bruce Davidson/Paul Caponigro: Two American Photographers in Britain and Ireland,” at the Yale Center for British Art, is a strange but memorable pairing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW HAVEN — “Bruce Davidson/Paul Caponigro: Two American Photographers in Britain and Ireland,” at the Yale Center for British Art, is a strange but memorable pairing. It joins the Magnum photojournalist Bruce Davidson, best known for his aggressive New York street and subway photography, to a spiritually minded landscape photographer in the mold of Ansel Adams and Minor White. And although its title suggests some shared expatriate experience, a split quickly develops.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BRUCE1/29BRUCE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 869, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BRUCE1/29BRUCE1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 869}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BRUCE1/29BRUCE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29BRUCE1/29BRUCE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1740, 'width': 1202, 's