ter narrates a sequence from his film “Life of Crime.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Schechter narrates a sequence from his film “Life of Crime.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29LIFECRIME/29LIFECRIME-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29LIFECRIME/29LIFECRIME-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29LIFECRIME/29LIFECRIME-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29LIFECRIME/29LIFECRIME-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29LIFECRIME/29LIFECRIME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29LIFECRIME/29LIFECRIME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/29LIFECRIME/29LIFECRIME-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anatomy of a Scene | ‘Life of Crime’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schechter, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Life of Crime (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T21:27:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/12e281fd-f7d5-5e56-b82d-58ad5704a97c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/12e281fd-f7d5-5e56-b82d-58ad5704a97c'}, {'abstract': 'As any depiction of the conflict between Israel and Gaza has the potential to stir controversy and raise questions, Jake Silverstein, editor in chief, offers this note as a window into some of the thinking behind the photo essay by Paolo Pellegrin and Peter van Agtmael in the Aug. 31 issue of The New York Times Magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/28/editors-note-how-we-thought-about-our-photo-essay-on-israel-and-gaza/', 'snippet': 'As any depiction of the conflict between Israel and Gaza has the potential to stir controversy and raise questions, Jake Silverstein, editor in chief, offers this note as a window into some of the thinking behind the photo essay by Paolo Pellegrin...', 'lead_paragraph': 'As any depiction of the conflict between Israel and Gaza has the potential to stir controversy and raise questions, I offer this note as a window into some of the thinking behind the photo essay by Paolo Pellegrin and Peter van Agtmael in the Aug. 31 issue of The New York Times Magazine. Toward the end of July, we began talking to Paolo and Peter about going into Gaza and Israel, respectively, to make some pictures. We had noticed that during this summer’s outbreak of violence, the prevalence of cellphone cameras and social media led to many more images of Gaza than in previous iterations of this long-running conflict. This imagery made the cost of war visually appreciable in a way that it had not been even as recently as 2009. Yet as powerful as these photos were, the speed and fervor of their dissemination tended to bring them to us isolated from context. Paolo and Peter, working more slowly, could try to capture a deeper and more narrative sense of the texture of life on the ground.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/magazine/GazaPhoto1/GazaPhoto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/28/magazine/GazaPhoto1/GazaPhoto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/magazine/GazaPhoto1/GazaPhoto1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/magazine/GazaPhoto1/GazaPhoto1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1306, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/magazine/GazaPhoto1/GazaPhoto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/28/magazine/GazaPhoto1/GazaPhoto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/magazine/GazaPhoto1/GazaPhoto1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Editor’s Note: How We Thought About Our Photo Essay on Israel and Gaza', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-28T21:27:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By JAKE SILVERSTEIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SILVERSTEIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3cc4421-e1e3-5be4-8f90-5d9e58fa59c6', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3cc4421-e1e3-5be4-8f90-5d9e58fa59c6'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif requested Thursday that the army chief help defuse a standoff that has brought thousands of protesters to the capital and crippled the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/world/asia/pakistani-army-steps-into-political-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif requested Thursday that the army chief help defuse a standoff that has brought thousands of protesters to the capital and crippled the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — The Pakistani Army stepped into the country’s two-week-old political crisis on Thursday when Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif requested that the army chief, Gen. Raheel Sharif, help defuse a standoff that has crippled the government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/world/29PAKISTAN/29PAKISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/29/world/29PAKISTAN/29PAKISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201