gest Internet companies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/to-compete-with-alibaba-a-chinese-e-commerce-company-is-born/', 'snippet': 'Dalian Wanda, the Chinese conglomerate controlled by the billionaire Wang Jianlin, announced it would enter the e-commerce industry in an $800 million partnership with two of China’s biggest Internet companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The Dalian Wanda Group, the Chinese real estate, cinema and retail conglomerate controlled by the billionaire Wang Jianlin, announced on Friday that it would enter the e-commerce industry in an $800 million partnership with Baidu and Tencent, two of China’s biggest Internet companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/business/30dealbook-ecommerce/30dealbook-ecommerce-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/29/business/30dealbook-ecommerce/30dealbook-ecommerce-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/business/30dealbook-ecommerce/30dealbook-ecommerce-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/business/30dealbook-ecommerce/30dealbook-ecommerce-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1473, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/business/30dealbook-ecommerce/29dealbook-wanda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/29/business/30dealbook-ecommerce/29dealbook-wanda-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/business/30dealbook-ecommerce/29dealbook-wanda-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Compete Against Alibaba, Wanda Joins Forces With Baidu and Tencent', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang Jianlin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alibaba Group Holding Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baidu Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dalian Wanda Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tencent Holdings Ltd', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-29T06:24:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/969bfcb9-43f1-5d0d-8c14-5c3cf159abc0', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/969bfcb9-43f1-5d0d-8c14-5c3cf159abc0'}, {'abstract': 'The cartoon series is said to be aimed at improving ethnic relations, but the show’s Han creators appear to lack cultural knowledge about Uighurs, a visiting scholar has said.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/princess-fragrant-mixes-messages-on-ethnic-unity-expert-says/', 'snippet': 'The cartoon series is said to be aimed at improving ethnic relations, but the show’s Han creators appear to lack cultural knowledge about Uighurs, a visiting scholar has said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, The New York Times reported on the production in China of an animated television series with an exotic 10-year-old heroine, Princess Fragrant. The 104-episode series is loosely based on murky historical narratives about the Fragrant Concubine, an ethnic Uighur woman who in the 18th century was brought thousands of miles east to the Chinese imperial court in Beijing of the Qianlong Emperor, an ethnic Manchu, to be one of his consorts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/world/29sino-xinjiang01/29sino-xinjiang01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/28/world/29sino-xinjiang01/29sino-xinjiang01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/world/29sino-xinjiang01/29sino-xinjiang01-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/world/29sino-xinjiang01/29sino-xinjiang01-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/28/world/29sino-xinjiang01/29sino-xinjiang01-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/28/world/29sino-xinjiang01/29sino-xinjiang01-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth'