its already depleted coffers, DealBook’s David Gelles writes. As a result, business income tax revenue remains stagnant at about 2 percent of gross domestic product even as corporate profits hit records. Business taxes now make up less than 10 percent of federal revenue, down sharply from the years after World War II, when about 30 percent of federal revenue came from corporate taxes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Playing the Tax Game', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-29T11:42:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be9c300-ef01-5aa3-b59a-64684f9d9546', 'word_count': 2095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be9c300-ef01-5aa3-b59a-64684f9d9546'}, {'abstract': 'Two childhood experiences with water left Attis Clopton with a phobia that lasted for decades, until another major life event inspired him to face his fears.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000003081590/swimming-lessons.html', 'snippet': 'Two childhood experiences with water left Attis Clopton with a phobia that lasted for decades, until another major life event inspired him to face his fears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two childhood experiences with water left Attis Clopton with a phobia that lasted for decades, until another major life event inspired him to face his fears.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/nyregion/30swim-promo-art/30swim-promo-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, '