: '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'International Arts Events Happening in the Week Ahead', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-29T13:49:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher D. Shea', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5998bdf2-75af-50fd-945f-8cca8c8f234b', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5998bdf2-75af-50fd-945f-8cca8c8f234b'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/classical-playlist-gluck-jonathan-biss-morton-feldman-and-more/', 'snippet': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘DUETS OF LOVE AND PASSION’James McCracken, tenor; Sandra Warfield, mezzo-soprano(Decca 480 8165) Though the tenor James McCracken and the mezzo-soprano Sandra Warfield, who were married, did not make a point of performing together, they shared the stage many times in operas and concerts. This reissued recording, “Duets of Love and Passion,” originally released in 1964, presents the couple in scenes from Saint-Saëns’ “Samson et Dalila,” Bizet’s “Carmen” and two Verdi operas, “Otello” and “Aida.” McCracken’s muscular voice and intensity combine excitingly with Warfield’s dark colorings and warmth. Though Warfield, who died in 2009, had to accommodate her voice with some awkwardness to the subtle demands of Verdi’s Desdemona, a classic soprano role, she smolders as Verdi’s Amneris. The recording includes bonus tracks from “McCracken on Stage,” an aria album that shows this important tenor, who died in 1988, was not just in his element in Wagner, but bending phrases sensitively in Verdi. (Anthony Tommasini)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/classical-biss/classical-biss-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/classical-biss/classical-biss-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/classical-biss/classical-biss-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/classical-biss/classical-biss-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1252, 'width': 1976, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/classical-biss/classical-biss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/classical-biss/classical-biss-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/29/arts/classical-biss/classical-biss-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Classical Playlist: Gluck, Jonathan Biss, Morton Feldman and More', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Classical Playlist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biss, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feldman, Morton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gluck, Christoph Willibald Ritter von (1714-87)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCracken, James (1926-88)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warfield, Sandra', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-29T14:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97621e78-55bd-5b33-a6b8-b85e92ab2121', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97621e78-55bd-5b33-a6b8-b85e92ab2121'}, {'abstract': 'More retired Americans are getting rid of their homes and traveling, with 360,000 of them receiving Social Security benefits at foreign addresses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/30/business/increasingly-retirees-dump-their-possessions-and-hit-the-road.html', 'snippet': 'More retired Americans are getting rid of their homes and traveling, with 360,000 of them receiving Social Security benefits at foreign addresses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME call themselves “senior gypsies.” Others prefer “international nomad.” David Law, 74, a retired executive recruiter who has primarily slept in tents in several countries in the last two years, likes the ring of “American Bedouin.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/business/Retiring1/Retiring1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/30/business/Retiring1/Retiring1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 798}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/business/Retiring1/Retiring1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/business/Retiring1/Retiring1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1540, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/business/Retiring1/Retiring1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/30/business/Retiring1/Retiring1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/business/Retiring1/Retiring1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Increasingly, Retirees Dump Their Possessions and Hit the Road', 'kicker': 'Retiring', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Increasingly, Retirees Dump Their Possessions and Hit the Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Americans Abroad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-29T14:01:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Wallis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wallis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ff3f820-ced3-54dc-8391-83d195e2968f', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ff3f820-ced3-54dc-8391-83d195e2968f'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Correspondent’s report from the war zone, The New York Herald in 1914.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/1914-correspondent-in-the-war-zone/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Correspondent’s report from the war zone, The New York Herald in 1914.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Location withheld:— I have just arrived here from the Belgian frontier after inspecting the situation in the North. There was an air of expectancy in — when I reached it on Monday forenoon. News was scant and people were evidently becoming restless. Crowds were massed in the principal square watching the arrival from time to time of French soldiers with trophies captured from the enemy. Knots of men and women were gathered around villagers from the countryside and listening intently to vague accounts of fighting outside the city. About five o’clock the atmosphere in the streets began to change. It seemed panicky. Rumors were afloat that the Germans were arriving; that the Prefect had given orders for all the flags to be hauled down; that the Prussian cavalry would enter the city at nine o’clock! What these reports were worth at the time I do not know. But when, an hour or two later, I saw the officers in my hotel suddenly begin to pack their bags and pay their bills I considered it was time I prepared to move on, too, having no desire to be taken prisoner by the Germans. The tactics of the German cavalry is to appear here, there and everywhere, and the effect on the population is inevitable. We reached —— at noon. We felt at once that the Germans were near. There was that unmistakable atmosphere. A general air of deadness, stagnation and stifled fear; suspense and anxiety on every face. Scant news has filtered through of the great battle between Mons and Charleroi. It is, of course, a secondary line which has wisely fallen back on a stronger line in order to cope better with the German cavalry movement on our left, a movement which must be watched.—\xa0The New York Herald, European Edition, Aug. 30, 1914', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-retrospective-Mons/30iht-retrospective-Mons-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-retrospective-Mons/30iht-retrospective-Mons-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-retrospective-Mons/30iht-retrospective-Mons-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-retrospective-Mons/30iht-retrospective-Mons-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-retrospective-Mons/30iht-retrospective-Mons-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-retrospective-Mons/30iht-retrospective-Mons-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/blogs/30iht-retrospective-Mons/30iht-retrospective-Mons-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarg