nk': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-29T15:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80856044-23e5-591f-ae03-4ed2af16f3ad', 'word_count': 1054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80856044-23e5-591f-ae03-4ed2af16f3ad'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of her new pop-up at Dover Street Market — and to kick off New York Fashion Week, which begins after Labor Day — the Paris-based designer shares a list of some of her favorite sources of visual inspiration in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/new-york-travel-and-art-guide-gaia-repossi/', 'snippet': 'In honor of her new pop-up at Dover Street Market — and to kick off New York Fashion Week, which begins after Labor Day — the Paris-based designer shares a list of some of her favorite sources of visual inspiration in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past seven years, the Repossi creative director Gaia Repossi has been turning out jewelry that toes the line between fashion and fine art. On September 3rd and 4th, her delicate new collection — called “White Noise” and informed by the mobiles of Alexander Calder and the color palette of Franz West — makes its debut in a special installation at Dover Street Market New York, marking the first time an entire Repossi collection will be available stateside. In honor of its arrival — and to kick off New York Fashion Week, which begins after Labor Day — the Paris-based designer shares a list of some of her favorite sources for visual inspiration in New York, where she frequently travels for work and to visit her boyfriend, the artist Jeremy Everett.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi