le/388910a2-0857-581e-b003-bcec4128cd74', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/388910a2-0857-581e-b003-bcec4128cd74'}, {'abstract': 'As part of a tourism project, the Hudson Valley town of New Lebanon, N.Y., is being reimagined as what it hopes will be a “living museum of contemporary rural American life.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/30/arts/design/behold-new-lebanon-offers-rural-tourism.html', 'snippet': 'As part of a tourism project, the Hudson Valley town of New Lebanon, N.Y., is being reimagined as what it hopes will be a “living museum of contemporary rural American life.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW LEBANON, N.Y. — Small rural communities are perpetually marketing themselves. Witness the annual Heritage Spudfest in Boonsboro, Md., or the World’s Largest Ball of Twine in Cawker City, Kan. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Green Acres, the Place to Be', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Green Acres, the Place to Be', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Patricia Leigh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Lebanaon (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-29T17:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Leigh Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d985fc88-c23d-5a53-ae41-e1023090e6ef', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d985fc88-c23d-5a53-ae41-e1023090e6ef'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Philipp Engelhorn spent eight days capturing swimmers in the northern Chinese city of Qingdao, where elaborate face masks and bodysuits are a local tradition.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/qingdao-masked-sunbathers-photographs-philipp-engelhorn/', 'snippet': 'The photographer Philipp Engelhorn spent eight days capturing swimmers in the northern Chinese city of Qingdao, where elaborate face masks and bodysuits are a local tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The German-born, New York-trained photographer Philipp Engelhorn has spent the past 11 years living just off the beach in a village near Hong Kong. There, he has long been accustomed to seeing the local “Po Pos” (a slang term for elderly women) going for their morning swim. Engelhorn became intrigued, however, when he heard about how women in the northern Chinese city of Qingdao undertake the same ritual wearing colorful head masks and bodysuits. (The custom originated as a method of protection against the area’s giant stinging jellyfish, though\xa0many bathers also told Engelhorn their objective was to block the sun’s rays.) For eight days, he captured Qingdao swimmers in their elaborate armor — much of which, it turned out, was homemade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On One Chinese Beach, a Parade of Curiously Covered-Up Style', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qingdao (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-29T17:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Hirsch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirsch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a7edb9a-db89-5607-b42d-ce31776d7d7b', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a7edb9a-db89-5607-b42d-ce31776d7d7b'}, {'abstract': 'Berg’n is a vast new place in Crown Heights, Brooklyn, with food vendors and craft brews.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/nyregion/in-crown-heights-small-batch-food-scene-meets-beer-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Berg’n is a vast new place in Crown Heights, Brooklyn, with food vendors and craft brews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After raising the tent on Brooklyn’s small-batch food scene, the Smorgasburg empire has expanded into Crown Heights. Berg’n, a new beer hall with longtime food vendors from the weekend festivals, threw open its glass garage doors on Wednesday, revealing a nearly 9,000-square-foot room of dark wood and light-painted brick walls that felt instantly cool and comfortably full by lunchtime. Culinary options include Asia Dog and Pizza Moto, while the bar offers craft brews like Peekskill Simple Sour and Sixpoint Sweet Action.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/nyregion/31TABLE1/31TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/31/nyregion/31TABLE1/31TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/nyregion/31TABLE1/31TABLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', '