tistic director, Ángel Corella, has replaced several longtime artistic leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/29/shakeup-at-the-pennsylvania-ballet/', 'snippet': 'The ballet’s new artistic director, Ángel Corella, has replaced several longtime artistic leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In what looks like a sudden bloodletting occasioned by a recent change of artistic leadership, the Pennsylvania Ballet has dismissed Jeffrey Gribler, who was ballet master, and Tamara Hadley, who was ballet mistress, as well as William DeGregory, who was director of the company’s ballet school and the Pennsylvania Ballet II training company. Michael Sheridan, the assistant to the artistic director, and others in the company’s marketing and fund-raising departments were also let go. Most of those who were fired had been with the company for most of their careers. Mr. Gribler, for example, came to the company as an apprentice in 1975.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/arts/29artsbeat-corella/29artsbeat-corella-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/30/arts/29artsbeat-corella/29artsbeat-corella-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 815}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/arts/29artsbeat-corella/29artsbeat-corella-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 755, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/arts/29artsbeat-corella/29artsbeat-corella-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1509, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'