multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Blogs', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/d51a49c6-1711-54ea-b202-0dcf61c18b6c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d51a49c6-1711-54ea-b202-0dcf61c18b6c'}, {'abstract': 'There are plenty of public events on Sept. 1, many of them free, to help entertain families in need of escape from their own backyards. After Labor Day, some of these outdoor attractions will continue for weekends to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/nyregion/in-new-jersey-making-labor-day-less-laborious.html', 'snippet': 'There are plenty of public events on Sept. 1, many of them free, to help entertain families in need of escape from their own backyards. After Labor Day, some of these outdoor attractions will continue for weekends to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Labor Day is supposed to be about honoring workers with a day of rest. But for families with young children, the holiday can be anything but relaxing. Camp is over, summer vacations are winding down and school, for many, hasn’t started yet. Thankfully there are plenty of public events on Sept. 1, many of them free, to help entertain families in need of escape from their own backyards. After Labor Day, some of these outdoor attractions will continue for weekends to come, as long as the temperate weather holds out. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/nyregion/31ARTSNJ1/31ARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/31/nyregion/31ARTSNJ1/31ARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/nyregion