ep.html', 'snippet': 'Mirjana Lucic-Baroni’s upset victory at the U.S. Open is the latest twist in a story of pain, perseverance and premature success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After she popped an ace past Simona Halep on match point, Mirjana Lucic-Baroni dropped her racket to the court, turned to a small group of family and friends who were sitting nearby and stretched her arms out wide with her palms up. It was an expression with a meaning understood by everyone at the Grandstand on Friday afternoon: What just happened?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/sports/UPSET/UPSET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/30/sports/UPSET/UPSET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/sports/UPSET/UPSET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/sports/UPSET/UPSET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1486, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/sports/UPSET/UPSET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/30/sports/UPSET/UPSET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/30/sports/UPSET/UPSET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'c