lavering enemies and Elven gymnastics,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times, noting the director’s tendency “to pile it on.” Once again, she said, there are “too many busy, uninterestingly staged battles that lean heavily on obvious, sometimes distracting digital sorcery. But there are also pacific, brooding interludes in which the actors — notably Mr. Freeman, an intensely appealing screen presence — remind you that there’s more to Middle-earth than clamor and struggle.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cb94d74-2f49-5013-b727-9da1f8be5960', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cb94d74-2f49-5013-b727-9da1f8be5960'}, {'abstract': 'Under the latest timetable, Alibaba will hope to price its stock sale toward the later half of the week of Sept. 15, a person briefed on the matter said.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2014/08/30/alibaba-to-begin-investor-roadshow-on-week-of-sept-8/', 'snippet': 'Under the latest timetable, Alibaba will hope to price its stock sale toward the later half of the week of Sept. 15, a person briefed on the matter said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investors hoping to finally buy a piece of the Alibaba Group will have to wait a little longer. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alibaba to Begin Investor Roadshow in Week