 shock many of his fans, who know him as one of the country’s most prominent and articulate atheists.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1850, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Between Godliness and Godlessness', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Between Godliness and Godlessness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Sam (1967- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Atheism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Waking Up (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T15:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/46951231-edfe-51e2-b377-06529d259f86', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46951231-edfe-51e2-b377-06529d259f86'}, {'abstract': 'ISIS, the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria, is using every contemporary mode of messaging to recruit fighters, intimidate enemies and promote its claim to have established a caliphate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/world/middleeast/isis-displaying-a-deft-command-of-varied-media.html', 'snippet': 'ISIS, the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria, is using every contemporary mode of messaging to recruit fighters, intimidate enemies and promote its claim to have established a caliphate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The extremists who have seized large parts of Syria and Iraq have riveted the world’s attention with their military prowess and unrestrained brutality. But Western intelligence services are also worried about their extraordinary command of seemingly less lethal weapons: state-of-the-art videos, ground images shot from drones and multilingual Twitter messages.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ISIS Displaying a Deft Command of Varied Media', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ISIS Displaying a Deft Command of Varied Media', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Propaganda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T15:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane and Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3584beb7-fdd9-549d-940c-3a7ad5e2916b', 'word_count': 1730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3584beb7-fdd9-549d-940c-3a7ad5e2916b'}, {'abstract': 'The writer of the popular career guide, first commercially published in 1972, updates the book each year, but some of its original points are still true.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/jobs/what-color-is-your-parachute-is-still-going-strong.html', 'snippet': 'The writer of the popular career guide, first commercially published in 1972, updates the book each year, but some of its original points are still true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Bolles does not mince words. “Let us put the matter simply and candidly,” he writes. “The whole process of the job hunt in this country is Neanderthal.”', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-WORKSTATION-3/31-WORKSTATION-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-WORKSTATION-3/31-WORKSTATION-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 698}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-WORKSTATION-3/31-WORKSTATION-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 881, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-WORKSTATION-3/31-WORKSTATION-3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1945, 'width': 1673, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-WORKSTATION-3/31-WORKSTATION-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-WORKSTATION-3/31-WORKSTATION-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-WORKSTATION-3/31-WORKSTATION-3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Career Guide, 42 Years of Soft Landings', 'kicker': 'Workstation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Career Guide, 42 Years of Soft Landings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Korkki, Phyllis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolles, Richard Nelson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ten Speed Press', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'What Color Is Your Parachute? (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T15:59:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phyllis Korkki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phyllis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Korkki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99d76934-5d7f-5ff1-b086-727c3ee54d22', 'word_count': 1233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99d76934-5d7f-5ff1-b086-727c3ee54d22'}, {'abstract': 'Can you find the proper names or titles that Will Shortz has hidden from us?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/30/variety-camouflage/', 'snippet': 'Can you find the proper names or titles that Will Shortz has hidden from us?', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARIETY PUZZLE — Well, this was a fun and refreshing puzzle. As it says in the instructions, this puzzle was completed in seven minutes and 40 seconds by Jeffrey Harris of Nashville, Tenn., at the recent National Puzzlers’ League Convention in Portland, Me. That’s not exactly news, as he is an exceptionally brilliant person who tends to win most of these things, so sincere congratulations, Mr. Harris. To the rest of you, a word of warning: If you ever see Mr. Harris sharpening his pencil within your line of sight at a puzzle tournament, run for your lives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Camouflage', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T16:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4804cd45-4e3e-58f8-a607-48a0271c0c08', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4804cd45-4e3e-58f8-a607-48a0271c0c08'}, {'abstract': 'Our family lived on the road for several years when I was young. This summer, we tried it again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/opinion/sunday/a-family-hits-the-road.html', 'snippet': 'Our family lived on the road for several years when I was young. This summer, we tried it again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RUSTED ROOT’s song “Send Me on My Way” is blaring as my sister, Cassidy, winds our little Nissan Sentra through the serpentine roads of the Cascade Mountains in Oregon. The fresh basil my dad bought as a “car freshener” is wilting on the dash, adding to the smells from our dirt-covered clothes, rich with the odors of helping out at a friend’s farm.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Family Hits the Road', 'kicker': 'Exposures', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Family Hits the Road', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'na