_paragraph': 'MANY white Americans say they are fed up with the coverage of the shooting of Michael Brown in Ferguson, Mo. A plurality of whites in a recent Pew survey said that the issue of race is getting more attention than it deserves.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Whites Just Don’t Get It', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Whites Just Don’t Get It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T16:49:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fd4ae41-ecd8-5b5c-b00f-65cf82d55e27', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fd4ae41-ecd8-5b5c-b00f-65cf82d55e27'}, {'abstract': 'The country’s prime minister said the actions amounted to a coup, although a spokesman for the army said the soldiers were only securing the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/world/africa/lesotho-military-moves-on-police.html', 'snippet': 'The country’s prime minister said the actions amounted to a coup, although a spokesman for the army said the soldiers were only securing the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAKAR, Senegal — A military coup in the tiny southern African kingdom of Lesotho has chased out the prime minister and apparently put the army in control of the landlocked nation, witnesses and journalists in the capital said on Saturday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lesotho Military Moves on Police', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lesotho’s Prime Minister Flees Amid Apparent Military Coup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lesotho', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thabane, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T16:57:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c46113aa-9d53-52e9-bf68-2eb6c10de6bd', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c46113aa-9d53-52e9-bf68-2eb6c10de6bd'}, {'abstract': 'In the second year of Hassan Rouhani’s presidency, he has struck a new tone, echoing the longstanding Iranian view that the United States can never be trusted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/world/middleeast/iran.html', 'snippet': 'In the second year of Hassan Rouhani’s presidency, he has struck a new tone, echoing the longstanding Iranian view that the United States can never be trusted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — For more than a year, Iran’s president, Hassan Rouhani, had been walking a political tightrope by trying to restore some level of relations with the country’s archenemy, the United States. His hard-line opponents pelted him with eggs for his efforts, while those who voted for him hoped for a possible thaw.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/IRAN/IRAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/31/world/IRAN/IRAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/IRAN/IRAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/IRAN/IRAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1320, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/IRAN/IRAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/31/world/IRAN/IRAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/IRAN/IRAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headl