aterial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b1480d2-913e-5f98-8bd5-07ab6ed218d2', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b1480d2-913e-5f98-8bd5-07ab6ed218d2'}, {'abstract': 'Gunfire broke out on Saturday between United Nations peacekeepers in southern Syria and the Islamist rebels who had been surrounding their base near the Israeli-occupied Golan Heights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/world/middleeast/syrian-rebels-trade-fire-with-un-peacekeepers.html', 'snippet': 'Gunfire broke out on Saturday between United Nations peacekeepers in southern Syria and the Islamist rebels who had been surrounding their base near the Israeli-occupied Golan Heights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — Two bases for United Nations peacekeepers came under fire in southern Syria on Saturday, the United Nations said. One base was evacuated, and soldiers on the second returned fire, and later left the area.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Rebels Trade Fire With Troops From U.N.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syrian Rebels Trade Fire With Troops From U.N.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Golan Heights', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T17:36:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09fabcfd-036d-5aae-93cb-f09bed89760a', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09fabcfd-036d-5aae-93cb-f09bed89760a'}, {'abstract': 'A pop-up restaurant company is dedicated to the notion that high-end chefs should listen to their customers’ feedback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/business/dinner-lab-brings-the-wisdom-of-crowds-to-haute-cuisine.html', 'snippet': 'A pop-up restaurant company is dedicated to the notion that high-end chefs should listen to their customers’ feedback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a late July evening, and Christopher Sorter had just finished cooking an exotic five-course meal that included such triple-dare dishes as beef heart ragù and crème brûlée with bone marrow. When the dinner began, there had been some apprehension about the food among the 120 guests who had gathered in a warehouselike space in Silver Spring, Md. But as waiters cleared the last plates, the event had a relieved and jubilant air, as if everyone had just narrowly dodged a bus.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-DINNERLAB-JP7/31-DINNERLAB-JP7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-DINNERLAB-JP7/31-DINNERLAB-JP7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/business/31-DINNERLAB-JP7/31-DINNERLAB-JP7-jumbo.jpg', 