ism on Thursday when he said, “we don’t have a strategy yet,” for military action against ISIS in Syria. Lawmakers will weigh in on Mr. Obama’s comments on the Sunday shows.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/30/sunday-breakfast-menu-aug-31/', 'snippet': 'President Obama drew criticism on Thursday when he said, “we don’t have a strategy yet,” for military action against ISIS in Syria. Lawmakers will weigh in on Mr. Obama’s comments on the Sunday shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a news briefing on Thursday, President Obama urged restraint and calm amid the continuing violence in Iraq and Ukraine, but he drew criticism when he said “we don’t have a strategy yet” for military action against Sunni extremists in Syria. Josh Earnest, the White House press secretary, appeared on several networks that evening to clarify the comment, saying that Mr. Obama was only speaking of Syria, and that the White House did have a strategy to combat the ISIS extremists who have crossed into Iraq.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, Aug. 31', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T19:28:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elena Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b222833c-983e-5c7c-bc90-1b938b27f7b6', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b222833c-983e-5c7c-bc90-1b938b27f7b6'}, {'abstract': 'Johnny Manziel has spurred ticket and merchandise sales as well as hopes that the Browns may someday win a championship, something that hasn’t happened since 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://www