, 'snippet': 'Welsh nationalists have made the Scottish independence bid their own in the hope that it will stir passions at home — if not for full independence, at least for more self-government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAERNARFON, Wales — Twm Morys was boiling carrots for his children when he momentarily stopped to recite a 15th-century battle chant in Welsh. Beating out the guttural consonants with a stave on his kitchen floor until they rang in every last corner of his farmhouse, Mr. Morys, a well-known poet, said it was time to put “fire in the belly” of his people.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/WALES-1/WALES-1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/31/world/WALES-1/WALES-1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/WALES-1/WALES-1-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/WALES-1/WALES-1-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/WALES-1/WALES-1-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/31/world/WALES-1/WALES-1-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/world/WALES-1/WALES-1-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Scots Weigh Independence, Wales Takes Note', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Scots Weigh Independence, Wales Takes Note', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wales', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-30T22:24:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrin Bennhold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a8a694d-a3f0-5f8e-baed-f1eb01f8c68c', 'word_count': 1301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a8a694d-a3f0-5f8e-baed-f1eb01f8c68c'}, {'abstract': 'Medicare may cover advance care planning that was once decried as “death panels,” and some private insurers are not waiting for the political process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/health/end-of-life-talks-may-finally-overcome-politics.html', 'snippet': 'Medicare may cover advance care planning that was once decried as “death panels,” and some private insurers are not waiting for the political process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUNDEE, N.Y. — Five years after it exploded into a political conflagration over “death panels,” the issue of paying doctors to talk to patients about end-of-life care is making a comeback, and such sessions may be covered for the 50 million Americans on Medicare as early as next year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/us/JP-ADVANCE-1/JP-ADVANCE-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/08/31/us/JP-ADVANCE-1/JP-ADVANCE-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/us/JP-ADVANCE-1/JP-ADVANCE-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/us/JP-ADVANCE-1/JP-ADVANCE-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/us/JP-ADVANCE-1/JP-ADVANCE-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/08/31/us/JP-ADVANCE-1/JP-ADVANCE-1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/08/31/us/JP-ADVANCE-1/JP-ADVANCE-1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coverage for End-of-Life Talks Gaining Ground', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coverage for End-of-Life Talks Gaining Ground', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belluck, Pam', 'rank': 1, 'ma