sees himself remaining in sports, tennis or otherwise, after his playing days are behind him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Murray won the United States Open boys’ singles title ten years ago, but since then, he has had few chances to play on the outer courts of major tournaments. In his latest conversation with The New York Times, Murray spoke of what makes a good court and his thoughts on life after tennis. In previous interviews at the\xa0U.S. Open, Murray has discussed\xa0his perspective on this year’s tournament,\xa0female coaches in tennis and the idea of an independent Scotland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Andy Murray Discusses Favorite Courts, and the Future', 'kicker': 'Q. And A.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Andy Murray Discusses Favorite Courts, and the Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy (1987- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2014-08-31T23:25:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/08e5efe3-dd63-5a40-8314-4b61623b199a', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08e5efe3-dd63-5a40-8314-4b61623b199a'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: The driver and passengers on a crosstown bus cooperated to help back up a woman’s threat to her misbehaving son.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2014/08/31/calling-time-out-on-the-bus/', 'snip